harnessTailCount":0,"harnessSectionHash":"4cb5b5da0b63f79c","content":[{"type":"text","text":"### Agent 7: Invariants, Failures, Gates, Degradation\n\nFocus:\n- Transcribe with perfect fidelity the ownership tables of §9 invariants (I1–I8), §10 failure catalogue (F1–F19), and §11 gates/degradation/observability, including every \"Asserted from\" / \"Closed at\" milestone attribution.\n\nRequirements Extracted:\n- [Invariant] I1 | `point_id = uuid5(page_id)`; unique `page_id` assert; `count(doc, rev) == pdf.page_count` after publish | asserted-from: M2a (Spec §9)\n- [Invariant] I2 | `probe.py` is the only writer of `text`; source-scan test; `lookup(\"K999\")` on a hallucinated code → `not_found`, and only `unverified_hits` when opted in | asserted-from: M1 (Spec §9)\n- [Invariant] I3 | one `exact_filter`; no `MatchText` in `serve/`; property test: every variant equals the label with whitespace stripped | asserted-from: M1 (Spec §9)\n- [Invariant] I4 | §6.4's two independent checks; failure bisects and re-bills | asserted-from: M2a (Spec §9)\n- [Invariant] I5 | the `SearchResponse` validator (Family A, §7.1) | asserted-from: M1 (Spec §9)\n- [Invariant] I6 | one `INDEXED` dict creates, gates and is asserted at boot | asserted-from: M1 (Spec §9)\n- [Invariant] I7 | `is_current=False` until gates pass; every tool injects `is_current=True` | asserted-from: M2a (Spec §9)\n- [Invariant] I8 | the answer gate, per `(claim, page)` | asserted-from: M6 (Spec §9)\n- [Failure] F1 | guard: I3 phrase-only | test: `lookup(\"SF 1.1A\")` → exactly 1 | closed-at: M1 (Spec §10)\n- [Failure] F2 | guard: the one `exact_filter` | test: `verify(\"SF 1.1A\", [p008])` → `absent` | closed-at: M1 (core) · M3 (tool) (Spec §10)\n- [Failure] F3 | guard: I3 variants | test: the 8 compact labels | closed-at: M1 (Spec §10)\n- [Failure] F4 | guard: `has_text` facet + I5 | test: scanned doc → `not_searchable` | closed-at: M2a · M3 (Spec §10)\n- [Failure] F5 | guard: label precedence, `label_verified`, ambiguity → list | test: misread label → flagged, never silent | closed-at: M2a · M4 (Spec §10)\n- [Failure] F6 | guard: per-page `grounded_rate`, reattribution, I8 | test: code moved → `moved_from` recorded | closed-at: M2a (Spec §10)\n- [Failure] F7 | guard: I4 | test: synthetic 3-window PDF fixture | closed-at: M2a (Spec §10)\n- [Failure] F8 | guard: canonical section key + carry-in + `series_id`; stateless + `effective_scope` | test: straddling-section fixture | closed-at: M2a (stitching) · M4 (stateless scope) · M8 (`series_id`) (Spec §10)\n- [Failure] F9 | guard: `is_current` injected by default; `found_only_in_superseded` | test: two revisions indexed | closed-at: M8 (Spec §10)\n- [Failure] F10 | guard: I6 | test: unknown scope key → 400 | closed-at: M1 (Spec §10)\n- [Failure] F11 | guard: key includes resolved model id + prompt version; aliases refused at boot | test: key changes when the prompt changes | closed-at: M0 (boot) · M2a (key) (Spec §10)\n- [Failure] F12 | guard: I1 + retirement scoped to the same `(doc_id, revision)` (§6.7) — never a blanket delete, which would destroy F9's evidence | test: re-ingest twice → same count | closed-at: M2a (Spec §10)\n- [Failure] F13 | guard: output-budget ladder; `MAX_TOKENS` → bisect | test: oversized window bisects | closed-at: M2a (Spec §10)\n- [Failure] F14 | guard: I2 | test: the hallucination test | closed-at: M1 (Spec §10)\n- [Failure] F15 | guard: `text` always from the full page | test: crop fixture → full text indexed | closed-at: M2a (Spec §10)\n- [Failure] F16 | guard: `present_instead` = capped prefix lookup over observed tokens, never a distance | test: `K73` on a K78 page → `absent` + `present_instead` | closed-at: M1 (Spec §10)\n- [Failure] F17 | guard: I7 | test: kill an ingest mid-run → 0 pages queryable | closed-at: M2a (Spec §10)\n- [Failure] F18 | guard: §7.3 caps, each a typed 400 | test: over-budget → error naming the bound | closed-at: M4 (`fetch`) · M5 (`read`) (Spec §10)\n- [Failure] F19 | guard: `read_key` includes the question | test: same pages, new question → cache miss | closed-at: M5 (Spec §10)\n- [PublishGate] `window_coverage` | pages with an S2 record ÷ page count | must be 1.0 after retries | block (Spec §11.1)\n- [PublishGate] `offset_check` | windows passing I4 | all | block (Spec §11.1)\n- [PublishGate] `grounded_rate` | median over pages with `has_text` (§5.7) | ≥ 0.8 (provisional — set from M2b distribution, R4) | block, hold for review, list worst pages; override path: `vsir publish --override grounded_rate --reason \"…\"` (§4.4) — reason recorded in the run, every page flagged `published_with_override` (Spec §11.1)\n- [PublishGate] `text_coverage` | pages with `has_text` ÷ total | no threshold specified (—) | never block, flag `mostly_scanned`; at 0.0 the `grounded_rate` gate is skipped entirely, document published and answers `not_searchable` (F4, D3) rather than being quarantined (Spec §11.1)\n- [PublishGate] `label_monotonic` | printed labels non-decreasing | — | flag `label_conflict` (Spec §11.1)\n- [AnswerGate] Codes usable only as `verify` cleared them (I8); abstention wording constrained (§8.5) (Spec §11.2)\n- [AnswerGate] A page whose `text_trust != ok` may support an answer only after a zoom-and-re-read; its codes carry the \"read from image\" badge (Spec §11.2)\n- [Degradation] Qdrant unreachable → `503 qdrant_unavailable`, retryable, never an empty result; `/ready` goes red, `/health` stays green (§15.1) (Spec §11.3)\n- [Degradation] Gemini unreachable → `503 vlm_unavailable` on `read`; every free tool keeps working (Spec §11.3)\n- [Degradation] index schema ≠ `INDEXED` → refuse to serve at boot (Spec §11.3)\n- [Degradation] embedding model ≠ collection fingerprint → refuse to upsert; new collection + re-embed + alias swap (Spec §11.3)\n- [Degradation] model id ends in `-latest` → refuse to start (Spec §11.3)\n- [Degradation] a document's `grounded_rate` collapses → `text_trust = \"untrusted\"` (§5.7); its pages count as unsearchable; `verify` → `unverifiable` (Spec §11.3)\n- [Degradation] per-caller `read` quota exhausted → `429 budget_exhausted`, not silent truncation (Spec §11.3)\n- [Degradation] over-budget `fetch` → typed 400 naming the bound — never a dpi clamp or a truncated page list (Spec §11.3)\n- [Observability] Prometheus gauges `ingest_grounded_rate_median{doc_id}`, `ingest_gate_failures_total{gate}`; `GET /runs/{run_id}` (§6.9); the audit log (§7.4); triage marks to telemetry (Spec §11.4)\n\nInvariants / Failure Rows Touched:\n- I1, I2, I3, I4, I5, I6, I7, I8, F1, F2, F3, F4, F5, F6, F7, F8, F9, F10, F11, F12, F13, F14, F15, F16, F17, F18, F19\n\nDependencies Identified:\n- Every failure row's guard depends on one or more invariants (F1/F3→I3, F2→exact_filter [I3 mechanism], F4→I5, F6→I8, F7→I4, F9→is_current [I7 mechanism], F10→I6, F12→I1, F14→I2, F17→I7) — so invariant assertion timing gates failure-closure timing.\n- Publish gates (§11.1) depend on per-page `grounded_rate` and `has_text` facet, which are also the guard mechanisms for F4 and F6.\n- The `grounded_rate` collapse degradation row (§11.3) depends on the same `text_trust` mechanism referenced in §11.2's answer gate.\n- F8's three-way split depends on three separate mechanisms maturing across milestones: canonical section key + carry-in (M2a), stateless + `effective_scope` (M4), `series_id` (M8).\n- F11's split depends on boot-time alias refusal (M0) preceding key-composition logic (M2a).\n- F18's split depends on `fetch`'s budget cap (M4) preceding `read`'s budget cap (M5).\n\nTechnical Constraints:\n- `grounded_rate` publish-gate threshold (≥ 0.8) is explicitly marked provisional, to be set from the M2b distribution (R4) — not yet final.\n- Publish gates apply atomically: a document is either fully published or quarantined, never partially.\n- `text_coverage` at exactly 0.0 causes the `grounded_rate` gate to be skipped entirely (special-cased zero-boundary behavior).\n- Retirement in F12's guard must be scoped to the same `(doc_id, revision)` — a blanket delete is explicitly forbidden because it would destroy the evidence F9 depends on.\n- `present_instead` (F16) must be a capped prefix lookup over observed tokens — explicitly never a distance-based/fuzzy match.\n- Every degradation row is defined as a refusal (typed error/status), never a best-effort fallback (e.g., never an empty result, never a dpi clamp, never silent truncation).\n\nSpec References:\n- Spec §9 (Invariants I1–I8)\n- Spec §10 (Failure catalogue F1–F19)\n- Spec §11.1 (Publish gates)\n- Spec §11.2 (Answer gates)\n- Spec §11.3 (Runtime degradation)\n- Spec §11.4 (Observability)\n- Cross-references within region: §6.4, §6.7, §6.9, §5.7, §7.1, §7.3, §7.4, §8.5, §4.4, §15.1\n\nContradictions Noticed (report only, do not resolve):\n- I8 is listed as \"asserted from M6\" (§9), yet F6's guard explicitly includes I8 and F6 is \"closed at M2a\" (§10) — a failure row closes at a milestone earlier than the invariant it depends on is even asserted.\n- The `text_coverage` publish gate lists its threshold as \"—\" (no numeric value) in the Threshold column, but the Action column then references a specific boundary value (\"At 0.0 the `grounded_rate` gate is skipped entirely\"), implying an implicit threshold that isn't stated in the Threshold column itself."}],"resolvedModel":"claude-sonnet-5","totalDurationMs":59250,"totalTokens":30206,"totalToolUseCount":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4239,"cache_read_input_tokens":18842,"output_tokens":7123,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":3065},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4239},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":7123,"cache_read_input_tokens":18842,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4239,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4239,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens"