y` (Spec §4.1)\n- [Layout] `backend/tests/unit/` (L0–L1), `api/` (L2–L3), `paid/` (L4) — no marker given (Spec §4.1)\n- [Layout] `frontend/` — React + TypeScript + Vite, M7 only; no marker given (Spec §4.1)\n- [Layout] `e2e/` — Playwright, \"exists\"; no marker given (Spec §4.1)\n- [Layout] `data/source/` — input PDFs, gitignored except generated fixtures; no marker given (Spec §4.1)\n- [Layout] `data/fixtures/` — frozen extractions, checked in; no marker given (Spec §4.1)\n- [Layout] `scripts/test-unit.sh`, `test-api.sh`, `test-e2e.sh`, `test-paid.sh` — \"exists, extend\"; no marker given (Spec §4.1)\n- [Pin] Python 3.11, exact minor pinned by the image digest — Factor II (Spec §4.2)\n- [Pin] `impl/requirements.txt`-carried pins: `fastapi==0.141.1`, `uvicorn[standard]==0.52.4`, `python-multipart==0.0.32`, `google-genai==2.22.0`, `qdrant-client==1.19.0`, `PyMuPDF==1.28.2`, `pillow==12.3.0`, `PyYAML>=6.0.2` (drop PyYAML if config is env-only, §15 III); bump deliberately, never incidentally (Spec §4.2)\n- [Pin] `qdrant-client` / Qdrant server: `1.19.0` / `qdrant/qdrant:v1.19.0` — required for `phrase_matching` (Spec §4.2)\n- [Pin] FastAPI + Pydantic v2, current versions — all request/response models typed (Spec §4.2)\n- [Pin] PyMuPDF pinned exact version, recorded in `probe_version` — F15, extractor is point of truth (Spec §4.2)\n- [Pin] Gemini SDK — `google-genai`, pinned (Spec §4.2)\n- [Pin] VLM model id — `VSIR_VLM_MODEL`, pinned id for Gemini 3.8 Flash; cost basis note on 1 Jan 2027 price step $0.75/$3.75 → $1.50/$7.50, programme prices at 2027 rate; boot refuses any id ending `-latest` (F11) (Spec §4.2)\n- [Pin] Embedding model — `VSIR_EMBED_MODEL`, Gemini Embedding 2 (text); cost basis $0.20/1M, $0.10 batch per `effort_and_llm_cost_estimation.md` §\"Pricing basis\"; provider-agnostic interface, `dim` recorded; text only, page rasters not embedded (C12); collection fingerprint (§6.6): a change is a new collection, never in-place mix; id pinned, never `-latest` (Spec §4.2)\n- [Pin] MCP — official Python SDK, stdio + SSE (Spec §4.2)\n- [Config] Store — Qdrant only, two collections: `vsir_pages` (page index) and `vsir_runs` (control plane: runs, windows, observed-token inventory; D9); no relational database, no ORM, no migrations, no queue service; conformance grep bans `alembic`, `sqlalchemy` (Spec §4.2)\n- [Config] Rasters — never persisted; rendered on demand into in-process LRU cache; cold instance returns identical results, only slower — §15 Factor VI; no blob store, no local source of truth (Spec §4.2)\n- [Config] Render dpi — `dpi_index = 150` (raster that gets embedded); `dpi_answer = 220` (raster `read` sees, pinned, part of `read_key`); both ported verbatim from `impl/config.yaml`; F19, §7.2.6; `fetch` defaults to 150, escalates on request (§7.3) (Spec §4.2)\n- [Config] Embedding parameters — `dim` ∈ {768, 1536, 3072} via `output_dimensionality` (MRL truncation, dim recorded in collection name); `concurrency=8`; `batch_size=8`; `max_edge_px=1568`; all from `impl/config.yaml`; changing `dim` is a re-embed, never in place (§6.6) (Spec §4.2)\n- [Config] Fusion parameters — surface weights `page=1.0`, `lexical=1.0`, `captions=0.4`; `rrf_k=60`; `cap_pages_per_window=30`; `lookup_cap=20`; ported from `impl/config.yaml` (D2) (Spec §4.2)\n- [Config] Ingest render dpi — `220`, recorded on every record, part of `extract_key` (Spec §4.2)\n- [Port] Backend dev port `8000` (Spec §4.2)\n- [Port] Backend test port `8001` (impl publishes `8100→8000`) (Spec §4.2)\n- [Port] Qdrant dev ports `6333` REST and `6334` gRPC (Spec §4.2)\n- [Port] Qdrant test port `6335` (never `6334`) (Spec §4.2)\n- [Port] Frontend dev port `5173` (Spec §4.2)\n- [Port] Frontend test port `5174` (Spec §4.2)\n- [Config] `docker-compose.test.yml` must be rewritten from Postgres to Qdrant at M0 (Spec §4.2)\n- [BootRefusal] Refuse to start (named reason, non-zero exit) when a configured model id ends in `-latest` (Spec §4.3)\n- [BootRefusal] Refuse to start when the live Qdrant payload schema lacks any key in `INDEXED` (Spec §4.3)\n- [BootRefusal] Refuse to start when the collection fingerprint does not match the configured embedding model (Spec §4.3)\n- [BootRefusal] Refuse to start when `text`/`vlm_codes` are not text indexes with `phrase_matching=True` (Spec §4.3)\n- [BootRefusal] Refuse to start when a required env var is missing (Spec §4.3)\n- [BootRefusal] Never degrade to a partial service — applies to all refusal conditions, and to server start in addition to `vsir doctor` (Spec §4.3)\n- [CLI] `vsir doctor` — the boot self-check of §4.3; prints `release_id`, resolved model ids, index fingerprint — first appears M0 (Spec §4.4)\n- [CLI] `vsir demo exact --synthetic` — seed synthetic pages, run the exact-surface assertions — first appears M1 (Spec §4.4)\n- [CLI] `vsir demo narrow` — the narrowing demo over the frozen fixture — first appears M4 (Spec §4.4)\n- [CLI] `vsir ingest <pdf> [--vlm stub] [--resume <run_id>] [--steal]` — steps 01–12; `--steal` required to take a live lease (D9) — first appears M2a (Spec §4.4)\n- [CLI] `vsir runs show <run_id>` — the run record of §6.9 — first appears M2a (Spec §4.4)\n- [CLI] `vsir gates rerun <run_id>` — re-evaluate the publish gates of §11.1 — first appears M2a (Spec §4.4)\n- [CLI] `vsir retire <doc_id> [--revision]` — remove a document (or one revision) from the index, replaces impl's `DELETE /api/v1/documents/{doc_id}` (§2.5 A) — first appears M8 (Spec §4.4)\n- [CLI] `vsir publish <run_id> --override <gate> --reason \"<text>\"` — release a document a gate is holding; reason recorded in the run, every page flagged `published_with_override` — first appears M2b (Spec §4.4)\n- [CLI] `vsir serve` — the HTTP surface of §7.4 — first appears M3 (Spec §4.4)\n- [CLI] `vsir mcp [--stdio|--sse]` — the MCP surface of §7.5 — first appears M3 (Spec §4.4)\n- [CLI] `vsir lookup` · `verify` · `resolve` · `skim` · `fetch` · `read` — one-shot tool calls for demos and scripts — first appears M3, through M5 (Spec §4.4)\n- [CLI] `vsir ask \"<question>\"` — the runner of §8 — first appears M6 (Spec §4.4)\n- [CLI] `vsir eval acceptance | abstention | corpus` — §12.3 · §12.4 · §12.6 — first appears M3, also M8 (Spec §4.4)\n\nInvariants / Failure Rows Touched:\n- F11 — boot refuses any VLM/embedding model id ending in `-latest` (Spec §4.2, §4.3)\n- F13 — `window.py`'s bisection ladder is a net addition over the ported `windows.py` (Spec §4.1)\n- F15 — PyMuPDF pinned exact version recorded in `probe_version`; extractor is the point of truth (Spec §4.2)\n- F19 — render dpi pinning (`dpi_index`/`dpi_answer`) referenced against §7.2.6 (Spec §4.2)\n\nDependencies Identified:\n- §2.4 — the port/adapt/write framing that the `←`/`≈`/`+` markers implement (Spec §4.1)\n- D4 — interleaved embedding referenced by `ingest/embed.py` (Spec §4.1)\n- D2 — sparse indexing and fusion parameters (Spec §4.1, §4.2)\n- D9 — control-plane collection `vsir_runs` and `--steal` lease semantics (Spec §4.2, §4.4)\n- C12 — text-only embedding constraint (rasters not embedded) (Spec §4.2)\n- §15 Factor II, VI, XII — image-digest pinning, no local source of truth for rasters, CLI as sole operational surface (Spec §4.2, §4.4)\n- §15 III — conditional PyYAML pin dependent on config being env-only (Spec §4.2)\n- §6.6 — collection fingerprint / re-embed-is-new-collection rule (Spec §4.2)\n- §7.2.6, §7.3 — dpi pinning and `fetch` escalation behavior (Spec §4.2)\n- §6.9 — run record shape referenced by `vsir runs show` (Spec §4.4)\n- §11.1 — publish gates referenced by `vsir gates rerun` and `vsir publish` (Spec §4.4)\n- §2.5 A — impl's `DELETE /api/v1/documents/{doc_id}` endpoint replaced by `vsir retire` (Spec §4.4)\n- §7.4, §7.5 — HTTP and MCP surfaces backing `vsir serve` / `vsir mcp` (Spec §4.4)\n- §8 — runner loop referenced by `vsir ask` (Spec §4.4)\n- §12.3, §12.4, §12.6 — eval subcommands' definitions (Spec §4.4)\n- `effort_and_llm_cost_estimation.md` §\"Pricing basis\" — external doc backing embedding-model pricing (Spec §4.2)\n\nTechnical Constraints:\n- No relational database, no ORM, no migrations, no queue service; conformance grep enforces this by banning `alembic` and `sqlalchemy` imports (Spec §4.2)\n- Rasters are never persisted to disk/blob store — only an in-process LRU cache, so a cold instance must still return identical results (Spec §4.2)\n- Any embedding `dim` change forces a brand-new collection, never an in-place mix/update (Spec §4.2)\n- Boot self-check and server start share the same refusal conditions; no partial-service degrade path exists (Spec §4.3)\n- `vsir` CLI is stated as \"the only supported operational surface\" (Spec §4.4)\n\nSpec References:\n- Spec §4.1, §4.2, §4.3, §4.4\n\nContradictions Noticed (report only, do not resolve):\n- Two dpi=220 values are given under different names with no stated relationship: `dpi_answer = 220` (pinned, part of `read_key`, §4.2 Render dpi row) vs. \"Ingest render dpi | `220`, recorded on every record ... part of `extract_key`\" (§4.2 Ingest render dpi row) — unclear whether these are the same physical render reused across two keys or two independent 220-dpi renders.\n- Two distinct `verify.py` modules are named in the layout with no cross-reference: `core/verify.py` (+ net new, alongside `status.py`/`indexed.py`) and `serve/tools/verify.py` (+ net new, alongside `fetch.py`) — the CLI table's `vsir ... verify ...` one-shot command (§4.4) does not indicate which module backs it, and the boot self-check's schema/index checks (§4.3) could plausibly draw on either.","usage":{"total_tokens":32947,"tool_uses":1,"duration_ms":102874},"uuid":"7d0b51d4-0ae8-49fc-ac78-dd884c40b5b9","session_id":"4eefb16f-3989-4441-9cd3-d294cfccb11f"}
