c §4.4)\n\nInvariants / Failure Rows Touched:\n- F11 — boot refuses any VLM/embedding model id ending in `-latest` (Spec §4.2, §4.3)\n- F13 — `window.py`'s bisection ladder is a net addition over the ported `windows.py` (Spec §4.1)\n- F15 — PyMuPDF pinned exact version recorded in `probe_version`; extractor is the point of truth (Spec §4.2)\n- F19 — render dpi pinning (`dpi_index`/`dpi_answer`) referenced against §7.2.6 (Spec §4.2)\n\nDependencies Identified:\n- §2.4 — the port/adapt/write framing that the `←`/`≈`/`+` markers implement (Spec §4.1)\n- D4 — interleaved embedding referenced by `ingest/embed.py` (Spec §4.1)\n- D2 — sparse indexing and fusion parameters (Spec §4.1, §4.2)\n- D9 — control-plane collection `vsir_runs` and `--steal` lease semantics (Spec §4.2, §4.4)\n- C12 — text-only embedding constraint (rasters not embedded) (Spec §4.2)\n- §15 Factor II, VI, XII — image-digest pinning, no local source of truth for rasters, CLI as sole operational surface (Spec §4.2, §4.4)\n- §15 III — conditional PyYAML pin dependent on config being env-only (Spec §4.2)\n- §6.6 — collection fingerprint / re-embed-is-new-collection rule (Spec §4.2)\n- §7.2.6, §7.3 — dpi pinning and `fetch` escalation behavior (Spec §4.2)\n- §6.9 — run record shape referenced by `vsir runs show` (Spec §4.4)\n- §11.1 — publish gates referenced by `vsir gates rerun` and `vsir publish` (Spec §4.4)\n- §2.5 A — impl's `DELETE /api/v1/documents/{doc_id}` endpoint replaced by `vsir retire` (Spec §4.4)\n- §7.4, §7.5 — HTTP and MCP surfaces backing `vsir serve` / `vsir mcp` (Spec §4.4)\n- §8 — runner loop referenced by `vsir ask` (Spec §4.4)\n- §12.3, §12.4, §12.6 — eval subcommands' definitions (Spec §4.4)\n- `effort_and_llm_cost_estimation.md` §\"Pricing basis\" — external doc backing embedding-model pricing (Spec §4.2)\n\nTechnical Constraints:\n- No relational database, no ORM, no migrations, no queue service; conformance grep enforces this by banning `alembic` and `sqlalchemy` imports (Spec §4.2)\n- Rasters are never persisted to disk/blob store — only an in-process LRU cache, so a cold instance must still return identical results (Spec §4.2)\n- Any embedding `dim` change forces a brand-new collection, never an in-place mix/update (Spec §4.2)\n- Boot self-check and server start share the same refusal conditions; no partial-service degrade path exists (Spec §4.3)\n- `vsir` CLI is stated as \"the only supported operational surface\" (Spec §4.4)\n\nSpec References:\n- Spec §4.1, §4.2, §4.3, §4.4\n\nContradictions Noticed (report only, do not resolve):\n- Two dpi=220 values are given under different names with no stated relationship: `dpi_answer = 220` (pinned, part of `read_key`, §4.2 Render dpi row) vs. \"Ingest render dpi | `220`, recorded on every record ... part of `extract_key`\" (§4.2 Ingest render dpi row) — unclear whether these are the same physical render reused across two keys or two independent 220-dpi renders.\n- Two distinct `verify.py` modules are named in the layout with no cross-reference: `core/verify.py` (+ net new, alongside `status.py`/`indexed.py`) and `serve/tools/verify.py` (+ net new, alongside `fetch.py`) — the CLI table's `vsir ... verify ...` one-shot command (§4.4) does not indicate which module backs it, and the boot self-check's schema/index checks (§4.3) could plausibly draw on either."},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: a38e2d4f62fd49662 (use SendMessage with to: 'a38e2d4f62fd49662', summary: '<5-10 word recap>' to continue this agent)\n<usage>subagent_tokens: 36122\ntool_uses: 1\nduration_ms: 102874</usage>"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4eefb16f-3989-4441-9cd3-d294cfccb11f","uuid":"1e9f4cbb-442b-4dc4-88c7-5b6db7667e07","timestamp":"2026-09-09T16:45:30.896Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"You are Extraction Agent 2 for a PLAN-ONLY implementation-planning task. Read ONLY this region of the spec:\n\n`sed -n '252,348p' /Users/sabesonk/Documents/DILMAH/dilmah-engineering-solutioning/poc/vision_seg