{"type":"system","subtype":"task_notification","task_id":"ac3b261a312432bff","tool_use_id":"toolu_01TMqsrdQFrgj39F5QxHHCv2","status":"completed","output_file":"/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-sabesonk-Documents-DILMAH-dilmah-engineering-solutioning-poc-vision-segmentation-index-and-retrieval/4eefb16f-3989-4441-9cd3-d294cfccb11f/tasks/ac3b261a312432bff.output","summary":"### Agent 3: Data Contracts\n\nFocus:\n- Every buildable data-contract artefact for the page record, its Pydantic extraction schema, the `INDEXED` filter-gate dict, Qdrant collection/text-index setup, tokenisation primitives, and the four health signals.\n\nRequirements Extracted:\n- [Id] `doc_id` — stable slug from the manifest, e.g. `\"TC1E-SF\"` (Spec §5.1)\n- [Id] `revision` — document revision string, e.g. `\"1.3\"` (Spec §5.1)\n- [Id] `page_id` — `\"{doc_id}@{revision}#p{NNN}\"`, NNN = 1-based absolute page, zero-padded to 3+ (Spec §5.1)\n- [Id] `section_id` — `\"{doc_id}@{revision}#s{NNN}\"`, NNN = section ordinal after stitching (Spec §5.1)\n- [Id] `series_id` — stable id of a section across revisions (F8) (Spec §5.1)\n- [Id] `point_id` — `uuid5(NAMESPACE_URL, page_id)`, idempotent: re-ingest overwrites (I1) (Spec §5.1)\n- [Id] `run_id` — ULID per ingest run (Spec §5.1)\n- [Schema] `Summary(BaseModel)`: `lang: str` (ISO code), `text: str` (2-3 sentences SPECIFIC to this page) (Spec §5.2)\n- [Schema] `SectionRef(BaseModel)`: `title: str`, `is_start: bool = False` (true only if section begins on this page) (Spec §5.2)\n- [Schema] `PageOut(BaseModel)`: `page_index: int` (1-based within excerpt, not the book), `printed_page_no: str = \"\"` (verbatim), `page_kind: str = \"prose\"` (prose|table|schematic|exploded|cover|toc|index|blank), `lang: list[str] = []`, `sections: list[SectionRef] = []`, `summaries: list[Summary]` (one per lang, D5), `codes: list[str] = []` (verbatim), `topics: list[str] = []` (short lowercase labels) (Spec §5.2)\n- [Schema] `WindowOut(BaseModel)`: `pages: list[PageOut]` (Spec §5.2)\n- [Schema] `sections[]` carries presence per page, never extent — this is what lets stitching survive window folds (Spec §5.2)\n- [Schema] Binding prompt rule for summaries: \"2-3 sentences on what is SPECIFIC to this page. Do not describe the document generally.\" — generic description weakens dense-vector discriminativeness (Spec §5.2)\n- [Schema] Permitted string normalisation (sole exception to \"no regexes\"): whitespace collapsing and letter↔digit boundary spacing inside `variants()`, proven character-preserving by the I3 property test (Spec §5.2)\n- [Record] FLAT · FACETS (indexed keyword/integer/bool): `doc_id · revision · is_current · doc_type · subjects[] · tags[] · page_kind · lang[] · page_no · section_id[] · series_id[] · has_text · text_trust · run_id` (Spec §5.3)\n- [Record] FLAT · FULL TEXT (indexed text): `text` (PyMuPDF-extracted full-page text, EXACT lookup, verified by construction), `vlm_codes` (`\" \".join(codes)`, opt-in, always labelled `verified:false`) (Spec §5.3)\n- [Record] VECTORS (one point, three surfaces, fused by RRF at query time, D2): `dense` (gemini-embedding-2, one fused vector per page, D4, built from ordered Parts: doc_title · section_titles · summaries[] one Part per language · topics · codes · text[:N] · page raster @ dpi_index, N = `VSIR_EMBED_TEXT_CHARS` default 2000), `lexical` (sparse, raw term frequencies over `text`, Qdrant `Modifier.IDF`), `captions` (sparse, over generated text with `dedupe(against=text)`, weight 0.4) (Spec §5.3)\n- [Record] NESTED under `content` (returned, never filtered): `printed_page_no · label_verified · interpolated · summaries[] · topics[] · sections[] · codes[] · codes_in_text[] · moved_from[] · grounded_rate · flags[]` (Spec §5.3)\n- [Record] PROVENANCE: `page_id · extract_key · embed_key · read_keys[] · run_id · release_id · schema_version · probe_version · vlm_model · prompt_version · dpi` (Spec §5.3)\n- [Record] `subjects` (machine/model) and `tags` (uploader/filename) are document-level; `page_kind` is the one page-level facet, enabling scope queries like \"the wiring diagrams in this manual\" (Spec §5.3)\n- [Record] `section_id` and `series_id` are keyword arrays (not scalars) so a page straddling two sections carries both ids and a scope filter matches on any element — a single-`section_id`-per-page design is how F8 happens (Spec §5.3)\n- [Record] There is no `image_path` field — rasters are re-rendered on demand from the PDF (§4.2) so no record depends on a file that may not exist on the serving instance (§15 Factor VI) (Spec §5.3)\n- [Indexed] `doc_id: \"keyword\"` (Spec §5.4)\n- [Indexed] `revision: \"keyword\"` (Spec §5.4)\n- [Indexed] `is_current: \"bool\"` (Spec §5.4)\n- [Indexed] `doc_type: \"keyword\"` (Spec §5.4)\n- [Indexed] `subjects: \"keyword\"` (Spec §5.4)\n- [Indexed] `tags: \"keyword\"` (Spec §5.4)\n- [Indexed] `page_kind: \"keyword\"` (Spec §5.4)\n- [Indexed] `lang: \"keyword\"` (Spec §5.4)\n- [Indexed] `page_no: \"integer\"` (Spec §5.4)\n- [Indexed] `section_id: \"keyword[]\"` (Spec §5.4)\n- [Indexed] `series_id: \"keyword[]\"` (Spec §5.4)\n- [Indexed] `has_text: \"bool\"` (Spec §5.4)\n- [Indexed] `text_trust: \"keyword\"` (Spec §5.4)\n- [Indexed] `run_id: \"keyword\"` (Spec §5.4)\n- [Indexed] `text: \"text\"` (Spec §5.4)\n- [Indexed] `vlm_codes: \"text\"` (Spec §5.4)\n- [Indexed] `INDEXED` is one module-level dict with three jobs (I6): it **creates** the payload indexes, **gates** every filter, and is **asserted** against the live collection at boot (Spec §5.4)\n- [Indexed] Scope keys = `INDEXED` minus `{text, vlm_codes}`; those two fields are reachable only through `lookup` and `verify`, never as a caller-supplied filter (Spec §5.4)\n- [IndexConfig] `client.create_collection(collection, vectors_config={\"dense\": qm.VectorParams(size=EMBED_DIM, distance=qm.Distance.COSINE)}, sparse_vectors_config={s: qm.SparseVectorParams(modifier=qm.Modifier.IDF) for s in (\"lexical\",\"captions\")})` — collection name carries the dim, e.g. `pages_1536`; sparse config ported from `impl` (D2) (Spec §5.5)\n- [IndexConfig] For `field in (\"text\",\"vlm_codes\")`: `client.create_payload_index(collection, field_name=field, field_schema=qm.TextIndexParams(type=\"text\", tokenizer=qm.TokenizerType.WORD, lowercase=True, phrase_matching=True, min_token_len=1))` (Spec §5.5)\n- [IndexConfig] `phrase_matching=True` is required for design viability: `\"SF 1.1A\" → phrase [sf, 1, 1a]` is precise, whereas any-order matching returns every page containing `sf` and `1` separately (Spec §5.5)\n- [IndexConfig] `min_token_len=1` is required to retain short alphanumeric tokens `SI3`, `84`, `0020` (Spec §5.5)\n- [Tokenisation] `tok(s) -> list[str]` mirrors the Qdrant WORD tokenizer exactly: lowercase, punctuation is a separator, min token length 1 (Spec §5.6)\n- [Tokenisation] `variants(label) -> list[str]` produces exactly three spellings of the same characters: as given · whitespace removed · space inserted at every letter↔digit boundary (Spec §5.6)\n- [Tokenisation] `exact_filter(label, scope)` is the only exact-match code path in the codebase: `should[ must[ MatchPhrase(text, v), *scope ] for v in variants ]` (Spec §5.6)\n- [Tokenisation] An L0 differential test asserts `tok()` agrees with Qdrant's WORD tokenizer on a fixed corpus of labels, because `verify` reasons in Python about what the index actually matched (Spec §5.6)\n- [Health] `grounded_rate` — level: page. `grounded_rate = (len(seen & have)/len(seen) if seen else 1.0) if page.has_text else None`; `seen = {c.lower() for c in page.codes}`, `have = token_set(page.text)`. None rule: undefined whenever `page.has_text == false` (scanned page with no text layer) — scoring 0.0 there would falsely read as broken extraction, drag the document median below the §11.1 gate, and quarantine exactly the scanned documents F4 requires to be published-and-unsearchable; every aggregate over `grounded_rate` ignores pages where it is None (Spec §5.7)\n- [Health] `text_trust` — level: page/doc. Enum `ok | degraded | untrusted | no_text`. Edge rule: `untrusted` and `no_text` pages both count as **unsearchable** for `lookup`, and `verify` returns `unverifiable` for them (Spec §5.7)\n- [Health] `has_text` — level: page. Facet; drives `not_searchable` (F4). Edge rule: `has_text == false ⇒ text_trust == \"no_text\"` (Spec §5.7)\n- [Health] `searchable_ratio` — level: document. `pages with has_text ÷ pages`, reported on every `skim_documents` row — described as making the agent's blind spot visible (Spec §5.7)\n- [Prohibited] No identifier grammar anywhere in extraction or derivation (Spec §5.2)\n- [Prohibited] No classification enum anywhere in extraction or derivation (Spec §5.2)\n- [Prohibited] No regex taxonomy anywhere in extraction or derivation (Spec §5.2)\n- [Prohibited] No per-corpus keyword list anywhere in extraction or derivation (Spec §5.2)\n- [Prohibited] Filtering on a nested `content.*` field is impossible by construction — only `INDEXED` keys are filterable, and `content.*` fields are not members of `INDEXED` (Spec §5.4)\n- [Prohibited] Do not port `impl`'s `TOKEN_RE` (which keeps `84-5140.0020` as one token) or `token_set()`'s adjacent-token joining — both existed only to make the old `entity_keys` gate work; Qdrant's WORD tokenizer yields `[84, 5140, 0020]`, so `tok()` must mirror Qdrant and multi-token labels are handled via `phrase_matching` + `variants()` instead (Spec §5.6, §2.4)\n\nInvariants / Failure Rows Touched:\n- I1 — `point_id = uuid5(NAMESPACE_URL, page_id)`; re-ingest is idempotent and overwrites the same point (§5.1)\n- I3 — `variants()` is proven character-preserving by a property test; it is the only permitted string-normalisation exception (§5.2)\n- I6 — `INDEXED` dict simultaneously creates payload indexes, gates filters, and is asserted at boot (§5.4)\n- F8 — single `section_id` per page (instead of a keyword array) is precisely how F8 occurs; `series_id` provides revision-stable identity to prevent it (§5.1, §5.3)\n- F4 — `has_text` facet drives `not_searchable`; `grounded_rate = None` on `has_text == false` prevents scanned docs required to be published-and-unsearchable from being wrongly quarantined (§5.3, §5.7)\n- D2 — dense/lexical/captions vectors fused by RRF at query time; sparse vectors config ported from `impl` (§5.3, §5.5)\n- D4 — `dense` is one fused vector per page, built from an ordered multi-Part `types.Content` (§5.3)\n- D5 — `summaries[]` carries one `Summary` per language (§5.2, §5.3)\n- C8 — `codes_in_text` is the export's allowlist, computed as `seen & have` (§5.7)\n- §15 Factor VI — no `image_path`; rasters re-rendered on demand keeps the record independent of any specific serving instance's filesystem (§5.3)\n\nDependencies Identified:\n- Qdrant client APIs: `create_collection`, `create_payload_index`, `qm.VectorParams`, `qm.SparseVectorParams`, `qm.TextIndexParams`, `qm.Modifier.IDF`, `qm.TokenizerType.WORD`, `qm.Distance.COSINE` (§5.5)\n- `gemini-embedding-2` as the dense embedding model (§5.3)\n- PyMuPDF for extracting the `text` field (§5.3)\n- ULID generator for `run_id` (§5.1)\n- stdlib `uuid.uuid5` + `NAMESPACE_URL` for `point_id` (§5.1)\n- `VSIR_EMBED_TEXT_CHARS` config value (default 2000) bounding embedded text length (§5.3)\n- `impl`'s prior sparse-vector configuration, explicitly ported forward (D2) (§5.5)\n- Mapping from `PageOut.page_index` (1-based within-excerpt) to the absolute-page `NNN` used in `page_id`/`page_no` is required but not defined within this region — presumably resolved during stitching (§4.2, outside this excerpt)\n\nTechnical Constraints:\n- Collection naming convention encodes vector dimensionality directly, e.g. `pages_1536` (§5.5)\n- `tok()` must exactly match Qdrant's WORD tokenizer behaviour (lowercase, punctuation-as-separator, min length 1) or the L0 differential test fails and `verify`'s Python-side reasoning about index matches becomes unsound (§5.6)\n- `exact_filter` is required to be the sole exact-match code path — no other code path may perform exact code matching (§5.6)\n- Filtering must be rejected as a typed `400` (not a slow scan) for any field not present in `INDEXED` (§5.4)\n- `text` and `vlm_codes` must remain filter-inaccessible outside `lookup`/`verify` despite being present in `INDEXED` (§5.4)\n\nSpec References:\n- Spec §5.1, §5.2, §5.3, §5.4, §5.5, §5.6, §5.7 (primary region read)\n- Cross-references within region: §2.4 (porting hazard), §4.2 (raster re-render), §11.1 (quarantine gate), §15 Factor VI (statelessness)\n\nContradictions Noticed (report only, do not resolve):\n- None found within this region (§5.1–§5.7) — all cross-references (I1, I3, I6, D2, D4, D5, F4, F8, C8, §15 Factor VI) are internally consistent with the field/type definitions given here.","usage":{"total_tokens":33361,"tool_uses":1,"duration_ms":101885},"uuid":"76759c25-a883-4390-a222-bb194b343cfb","session_id":"4eefb16f-3989-4441-9cd3-d294cfccb11f"}
