{"type":"system","subtype":"task_notification","task_id":"a49dacc20a5e0190a","tool_use_id":"toolu_018af8SETgNpT3U7BujTX7cB","status":"completed","output_file":"/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-sabesonk-Documents-DILMAH-dilmah-engineering-solutioning-poc-vision-segmentation-index-and-retrieval/4eefb16f-3989-4441-9cd3-d294cfccb11f/tasks/a49dacc20a5e0190a.output","summary":"### Agent 6: The Agentic Runner\n\nFocus:\n- Buildable structure of the runner loop (lookup/skim → triage → fetch-or-read → draft → verify → answer), the fetch-vs-read routing rule, tri-state triage with its five safeguards, the six correction loops, the server-side answer gate, the read budget, and abstention wording.\n\nRequirements Extracted:\n- [Loop] Runner branches on `handle?`: yes → `lookup`; no → `skim_documents` → `skim_sections` → `skim_pages`; both paths converge on `TRIAGE` (Spec §8.1)\n- [Loop] After `TRIAGE`, `enough?` gate routes to either `fetch` (agent looks at page) or `read` (sub-model looks and extracts) → draft the answer → `verify` → `ANSWER`, with `contradicted` looping back up to `TRIAGE` (Spec §8.1)\n- [Loop] TRIAGE-empty exit 1: scope WAS searchable → ABSTAIN, naming what was searched (Spec §8.1)\n- [Loop] TRIAGE-empty exit 2: pages have no text → fetch/read the image-only pages first (Spec §8.1)\n- [Loop] Three structural properties to preserve: narrowing is the same move repeated at three zoom levels; the expensive step happens once, late, after free narrowing; verification happens after drafting, not before (Spec §8.1)\n- [Routing] No answer is composed from text alone — narrowing is text-driven (cheap triage, P2) but the draft is always written against a page raster; runner must deliberately choose between `fetch` and `read` to supply that raster (Spec §8.1a)\n- [Routing] who sees the pixels: `fetch` = calling agent at `dpi=150` default, escalating to `region` crop at 300/400; `read` = Gemini, server-side, at pinned `dpi_answer=220` (Spec §8.1a)\n- [Routing] what comes back: `fetch` = rasters themselves (≤5 pages, ≤12 MP); `read` = bounded extract + `sufficient` flag + every code stamped `present`/`absent`/`unverifiable` (Spec §8.1a)\n- [Routing] cross-page reasoning: `fetch` = yes, both pages in one context; `read` = no, one independent extract per page (Spec §8.1a)\n- [Routing] follow-up cost: `fetch` = free (evidence stays in context); `read` = re-bills the whole vision call (Spec §8.1a)\n- [Routing] zoom capability: `fetch` = yes, `region` at higher dpi; `read` = no (Spec §8.1a)\n- [Routing] cost profile: `fetch` = agent's own context, ~1–2k tokens per image; `read` = a Gemini call, the entire paid budget (Spec §8.1a)\n- [Routing] Default route is `fetch`; `read` is for delegation (cheap bounded sub-answer, keeping agent context small, or when caller is not vision-capable / text-only MCP client) (Spec §8.1a)\n- [Routing] `read` implements the master contract's \"directed vision RAG\" (POC doc §4) (Spec §8.1a)\n- [Safeguard] Correction Loop 1 (automatic per-code transcription stamping) lives inside `read` (§7.2.6); the `fetch` route bypasses this automatic stamp, so the agent can read codes off a raster unchecked (Spec §8.1a)\n- [AnswerGate] The gate is server-side and unconditional specifically because `fetch` skips Loop 1's automatic stamping — I8 requires it so no code reaches a rendered answer that `verify` did not clear for its cited page (Spec §8.1a, §8.4, I8)\n- [Triage] Every skim candidate is marked `relevant` | `uncertain` | `irrelevant` from its summary, for free, before any money is spent (Loop 0) (Spec §8.2)\n- [Triage] Mapping: `relevant` → `read`; `uncertain` → fallback pool; `irrelevant` → `exclude` on subsequent skims (Spec §8.2)\n- [Triage] Binary marking is disallowed because it discards the fallback pool and forces a full re-skim from scratch (Spec §8.2)\n- [Safeguard] Rejections stay soft: on `sufficient: false`, try the `uncertain` pool before widening scope (Spec §8.2)\n- [Safeguard] Do not filter a small set: with ≤3 candidates, read them all (Spec §8.2)\n- [Safeguard] Use `why` as a signal: a `lexical` hit on an exact code outranks a dense-only hit (Spec §8.2)\n- [Safeguard] Auto-promote exact hits: query contains an exact identifier + hit `why` is `lexical` → bypass triage entirely (Spec §8.2)\n- [Safeguard] Tri-state is mandatory: enforced both in the system prompt and in the runner's state machine (Spec §8.2)\n- [Telemetry] Triage marks (`query → page → relevant?`) are written to telemetry as free evaluation data — never as a mandatory tool call (Spec §8.2)\n- [CorrectionLoop] Loop 0 — trigger: candidate looks wrong in triage → correction: mark `irrelevant`, `exclude` it → where: the loop, before any spend (Spec §8.3)\n- [CorrectionLoop] Loop 1 — trigger: a code was misread → correction: stamp `status: absent` on that code → where: inside `read`, automatic (Spec §8.3)\n- [CorrectionLoop] Loop 2 — trigger: about to assert a claim → correction: `verify(claims, page_ids)` → where: after `read`, deliberate (Spec §8.3)\n- [CorrectionLoop] Loop 3 — trigger: `sufficient: false` → correction: try `uncertain`, then widen and re-skim → where: the loop (Spec §8.3)\n- [CorrectionLoop] Loop 4 — trigger: `verify` contradicts the draft → correction: try a different page → where: the loop (Spec §8.3)\n- [CorrectionLoop] Loop 5 — trigger: nothing found **and** `searchable_ratio < 1` → correction: `fetch`/`read` the image-only pages; `lookup(include_unverified=True)` → where: the loop (Spec §8.3)\n- [AnswerGate] `POST /ask` is the only surface permitted to return prose (Spec §8.4, I8)\n- [AnswerGate] Gate renders nothing a check has not cleared; iterates `codes_in_draft`, calling `verify([code], [cited_page_id])` → Family B envelope (§7.1) (Spec §8.4)\n- [AnswerGate] Branch \"present\": `v.status == \"present\"` → `render(code)` (Spec §8.4)\n- [AnswerGate] Branch \"unverifiable\": `v.status == \"unverifiable\"` → `render(code, badge=\"read from image, not text-verified\")` (Spec §8.4)\n- [AnswerGate] Branch \"other\" (absent/contradicted): else → `reject_draft(code, v.present_instead)` (Spec §8.4)\n- [Budget] Target is one paid `read` per question; the worked trace achieves this (Spec §8.4)\n- [Budget] Loop 3 (`sufficient: false`) legitimately spends a second `read` call (Spec §8.4)\n- [Budget] Hard ceiling enforced via `VSIR_READS_PER_QUESTION` (default **3**) (Spec §8.4)\n- [Budget] Ceiling is reported as `reads_remaining` and exhausted as `429 budget_exhausted` — never a silent extra call, never an answer composed from a page the model said did not answer (Spec §8.4)\n- [Abstention] *\"Not in these documents\"* is forbidden while `pages_no_text_read < scope_stats.pages_no_text` (Spec §8.5)\n- [Abstention] Constraint ties to \"one name for one thing\" — the same field the envelope reports (§7.1) (Spec §8.5)\n- [Abstention] Honest wording must name the gap explicitly (worked example: names the two documents searched and the count of image-only pages not examined) (Spec §8.5)\n\nInvariants / Failure Rows Touched:\n- I8 — server-side, unconditional answer gate: no code reaches a rendered answer that `verify` did not clear for its cited page (Spec §8.1a, §8.4)\n\nDependencies Identified:\n- §7.2.6 — automatic per-code transcription stamping inside `read`, which is Correction Loop 1\n- §7.1 — Family B envelope structure used by `verify`; `scope_stats.pages_no_text` field referenced by the abstention rule\n- §1.1 — \"the one failure\" the answer gate exists to prevent\n- POC doc §4 — master contract's \"directed vision RAG,\" identified as the `read` route\n- plan2 §1 move 4, §3.3, §12 — design rationale cited for defaulting to `fetch` (human move of looking at the picture first; unreachable raster as \"the single biggest gap\"; \"build only `fetch` and `verify`\")\n- P2 (referenced, not detailed in this region) — principle requiring triage to be cheap, which is why narrowing is text-driven\n\nTechnical Constraints:\n- `fetch`: default `dpi=150`, escalates to `region` crop at 300/400 dpi; ≤5 pages, ≤12 MP per call; ~1–2k tokens of agent context per image\n- `read`: pinned `dpi_answer=220`, executed server-side via Gemini, billed against the paid budget; one independent extract per page (no cross-page reasoning)\n- `VSIR_READS_PER_QUESTION` env var, default value 3, drives `reads_remaining` telemetry and `429 budget_exhausted` error\n- Triage state is strictly tri-state (`relevant`/`uncertain`/`irrelevant`); binary marking is explicitly disallowed\n\nSpec References:\n- Spec §8.1, §8.1a, §8.2, §8.3, §8.4, §8.5 (primary); cross-references to §7.1, §7.2.6, §1.1, POC doc §4, plan2 §1/§3.3/§12\n\nContradictions Noticed (report only, do not resolve):\n- §8.2's triage mapping states \"`relevant` → `read`\" (implying triage-approved candidates go through the `read` sub-model route) versus §8.1a's explicit \"**Default: `fetch`**\" guidance (implying the agent should look at the page itself by default). It's unclear from this region whether §8.2's use of \"read\" is the generic verb or the specific `read` tool/route defined in §8.1a — the two sections appear to name different default routes for the same relevant-candidate handoff.\n- §8.4's read-budget language (\"One paid `read` is the target,\" `VSIR_READS_PER_QUESTION`) only meters `read` calls, while §8.1a frames `fetch` as costing \"the agent's own context\" rather than the paid budget — the spec in this region never states whether `fetch` calls are unbounded per question or subject to any ceiling at all, leaving the two routes on visibly asymmetric cost-control treatment without reconciling why only one is capped.","usage":{"total_tokens":29307,"tool_uses":1,"duration_ms":76799},"uuid":"bbf1af08-67a0-49be-956e-3d07972f13a5","session_id":"4eefb16f-3989-4441-9cd3-d294cfccb11f"}
