{"type":"system","subtype":"task_notification","task_id":"a383642e911414548","tool_use_id":"toolu_013PSifteXcwnn6ZB8SGEbSk","status":"completed","output_file":"/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-sabesonk-Documents-DILMAH-dilmah-engineering-solutioning-poc-vision-segmentation-index-and-retrieval/4eefb16f-3989-4441-9cd3-d294cfccb11f/tasks/a383642e911414548.output","summary":"### Agent 9: Cloud-Native Contract and NFRs\n\nFocus:\n- The twelve-factor cloud-native contract (config-from-env, statelessness, disposability, dev/prod parity, JSON logs, process types, health/ready split) and the explicit bans/NFRs that constrain every later build unit from M0 onward.\n\nRequirements Extracted:\n- [Factor] I Codebase: one repo, one image, deploys differ only by env; no per-environment branch, no per-customer fork; single-tenant deploy (Spec §15, R5)\n- [Factor] II Dependencies: everything pinned transitively in a lock file, no reliance on host packages; `vsir doctor` prints resolved versions (Spec §15)\n- [Factor] III Config: every deployment-varying value is an env var, never a committed file or literal; model ids/prompt versions are config *and* cache-key/fingerprint inputs; boot refuses a missing var or a `-latest` id (Spec §15, §4.3, §6.3)\n- [Factor] IV Backing services: Qdrant, Gemini endpoint, raster cache, audit sink attached by URL/credential, swappable without code change; each has a typed failure and never degrades into an empty result (Spec §15, §11.3)\n- [Factor] V Build/release/run strictly separated: build = image (pinned-digest base, non-root, read-only rootfs, tmpfs rasters); release = image+config with immutable `release_id`; run = process; image never tagged `latest` (Spec §15, §6.9)\n- [Factor] VI Processes stateless, share-nothing: no session held; `scope`/`exclude` are parameters, `effective_scope` echoed back; rasters re-rendered into in-process LRU cache; no sticky sessions (Spec §15, F8, C11)\n- [Factor] VII Port binding: app binds `$VSIR_PORT` and exports HTTP itself; MCP SSE shares the port; MCP stdio is a one-off process, not a second server (Spec §15)\n- [Factor] VIII Concurrency: three process types from one image scale independently; ingest throughput bounded by the Gemini token bucket, not replica count (Spec §15, §6.3, D9)\n- [Factor] IX Disposability: fast start (boot self-check + index assertion, no warm-up); SIGTERM drains in-flight requests and checkpoints the ingest window in progress (Spec §15, I7, F17, M8)\n- [Factor] X Dev/prod parity: `docker-compose.test.yml` runs the same backend image as production, differing only in env/ports; stub VLM selected by config, never a code branch (Spec §15, §4.2)\n- [Factor] XI Logs: structured JSON to stdout, one event per line, carrying `release_id`/`run_id`/`session_id`/`request_id`/`tool`; app never opens, rotates or ships log files (Spec §15, §7.4)\n- [Factor] XII Admin processes: `vsir ingest`, `--resume`, `eval`, gate re-runs, collection/alias swaps run as one-off processes from the same image and release as `web` (Spec §15)\n- [EnvVar] `VSIR_PORT` — port the app binds and exports HTTP on (default 8000) (Spec §15 Factor III, VII)\n- [EnvVar] `VSIR_QDRANT_URL` — URL of the attached Qdrant backing service (Spec §15 Factor III)\n- [EnvVar] `VSIR_COLLECTION` — name of the Qdrant collection targeted (Spec §15 Factor III)\n- [EnvVar] `VSIR_VLM` — selects VLM backend, `gemini` or `stub`, driving dev/prod parity (Spec §15 Factor III, X)\n- [EnvVar] `VSIR_VLM_MODEL` — pinned VLM model id; boot refuses a `-latest` value (Spec §15 Factor III, §4.3)\n- [EnvVar] `VSIR_EMBED_MODEL` — pinned embedding model id, also a cache-key input (Spec §15 Factor III)\n- [EnvVar] `VSIR_PROMPT_VERSION` — pinned prompt version; config and cache-key/fingerprint input (Spec §15 Factor III, F11)\n- [EnvVar] `VSIR_API_TOKENS` — bearer auth token set; secret, never logged (Spec §15 Factor III, §15.1 Secrets)\n- [EnvVar] `VSIR_READ_QUOTA` — quota governing paid `read` operations (Spec §15 Factor III)\n- [EnvVar] `VSIR_ALLOW_PAID` — toggle permitting paid operations (Spec §15 Factor III)\n- [EnvVar] `VSIR_LOG_LEVEL` — log verbosity level for structured JSON output (Spec §15 Factor III, XI)\n- [EnvVar] `VSIR_RELEASE_ID` — immutable release identifier stamped on run records/provenance (Spec §15 Factor III, V, §6.9)\n- [ProcessType] `web` — runs tools + runner; scales horizontally, N replicas scaled on RPS (Spec §15 Factor VIII)\n- [ProcessType] `ingest-worker` — one worker per run, N runs in parallel, no window-level queue; throughput bounded by Gemini token bucket (Spec §15 Factor VIII, D9, §6.3)\n- [ProcessType] `oneoff` — CLI admin process type (`vsir ingest`, `eval`, gate re-runs, collection/alias swaps); invoked per-action, same image/release as `web` (Spec §15 Factor VIII, XII)\n- [Probe] `GET /health` = liveness only: process is up; MUST NOT fail due to Qdrant/Gemini unreachability; free — no `read`, no embedding, no vector search beyond capped `count` (Spec §15.1)\n- [Probe] `GET /ready` = readiness: boot self-check passed AND Qdrant reachable AND pinned index schema present; red `/ready` removes instance from load balancer; same free-probe cost cap as `/health` (Spec §15.1)\n- [Ban] Local disk as a source of truth — rasters, index data, run state, or logs on an instance's filesystem (Spec §15.2)\n- [Ban] In-process mutable session state, including the `RetrievalState` singleton (Spec §15.2, C11)\n- [Ban] Secrets or model ids as literals in code; config read from a file committed to the repo (Spec §15.2)\n- [Ban] A `latest`-tagged container image or a `-latest` model id (Spec §15.2, F11, §4.3)\n- [Ban] Test-only branches (`if TESTING:`) in the production path — config selects the stub, not an `if` (Spec §15.2)\n- [Ban] App-managed log files, rotation or shipping (Spec §15.2)\n- [Ban] Sticky sessions, instance affinity, or any warm-up requirement before a replica can serve (Spec §15.2)\n- [NFR] Latency — free tools ≤ 300 ms p95 per call on the pilot corpus; a three-rung descent < 1 s (Spec §16)\n- [NFR] Cost — unchanged-page re-ingest costs $0; full-corpus runs via Batch API at 50% discount; ≤ 1 paid `read` on worked trace, hard ceiling `VSIR_READS_PER_QUESTION` (default 3) elsewhere (Spec §16, §6.3)\n- [NFR] Reproducibility — identical `(query, image, scope, exclude)` returns identical rows in identical order; no score, no nondeterministic fusion (Spec §16, §7.2.1)\n- [NFR] Laziness — an `ImageRef` in a triage row renders nothing; rasters produced only on `url` dereference or `fetch(inline=true)` (Spec §16)\n- [NFR] Determinism — identical inputs + pinned model + pinned prompt ⇒ identical `extract_key` ⇒ cache hit (Spec §16)\n- [NFR] Idempotence — re-ingest overwrites by `point_id`; totals never double (Spec §16)\n- [NFR] Concurrency — the service is stateless; `scope`/`exclude` are parameters (Spec §16)\n- [NFR] Security — bearer auth on every tool; identity from propagated header only; rasters never returned without auth (Spec §16)\n- [NFR] Async hygiene — no blocking I/O in async paths (Spec §16)\n- [NFR] Typing — Pydantic v2 for every request/response; no untyped dict passthrough; no `any` in new TypeScript (Spec §16)\n- [NFR] Frontend — colors via CSS variables/utilities, no raw hex in components; lists > 50 items virtualized (Spec §16)\n- [NFR] Deployment — twelve-factor per §15: one image, config from env, stateless `web`, one-off admin processes, JSON logs to stdout (Spec §16, §15)\n\nInvariants / Failure Rows Touched:\n- F11 — a cache serving another model's output; made detectable by config-as-environment (model id/prompt version as cache-key inputs)\n- F8 — searching a subset while believing you searched the chapter; made impossible by statelessness (Factor VI)\n- F17 — a half-finished run answering queries; prevented by disposability + SIGTERM checkpoint of the in-progress ingest window\n- I1 — advisory lease in `vsir_runs`; paired with I7 to keep duplicate workers a cost bug, not corruption\n- I7 — no compare-and-swap in Qdrant; paired with I1 so a duplicated ingest-worker is a cost bug, not a corruption bug\n- C11 — the `RetrievalState` singleton plan2 sketched is the named example of banned in-process mutable session state\n- D9 — ingest-worker is one worker per run with no window-level queue; also the control-plane table (`vsir_runs`) referenced under data gravity\n- R5 — a deploy is single-tenant, backing Factor I's \"no per-customer fork\" rule\n- M8 — `--resume` is the mechanism that lets SIGTERM-checkpointed ingest windows continue\n\nDependencies Identified:\n- Factor II/X depend on §4.2's pinned dependency/version table (lock file, Qdrant version pin)\n- Factor III/§15.2 ban depend on §4.3's boot-refusal rules (missing var, `-latest` id)\n- Factor V's `release_id`/`schema_version` stamping depends on §6.9 run-record and envelope provenance\n- Factor VIII's ingest-worker throughput bound depends on §6.3's Gemini token bucket / Batch API mechanics, which also supplies §16 Cost NFR figures\n- Factor XI's export handling depends on §6.8's `GET /runs/{run_id}/export/…` streaming endpoint\n- Factor VI's \"no record points at a file\" depends on §5.3\n- §16 Reproducibility NFR depends on §7.2.1's ordering rule\n- §15.1 Resource limits (raster memory spike) depends on §7.3's `fetch` ≤ 12 MP cap\n- §15.1 Retention and Factor XI audit stream both depend on §7.4's audit-line schema (`user_id`)\n\nTechnical Constraints:\n- Build image: base pinned by digest, non-root user, read-only root filesystem, writable `tmpfs` only for rasters, no build tools in the runtime layer\n- Probes must incur zero cost beyond a capped `count` — no embedding, no `read`, no unbounded vector search\n- Every process type must declare CPU/memory requests and limits; raster rendering is the dominant memory spike, bounded by the 12 MP `fetch` cap\n- Ingest scaling is throughput-bound by the Gemini token bucket, not by replica count or a shared file lock\n- Advisory lease in `vsir_runs` is the only concurrency-control mechanism for ingest runs (no Qdrant compare-and-swap)\n- Secrets (`VSIR_API_TOKENS`, VLM key) must never appear in a log line, response, or error message\n\nSpec References:\n- Spec §15, §15.1, §15.2, §16\n- Spec §4.2, §4.3, §5.3, §6.3, §6.8, §6.9, §7.2.1, §7.3, §7.4, §11.3\n\nContradictions Noticed (report only, do not resolve):\n- Factor VIII states ingest-worker scaling is \"one worker per run, N runs in parallel — there is no window-level queue\" (§15 row VIII), while §15.1's \"Horizontal scale\" row states \"ingest scales by queue claim, never by a shared file lock\" — one place denies a queue exists for ingest, the other describes ingest scaling in terms of a queue claim.","usage":{"total_tokens":30276,"tool_uses":1,"duration_ms":71817},"uuid":"547bc98e-f087-419f-8830-6160f7f7a67c","session_id":"4eefb16f-3989-4441-9cd3-d294cfccb11f"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013PSifteXcwnn6ZB8SGEbSk","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"### Agent 9: Cloud-Native Contract and NFRs\n\nFocus:\n- The twelve-factor cloud-native contract (config-from-env, statelessness, disposability, dev/prod parity, JSON logs, process types, health/ready split) and the explicit bans/NFRs that constrain every later build unit from M0 onward.\n\nRequirements Extracted:\n- [Factor] I Codebase: one repo, one image, deploys differ only by env; no per-environment branch, no per-customer fork; single-tenant deploy (Spec §15, R5)\n- [Factor] II Dependencies: everything pinned transitively in a lock file, no reliance on host packages; `vsir doctor` prints resolved versions (Spec §15)\n- [Factor] III Config: every deployment-varying value is an env var, never a committed file or literal; model ids/prompt versions are config *and* cache-key/fingerprint inputs; boot refuses a missing var or a `-latest` id (Spec §15, §4.3, §6.3)\n- [Factor] IV Backing services: Qdrant, Gemini endpoint, raster cache, audit sink attached by URL/credential, swappable without code change; each has a typed failure and never degrades into an empty result (Spec §15, §11.3)\n- [Factor] V Build/release/run strictly separated: build = image (pinned-digest base, non-root, read-only rootfs, tmpfs rasters); release = image+config with immutable `release_id`; run = process; image never tagged `latest` (Spec §15, §6.9)\n- [Factor] VI Processes stateless, share-nothing: no session held; `scope`/`exclude` are parameters, `effective_scope` echoed back; rasters re-rendered into in-process LRU cache; no sticky sessions (Spec §15, F8, C11)\n- [Factor] VII Port binding: app binds `$VSIR_PORT` and exports HTTP itself; MCP SSE shares the port; MCP stdio is a one-off process, not a second server (Spec §15)\n- [Factor] VIII Concurrency: three process types from one image scale independently; ingest throughput bounded by the Gemini token bucket, not replica count (Spec §15, §6.3, D9)\n- [Factor] IX Disposability: fast start (boot self-check + index assertion, no warm-up); SIGTERM drains in-flight requests and checkpoints the ingest window in progress (Spec §15, I7, F17, M8)\n- [Factor] X Dev/prod parity: `docker-compose.test.yml` runs the same backend image as production, differing only in env/ports; stub VLM selected by config, never a code branch (Spec §15, §4.2)\n- [Factor] XI Logs: structured JSON to stdout, one event per line, carrying `release_id`/`run_id`/`session_id`/`request_id`/`tool`; app never opens, rotates or ships log files (Spec §15, §7.4)\n- [Factor] XII Admin processes: `vsir ingest`, `--resume`, `eval`, gate re-runs, collection/alias swaps run as one-off processes from the same image and release as `web` (Spec §15)\n- [EnvVar] `VSIR_PORT` — port the app binds and exports HTTP on (default 8000) (Spec §15 Factor III, VII)\n- [EnvVar] `VSIR_QDRANT_URL` — URL of the attached Qdrant backing service (Spec §15 Factor III)\n- [EnvVar] `VSIR_COLLECTION` — name of the Qdrant collection targeted (Spec §15 Factor III)\n- [EnvVar] `VSIR_VLM` — selects VLM backend, `gemini` or `stub`, driving dev/prod parity (Spec §15 Factor III, X)\n- [EnvVar] `VSIR_VLM_MODEL` — pinned VLM model id; boot refuses a `-latest` value (Spec §15 Factor III, §4.3)\n- [EnvVar] `VSIR_EMBED_MODEL` — pinned embedding model id, also a cache-key input (Spec §15 Factor III)\n- [EnvVar] `VSIR_PROMPT_VERSION` — pinned prompt version; config and cache-key/fingerprint input (Spec §15 Factor III, F11)\n- [EnvVar] `VSIR_API_TOKENS` — bearer auth token set; secret, never logged (Spec §15 Factor III, §15.1 Secrets)\n- [EnvVar] `VSIR_READ_QUOTA` — quota governing paid `read` operations (Spec §15 Factor III)\n- [EnvVar] `VSIR_ALLOW_PAID` — toggle permitting paid operations (Spec §15 Factor III)\n- [EnvVar] `VSIR_LOG_LEVEL` — log verbosity level for structured JSON output (Spec §15 Factor III, XI)\n- [EnvVar] `VSIR_RELEASE_ID` — immutable release identifier stamped on run records/provenance (Spec §15 Factor III, V, §6.9)\n- [ProcessType] `web` — runs tools + runner; scales horizontally, N replicas scaled on RPS (Spec §15 Factor VIII)\n- [ProcessType] `ingest-worker` — one worker per run, N runs in parallel, no window-level queue; throughput bounded by Gemini token bucket (Spec §15 Factor VIII, D9, §6.3)\n- [ProcessType] `oneoff` — CLI admin process type (`vsir ingest`, `eval`, gate re-runs, collection/alias swaps); invoked per-action, same image/release as `web` (Spec §15 Factor VIII, XII)\n- [Probe] `GET /health` = liveness only: process is up; MUST NOT fail due to Qdrant/Gemini unreachability; free — no `read`, no embedding, no vector search beyond capped `count` (Spec §15.1)\n- [Probe] `GET /ready` = readiness: boot self-check passed AND Qdrant reachable AND pinned index schema present; red `/ready` removes instance from load balancer; same free-probe cost cap as `/health` (Spec §15.1)\n- [Ban] Local disk as a source of truth — rasters, index data, run state, or logs on an instance's filesystem (Spec §15.2)\n- [Ban] In-process mutable session state, including the `RetrievalState` singleton (Spec §15.2, C11)\n- [Ban] Secrets or model ids as literals in code; config read from a file committed to the repo (Spec §15.2)\n- [Ban] A `latest`-tagged container image or a `-latest` model id (Spec §15.2, F11, §4.3)\n- [Ban] Test-only branches (`if TESTING:`) in the production path — config selects the stub, not an `if` (Spec §15.2)\n- [Ban] App-managed log files, rotation or shipping (Spec §15.2)\n- [Ban] Sticky sessions, instance affinity, or any warm-up requirement before a replica can serve (Spec §15.2)\n- [NFR] Latency — free tools ≤ 300 ms p95 per call on the pilot corpus; a three-rung descent < 1 s (Spec §16)\n- [NFR] Cost — unchanged-page re-ingest costs $0; full-corpus runs via Batch API at 50% discount; ≤ 1 paid `read` on worked trace, hard ceiling `VSIR_READS_PER_QUESTION` (default 3) elsewhere (Spec §16, §6.3)\n- [NFR] Reproducibility — identical `(query, image, scope, exclude)` returns identical rows in identical order; no score, no nondeterministic fusion (Spec §16, §7.2.1)\n- [NFR] Laziness — an `ImageRef` in a triage row renders nothing; rasters produced only on `url` dereference or `fetch(inline=true)` (Spec §16)\n- [NFR] Determinism — identical inputs + pinned model + pinned prompt ⇒ identical `extract_key` ⇒ cache hit (Spec §16)\n- [NFR] Idempotence — re-ingest overwrites by `point_id`; totals never double (Spec §16)\n- [NFR] Concurrency — the service is stateless; `scope`/`exclude` are parameters (Spec §16)\n- [NFR] Security — bearer auth on every tool; identity from propagated header only; rasters never returned without auth (Spec §16)\n- [NFR] Async hygiene — no blocking I/O in async paths (Spec §16)\n- [NFR] Typing — Pydantic v2 for every request/response; no untyped dict passthrough; no `any` in new TypeScript (Spec §16)\n- [NFR] Frontend — colors via CSS variables/utilities, no raw hex in components; lists > 50 items virtualized (Spec §16)\n- [NFR] Deployment — twelve-factor per §15: one image, config from env, stateless `web`, one-off admin processes, JSON logs to stdout (Spec §16, §15)\n\nInvariants / Failure Rows Touched:\n- F11 — a cache serving another model's output; made detectable by config-as-environment (model id/prompt version as cache-key inputs)\n- F8 — searching a subset while believing you searched the chapter; made impossible by statelessness (Factor VI)\n- F17 — a half-finished run answering queries; prevented by disposability + SIGTERM checkpoint of the in-progress ingest window\n- I1 — advisory lease in `vsir_runs`; paired with I7 to keep duplicate workers a cost bug, not corruption\n- I7 — no compare-and-swap in Qdrant; paired with I1 so a duplicated ingest-worker is a cost bug, not a corruption bug\n- C11 — the `RetrievalState` singleton plan2 sketched is the named example of banned in-process mutable session state\n- D9 — ingest-worker is one worker per run with no window-level queue; also the control-plane table (`vsir_runs`) referenced under data gravity\n- R5 — a deploy is single-tenant, backing Factor I's \"no per-customer fork\" rule\n- M8 — `--resume` is the mechanism that lets SIGTERM-checkpointed ingest windows continue\n\nDependencies Identified:\n- Factor II/X depend on §4.2's pinned dependency/version table (lock file, Qdrant version pin)\n- Factor III/§15.2 ban depend on §4.3's boot-refusal rules (missing var, `-latest` id)\n- Factor V's `release_id`/`schema_version` stamping depends on §6.9 run-record and envelope provenance\n- Factor VIII's ingest-worker throughput bound depends on §6.3's Gemini token bucket / Batch API mechanics, which also supplies §16 Cost NFR figures\n- Factor XI's export handling depends on §6.8's `GET /runs/{run_id}/export/…` streaming endpoint\n- Factor VI's \"no record points at a file\" depends on §5.3\n- §16 Reproducibility NFR depends on §7.2.1's ordering rule\n- §15.1 Resource limits (raster memory spike) depends on §7.3's `fetch` ≤ 12 MP cap\n- §15.1 Retention and Factor XI audit stream both depend on §7.4's audit-line schema (`user_id`)\n\nTechnical Constraints:\n- Build image: base pinned by digest, non-root user, read-only root filesystem, writable `tmpfs` only for rasters, no build tools in the runtime layer\n- Probes must incur zero cost beyond a capped `count` — no embedding, no `read`, no unbounded vector search\n- Every process type must declare CPU/memory requests and limits; raster rendering is the dominant memory spike, bounded by the 12 MP `fetch` cap\n- Ingest scaling is throughput-bound by the Gemini token bucket, not by replica count or a shared file lock\n- Advisory lease in `vsir_runs` is the only concurrency-control mechanism for ingest runs (no Qdrant compare-and-swap)\n- Secrets (`VSIR_API_TOKENS`, VLM key) must never appear in a log line, response, or error message\n\nSpec References:\n- Spec §15, §15.1, §15.2, §16\n- Spec §4.2, §4.3, §5.3, §6.3, §6.8, §6.9, §7.2.1, §7.3, §7.4, §11.3\n\nContradictions Noticed (report only, do not resolve):\n- Factor VIII states ingest-worker scaling is \"one worker per run, N runs in parallel — there is no window-level queue\" (§15 row VIII), while §15.1's \"Horizontal scale\" row states \"ingest scales by queue claim, never by a shared file lock\" — one place denies a queue exists for ingest, the other describes ingest scaling in terms of a queue claim."},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: a383642e911414548 (use SendMessage with to: 'a383642e911414548', summary: '<5-10 word recap>' to continue this agent)\n<usage>subagent_tokens: 32201\ntool_uses: 1\nduration_ms: 71819</usage>"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4eefb16f-3989-4441-9cd3-d294cfccb11f","uuid":"d295a364-b386-467d-8725-0f259ab3dc27","timestamp":"2026-09-09T16:46:04.561Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"You are Extraction Agent 9 for a PLAN-ONLY implementation-planning task. Read ONLY this region of the spec:\n\n`sed -n '1557,1622p' /Users/sabesonk/Documents/DILMAH/dilmah-engineering-solutioning/poc/vision_segmentation_index_and_retrieval/development/cr1/spec/spec.md`\n\n(That covers §15 the twelve factors applied, §15.1 orchestrator requirements, §15.2 explicitly banned, §16 non-functional requirements.)\n\nDo NOT read any other file. Do NOT quote spec text — use pointers only, except that you MUST list the env-var names of Factor III literally.\n\nYour focus: the cloud-native contract as buildable, testable work that lands in M0 and is inherited by every later unit — one image / three process types, config-from-env, statelessness, disposability + SIGTERM checkpointing, dev/prod parity via config-selected stub, JSON logs to stdout, the `/health` vs `/ready` split, and every explicitly banned construct.\n\nOutput EXACTLY this format, structured lists only:\n\n### Agent 9: Cloud-Native Contract and NFRs\n\nFocus:\n- <one line>\n\nRequirements 