{"type":"system","subtype":"task_notification","task_id":"a503835346fab1169","tool_use_id":"toolu_01MWYsAg9R7sudNw6uPTuzeg","status":"completed","output_file":"/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-sabesonk-Documents-DILMAH-dilmah-engineering-solutioning-poc-vision-segmentation-index-and-retrieval/4eefb16f-3989-4441-9cd3-d294cfccb11f/tasks/a503835346fab1169.output","summary":"### Agent 4: Ingestion Pipeline\n\nFocus:\n- The twelve ingestion steps as independently buildable units, the three cache-key/tier/replay rules in §6.3, the offset proof, code reattribution, embedding fingerprint gate, publish/retirement rules, run/window control-plane state, and the two streamed export endpoints.\n\nRequirements Extracted:\n\n- [Step] 01 manifest: file + uploader metadata → `doc_id`, `revision`, `doc_type`, `subjects`, `tags`; guard: facets from filename/metadata/uploader only, no content-sniffing grammar (Spec §6.1)\n- [Step] 02 probe + text: PDF → per-page `text`, `has_text`, `page_count`, `probe_version`; guard: the only writer of `text` (I2); text always from the full page, never a crop (F15) (Spec §6.1)\n- [Step] 03 render: PDF → page rasters at dpi 220; guard: cached by page content hash (Spec §6.1)\n- [Step] 04 S1 document facts: doc head rasters → doc-level facts, picks the window ladder; guard: prompt generalised, no per-corpus grammar (Spec §6.1)\n- [Step] 05 window + `extract_key`: pages → windows (target 30 pages); guard: per §6.2 (Spec §6.1, §6.2)\n- [Step] 06 S2 extraction: window rasters → `WindowOut`; guard: schema §5.2, content-addressable cache §6.3 (Spec §6.1)\n- [Step] 07 derivation: `WindowOut` + probe text → page records; guard: offset proof §6.4, `grounded_rate`, code reattribution §6.5, no verification gate (Spec §6.1)\n- [Step] 08 stitching: per-page `sections[]` → `section_id`, `page_range`, `series_id`; guard: canonical key + carry-in across folds (F8) (Spec §6.1)\n- [Step] 09 embedding: record → dense vector; guard: fingerprint §6.6 (Spec §6.1)\n- [Step] 10 indexing: records → Qdrant points, `is_current=False`; guard: `point_id = uuid5(page_id)` (I1) (Spec §6.1)\n- [Step] 11 gates + publish: run → gate results, flips `is_current`, retires prior points; guard: §11.1, §6.7, I7 (Spec §6.1)\n- [Step] 12 export: published run → `labels.jsonl` + observed-token inventory, both served over HTTP; guard: §6.8 (Spec §6.1)\n\n- [Windowing] Target 30 pages/window subject to an output-budget ladder (Spec §6.2)\n- [Windowing] On `MAX_TOKENS`, truncated/schema-invalid response, or offset failure: bisect and re-bill — never pad, never offset-guess, never accept a partial window (F13); a single page still exceeding budget fails the run typed `window_unsplittable` (Spec §6.2)\n- [Windowing] Three-rung ladder: Level 0/1 cut on S1's table of contents and are parallelisable; Level 2 is a blind cut that must run sequentially with a carry chain (per `impl/pipeline-guide/04-windowing-and-keys.md` §5) (Spec §6.2)\n- [Windowing] v1 implements Level 0/1 plus bisection only; Level 2 and its carry chain are out of scope (Spec §6.2)\n- [Windowing] POC corpus slice (6 docs, 142 pages) ingests without Level 2; `impl/corpus.yaml` records that the 1,440-page manual and 592-page E-diagram are the only two docs needing Level 2 and are excluded from the slice for that reason (Spec §6.2)\n- [Windowing] Attempting the 1,440-page manual must fail typed `ladder_level_2_required` naming the document — never a blind cut that silently straddles a safety function across a fold (that failure is F8, one level up) (Spec §6.2)\n- [Windowing] M8's resume test runs on a generated large PDF, not the excluded manual (Spec §6.2, §13 M8)\n- [Windowing] The ladder depends on an uncached model call (S1); §6.3 caches S1 per document, which `impl` does not (IMPROVEMENTS B2) — this motivates `facts_key` (Spec §6.2, §6.3)\n\n- [CacheKey] `facts_key = sha256(document content hash ‖ resolved vlm model id ‖ prompt_version)` — caches S1 document facts per DOCUMENT; uncached in `impl`, so every re-run re-bills S1 and can silently re-pick a different window ladder (IMPROVEMENTS B2) (Spec §6.3)\n- [CacheKey] `extract_key = sha256(ordered page image hashes ‖ resolved vlm model id ‖ prompt_version ‖ dpi ‖ schema hash)` — keys S2 extraction cache (Spec §6.3)\n- [CacheKey] `read_key = extract_key inputs ‖ question` — a new question is a cache miss (F19) (Spec §6.3)\n- [CacheKey] `embed_key = sha256(composition version ‖ embed model id ‖ composed string)` (Spec §6.3)\n- [CacheKey] `VSIR_VLM_TIER ∈ {batch, standard}` is deliberately excluded from `extract_key` because the tier does not change the output (Spec §6.3)\n\n- [OffsetProof] `abs_page = window.start + page_index - 1` (I4) (Spec §6.4)\n- [OffsetProof] Check 1 (structural): window returned exactly the page indices it was given — `sorted(p.page_index) == list(range(1, window.pages + 1))` (Spec §6.4)\n- [OffsetProof] Check 2 (independent observation): when the page has text and the model read a `printed_page_no`, that label must phrase-match this page's text; if it matches a neighbour's instead, raise `OffsetError` and bisect (the off-by-one signature) (Spec §6.4)\n- [OffsetProof] Both checks are required; a wrong offset shifts every page/citation/summary and nothing else errors — called the single most dangerous line in the pipeline (Spec §6.4)\n\n- [Labels] `printed_page_no` is model-read; precedence: text-layer-confirmed label > model-read label > interpolated from neighbours; `label_verified` and `interpolated` recorded per page; an ambiguous label resolves to a list, never a silent pick (F5) (Spec §6.5)\n- [Labels] Code reattribution (F6): a code reported on page *i* but absent from *i*'s text and present in an adjacent page's text within the same window is reattributed to the page whose text contains it; `content.moved_from` records `{code, from_page_id}` on the receiving page (Spec §6.5)\n- [Labels] A code grounded in no page's text stays where the model put it, counts against that page's `grounded_rate`, and never enters the exact surface (I2) (Spec §6.5)\n\n- [Fingerprint] Collection stores `{embed_model, dim, distance, composition_version}`; on mismatch, refuse to upsert (Spec §6.6)\n- [Fingerprint] A model change requires a new collection + full re-embed + alias swap, never an in-place mix (Spec §6.6)\n\n- [Publish] Step 10 writes every point `is_current=False`; step 11 is the only thing that flips it, and only when every blocking gate passes (I7) (Spec §6.7)\n- [Publish] Every tool injects `is_current=True` server-side, always; the filtered `set_payload` is idempotent and retried; `published_at` is recorded only after it returns (Spec §6.7)\n- [Publish] For full-corpus rebuilds, prefer the atomic path: new collection + one alias swap (Spec §6.7)\n- [Publish] A crash at window 700 of a 1,440-page manual must leave 0 pages queryable, otherwise `searchable_ratio` lies and the loop abstains about a page that is actually in the document (F17) (Spec §6.7)\n\n- [Retirement] Clause 1: points of the same `(doc_id, revision)` written by an earlier `run_id` are deleted by filter — stops totals doubling and stale pages staying findable; protects F12 (Spec §6.7)\n- [Retirement] Clause 2: points of the previously current *other* revision are set `is_current=False` and kept — they are what `found_only_in_superseded` reads from; protects F9 (Spec §6.7)\n- [Retirement] Clause 3: points of any other document are never touched — no explicit failure-row number is attached to this clause in this region, unlike clauses 1 and 2 (Spec §6.7)\n- [Retirement] A blanket \"delete every point whose `run_id` is not the current run\" would satisfy F12 by destroying F9's evidence; both deletions must be filter-based, idempotent, and retried (Spec §6.7)\n\n- [RunState] Run point shape (one per run in `vsir_runs`, D9): `{state, step, windows_done, windows_total, gate_results, lease_owner, lease_expires_at}` (Spec §6.7)\n- [RunState] Window point shape (one per window in `vsir_runs`, D9): `{state, attempts, checkpoint, extract_key}` (Spec §6.7)\n- [RunState] Lease rule: one worker owns one run under a lease; `vsir ingest --resume` refuses a run whose lease is still live unless `--steal` is passed; the lease is advisory (Qdrant has no compare-and-swap) — a duplicated worker re-bills windows but cannot corrupt the index because `point_id` is idempotent (I1) and nothing is queryable until gates flip `is_current` (I7) (Spec §6.7)\n- [RunState] State enum: `state ∈ {queued, running, stopped, gated, published, failed}`; `stopped` is what a `SIGTERM` leaves behind (§15 Factor IX) and is the only state `--resume` accepts without `--steal` (Spec §6.9)\n- [RunState] Run record shape (`GET /runs/{run_id}`): `{run_id, doc_id, revision, release_id, state, step, windows_done, windows_total, pages_indexed, gate_results, overrides: [{gate, reason, by}], published_at, lease: {owner, expires_at}, failed: {step, reason}, cost: {input_tokens, output_tokens, cache_hits}}` — a superset of the control-plane run point adding doc/revision/release identity, overrides, publish timestamp, failure detail, and cost (Spec §6.9)\n\n- [Export] `GET /runs/{run_id}/export/labels.jsonl` — streamed, one line per page (Spec §6.8)\n- [Export] `GET /runs/{run_id}/export/observed_tokens.jsonl` — streamed, one line per document (Spec §6.8)\n- [Export] `labels.jsonl` line fields: `page_id, doc_id, revision, page_no, printed_page_no, label_verified, sections[] {section_id, title, page_range, series_id}, summaries[] {lang, text}, codes_in_text[], grounded_rate, safety_flag, vlm_model, prompt_version, dpi` (Spec §6.8)\n- [Export] `safety_flag` replacement formula: `safety_flag = (doc_type in SAFETY_DOC_TYPES or any(t in page.topics for t in SAFETY_TOPICS))`; `SAFETY_DOC_TYPES` is a manifest facet set by the uploader (not inferred from content); `SAFETY_TOPICS` matches the model's own lowercase `topics[]` — replaces `impl`'s `_is_safety()` (Unit.kind grammar + hardcoded keyword list), both of which this CR deletes (Spec §6.8)\n- [Export] `safety_flag` is advisory metadata for Part A's answer policy only — never a gate, never a filter default, never a reason to hide a page; becoming load-bearing needs its own trust level (open question, IMPROVEMENTS C2, §20.1) (Spec §6.8)\n- [Export] `codes_in_text` is the old `verified_identifiers[]`, computed structurally instead of by a gate (Spec §6.8)\n- [Export] Nothing is written to the instance's filesystem (§15 Factor VI); both artefacts are generated from the index and served over HTTP (Spec §6.8)\n- [Export] The observed-token inventory backing `present_instead` (C7) is stored as payload on the document's control point in `vsir_runs` (D9) and held in an in-process LRU cache for prefix lookup (Spec §6.8)\n- [Export] The code-like heuristic (a token containing at least one digit) is display-only: unreachable from `lookup` and `verify`, enforced by module boundary and a test asserting `present_instead` can never appear in `hits` (Spec §6.8)\n\n- [Replay] With `VSIR_VLM=stub` and `VSIR_FIXTURE=<dir>` (D10), both S2 extraction and `read` are served from frozen responses keyed by exactly the §6.3 hashes (Spec §6.3)\n- [Replay] A key not in the fixture is a typed `fixture_miss` error — never a live call, never a fabricated response (Spec §6.3)\n- [Replay] Same code path as production with a different attached service (§15 Factor IV, X) — lets CI, the E2E suite and the console drive the whole loop for free (Spec §6.3)\n\nInvariants / Failure Rows Touched:\n- I1 — `point_id = uuid5(page_id)` makes indexing idempotent; also what makes a duplicated lease-holder safe (§6.1 step10, §6.7)\n- I2 — probe+text is the sole writer of `text` (step02); ungrounded codes never enter the exact surface (§6.5)\n- I4 — the offset proof, both checks required (§6.4)\n- I7 — publish gating: only step 11 flips `is_current`, only when every blocking gate passes (§6.1 step11, §6.7)\n- F5 — ambiguous printed-label resolves to a list, never a silent pick (§6.5)\n- F6 — code reattribution across a window fold, recorded via `content.moved_from` (§6.5)\n- F8 — stitching's canonical key + carry-in across folds; also the failure a blind Level-2 cut would cause one level up from `ladder_level_2_required` (§6.1 step08, §6.2)\n- F9 — `found_only_in_superseded` reads from retained, non-current points of a superseded revision (§6.7 retirement clause 2)\n- F12 — stale/duplicate points from an earlier `run_id` of the same `(doc_id, revision)` must not double totals or stay findable (§6.7 retirement clause 1)\n- F13 — never pad, never offset-guess, never accept a partial window; bisect and re-bill instead (§6.2)\n- F15 — text always sourced from the full page, never a crop (§6.1 step02)\n- F17 — a mid-run crash must leave 0 pages queryable rather than a misleading `searchable_ratio` (§6.7)\n- F19 — a new question is a `read_key` cache miss (§6.3)\n\nDependencies Identified:\n- Step 05 (windowing) depends on the ladder step 04 (S1) selects (§6.1, §6.2)\n- Step 06 (S2 extraction) depends on `extract_key` from §6.3 for its cache\n- Step 07 (derivation) depends on step 02's probe text (for the offset proof and code reattribution) and step 06's `WindowOut`\n- Step 08 (stitching) depends on step 07's per-page `sections[]`\n- Step 09 (embedding) depends on step 07/08 records and must check collection fingerprint compatibility (§6.6) before upsert\n- Step 10 (indexing) depends on step 09's vectors and the `point_id = uuid5(page_id)` scheme (I1)\n- Step 11 (gates + publish) depends on step 10's `is_current=False` points and on gate definitions in §11.1 (outside this region)\n- Step 12 (export) depends on step 11 having published the run, and on the observed-token inventory accumulated on the `vsir_runs` control point (D9)\n- The ladder pick in step 04 depends on `impl/corpus.yaml`'s per-document Level-2 classification (external file, not read in this region)\n- Replay mode depends on a fixture directory keyed by exactly the same hashes as the live cache keys (§6.3)\n- Retirement in step 11 depends on prior runs' `(doc_id, revision, run_id, is_current)` bookkeeping being intact\n\nTechnical Constraints:\n- v1 supports only Level 0/1 windowing plus bisection; Level 2 (blind cut, sequential carry chain) is explicitly out of scope (§6.2)\n- The 1,440-page manual and 592-page E-diagram require Level 2 and are excluded from the POC corpus (6 docs / 142 pages) for that reason (§6.2)\n- Batch API (50% discount) is used for full-corpus ingestion (no latency requirement); the standard endpoint is used for interactive prompt tuning and single-document ingest; selected via `VSIR_VLM_TIER ∈ {batch, standard}` (§6.3)\n- Re-running on identical pages costs $0 (cache hit); the Gemini client carries a token-bucket rate limiter and exponential backoff (§6.3)\n- Nothing is written to the instance filesystem — exports are generated from the index and streamed over HTTP (§15 Factor VI) (§6.8)\n- The run/window lease is advisory only, since Qdrant has no compare-and-swap (§6.7)\n\nSpec References:\n- Spec §6.1, §6.2, §6.3, §6.4, §6.5, §6.6, §6.7, §6.8, §6.9\n- Cross-references appearing within region (not read): §2.5 B, §5.2, §11.1, §13 M8, §15 Factor IV/VI/IX/X, §20.1, IMPROVEMENTS B2/C2, `impl/pipeline-guide/04-windowing-and-keys.md` §5, `impl/corpus.yaml`\n\nContradictions Noticed (report only, do not resolve):\n- Task framing describes \"the three cache keys\" while §6.3 itself defines four formulas (`facts_key`, `extract_key`, `read_key`, `embed_key`) — unclear whether `read_key` is meant to be treated as a variant of `extract_key` rather than a fourth independent key.\n- Retirement clause 3 (\"points of any other document are never touched,\" §6.7) is not tied to a named failure row in this region, unlike clauses 1 (F12) and 2 (F9), even though the task instructions ask for a protected failure row per clause.","usage":{"total_tokens":39340,"tool_uses":1,"duration_ms":150654},"uuid":"8d0932b3-46a8-479e-8d9a-69b23d74826f","session_id":"4eefb16f-3989-4441-9cd3-d294cfccb11f"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MWYsAg9R7sudNw6uPTuzeg","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"### Agent 4: Ingestion Pipeline\n\nFocus:\n- The twelve ingestion steps as independently buildable units, the three cache-key/tier/replay rules in §6.3, the offset proof, code reattribution, embedding fingerprint gate, publish/retirement rules, run/window control-plane state, and the two streamed export endpoints.\n\nRequirements Extracted:\n\n- [Step] 01 manifest: file + uploader metadata → `doc_id`, `revision`, `doc_type`, `subjects`, `tags`; guard: facets from filename/metadata/uploader only, no content-sniffing grammar (Spec §6.1)\n- [Step] 02 probe + text: PDF → per-page `text`, `has_text`, `page_count`, `probe_version`; guard: the only writer of `text` (I2); text always from the full page, never a crop (F15) (Spec §6.1)\n- [Step] 03 render: PDF → page rasters at dpi 220; guard: cached by page content hash (Spec §6.1)\n- [Step] 04 S1 document facts: doc head rasters → doc-level facts, picks the window ladder; guard: prompt generalised, no per-corpus grammar (Spec §6.1)\n- [Step] 05 window + `extract_key`: pages → windows (target 30 pages); guard: per §6.2 (Spec §6.1, §6.2)\n- [Step] 06 S2 extraction: window rasters → `WindowOut`; guard: schema §5.2, content-addressable cache §6.3 (Spec §6.1)\n- [Step] 07 derivation: `WindowOut` + probe text → page records; guard: offset proof §6.4, `grounded_rate`, code reattribution §6.5, no verification gate (Spec §6.1)\n- [Step] 08 stitching: per-page `sections[]` → `section_id`, `page_range`, `series_id`; guard: canonical key + carry-in across folds (F8) (Spec §6.1)\n- [Step] 09 embedding: record → dense vector; guard: fingerprint §6.6 (Spec §6.1)\n- [Step] 10 indexing: records → Qdrant points, `is_current=False`; guard: `point_id = uuid5(page_id)` (I1) (Spec §6.1)\n- [Step] 11 gates + publish: run → gate results, flips `is_current`, retires prior points; guard: §11.1, §6.7, I7 (Spec §6.1)\n- [Step] 12 export: published run → `labels.jsonl` + observed-token inventory, both served over HTTP; guard: §6.8 (Spec §6.1)\n\n- [Windowing] Target 30 pages/window subject to an output-budget ladder (Spec §6.2)\n- [Windowing] On `MAX_TOKENS`, truncated/schema-invalid response, or offset failure: bisect and re-bill — never pad, never offset-guess, never accept a partial window (F13); a single page still exceeding budget fails the run typed `window_unsplittable` (Spec §6.2)\n- [Windowing] Three-rung ladder: Level 0/1 cut on S1's table of contents and are parallelisable; Level 2 is a blind cut that must run sequentially with a carry chain (per `impl/pipeline-guide/04-windowing-and-keys.md` §5) (Spec §6.2)\n- [Windowing] v1 implements Level 0/1 plus bisection only; Level 2 and its carry chain are out of scope (Spec §6.2)\n- [Windowing] POC corpus slice (6 docs, 142 pages) ingests without Level 2; `impl/corpus.yaml` records that the 1,440-page manual and 592-page E-diagram are the only two docs needing Level 2 and are excluded from the slice for that reason (Spec §6.2)\n- [Windowing] Attempting the 1,440-page manual must fail typed `ladder_level_2_required` naming the document — never a blind cut that silently straddles a safety function across a fold (that failure is F8, one level up) (Spec §6.2)\n- [Windowing] M8's resume test runs on a generated large PDF, not the excluded manual (Spec §6.2, §13 M8)\n- [Windowing] The ladder depends on an uncached model call (S1); §6.3 caches S1 per document, which `impl` does not (IMPROVEMENTS B2) — this motivates `facts_key` (Spec §6.2, §6.3)\n\n- [CacheKey] `facts_key = sha256(document content hash ‖ resolved vlm model id ‖ prompt_version)` — caches S1 document facts per DOCUMENT; uncached in `impl`, so every re-run re-bills S1 and can silently re-pick a different window ladder (IMPROVEMENTS B2) (Spec §6.3)\n- [CacheKey] `extract_key = sha256(ordered page image hashes ‖ resolved vlm model id ‖ prompt_version ‖ dpi ‖ schema hash)` — keys S2 extraction cache (Spec §6.3)\n- [CacheKey] `read_key = extract_key inputs ‖ question` — a new question is a cache miss (F19) (Spec §6.3)\n- [CacheKey] `embed_key = sha256(composition version ‖ embed model id ‖ composed string)` (Spec §6.3)\n- [CacheKey] `VSIR_VLM_TIER ∈ {batch, standard}` is deliberately excluded from `extract_key` because the tier does not change the output (Spec §6.3)\n\n- [OffsetProof] `abs_page = window.start + page_index - 1` (I4) (Spec §6.4)\n- [OffsetProof] Check 1 (structural): window returned exactly the page indices it was given — `sorted(p.page_index) == list(range(1, window.pages + 1))` (Spec §6.4)\n- [OffsetProof] Check 2 (independent observation): when the page has text and the model read a `printed_page_no`, that label must phrase-match this page's text; if it matches a neighbour's instead, raise `OffsetError` and bisect (the off-by-one signature) (Spec §6.4)\n- [OffsetProof] Both checks are required; a wrong offset shifts every page/citation/summary and nothing else errors — called the single most dangerous line in the pipeline (Spec §6.4)\n\n- [Labels] `printed_page_no` is model-read; precedence: text-layer-confirmed label > model-read label > interpolated from neighbours; `label_verified` and `interpolated` recorded per page; an ambiguous label resolves to a list, never a silent pick (F5) (Spec §6.5)\n- [Labels] Code reattribution (F6): a code reported on page *i* but absent from *i*'s text and present in an adjacent page's text within the same window is reattributed to the page whose text contains it; `content.moved_from` records `{code, from_page_id}` on the receiving page (Spec §6.5)\n- [Labels] A code grounded in no page's text stays where the model put it, counts against that page's `grounded_rate`, and never enters the exact surface (I2) (Spec §6.5)\n\n- [Fingerprint] Collection stores `{embed_model, dim, distance, composition_version}`; on mismatch, refuse to upsert (Spec §6.6)\n- [Fingerprint] A model change requires a new collection + full re-embed + alias swap, never an in-place mix (Spec §6.6)\n\n- [Publish] Step 10 writes every point `is_current=False`; step 11 is the only thing that flips it, and only when every blocking gate passes (I7) (Spec §6.7)\n- [Publish] Every tool injects `is_current=True` server-side, always; the filtered `set_payload` is idempotent and retried; `published_at` is recorded only after it returns (Spec §6.7)\n- [Publish] For full-corpus rebuilds, prefer the atomic path: new collection + one alias swap (Spec §6.7)\n- [Publish] A crash at window 700 of a 1,440-page manual must leave 0 pages queryable, otherwise `searchable_ratio` lies and the loop abstains about a page that is actually in the document (F17) (Spec §6.7)\n\n- [Retirement] Clause 1: points of the same `(doc_id, revision)` written by an earlier `run_id` are deleted by filter — stops totals doubling and stale pages staying findable; protects F12 (Spec §6.7)\n- [Retirement] Clause 2: points of the previously current *other* revision are set `is_current=False` and kept — they are what `found_only_in_superseded` reads from; protects F9 (Spec §6.7)\n- [Retirement] Clause 3: points of any other document are never touched — no explicit failure-row number is attached to this clause in this region, unlike clauses 1 and 2 (Spec §6.7)\n- [Retirement] A blanket \"delete every point whose `run_id` is not the current run\" would satisfy F12 by destroying F9's evidence; both deletions must be filter-based, idempotent, and retried (Spec §6.7)\n\n- [RunState] Run point shape (one per run in `vsir_runs`, D9): `{state, step, windows_done, windows_total, gate_results, lease_owner, lease_expires_at}` (Spec §6.7)\n- [RunState] Window point shape (one per window in `vsir_runs`, D9): `{state, attempts, checkpoint, extract_key}` (Spec §6.7)\n- [RunState] Lease rule: one worker owns one run under a lease; `vsir ingest --resume` refuses a run whose lease is still live unless `--steal` is passed; the lease is advisory (Qdrant has no compare-and-swap) — a duplicated worker re-bills windows but cannot corrupt the index because `point_id` is idempotent (I1) and nothing is queryable until gates flip `is_current` (I7) (Spec §6.7)\n- [RunState] State enum: `state ∈ {queued, running, stopped, gated, published, failed}`; `stopped` is what a `SIGTERM` leaves behind (§15 Factor IX) and is the only state `--resume` accepts without `--steal` (Spec §6.9)\n- [RunState] Run record shape (`GET /runs/{run_id}`): `{run_id, doc_id, revision, release_id, state, step, windows_done, windows_total, pages_indexed, gate_results, overrides: [{gate, reason, by}], published_at, lease: {owner, expires_at}, failed: {step, reason}, cost: {input_tokens, output_tokens, cache_hits}}` — a superset of the control-plane run point adding doc/revision/release identity, overrides, publish timestamp, failure detail, and cost (Spec §6.9)\n\n- [Export] `GET /runs/{run_id}/export/labels.jsonl` — streamed, one line per page (Spec §6.8)\n- [Export] `GET /runs/{run_id}/export/observed_tokens.jsonl` — streamed, one line per document (Spec §6.8)\n- [Export] `labels.jsonl` line fields: `page_id, doc_id, revision, page_no, printed_page_no, label_verified, sections[] {section_id, title, page_range, series_id}, summaries[] {lang, text}, codes_in_text[], grounded_rate, safety_flag, vlm_model, prompt_version, dpi` (Spec §6.8)\n- [Export] `safety_flag` replacement formula: `safety_flag = (doc_type in SAFETY_DOC_TYPES or any(t in page.topics for t in SAFETY_TOPICS))`; `SAFETY_DOC_TYPES` is a manifest facet set by the uploader (not inferred from content); `SAFETY_TOPICS` matches the model's own lowercase `topics[]` — replaces `impl`'s `_is_safety()` (Unit.kind grammar + hardcoded keyword list), both of which this CR deletes (Spec §6.8)\n- [Export] `safety_flag` is advisory metadata for Part A's answer policy only — never a gate, never a filter default, never a reason to hide a page; becoming load-bearing needs its own trust level (open question, IMPROVEMENTS C2, §20.1) (Spec §6.8)\n- [Export] `codes_in_text` is the old `verified_identifiers[]`, computed structurally instead of by a gate (Spec §6.8)\n- [Export] Nothing is written to the instance's filesystem (§15 Factor VI); both artefacts are generated from the index and served over HTTP (Spec §6.8)\n- [Export] The observed-token inventory backing `present_instead` (C7) is stored as payload on the document's control point in `vsir_runs` (D9) and held in an in-process LRU cache for prefix lookup (Spec §6.8)\n- [Export] The code-like heuristic (a token containing at least one digit) is display-only: unreachable from `lookup` and `verify`, enforced by module boundary and a test asserting `present_instead` can never appear in `hits` (Spec §6.8)\n\n- [Replay] With `VSIR_VLM=stub` and `VSIR_FIXTURE=<dir>` (D10), both S2 extraction and `read` are served from frozen responses keyed by exactly the §6.3 hashes (Spec §6.3)\n- [Replay] A key not in the fixture is a typed `fixture_miss` error — never a live call, never a fabricated response (Spec §6.3)\n- [Replay] Same code path as production with a different attached service (§15 Factor IV, X) — lets CI, the E2E suite and the console drive the whole loop for free (Spec §6.3)\n\nInvariants / Failure Rows Touched:\n- I1 — `point_id = uuid5(page_id)` makes indexing idempotent; also what makes a duplicated lease-holder safe (§6.1 step10, §6.7)\n- I2 — probe+text is the sole writer of `text` (step02); ungrounded codes never enter the exact surface (§6.5)\n- I4 — the offset proof, both checks required (§6.4)\n- I7 — publish gating: only step 11 flips `is_current`, only when every blocking gate passes (§6.1 step11, §6.7)\n- F5 — ambiguous printed-label resolves to a list, never a silent pick (§6.5)\n- F6 — code reattribution across a window fold, recorded via `content.moved_from` (§6.5)\n- F8 — stitching's canonical key + carry-in across folds; also the failure a blind Level-2 cut would cause one level up from `ladder_level_2_required` (§6.1 step08, §6.2)\n- F9 — `found_only_in_superseded` reads from retained, non-current points of a superseded revision (§6.7 retirement clause 2)\n- F12 — stale/duplicate points from an earlier `run_id` of the same `(doc_id, revision)` must not double totals or stay findable (§6.7 retirement clause 1)\n- F13 — never pad, never offset-guess, never accept a partial window; bisect and re-bill instead (§6.2)\n- F15 — text always sourced from the full page, never a crop (§6.1 step02)\n- F17 — a mid-run crash must leave 0 pages queryable rather than a misleading `searchable_ratio` (§6.7)\n- F19 — a new question is a `read_key` cache miss (§6.3)\n\nDependencies Identified:\n- Step 05 (windowing) depends on the ladder step 04 (S1) selects (§6.1, §6.2)\n- Step 06 (S2 extraction) depends on `extract_key` from §6.3 for its cache\n- Step 07 (derivation) depends on step 02's probe text (for the offset proof and code reattribution) and step 06's `WindowOut`\n- Step 08 (stitching) depends on step 07's per-page `sections[]`\n- Step 09 (embedding) depends on step 07/08 records and must check collection fingerprint compatibility (§6.6) before upsert\n- Step 10 (indexing) depends on step 09's vectors and the `point_id = uuid5(page_id)` scheme (I1)\n- Step 11 (gates + publish) depends on step 10's `is_current=False` points and on gate definitions in §11.1 (outside this region)\n- Step 12 (export) depends on step 11 having published the run, and on the observed-token inventory accumulated on the `vsir_runs` control point (D9)\n- The ladder pick in step 04 depends on `impl/corpus.yaml`'s per-document Level-2 classification (external file, not read in this region)\n- Replay mode depends on a fixture directory keyed by exactly the same hashes as the live cache keys (§6.3)\n- Retirement in step 11 depends on prior runs' `(doc_id, revision, run_id, is_current)` bookkeeping being intact\n\nTechnical Constraints:\n- v1 supports only Level 0/1 windowing plus bisection; Level 2 (blind cut, sequential carry chain) is explicitly out of scope (§6.2)\n- The 1,440-page manual and 592-page E-diagram require Level 2 and are excluded from the POC corpus (6 docs / 142 pages) for that reason (§6.2)\n- Batch API (50% discount) is used for full-corpus ingestion (no latency requirement); the standard endpoint is used for interactive prompt tuning and single-document ingest; selected via `VSIR_VLM_TIER ∈ {batch, standard}` (§6.3)\n- Re-running on identical pages costs $0 (cache hit); the Gemini client carries a token-bucket rate limiter and exponential backoff (§6.3)\n- Nothing is written to the instance filesystem — exports are generated from the index and streamed over HTTP (§15 Factor VI) (§6.8)\n- The run/window lease is advisory only, since Qdrant has no compare-and-swap (§6.7)\n\nSpec References:\n- Spec §6.1, §6.2, §6.3, §6.4, §6.5, §6.6, §6.7, §6.8, §6.9\n- Cross-references appearing within region (not read): §2.5 B, §5.2, §11.1, §13 M8, §15 Factor IV/VI/IX/X, §20.1, IMPROVEMENTS B2/C2, `impl/pipeline-guide/04-windowing-and-keys.md` §5, `impl/corpus.yaml`\n\nContradictions Noticed (report only, do not resolve):\n- Task framing describes \"the three cache keys\" while §6.3 itself defines four formulas (`facts_key`, `extract_key`, `read_key`, `embed_key`) — unclear whether `read_key` is meant to be treated as a variant of `extract_key` rather than a fourth independent key.\n- Retirement clause 3 (\"points of any other document are never touched,\" §6.7) is not tied to a named failure row in this region, unlike clauses 1 (F12) and 2 (F9), even though the task instructions ask for a protected failure row per clause."},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: a503835346fab1169 (use SendMessage with to: 'a503835346fab1169', summary: '<5-10 word recap>' to continue this agent)\n<usage>subagent_tokens: 41939\ntool_uses: 1\nduration_ms: 150657</usage>"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4eefb16f-3989-4441-9cd3-d294cfccb11f","uuid":"acccfe98-da9f-4118-84e7-e6e530d6a263","timestamp":"2026-09-09T16:46:36.780Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"You are Extraction Agent 4 for a PLAN-ONLY implementation-planning task. Read ONLY this region of the spec:\n\n`sed -n '522,719p' /Users/sabesonk/Documents/DILMAH/dilmah-engineering-solutioning/poc/vision_segmentation_index_and_retrieval/development/cr1/spec/spec.md`\n\n(That covers §6.1 steps 01–12, §6.2 windowing + bisection, §6.3 cache keys + batch tier + replay mode, §6.4 the offset proof, §6.5 printed labels + code reattribution, §6.6 embedding fingerprint, §6.7 publish gating + retirement + run/window state, §6.8 exports, §6.9 the run record.)\n\nDo NOT read any other file. Do NOT quote spec text — use pointers only.\n\nYour focus: the twelve ingestion steps as independently buildable work, the exact guard on each, the three cache keys and what goes into each, the two independent offset checks, the code-reattribution rule, the three-part retirement rule, the `vsir_runs` control-plane shape and lease semantics, the two streamed export endpoints, and the run-record shape + state enum.\n\nOutput EXACTLY this format, structured lists only:\n\n### Agent 4: Ingestion Pipeline\n\nFocus:\n- <one line>\n\nRequirements Extracted:\n- [Category] Requirement description (Spec §X.Y)\n(Categories: Step, Windowing, CacheKey, OffsetProof, Labels, Fingerprint, Publish, Retirement, RunState, Export, Replay)\n(Emit one [Step] line per step 01–12: name, in→out, guard.)\n(Emit one [CacheKey] line per key naming every input component.)\n(Emit one [Retirement] line per each of the three retirement clauses in §6.7 and state which failure row each protects.)\n(Emit one [RunState] line for the run point shape, one for the window point shape, one for the lease rule, one for the state enum.)\n\nInvariants / Failure Rows Touched:\n- I<n>, F<n> — <one line each>\n\nDependencies Identified:\n- <…>\n\nTechnical Constraints:\n- <…>\n\nSpec References:\n- Spec §<pointers>\n\nContradictions Noticed (report only, do not resolve):\n- <item> — <the two places that disagree>\n","agentId":"a503835346fab1169","agentType":"general-purpose","harnessNoteCount":0,"harnessTailCount":0,"harnessSectionHash":"78e8c8fe2e62be12","content":[{"type":"text","text":"### Agent 4: Ingestion Pipeline\n\nFocus:\n- The twelve ingestion steps as independently buildable units, the three cache-key/tier/replay rules in §6.3, the offset proof, code reattribution, embedding fingerprint gate, publish/retirement rules, run/window control-plane state, and the two streamed export endpoints.\n\nRequirements Extracted:\n\n- [Step] 01 manifest: file + uploader metadata → `doc_id`, `revision`, `doc_type`, `subjects`, `tags`; guard: facets from filename/metadata/uploader only, no content-sniffing grammar (Spec §6.1)\n- [Step] 02 probe + text: PDF → per-page `text`, `has_text`, `page_count`, `probe_version`; guard: the only writer of `text` (I2); text always from the full page, never a crop (F15) (Spec §6.1)\n- [Step] 03 render: PDF → page rasters at dpi 220; guard: cached by page content hash (Spec §6.1)\n- [Step] 04 S1 document facts: doc head rasters → doc-level facts, picks the window ladder; guard: prompt generalised, no per-corpus grammar (Spec §6.1)\n- [Step] 05 window + `extract_key`: pages → windows (target 30 pages); guard: per §6.2 (Spec §6.1, §6.2)\n- [Step] 06 S2 extraction: window rasters → `WindowOut`; guard: schema §5.2, content-addressable cache §6.3 (Spec §6.1)\n- [Step] 07 derivation: `WindowOut` + probe text → page records; guard: offset proof §6.4, `grounded_rate`, code reattribution §6.5, no verification gate (Spec §6.1)\n- [Step] 08 stitching: per-page `sections[]` → `section_id`, `page_range`, `series_id`; guard: canonical key + carry-in across folds (F8) (Spec §6.1)\n- [Step] 09 embedding: record → dense vector; guard: fingerprint §6.6 (Spec §6.1)\n- [Step] 10 indexing: records → Qdrant points, `is_current=False`; guard: `point_id = uuid5(page_id)` (I1) (Spec §6.1)\n- [Step] 11 gates + publish: run → gate results, flips `is_current`, retires prior points; guard: §11.1, §6.7, I7 (Spec §6.1)\n- [Step] 12 export: published run → `labels.jsonl` + observed-token inventory, both served over HTTP; guard: §6.8 (Spec §6.1)\n\n- [Windowing] Target 30 pages/window subject to an output-budget ladder (Spec §6.2)\n- [Windowing] On `MAX_TOKENS`, truncated/schema-invalid response, or offset failure: bisect and re-bill — never pad, never offset-guess, never accept a partial window (F13); a single page still exceeding budget fails the run typed `window_unsplittable` (Spec §6.2)\n- [Windowing] Three-rung ladder: Level 0/1 cut on S1's table of contents and are parallelisable; Level 2 is a blind cut that must run sequentially with a carry chain (per `impl/pipeline-guide/04-windowing-and-keys.md` §5) (Spec §6.2)\n- [Windowing] v1 implements Level 0/1 plus bisection only; Level 2 and its carry chain are out of scope (Spec §6.2)\n- [Windowing] POC corpus slice (6 docs, 142 pages) ingests without Level 2; `impl/corpus.yaml` records that the 1,440-page manual and 592-page E-diagram are the only two docs needing Level 2 and are excluded from the slice for that reason (Spec §6.2)\n- [Windowing] Attempting the 1,440-page manual must fail typed `ladder_level_2_required` naming the document — never a blind cut that silently straddles a safety function across a fold (that failure is F8, one level up) (Spec §6.2)\n- [Windowing] M8's resume test runs on a generated large PDF, not the excluded manual (Spec §6.2, §13 M8)\n- [Windowing] The ladder depends on an uncached model call (S1); §6.3 caches S1 per document, which `impl` does not (IMPROVEMENTS B2) — this motivates `facts_key` (Spec §6.2, §6.3)\n\n- [CacheKey] `facts_key = sha256(document content hash ‖ resolved vlm model id ‖ prompt_version)` — caches S1 document facts per DOCUMENT; uncached in `impl`, so every re-run re-bills S1 and can silently re-pick a different window ladder (IMPROVEMENTS B2) (Spec §6.3)\n- [CacheKey] `extract_key = sha256(ordered page image hashes ‖ resolved vlm model id ‖ prompt_version ‖ dpi ‖ schema hash)` — keys S2 extraction cache (Spec §6.3)\n- [CacheKey] `read_key = extract_key inputs ‖ question` — a new question is a cache miss (F19) (Spec §6.3)\n- [CacheKey] `embed_key = sha256(composition version ‖ embed model id ‖ composed string)` (Spec §6.3)\n- [CacheKey] `VSIR_VLM_TIER ∈ {batch, standard}` is deliberately excluded from `extract_key` because the tier does not change the output (Spec §6.3)\n\n- [OffsetProof] `abs_page = window.start + page_index - 1` (I4) (Spec §6.4)\n- [OffsetProof] Check 1 (structural): window returned exactly the page indices it was given — `sorted(p.page_index) == list(range(1, window.pages + 1))` (Spec §6.4)\n- [OffsetProof] Check 2 (independent observation): when the page has text and the model read a `printed_page_no`, that label must phrase-match this page's text; if it matches a neighbour's instead, raise `OffsetError` and bisect (the off-by-one signature) (Spec §6.4)\n- [OffsetProof] Both checks are required; a wrong offset shifts every page/citation/summary and nothing else errors — called the single most dangerous line in the pipeline (Spec §6.4)\n\n- [Labels] `printed_page_no` is model-read; precedence: text-layer-confirmed label > model-read label > interpolated from neighbours; `label_verified` and `interpolated` recorded per page; an ambiguous label resolves to a list, never a silent pick (F5) (Spec §6.5)\n- [Labels] Code reattribution (F6): a code reported on page *i* but absent from *i*'s text and present in an adjacent page's text within the same window is reattributed to the page whose text contains it; `content.moved_from` records `{code, from_page_id}` on the receiving page (Spec §6.5)\n- [Labels] A code grounded in no page's text stays where the model put it, counts against that page's `grounded_rate`, and never enters the exact surface (I2) (Spec §6.5)\n\n- [Fingerprint] Collection stores `{embed_model, dim, distance, composition_version}`; on mismatch, refuse to upsert (Spec §6.6)\n- [Fingerprint] A model change requires a new collection + full re-embed + alias swap, never an in-place mix (Spec §6.6)\n\n- [Publish] Step 10 writes every point `is_current=False`; step 11 is the only thing that flips it, and only when every blocking gate passes (I7) (Spec §6.7)\n- [Publish] Every tool injects `is_current=True` server-side, always; the filtered `set_payload` is idempotent and retried; `published_at` is recorded only after it returns (Spec §6.7)\n- [Publish] For full-corpus rebuilds, prefer the atomic path: new collection + one alias swap (Spec §6.7)\n- [Publish] A crash at window 700 of a 1,440-page manual must leave 0 pages queryable, otherwise `searchable_ratio` lies and the loop abstains about a page that is actually in the document (F17) (Spec §6.7)\n\n- [Retirement] Clause 1: points of the same `(doc_id, revision)` written by an earlier `run_id` are deleted by filter — stops totals doubling and stale pages staying findable; protects F12 (Spec §6.7)\n- [Retirement] Clause 2: points of the previously current *other* revision are set `is_current=False` and kept — they are what `found_only_in_superseded` reads from; protects F9 (Spec §6.7)\n- [Retirement] Clause 3: points of any other document are never touched — no explicit failure-row number is attached to this clause in this region, unlike clauses 1 and 2 (Spec §6.7)\n- [Retirement] A blanket \"delete every point whose `run_id` is not the current run\" would satisfy F12 by destroying F9's evidence; both deletions must be filter-based, idempotent, and retried (Spec §6.7)\n\n- [RunState] Run point shape (one per run in `vsir_runs`, D9): `{state, step, windows_done, windows_total, gate_results, lease_owner, lease_expires_at}` (Spec §6.7)\n- [RunState] Window point shape (one per window in `vsir_runs`, D9): `{state, attempts, checkpoint, extract_key}` (Spec §6.7)\n- [RunState] Lease rule: one worker owns one run under a lease; `vsir ingest --resume` refuses a run whose lease is still live unless `--steal` is passed; the lease is advisory (Qdrant has no compare-and-swap) — a duplicated worker re-bills windows but cannot corrupt the index because `point_id` is idempotent (I1) and nothing is queryable until gates flip `is_current` (I7) (Spec §6.7)\n- [RunState] State enum: `state ∈ {queued, running, stopped, gated, published, failed}`; `stopped` is what a `SIGTERM` leaves behind (§15 Factor IX) and is the only state `--resume` accepts without `--steal` (Spec §6.9)\n- [RunState] Run record shape (`GET /runs/{run_id}`): `{run_id, doc_id, revision, release_id, state, step, windows_done, windows_total, pages_indexed, gate_results, overrides: [{gate, reason, by}], published_at, lease: {owner, expires_at}, failed: {step, reason}, cost: {input_tokens, output_tokens, cache_hits}}` — a superset of the control-plane run point adding doc/revision/release identity, overrides, publish timestamp, failure detail, and cost (Spec §6.9)\n\n- [Export] `GET /runs/{run_id}/export/labels.jsonl` — streamed, one line per page (Spec §6.8)\n- [Export] `GET /runs/{run_id}/export/observed_tokens.jsonl` — streamed, one line per document (Spec §6.8)\n- [Export] `labels.jsonl` line fields: `page_id, doc_id, revision, page_no, printed_page_no, label_verified, sections[] {section_id, title, page_range, series_id}, summaries[] {lang, text}, codes_in_text[], grounded_rate, safety_flag, vlm_model, prompt_version, dpi` (Spec §6.8)\n- [Export] `safety_flag` replacement formula: `safety_flag = (doc_type in SAFETY_DOC_TYPES or any(t in page.topics for t in SAFETY_TOPICS))`; `SAFETY_DOC_TYPES` is a manifest facet set by the uploader (not inferred from content); `SAFETY_TOPICS` matches the model's own lowercase `topics[]` — replaces `impl`'s `_is_safety()` (Unit.kind grammar + hardcoded keyword list), both of which this CR deletes (Spec §6.8)\n- [Export] `safety_flag` is advisory metadata for Part A's answer policy only — never a gate, never a filter default, never a reason to hide a page; becoming load-bearing needs its own trust level (open question, IMPROVEMENTS C2, §20.1) (Spec §6.8)\n- [Export] `codes_in_text` is the old `verified_identifiers[]`, computed structurally instead of by a gate (Spec §6.8)\n- [Export] Nothing is written to the instance's filesystem (§15 Factor VI); both artefacts are generated from the index and served over HTTP (Spec §6.8)\n- [Export] The observed-token inventory backing `present_instead` (C7) is stored as payload on the document's control point in `vsir_runs` (D9) and held in an in-process LRU cache for prefix lookup (Spec §6.8)\n- [Export] The code-like heuristic (a token containing at least one digit) is display-only: unreachable from `lookup` and `verify`, enforced by module boundary and a test asserting `present_instead` can never appear in `hits` (Spec §6.8)\n\n- [Replay] With `VSIR_VLM=stub` and `VSIR_FIXTURE=<dir>` (D10), both S2 extraction and `read` are served from frozen responses keyed by exactly the §6.3 hashes (Spec §6.3)\n- [Replay] A key not in the fixture is a typed `fixture_miss` error — never a live call, never a fabricated response (Spec §6.3)\n- [Replay] Same code path as production with a different attached service (§15 Factor IV, X) — lets CI, the E2E suite and the console drive the whole loop for free (Spec §6.3)\n\nInvariants / Failure Rows Touched:\n- I1 — `point_id = uuid5(page_id)` makes indexing idempotent; also what makes a duplicated lease-holder safe (§6.1 step10, §6.7)\n- I2 — probe+text is the sole writer of `text` (step02); ungrounded codes never enter the exact surface (§6.5)\n- I4 — the offset proof, both checks required (§6.4)\n- I7 — publish gating: only step 11 flips `is_current`, only when every blocking gate passes (§6.1 step11, §6.7)\n- F5 — ambiguous printed-label resolves to a list, never a silent pick (§6.5)\n- F6 — code reattribution across a window fold, recorded