{"type":"system","subtype":"task_notification","task_id":"a59e7e455f061a784","tool_use_id":"toolu_01JnTcddmjVPNrAmCTrahf1F","status":"completed","output_file":"/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-sabesonk-Documents-DILMAH-dilmah-engineering-solutioning-poc-vision-segmentation-index-and-retrieval/4eefb16f-3989-4441-9cd3-d294cfccb11f/tasks/a59e7e455f061a784.output","summary":"### Agent 1: Scope, Corrections, Port Ledger, Decisions\n\nFocus:\n- Scope boundaries, plan2 corrections, the impl→CR1 port ledger, and the twelve closed decisions (Spec §0–§3)\n\nRequirements Extracted:\n\n**Scope**\n- [Scope] In-scope: ingestion pipeline manifest→probe→render→windowed VLM extraction→derivation→stitching→embedding→indexing→publish gates→exports (Spec §2.1)\n- [Scope] In-scope: one Qdrant collection, one point per page, two full-text indexes (Spec §2.1, §5.4–5.5)\n- [Scope] In-scope: eight tools over HTTP+MCP — skim_documents, skim_sections, skim_pages, lookup, resolve, fetch, read, verify (Spec §2.1, §7)\n- [Scope] In-scope: reference runner — loop, tri-state triage, six correction loops, answer gate (Spec §2.1, §8)\n- [Scope] In-scope: invariants I1–I8 as assertions, failure catalogue F1–F19 as tests (Spec §2.1, §9–§10)\n- [Scope] In-scope: test pyramid L0–L5 with a frozen fixture (Spec §2.1, §12)\n- [Scope] In-scope: one operator console, M7 (Spec §2.1, §13)\n- [Scope] In-scope: evaluation on the corpus's own ground-truth sets (Spec §2.1, §12.6, M8)\n- [Scope] Out of scope: the retrieval agent as a product surface — owned by POC Part A (Spec §2.2)\n- [Scope] Out of scope: correlation graph, dictionary, resolve/describe/neighbors over entities — this CR only exports to Part A (Spec §2.2, §6.8)\n- [Scope] Out of scope: ERP, spare-parts capture images (Spec §2.2)\n- [Scope] Out of scope: multi-tenancy / tenant_id filters — single-tenant, auth boundary is the whole service (Spec §2.2, R6)\n- [Scope] Out of scope: sparse/lexical vector fusion measurement deferred to M8 (not the vector itself — see Contradictions) (Spec §2.2, D2)\n- [Scope] Out of scope: bounding boxes, around=\"K158\" — region coordinates only in v1 (Spec §2.2, D6)\n- [Scope] Out of scope: OCR of scanned pages — disclosed via not_text/not_searchable, never silently patched (Spec §2.2)\n\n**Corrections (C1–C12)**\n- [Correction] C1: CR1 is a restructured port of `impl` (3,268 lines/16 modules/7 docs/no tests) done in this repo, not an in-place refactor of plan2's line-count target (Spec §2.3)\n- [Correction] C2: `lookup()` must use `MatchPhrase` over `variants(label)` only; `MatchText` (any-order) is banned by a serve/ conformance grep — impl has no text index at all today (Spec §2.3)\n- [Correction] C3: Eight invariants I1–I8 (not seven) — plan2 dropped publish-gating I7 while still citing it in F17 (Spec §2.3)\n- [Correction] C4: 19 failure rows F1–F19 (not 17) — F17 half-finished run, F18 spend, F19 read cache ignoring the question (Spec §2.3)\n- [Correction] C5: fetch default dpi=150 (not 220); dpi ∈ {150,220,300,400}; dpi>220 requires region (Spec §2.3)\n- [Correction] C6: Absence is a six-value enum — ok, four absences (not_found/not_searchable/out_of_scope/found_only_in_superseded), error — fixed from M1 (Spec §2.3, §7.1)\n- [Correction] C7: present_instead becomes an observed-token inventory written at publish time, prefix-only, capped at 5, advisory, cannot affect lookup/verify (Spec §2.3, §6.8, §7.2.4)\n- [Correction] C8: Part A's verified_identifiers[] contract survives as page-level codes_in_text = codes ∩ tokens(text); page_id replaces segment_id (Spec §2.3, D1)\n- [Correction] C9: M2 splits into M2a (generated PDF, stub VLM, no spend) and M2b (pilot PDF ingest) so an absent corpus/API key can't block a deliverable (Spec §2.3)\n- [Correction] C11: Struck — no server-side RetrievalState; service is stateless, scope/exclude are parameters, effective_scope is echoed back (Spec §2.3, §7.5, §15 Factor VI)\n- [Correction] C12: Confirmed and kept — dense vector is a fused image+text interleaved embedding via gemini-embedding-2 (impl/app/embedder.py::embed_page_interleaved); per-page image embedding is unbudgeted (~$0.66/5,505-page run) (Spec §2.3)\n- [Correction] C10: Acceptance-table page counts for TC1E-SF are normative; disagreement on first real ingest is a blocking finding until proven a corpus difference (Spec §2.3)\n\n**Port Ledger (§2.4)**\n- [Port] app/render.py (94 lines) — port as-is; raster rendering, dpi_index=150/dpi_answer=220 split (Spec §2.4, §4.2)\n- [Port] app/windows.py (99 lines) — port as-is; windowing + extract_key; add bisection ladder F13 (Spec §2.4, §6.2)\n- [Port] app/stitch.py (126 lines) — port, retarget from units to sections; add series_id for F8 (Spec §2.4)\n- [Port] app/embedder.py (241 lines) — port as-is, load-bearing; gemini-embedding-2 interleaved image+text (D4); keep retry/backoff, prepare_image (max_edge_px=1568), batch-count verification, per-item fallback (Spec §2.4)\n- [Port] app/sparse.py (42 lines) — port as-is; raw term frequencies + Qdrant Modifier.IDF; keep dedupe() (Spec §2.4, D2)\n- [Port] app/segstore.py (219 lines) — port with changes; add two text indexes with phrase_matching (§5.5) and is_current publish flag (I7) (Spec §2.4)\n- [DoNotPort] app/segstore.py — remove the entity_keys payload index and its MatchValue lookup (Spec §2.4, C2)\n- [Port] app/retrieve.py (430 lines) — port selectively; keep rrf() (ranks-only), decompose(), resolve()/interpolated; rewrite lookup() as phrase filter, replace search() with skim_* rungs, replace expand() with next.expand, supersede /compare with fetch (Spec §2.4)\n- [Port] app/textlayer.py (139 lines) — port partially; keep probe(), page_texts() (layout mode, not flattened), content_hash(), Probe.s2_input_mode (Spec §2.4)\n- [DoNotPort] app/textlayer.py — do not port gate(), backs(), identifiers_from_text() (I2 makes them unnecessary) or token_set()'s adjacent-token joins (superseded by phrase_matching + variants()) (Spec §2.4)\n- [DoNotPort] app/p