84-5140.0020 into [84,5140,0020]), not impl's TOKEN_RE which keeps it as one token (Spec §2.4)\n- [Correction] max_read_pages tightened to 3 (impl uses 4; plan2 and §7.3 already say 3) — deliberate, not a porting slip (Spec §2.4)\n\n**Feature-removal ledger (§2.5, selected)**\n- [DoNotPort] 200-empty abstention path — removed deliberately, replaced by four typed absences (I5) (Spec §2.5A)\n- [DoNotPort] POST /api/v1/compare — removed, replaced by fetch (agent compares pages itself) (Spec §2.5A)\n- [DoNotPort] POST /api/v1/expand as an endpoint — removed, capability survives as next.expand + re-scoped skim (Spec §2.5A)\n- [DoNotPort] DELETE /api/v1/documents/{doc_id} — not in HTTP surface, replaced by `vsir retire` admin process (Spec §2.5A)\n- [DoNotPort] entity_keys curated exact-match index — removed, replaced by phrase-matching text index (Spec §2.5B, C2, §5.5)\n- [DoNotPort] Allowlist gate (gate(), backs()) and withheld.jsonl — removed, replaced by grounded_rate + codes_in_text (Spec §2.5B)\n- [DoNotPort] Identifier grammar (SCHEMA_CARD, IdClass, classify(), normalise(), nine regexes) — removed, no grammar at all (Spec §2.5B, §5.2)\n- [DoNotPort] Unit grammar (STRICT_KINDS, key_for_unit, Unit.kind, attrs) — removed, replaced by sections[] = title + is_start (Spec §2.5B)\n- [DoNotPort] refs[] in S2 schema — removed, measured at 0 reads in impl; cross-references live in next.references (Spec §2.5B)\n- [DoNotPort] Level 2 window ladder and its carry chain — not included in v1 (§6.2), the one exclusion that changes what the POC can ingest (Spec §2.5B)\n- [DoNotPort] config.yaml/corpus.yaml as runtime config — removed, env-only (§15 Factor III) (Spec §2.5B)\n- [DoNotPort] Job state as dict on daemon threads — removed, replaced by vsir_runs + lease (D9) (Spec §2.5C)\n- [DoNotPort] On-disk exports at data/exports/{run_id} — changed to streamed HTTP (§6.8); flagged OQ-7 (Spec §2.5C)\n- [DoNotPort] Rendered pages persisted under /data/pages/<doc_id>/ — removed, rasters re-rendered on demand (Spec §2.5C, §4.2)\n\n**Decisions (D1–D12)**\n- [Decision] D1: Yes — export stays, shape changes to page-level labels.jsonl with page_range/sections/summary/codes_in_text/safety_flag (Spec §3)\n- [Decision] D2: Yes — sparse/lexical vector ported; captions surface finally populated from summaries+topics (Spec §3)\n- [Decision] D3: Yes, vlm_codes ships in v1, opt-in, always verified:false (Spec §3)\n- [Decision] D4: gemini-embedding-2, one page → one fused interleaved image+text vector (Spec §3)\n- [Decision] D5: One summary per page per dominant language; no blending (Spec §3)\n- [Decision] D6: Deferred — region=[x0,y0,x1,y1] normalised only, no bounding boxes (Spec §3)\n- [Decision] D7: Both MCP and runner ship; only the runner may compose an answer (Spec §3)\n- [Decision] D8: Superseded by D4 — no multivector, no second point, no blending (Spec §3)\n- [Decision] D9: Control-plane vsir_runs collection; one worker per run under advisory lease (Spec §3)\n- [Decision] D10: Deterministic replay via VSIR_VLM=stub + VSIR_FIXTURE; a miss is typed fixture_miss (Spec §3)\n- [Decision] D12: Yes — image query optional on all skim_* rungs; hits carry ImageRef/preview (Spec §3)\n- [Decision] D11: Hard gates: precision=1.00, abstention=1.00, recall≥0.95 (block<0.90), alarm_hit≥0.99, xref_resolve≥0.99 (Spec §3)\n\n**Breaking changes (§2.5D, the five ⚠ exclusions)**\n- [BreakingChange] 200-empty → typed absence: any caller treating empty 200 as \"no results\" must learn four new statuses (Spec §2.5D-1, I5)\n- [BreakingChange] segment_id → page_id, verified_identifiers[] → codes_in_text[]: Part A's attachment evidence keeps meaning under new name/granularity (Spec §2.5D-2, C8, D1)\n- [BreakingChange] Exports move from disk (data/exports/{run_id}) to HTTP — breaks Part A if it reads files directly (Spec §2.5D-3, §6.8, OQ-7)\n- [BreakingChange] Bearer auth everywhere — every existing script/notebook needs a token (Spec §2.5D-4, §7.4)\n- [BreakingChange] No UI until M7 — impl's upload-and-search page is unavailable for the duration (Spec §2.5D-5)\n\n**Deliverable ledger (§0, M0–M8)**\n- [DemoLedger] M0: Repo skeleton, pinned config, test harness (Qdrant), boot self-check — `vsir doctor && bash scripts/test-unit.sh` — spend: none (Spec §0)\n- [DemoLedger] M1: Exact-match surface proved on synthetic text — `vsir demo exact --synthetic` — spend: none (Spec §0)\n- [DemoLedger] M2a: Full ingest of a generated PDF with a stubbed VLM — `vsir ingest data/source/synthetic_3window.pdf --vlm stub` — spend: none (Spec §0)\n- [DemoLedger] M2b: Full ingest of the pilot PDF; fixture frozen — `VSIR_ALLOW_PAID=1 vsir ingest data/source/TC1E-SF.pdf` — spend: S2 + embed, once (Spec §0)\n- [DemoLedger] M3: lookup + verify over HTTP and MCP, typed absence — `vsir serve & vsir lookup \"SF 1.1A\" && vsir eval acceptance` — spend: none (Spec §0)\n- [DemoLedger] M4: skim_pages + fetch + resolve, caps, auth, audit — `vsir demo narrow` — spend: none (Spec §0)\n- [DemoLedger] M5: Ladder rungs + read (paid step) with stamped codes — `VSIR_ALLOW_PAID=1 vsir read --pages … --question …` — spend: read (Spec §0)\n- [DemoLedger] M6: The runner: loop, tri-state triage, answer gate, abstention — `VSIR_ALLOW_PAID=1 vsir ask \"carton discharge won't restart after an E-stop reset\"` — spend: read (Spec §0)\n- [DemoLedger] M7: Operator console (viewer + agent console + trust badges) — `bash scripts/test-e2e.sh` then browse `http://localhost:5174` — spend: none (fixture-backed) (Spec §0)\n- [DemoLedger] M8: Revisions, resumable ingest, corpus scale-out + evaluation report — `vsir ingest --resume <run_id>` and `vsir eval corpus` — spend: ingest (Spec §0)\n\nInvariants / Failure Rows Touched:\n- I1 — idempotent point_id; duplicated worker wastes money but cannot corrupt index (Spec §3, D9)\n- I2 — hallucinated codes can't be in exact surface; makes gate()/backs() unneeded (Spec §1.2, §2.4)\n- I3 — MatchPhrase-only conformance grep bans MatchText in serve/ (Spec §2.3, C2)\n- I5 — six-value absence enum (ok + 4 absences + error), fixed from M1 (Spec §2.3, C6)\n- I7 — publish gating; dropped from plan2's \"seven invariants\" yet still cited by F17 (Spec §2.3, C3)\n- I8 — total invariant count is eight per FAILPROOF §1 (Spec §2.3, C3)\n- F1 — any-order MatchText matching is the banned failure mode (Spec §2.3, C2)\n- F8 — server-held scope causes search-a-subset-believing-you-searched-the-chapter failure; forces stateless design (Spec §2.3, C11)\n- F11 — \"-latest\" model id drift; boot must refuse (Spec §2.4)\n- F13 — bisection ladder added to windows.py that impl lacked (Spec §2.4, §6.2)\n- F16 — present_instead guard needs a home: the observed-token inventory (Spec §2.3, C7)\n- F17 — half-finished run exposed; also the row PLAN kept citing after dropping I7 (Spec §2.3, C3–C4)\n- F18 — unbounded/uncapped spend (Spec §2.3, C4)\n- F19 — read cache ignoring the question (Spec §2.3, C4)\n\nDependencies Identified:\n- §4.1 (restructured module layout), §4.2 (dpi split), §4.3 (boot refusal on model ids), §4.4 (CLI: vsir demo/retire)\n- §5.1–5.7 (schema, text index design, tokenizer, grounded_rate), §6 incl. §6.2 (ladder), §6.6 (fingerprint), §6.8 (exports, observed-token inventory, safety_flag rule)\n- §7 (tool surface: §7.1 envelopes, §7.2.1–7.2.5 tool specs, §7.3 max_read_pages, §7.4 HTTP paths/auth, §7.5 statelessness, §7.6 no-score-in-fusion refusal)\n- §8 (runner: §8.2 auto-promote exact hits, §8.4 answer gate), §9–§10 (invariants/failure catalogue as tests), §11.1 (publish gates)\n- §12 (test pyramid, §12.1 fixtures, §12.5 greps, §12.6 eval gate numbers), §13 (M7 console, milestone dependency graph), §15 (twelve-factor runtime, Factors III/VI/X/XII), §17 and OQ-1/OQ-6(resolved as D12)/OQ-7 (open questions)\n- External: Qdrant (WORD tokenizer, Modifier.IDF, no compare-and-swap), Gemini (gemini-embedding-2, gemini-pro-latest aliasing), POC Part A / correlation graph (export consumer), source repo `VisionRag/…/impl` (port origin)\n\nTechnical Constraints:\n- `text` field is written only by the PyMuPDF probe (Spec §1.2)\n- lookup uses MatchPhrase over variants(label), never MatchText (Spec §2.3, C2)\n- tok() must mirror Qdrant's WORD tokenizer, not impl's TOKEN_RE (Spec §2.4)\n- fetch default dpi=150; dpi ∈ {150,220,300,400}; dpi>220 requires region (Spec §2.3, C5)\n- max_read_pages = 3 (Spec §2.4)\n- No model id may end in `-latest`; boot must refuse otherwise (Spec §2.4)\n- Config sourced from environment only; no config.yaml/corpus.yaml at runtime (Spec §2.4, §15 Factor III)\n- Dense vector: gemini-embedding-2, per-page single fused Content; text parts separate from image part; task_type rejected by model; bare list in contents returns one aggregated embedding — must wrap per-page Content and verify count with per-item fallback; output_dimensionality via MRL truncation 768→1536→3072 recorded in collection name + fingerprint (Spec §3, D4)\n- RRF fusion is ranks-only, rrf_k=60, no similarity score enters the arithmetic (Spec §3, D2, §7.6)\n- Captions surface written from summaries[]+topics via sparse.dedupe(against=text) to avoid double-counting (Spec §3, D2)\n- Service is stateless: scope/exclude are parameters, effective_scope is echoed back, no server-side RetrievalState (Spec §2.3, C11)\n- vlm_codes always verified:false, opt-in (Spec §3, D3)\n- region=[x0,y0,x1,y1] normalized only, no bounding boxes (Spec §3, D6)\n- vsir_runs: one point per run/window, lease is advisory not atomic, safety via I1+I7 (Spec §3, D9)\n- Deterministic replay keyed by extract_key/read_key; miss = typed fixture_miss, never a live call (Spec §3, D10)\n- Image query optional on all three skim_* rungs; ImageRef/preview are references, never bytes (Spec §3, D12)\n- Hard gate numbers re-baselined once after M2b under the C10 rule (Spec §3, D11, C10)\n- M0/M1/M2a/M3/M4/M7 cost nothing; M2b/M5/M6/M8 are paid, each gated behind VSIR_ALLOW_PAID=1 (Spec §0)\n\nSpec References:\n- Spec §0, §1.1, §1.2, §1.3, §2.1, §2.2, §2.3 (C1–C12), §2.4, §2.5 (A/B/C/D), §3 (D1–D12)\n\nContradictions Noticed (report only, do not resolve):\n- §2.2's out-of-scope table lists \"Sparse/lexical vector + RRF fusion\" as excluded, citing D2 — but §3's D2 ruling says the sparse vector and RRF fusion are kept/ported for v1 (\"Yes — ported, and the third surface finally populated... Fusion stays rrf() at rrf_k=60\"); only the *measurement* of value (plan2 §9.2) is deferred to M8, not the feature itself. §2.2 vs §3-D2.\n- C5: PLAN §3.7 (fetch dpi=220 default) vs PLAN §3.9 (dpi=150 default) — resolved to 150 but the two source sections disagree.\n- C6: PLAN §5.1 I5 (five absence states) vs FAILPROOF §1 I5 (six absence states) — resolved to six.\n- C11: MCP_ARCHITECTURE §4.4 / PLAN §4.4 (server-side RetrievalState) vs AGENTIC-RETRIEVAL §9 / F8 (requires statelessness) — resolved as struck.\n- C8: POC doc §5 (promises per-segment verified_identifiers[] from an allowlist gate) vs plan2 (deletes the gate entirely) — resolved via codes_in_text rename at page granularity.\n- C3: PLAN §5.1 states \"seven invariants\" I1–I7, yet PLAN's own F17 citation presumes an invariant (publish gating) not in that list — internal PLAN self-contradiction, resolved to eight invariants I1–I8 per FAILPROOF §1.","usage":{"total_tokens":47913,"tool_uses":1,"duration_ms":182921},"uuid":"634686fe-0c6c-4c9e-8d83-c84087a4a978","session_id":"4eefb16f-3989-4441-9cd3-d294cfccb11f"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JnTcddmjVPNrAmCTrahf1F","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"### Agent 1: Scope, Corrections, Port Ledger, Decisions\n\nFocus:\n- Scope boundaries, plan2 corrections, the impl→CR1 port ledger, and the twelve closed decisions (Spec §0–§3)\n\nRequirements Extracted:\n\n**Scope**\n- [Scope] In-scope: ingestion pipeline manifest→probe→render→windowed VLM extraction→derivation→stitching→embedding→indexing→publish gates→exports (Spec §2.1)\n- [Scope] In-scope: one Qdrant collection, one point per page, two full-text indexes (Spec §2.1, §5.4–5.5)\n- [Scope] In-scope: eight tools over HTTP+MCP — skim_documents, skim_sections, skim_pages, lookup, resolve, fetch, read, verify (Spec §2.1, §7)\n- [Scope] In-scope: reference runner — loop, tri-state triage, six correction loops, answer gate (Spec §2.1, §8)\n- [Scope] In-scope: invariants I1–I8 as assertions, failure catalogue F1–F19 as tests (Spec §2.1, §9–§10)\n- [Scope] In-scope: test pyramid L0–L5 with a frozen fixture (Spec §2.1, §12)\n- [Scope] In-scope: one operator console, M7 (Spec §2.1, §13)\n- [Scope] In-scope: evaluation on the corpus's own ground-truth sets (Spec §2.1, §12.6, M8)\n- [Scope] Out of scope: the retrieval agent as a product surface — owned by POC Part A (Spec §2.2)\n- [Scope] Out of scope: correlation graph, dictionary, resolve/describe/neighbors over entities — this CR only exports to Part A (Spec §2.2, §6.8)\n- [Scope] Out of scope: ERP, spare-parts capture images (Spec §2.2)\n- [Scope] Out of scope: multi-tenancy / tenant_id filters — single-tenant, auth boundary is the whole service (Spec §2.2, R6)\n- [Scope] Out of scope: sparse/lexical vector fusion measurement deferred to M8 (not the vector itself — see Contradictions) (Spec §2.2, D2)\n- [Scope] Out of scope: bounding boxes, around=\"K158\" — region coordinates only in v1 (Spec §2.2, D6)\n- [Scope] Out of scope: OCR of scanned pages — disclosed via not_text/not_searchable, never silently patched (Spec §2.2)\n\n**Corrections (C1–C12)**\n- [Correction] C1: CR1 is a restructured port of `impl` (3,268 lines/16 modules/7 docs/no tests) done in this repo, not an in-place refactor of plan2's line-count target (Spec §2.3)\n- [Correction] C2: `lookup()` must use `MatchPhrase` over `variants(label)` only; `MatchText` (any-order) is banned by a serve/ conformance grep — impl has no text index at all today (Spec §2.3)\n- [Correction] C3: Eight invariants I1–I8 (not seven) — plan2 dropped publish-gating I7 while still citing it in F17 (Spec §2.3)\n- [Correction] C4: 19 failure rows F1–F19 (not 17) — F17 half-finished run, F18 spend, F19 read cache ignoring the question (Spec §2.3)\n- [Correction] C5: fetch default dpi=150 (not 220); dpi ∈ {150,220,300,400}; dpi>220 requires region (Spec §2.3)\n- [Correction] C6: Absence is a six-value enum — ok, four absences (not_found/not_searchable/out_of_scope/found_only_in_superseded), error — fixed from M1 (Spec §2.3, §7.1)\n- [Correction] C7: present_instead becomes an observed-token inventory written at publish time, prefix-only, capped at 5, advisory, cannot affect lookup/verify (Spec §2.3, §6.8, §7.2.4)\n- [Correction] C8: Part A's verified_identifiers[] contract survives as page-level codes_in_text = codes ∩ tokens(text); page_id replaces segment_id (Spec §2.3, D1)\n- [Correction] C9: M2 splits into M2a (generated PDF, stub VLM, no spend) and M2b (pilot PDF ingest) so an absent corpus/API key can't block a deliverable (Spec §2.3)\n- [Correction] C11: Struck — no server-side RetrievalState; service is stateless, scope/exclude are parameters, effective_scope is echoed back (Spec §2.3, §7.5, §15 Factor VI)\n- [Correction] C12: Confirmed and kept — dense vector is a fused image+text interleaved embedding via gemini-embedding-2 (impl/app/embedder.py::embed_page_interleaved); per-page image embedding is unbudgeted (~$0.66/5,505-page run) (Spec §2.3)\n- [Correction] C10: Acceptance-table page counts for TC1E-SF are normative; disagreement on first real ingest is a blocking finding until proven a corpus difference (Spec §2.3)\n\n**Port Ledger (§2.4)**\n- [Port] app/render.py (94 lines) — port as-is; raster rendering, dpi_index=150/dpi_answer=220 split (Spec §2.4, §4.2)\n- [Port] app/windows.py (99 lines) — port as-is; windowing + extract_key; add bisection ladder F13 (Spec §2.4, §6.2)\n- [Port] app/stitch.py (126 lines) — port, retarget from units to sections; add series_id for F8 (Spec §2.4)\n- [Port] app/embedder.py (241 lines) — port as-is, load-bearing; gemini-embedding-2 interleaved image+text (D4); keep retry/backoff, prepare_image (max_edge_px=1568), batch-count verification, per-item fallback (Spec §2.4)\n- [Port] app/sparse.py (42 lines) — port as-is; raw term frequencies + Qdrant Modifier.IDF; keep dedupe() (Spec §2.4, D2)\n- [Port] app/segstore.py (219 lines) — port with changes; add two text indexes with phrase_matching (§5.5) and is_current publish flag (I7) (Spec §2.4)\n- [DoNotPort] app/segstore.py — remove the entity_keys payload index and its MatchValue lookup (Spec §2.4, C2)\n- [Port] app/retrieve.py (430 lines) — port selectively; keep rrf() (ranks-only), decompose(), resolve()/interpolated; rewrite lookup() as phrase filter, replace search() with skim_* rungs, replace expand() with next.expand, supersede /compare with fetch (Spec §2.4)\n- [Port] app/textlayer.py (139 lines) — port partially; keep probe(), page_texts() (layout mode, not flattened), content_hash(), Probe.s2_input_mode (Spec §2.4)\n- [DoNotPort] app/textlayer.py — do not port gate(), backs(), identifiers_from_text() (I2 makes them unnecessary) or token_set()'s adjacent-token joins (superseded by phrase_matching + variants()) (Spec §2.4)\n- [DoNotPort] app/pagemodel.py (306 lines) — do not port identifier machinery: SCHEMA_CARD, IdClass, classify(), normalise(), Identifier, backed_keys(), entity_keys_for() (kept out by §12.5 greps); only record/page-id shape carried over, restated in §5.1–5.3 (Spec §2.4)\n- [Port] app/segment.py (341 lines) — rewrite; S2 schema changes units[]→sections[], identifiers[]→codes[], plus summaries/topics; drop _is_safety() keyword list and identifier merge (Spec §2.4, §5.2)\n- [Port] app/pipeline.py (334 lines) — rewrite; same step order, allowlist/class_totality gates and withheld.jsonl export replaced by grounded_rate (§5.7) and §11.1 gates (Spec §2.4)\n- [Port] app/segjobs.py (110 lines) — port with changes; job tracking moves into vsir_runs control collection with a lease (D9) instead of process-local state (Spec §2.4)\n- [Port] app/config.py (96 lines) — port, restructure; keep shape, config from environment only (§15 Factor III), config.yaml becomes .env.example defaults, no -latest model ids (Spec §2.4)\n- [Port] app/main.py (293 lines) — port with changes; FastAPI surface maps to §7.4 paths; add bearer auth, audit log, /ready, /runs/{run_id} (Spec §2.4)\n- [Port] app/api_models.py (398 lines) — port with changes; re-shape to the two envelope families of §7.1, delete every entity_keys field (Spec §2.4)\n- [Port] app/embedder.py::embed_query_image — port and wire it; image is an optional parameter on all three skim_* rungs (D12), image-only query runs dense branch alone (Spec §2.4, §7.2.1)\n- [Port] scripts/interfaces_demo.py — port as the demo spine, ancestor of `vsir demo` (Spec §2.4, §4.4)\n- [NetNew] Text index (§5.5), verify (§7.2.4), fetch (§7.2.5), three skim_* rungs, the runner (§8), invariants as assertions (§9), the entire test pyramid (§12), the twelve-factor runtime (§15) (Spec §2.4)\n- [NetNew] Boot refusal on -latest model ids (correction of impl, which uses gemini-pro-latest for extract and read) (Spec §2.4)\n- [NetNew] tok() must mirror Qdrant's WORD tokenizer (splits 84-5140.0020 into [84,5140,0020]), not impl's TOKEN_RE which keeps it as one token (Spec §2.4)\n- [Correction] max_read_pages tightened to 3 (impl uses 4; plan2 and §7.3 already say 3) — deliberate, not a porting slip (Spec §2.4)\n\n**Feature-removal ledger (§2.5, selected)**\n- [DoNotPort] 200-empty abstention path — removed deliberately, replaced by four typed absences (I5) (Spec §2.5A)\n- [DoNotPort] POST /api/v1/compare — removed, replaced by fetch (agent compares pages itself) (Spec §2.5A)\n- [DoNotPort] POST /api/v1/expand as an endpoint — removed, capability survives as next.expand + re-scoped skim (Spec §2.5A)\n- [DoNotPort] DELETE /api/v1/documents/{doc_id} — not in HTTP surface, replaced by `vsir retire` admin process (Spec §2.5A)\n- [DoNotPort] entity_keys curated exact-match index — removed, replaced by phrase-matching text index (Spec §2.5B, C2, §5.5)\n- [DoNotPort] Allowlist gate (gate(), backs()) and withheld.jsonl — removed, replaced by grounded_rate + codes_in_text (Spec §2.5B)\n- [DoNotPort] Identifier grammar (SCHEMA_CARD, IdClass, classify(), normalise(), nine regexes) — removed, no grammar at all (Spec §2.5B, §5.2)\n- [DoNotPort] Unit grammar (STRICT_KINDS, key_for_unit, Unit.kind, attrs) — removed, replaced by sections[] = title + is_start (Spec §2.5B)\n- [DoNotPort] refs[] in S2 schema — removed, measured at 0 reads in impl; cross-references live in next.references (Spec §2.5B)\n- [DoNotPort] Level 2 window ladder and its carry chain — not included in v1 (§6.2), the one exclusion that changes what the POC can ingest (Spec §2.5B)\n- [DoNotPort] config.yaml/corpus.yaml as runtime config — removed, env-only (§15 Factor III) (Spec §2.5B)\n- [DoNotPort] Job state as dict on daemon threads — removed, replaced by vsir_runs + lease (D9) (Spec §2.5C)\n- [DoNotPort] On-disk exports at data/exports/{run_id} — changed to streamed HTTP (§6.8); flagged OQ-7 (Spec §2.5C)\n- [DoNotPort] Rendered pages persisted under /data/pages/<doc_id>/ — removed, rasters re-rendered on demand (Spec §2.5C, §4.2)\n\n**Decisions (D1–D12)**\n- [Decision] D1: Yes — export stays, shape changes to page-level labels.jsonl with page_range/sections/summary/codes_in_text/safety_flag (Spec §3)\n- [Decision] D2: Yes — sparse/lexical vector ported; captions surface finally populated from summaries+topics (Spec §3)\n- [Decision] D3: Yes, vlm_codes ships in v1, opt-in, always verified:false (Spec §3)\n- [Decision] D4: gemini-embedding-2, one page → one fused interleaved image+text vector (Spec §3)\n- [Decision] D5: One summary per page per dominant language; no blending (Spec §3)\n- [Decision] D6: Deferred — region=[x0,y0,x1,y1] normalised only, no bounding boxes (Spec §3)\n- [Decision] D7: Both MCP and runner ship; only the runner may compose an answer (Spec §3)\n- [Decision] D8: Superseded by D4 — no multivector, no second point, no blending (Spec §3)\n- [Decision] D9: Control-plane vsir_runs collection; one worker per run under advisory lease (Spec §3)\n- [Decision] D10: Deterministic replay via VSIR_VLM=stub + VSIR_FIXTURE; a miss is typed fixture_miss (Spec §3)\n- [Decision] D12: Yes — image query optional on all skim_* rungs; hits carry ImageRef/preview (Spec §3)\n- [Decision] D11: Hard gates: precision=1.00, abstention=1.00, recall≥0.95 (block<0.90), alarm_hit≥0.99, xref_resolve≥0.99 (Spec §3)\n\n**Breaking changes (§2.5D, the five ⚠ exclusions)**\n- [BreakingChange] 200-empty → typed absence: any caller treating empty 200 as \"no results\" must learn four new statuses (Spec §2.5D-1, I5)\n- [BreakingChange] segment_id → page_id, verified_identifiers[] → codes_in_text[]: Part A's attachment evidence keeps meaning under new name/granularity (Spec §2.5D-2, C8, D1)\n- [BreakingChange] Exports move from disk (data/exports/{run_id}) to HTTP — breaks Part A if it reads files directly (Spec §2.5D-3, §6.8, OQ-7)\n- [BreakingChange] Bearer auth everywhere — every existing script/notebook needs a token (Spec §2.5D-4, §7.4)\n- [BreakingChange] No UI until M7 — impl's upload-and-search page is unavailable for the duration (Spec §2.5D-5)\n\n**Deliverable ledger (§0, M0–M8)**\n- [DemoLedger] M0: Repo skeleton, pinned config, test harness (Qdrant), boot self-check — `vsir doctor && bash scripts/test-unit.sh` — spend: none (Spec §0)\n- [DemoLedger] M1: Exact-match surface proved on synthetic text — `vsir demo exact --synthetic` — spend: none (Spec §0)\n- [DemoLedger] M2a: Full ingest of a generated PDF with a stubbed VLM — `vsir ingest data/source/synthetic_3window.pdf --vlm stub` — spend: none (Spec §0)\n- [DemoLedger] M2b: Full ingest of the pilot PDF; fixture frozen — `VSIR_ALLOW_PAID=1 vsir ingest data/source/TC1E-SF.pdf` — spend: S2 + embed, once (Spec §0)\n- [DemoLedger] M3: lookup + verify over HTTP and MCP, typed absence — `vsir serve & vsir lookup \"SF 1.1A\" && vsir eval acceptance` — spend: none (Spec §0)\n- [DemoLedger] M4: skim_pages + fetch + resolve, caps, auth, audit — `vsir demo narrow` — spend: none (Spec §0)\n- [DemoLedger] M5: Ladder rungs + read (paid step) with stamped codes — `VSIR_ALLOW_PAID=1 vsir read --pages … --question …` — spend: read (Spec §0)\n- [DemoLedger] M6: The runner: loop, tri-state triage, answer gate, abstention — `VSIR_ALLOW_PAID=1 vsir ask \"carton discharge won't restart after an E-stop reset\"` — spend: read (Spec §0)\n- [DemoLedger] M7: Operator console (viewer + agent console + trust badges) — `bash scripts/test-e2e.sh` then browse `http://localhost:5174` — spend: none (fixture-backed) (Spec §0)\n- [DemoLedger] M8: Revisions, resumable ingest, corpus scale-out + evaluation report — `vsir ingest --resume <run_id>` and `vsir eval corpus` — spend: ingest (Spec §0)\n\nInvariants / Failure Rows Touched:\n- I1 — idempotent point_id; duplicated worker wastes money but cannot corrupt index (Spec §3, D9)\n- I2 — hallucinated codes can't be in exact surface; makes gate()/backs() unneeded (Spec §1.2, §2.4)\n- I3 — MatchPhrase-only conformance grep bans MatchText in serve/ (Spec §2.3, C2)\n- I5 — six-value absence enum (ok + 4 absences + error), fixed from M1 (Spec §2.3, C6)\n- I7 — publish gating; dropped from plan2's \"seven invariants\" yet still cited by F17 (Spec §2.3, C3)\n- I8 — total invariant count is eight per FAILPROOF §1 (Spec §2.3, C3)\n- F1 — any-order MatchText matching is the banned failure mode (Spec §2.3, C2)\n- F8 — server-held scope causes search-a-subset-believing-you-searched-the-chapter failure; forces stateless design (Spec §2.3, C11)\n- F11 — \"-latest\" model id drift; boot must refuse (Spec §2.4)\n- F13 — bisection ladder added to windows.py that impl lacked (Spec §2.4, §6.2)\n- F16 — present_instead guard needs a home: the observed-token inventory (Spec §2.3, C7)\n- F17 — half-finished run exposed; also the row PLAN kept citing after dropping I7 (Spec §2.3, C3–C4)\n- F18 — unbounded/uncapped spend (Spec §2.3, C4)\n- F19 — read cache ignoring the question (Spec §2.3, C4)\n\nDependencies Identified:\n- §4.1 (restructured module layout), §4.2 (dpi split), §4.3 (boot refusal on model ids), §4.4 (CLI: vsir demo/retire)\n- §5.1–5.7 (schema, text index design, tokenizer, grounded_rate), §6 incl. §6.2 (ladder), §6.6 (fingerprint), §6.8 (exports, observed-token inventory, safety_flag rule)\n- §7 (tool surface: §7.1 envelopes, §7.2.1–7.2.5 tool specs, §7.3 max_read_pages, §7.4 HTTP paths/auth, §7.5 statelessness, §7.6 no-score-in-fusion refusal)\n- §8 (runner: §8.2 auto-promote exact hits, §8.4 answer gate), §9–§10 (invariants/failure catalogue as tests), §11.1 (publish gates)\n- §12 (test pyramid, §12.1 fixtures, §12.5 greps, §12.6 eval gate numbers), §13 (M7 console, milestone dependency graph), §15 (twelve-factor runtime, Factors III/VI/X/XII), §17 and OQ-1/OQ-6(resolved as D12)/OQ-7 (open questions)\n- External: Qdrant (WORD tokenizer, Modifier.IDF, no compare-and-swap), Gemini (gemini-embedding-2, gemini-pro-latest aliasing), POC Part A / correlation graph (export consumer), source repo `VisionRag/…/impl` (port origin)\n\nTechnical Constraints:\n- `text` field is written only by the PyMuPDF probe (Spec §1.2)\n- lookup uses MatchPhrase over variants(label), never MatchText (Spec §2.3, C2)\n- tok() must mirror Qdrant's WORD tokenizer, not impl's TOKEN_RE (Spec §2.4)\n- fetch default dpi=150; dpi ∈ {150,220,300,400}; dpi>220 requires region (Spec §2.3, C5)\n- max_read_pages = 3 (Spec §2.4)\n- No model id may end in `-latest`; boot must refuse otherwise (Spec §2.4)\n- Config sourced from environment only; no config.yaml/corpus.yaml at runtime (Spec §2.4, §15 Factor III)\n- Dense vector: gemini-embedding-2, per-page single fused Content; text parts separate from image part; task_type rejected by model; bare list in contents returns one aggregated embedding — must wrap per-page Content and verify count with per-item fallback; output_dimensionality via MRL truncation 768→1536→3072 recorded in collection name + fingerprint (Spec §3, D4)\n- RRF fusion is ranks-only, rrf_k=60, no similarity score enters the arithmetic (Spec §3, D2, §7.6)\n- Captions surface written from summaries[]+topics via sparse.dedupe(against=text) to avoid double-counting (Spec §3, D2)\n- Service is stateless: scope/exclude are parameters, effective_scope is echoed back, no server-side RetrievalState (Spec §2.3, C11)\n- vlm_codes always verified:false, opt-in (Spec §3, D3)\n- region=[x0,y0,x1,y1] normalized only, no bounding boxes (Spec §3, D6)\n- vsir_runs: one point per run/window, lease is advisory not atomic, safety via I1+I7 (Spec §3, D9)\n- Deterministic replay keyed by extract_key/read_key; miss = typed fixture_miss, never a live call (Spec §3, D10)\n- Image query optional on all three skim_* rungs; ImageRef/preview are references, never bytes (Spec §3, D12)\n- Hard gate numbers re-baselined once after M2b under the C10 rule (Spec §3, D11, C10)\n- M0/M1/M2a/M3/M4/M7 cost nothing; M2b/M5/M6/M8 are paid, each gated behind VSIR_ALLOW_PAID=1 (Spec §0)\n\nSpec References:\n- Spec §0, §1.1, §1.2, §1.3, §2.1, §2.2, §2.3 (C1–C12), §2.4, §2.5 (A/B/C/D), §3 (D1–D12)\n\nContradictions Noticed (report only, do not resolve):\n- §2.2's out-of-scope table lists \"Sparse/lexical vector + RRF fusion\" as excluded, citing D2 — but §3's D2 ruling says the sparse vector and RRF fusion are kept/ported for v1 (\"Yes — ported, and the third surface finally populated... Fusion stays rrf() at rrf_k=60\"); only the *measurement* of value (plan2 §9.2) is deferred to M8, not the feature itself. §2.2 vs §3-D2.\n- C5: PLAN §3.7 (fetch dpi=220 default) vs PLAN §3.9 (dpi=150 default) — resolved to 150 but the two source sections disagree.\n- C6: PLAN §5.1 I5 (five absence states) vs FAILPROOF §1 I5 (six absence states) — resolved to six.\n- C11: MCP_ARCHITECTURE §4.4 / PLAN §4.4 (server-side RetrievalState) vs AGENTIC-RETRIEVAL §9 / F8 (requires statelessness) — resolved as struck.\n- C8: POC doc §5 (promises per-segment verified_identifiers[] from an allowlist gate) vs plan2 (deletes the gate entirely) — resolved via codes_in_text rename at page granularity.\n- C3: PLAN §5.1 states \"seven invariants\" I1–I7, yet PLAN's own F17 citation presumes an invariant (publish gating) not in that list — internal PLAN self-contradiction, resolved to eight invariants I1–I8 per FAILPROOF §1."},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: a59e7e455f061a784 (use SendMessage with to: 'a59e7e455f061a784', summary: '<5-10 word recap>' to continue this agent)\n<usage>subagent_tokens: 52060\ntool_uses: 1\nduration_ms: 182924</usage>"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4eefb16f-3989-4441-9cd3-d294cfccb11f","uuid":"8a2c1b5e-96a9-480c-aa84-a6ae4ae8ca96","timestamp":"2026-09-09T16:46:42.906Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"You are Extraction Agent 1 for a PLAN-ONLY implementation-planning task. Read ONLY this region of the spec:\n\n`sed -n '14,251p' /Users/sabesonk/Documents/DILMAH/dilmah-engineering-solutioning/poc/vision_segmentation_index_and_retrieval/development/cr1/spec/spec.md`\n\n(That covers §0 deliverable ledger, §1 overview, §2.1–2.5 scope + corrections C1–C12 + the port ledger + the feature-removal ledger, §3 closed decisions D1–D12.)\n\nDo NOT read any other file. Do NOT quote spec text — use pointers only (\"Spec 