{"type":"system","subtype":"task_notification","task_id":"ac48122ec21c0694b","tool_use_id":"toolu_01LiRsJMSVY7pKE57tS6vS6t","status":"completed","output_file":"/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-sabesonk-Documents-DILMAH-dilmah-engineering-solutioning-poc-vision-segmentation-index-and-retrieval/4eefb16f-3989-4441-9cd3-d294cfccb11f/tasks/ac48122ec21c0694b.output","summary":"### Agent 5: Tool Surface\n\nFocus:\n- §7.1–7.6 of the spec: the two response envelope families, six-value status enum, hit models, ImageRef rules, the eight tools (§7.2.1–7.2.6), caps/typed errors, HTTP surface/auth/audit, MCP server, and the four enforced refusals.\n\nRequirements Extracted:\n\n- [EnvelopeA] Family A (`skim_documents`, `skim_sections`, `skim_pages`, `lookup`, `resolve`) uses `SearchResponse[HitT]` with fields: `status`, `hits`, `unverified_hits`, `total`, `capped`, `weak`, `needs_scope`, `next`, `effective_scope`, `scope_stats`, `reads_remaining`, `provenance` (Spec §7.1)\n- [EnvelopeA] Validator `empty_is_never_ok`: asserts `hits` or `unverified_hits` non-empty, or `status != \"ok\"` — an empty result can never claim `ok` (Spec §7.1)\n- [EnvelopeA] `total` is `count(exact=True)` — the SET size, not `len(hits)` (Spec §7.1)\n- [EnvelopeA] `unverified_hits` is `vlm_codes`-only, `verified=False`, and is never merged into `hits` (Spec §7.1)\n- [EnvelopeB] Family B (`fetch`, `read`, `verify`) uses `ToolEnvelope[ResultT]` with fields: `status` (`ok`|`error`, describes whether the call ran, not what it found), `result`, `reads_remaining`, `provenance` (Spec §7.1)\n- [EnvelopeB] A `verify` where every claim is `absent` is still `status: ok` with three `absent` verdicts; a missing `page_id` is `404 page_not_found`; a backend failure is a 5xx — a failed call must never look like an empty successful call (Spec §7.1)\n- [Status] `ok` — hits/result present; agent proceeds normally (not itemized in the spec's action table, which only tabulates the five non-`ok` values) (Spec §7.1)\n- [Status] `not_found` (searched, genuinely absent) — agent action: abstain, but check `next.suggest` first (Spec §7.1)\n- [Status] `not_searchable` (candidate pages have no text layer) — agent action: escalate to vision (`fetch`/`read`) (Spec §7.1)\n- [Status] `out_of_scope` (no document matched filters) — agent action: re-orient, widen scope (Spec §7.1)\n- [Status] `found_only_in_superseded` — agent action: surface the revision and let the caller decide (Spec §7.1)\n- [Status] `error` — agent action: retry or report, never abstain (Spec §7.1)\n- [Status] `next.suggest` softens a `not_found`: e.g. `lookup(\"alarm 152\")` returns `status: not_found` with `next.suggest: [\"skim_pages\"]` plus tokens that did occur, so status stays honest while the affordance prevents abstention on a phrasing accident (Spec §7.1, §12.3)\n- [Status] `weak`/`needs_scope` are caller-independent: `WEAK_ABS = 20` (server constant), `weak = needs_scope = total > max(WEAK_ABS, 0.25 * scope_stats.pages)`; `cap` only bounds returned hits, never affects `weak` (Spec §7.1)\n- [HitModel] `ImageRef` = `{url, thumb_url, dpi, width, height}` — a reference, never bytes (Spec §7.1)\n- [HitModel] `Preview` = `{page_id, thumb_url}` — the group's best-ranked page (Spec §7.1)\n- [HitModel] `DocHit` = `{doc_id, title, doc_type, pages_matched, best_rank, searchable_ratio, summary, preview}` (Spec §7.1)\n- [HitModel] `SectionHit` = `{section_id, title, page_range, pages_matched, best_rank, preview}` (Spec §7.1)\n- [HitModel] `PageHit` = `{page_id, printed_page_no, summary, summary_lang, page_kind, why, rank, flags, grounded_rate, text_trust, image, next}` (Spec §7.1)\n- [HitModel] `LookupHit` = `{page_id, page_no, printed_page_no, page_kind, verified, text_trust, image, next}` (Spec §7.1)\n- [HitModel] `ResolveHit` = `{page_id, printed_page_no, label_verified, interpolated, image}` (Spec §7.1)\n- [ImageQuery] Every search result carries an `ImageRef`; no search result carries image bytes — the sharpened form of P2 (Spec §7.1)\n- [ImageQuery] `skim_pages`, `lookup`, `resolve` hand back `page_id` + ready-made `ImageRef`; caller never constructs a URL; URL is lazy so nothing renders until dereferenced (Spec §7.1)\n- [ImageQuery] `DocHit`/`SectionHit` carry no `page_id` (answer \"which binder/chapter\") but carry `preview` = `thumb_url` of the group's best-ranked matched page, falling back to page 1 when nothing matched (useful for `searchable_ratio: 0.00` binders) (Spec §7.1)\n- [ImageQuery] Image *bytes* in a triage row are refused — would let the agent answer from the search result instead of choosing then paying (the failure P2 prevents), at 1–2k tokens/row (Spec §7.1)\n- [HitModel] `verified` on `LookupHit` is a boolean about the surface (`text`=true, `vlm_codes`=false), distinct from the three-state `present|absent|unverifiable` vocabulary used by per-claim checks (Spec §7.1, §7.2.4, §7.2.6)\n- [Tool] `skim_documents(query, image=None, scope?, exclude?) → [DocHit]` — free — Family A — no milestone stated (Spec §7.2.1)\n- [Tool] `skim_sections(query, image=None, scope, exclude?) → [SectionHit]` — free — Family A — no milestone stated (Spec §7.2.1)\n- [Tool] `skim_pages(query, image=None, scope, exclude?, limit=10) → [PageHit]` — free — Family A — no milestone stated (Spec §7.2.1)\n- [Tool] `lookup(label, scope?, include_unverified=False, cap=20)` — free — Family A — no milestone stated (Spec §7.2.2)\n- [Tool] `resolve(printed_label, doc_id?)` — free — Family A — no milestone stated (Spec §7.2.3)\n- [Tool] `verify(claims, page_ids)` — free — Family B — no milestone stated (Spec §7.2.4)\n- [Tool] `fetch(page_ids, include=[\"image\",\"text\",\"summary\"], dpi=150, region=None, inline=True)` — free/paid label NOT stated in the tool header (unlike all other tools) — Family B — milestone: `url` field is \"what M7's viewer displays\" (Spec §7.2.5)\n- [Tool] `read(page_ids, question)` — explicitly **\"the paid step\"** — Family B — renders at pinned dpi 220, no milestone stated (Spec §7.2.6)\n- [Ordering] `query` optional when `image` given and vice versa; one implementation exposed as three tool names so the agent chooses between names, not a `granularity` enum (Spec §7.2.1)\n- [Ordering] `why ∈ {\"dense\", \"lexical\"}`; `lexical` = text-index phrase/token hit (no sparse vector, D2) (Spec §7.2.1)\n- [Ordering] Triage-row `summary` is in caller's requested `lang`, falling back to page's dominant language (D5); row states which language it returned (Spec §7.2.1)\n- [Ordering] No full text in a triage row (P2) (Spec §7.2.1)\n- [Ordering] `next: {expand: section_id, neighbours: [page_id,…], references: [printed labels]}` turns retrieval into navigation (P4) (Spec §7.2.1)\n- [Ordering] Three branches run inside `scope` minus `exclude`: `page` (dense), `lexical` (sparse over extracted text), `captions` (sparse over generated text); `decompose(query)` splits exact identifiers to `lookup`/phrase filter before embedding (Spec §7.2.1)\n- [Ordering] Branches fused client-side via reciprocal rank fusion at `rrf_k=60`, weights `page 1.0 · lexical 1.0 · captions 0.4`; only ranks enter the arithmetic — no score computed, stored, or returned (Spec §7.2.1, §7.6)\n- [Ordering] `rank` = 1-based ordinal of fused list; `why` names every contributing branch (e.g. `[\"dense\"]`, `[\"lexical\"]`, `[\"dense\",\"lexical\"]`), enabling §8.2's auto-promote-exact-hits and use-`why`-as-signal (Spec §7.2.1, §8.2)\n- [Ordering] `skim_pages` returns ≤10 rows (`limit`, max 25); `skim_sections`/`skim_documents` group same fused candidates: `pages_matched`=group size, `best_rank`=best page rank in group, rows ordered by `(best_rank, -pages_matched)`, ≤10 rows (Spec §7.2.1)\n- [Ordering] Fusion is deterministic given the same branches — identical `(query, image, scope, exclude)` yields identical order, required for E2E/L2 assertion stability (Spec §7.2.1)\n- [ImageQuery] Query vector for an image comes from `embed_query_image(image, text=query)`, fusing photo+words in one `types.Content` so both land in the same vector space as indexed page vectors (D4) (Spec §7.2.1, D12)\n- [ImageQuery] Rule 1: no instruction prefix when the query is multimodal — prefix applies only to a bare text query (impl's constraint, from Google's guidance) (Spec §7.2.1)\n- [ImageQuery] Rule 2: an image-only query runs the dense branch alone; `lexical`/`captions` (sparse, text-built) are skipped; RRF degenerates to dense ranking; every row's `why` = `[\"dense\"]`, stated not silent (Spec §7.2.1, §8.2)\n- [ImageQuery] Rule 3: an image can never reach the exact surface — `lookup` and `verify` take a text label only (I2, I3); a photo may find a candidate page but never confirm a code (Spec §7.2.1)\n- [Tool] `lookup` is exact, phrase-only, a set not a ranking; `total` = `count(exact=True)`, then `scroll` to `cap`; `cap` bounds the returned page of the set and sets `capped`, never affects `weak` (Spec §7.2.2, §7.1)\n- [Tool] `lookup(include_unverified=True)` repeats the query against `vlm_codes`, returning results in `unverified_hits` with `verified: false`; scores and lists are never merged (Spec §7.2.2)\n- [Tool] `lookup` on candidate pages with no text layer returns `not_searchable`, never a bare empty set (Spec §7.2.2)\n- [Tool] `resolve(printed_label, doc_id?) → page_id + interpolated + label_verified`; ambiguity returns every candidate (Spec §7.2.3)\n- [Tool] `verify(claims, page_ids)` checks per `(claim, page)`, not per claim — prevents a draft citing `p001–p002` from letting a code from the neighbouring page through (I8) (Spec §7.2.4)\n- [Tool] `VerifyResult` is a map of claim → verdict inside the Family B envelope; three states: `present`, `absent` (with `present_instead`), `unverifiable` (with `reason`) (Spec §7.2.4)\n- [Tool] Collapsing `unverifiable` into `absent` would falsely tell the agent \"not on the page\" about a page it couldn't examine (Spec §7.2.4)\n- [Tool] `present_instead` = prefix lookup over observed tokens, capped at 5, labelled \"different part\" — never a distance or nearest-match (Spec §7.2.4)\n- [Tool] `fetch` returns material, not an answer; `region` is normalised `[x0,y0,x1,y1]`; PyMuPDF renders the clip on demand with no new storage; rendered rasters cached in-process across turns (§4.2) (Spec §7.2.5)\n- [Tool] `fetch` result `url` is always present — a bearer-authenticated GET usable directly by a browser `<img>` or renderer; `bytes_b64` present only when `inline=true` (default true, since an agent needs pixels in context and an MCP client cannot follow a URL); `inline=false` returns reference only (used by the console to avoid moving megabytes through JSON twice) (Spec §7.2.5)\n- [Tool] `fetch`'s `include` controls parts returned; dropping `\"image\"` makes `fetch` a cheap text/summary read (Spec §7.2.5)\n- [Tool] `read` renders at pinned dpi 220 — caller cannot change it because dpi is part of `read_key` (§4.2, §6.3) (Spec §7.2.6)\n- [Tool] `ReadResult` fields: `extract`, `codes` (list of `{raw, status}` with `present_instead` when absent), `sufficient`, `flags`, `page_provenance` (list of `{page_id, text_trust}`) (Spec §7.2.6)\n- [Tool] Transcription correction is inside `read`, automatic and always (Loop 1): every emitted code is phrase-checked against page text and stamped with the same three states `verify` uses — one vocabulary, one meaning; a page with no text layer makes every code `unverifiable` (Spec §7.2.6, §7.2.4)\n- [Tool] `sufficient` is mandatory — without it the agent can't separate \"the answer is no\" from \"wrong page,\" and might compose an answer from a page that never contained one (Spec §7.2.6)\n- [Tool] Retrieval judgment never happens inside `read` — that would make the engine the answerer (Spec §7.2.6)\n- [Cap] `read` page images per call: ≤3 → `read_page_cap_exceeded` (Spec §7.3)\n- [Cap] `fetch` pages per call: ≤5 and ≤12 MP total → `fetch_budget_exceeded {limit, requested}` (Spec §7.3)\n- [Cap] `dpi` ∈ {36, 72, 150, 220, 300, 400} (36/72 = triage thumbnail tiers behind `thumb_url`, 150 = `fetch` default, 220 = `read`) → `dpi_not_allowed` (Spec §7.3)\n- [Cap] `dpi > 220` requires `region` → `dpi_requires_region` (Spec §7.3)\n- [Cap] unknown scope key → `filter_unknown_key {keys}` (Spec §7.3)\n- [Cap] per-caller `read` quota, server-side, surfaced as `reads_remaining` in every envelope → `429 budget_exhausted` (Spec §7.3)\n- [Cap] All caps are typed 400s, never a clamp, never a silent truncation (F18) (Spec §7.3)\n- [Route] `POST /tools/{tool_name}` — the eight tools of §7.2, one envelope each — bearer (Spec §7.4)\n- [Route] `POST /ask` — the runner; the only surface that may return prose (§8.4) — bearer (Spec §7.4)\n- [Route] `GET /pages/{page_id}/image?dpi=&region=` — the page raster, rendered on demand, browser-renderable half of `fetch`, same caps/typed 400s as §7.3, ported from `impl`'s `/api/v1/page-image/{page_id}` — bearer (Spec §7.4)\n- [Route] `GET /runs/{run_id}` — the run record of §6.9 — bearer (Spec §7.4)\n- [Route] `GET /runs/{run_id}/export/{labels,observed_tokens}.jsonl` — streamed exports of §6.8 — bearer (Spec §7.4)\n- [Route] `GET /health` — liveness, process up; MUST NOT fail on a backing-service outage (§15.1) — none (Spec §7.4)\n- [Route] `GET /ready` — readiness: boot self-check passed, Qdrant reachable, pinned index schema present — none (Spec §7.4)\n- [Route] `GET /metrics` — Prometheus (§11.4) — none (internal network) (Spec §7.4)\n- [Auth] Bearer token required on every tool call; `401` without one; identity is propagated, never client-supplied (Spec §7.4)\n- [Audit] One append-only audit line per `read` and `fetch`: `(user_id, run_id, session_id, tool, page_ids, dpi, input_tokens, output_tokens, cache_hit, latency_ms)` (Spec §7.4)\n- [Audit] Cost goes in the audit log, not the response body — agent gets one integer, `reads_remaining`; a `usd_estimate` beside verification stamps would be noise next to must-not-miss fields (Spec §7.4)\n- [MCP] `vision-segmentation-retriever` exposes the same eight tools over stdio + SSE, calling identical implementations — no second code path (Spec §7.5)\n- [MCP] MCP server is stateless: `scope` and `exclude` are parameters; `effective_scope` is echoed back (Spec §7.5)\n- [Refusal] Returning a similarity score — enforcement: conformance grep for no field named `score` in any response model; ordinal `rank`/`best_rank` permitted and required (§7.2.1) since a position is not a confidence (Spec §7.6)\n- [Refusal] Routing the query — enforcement: no tool picks the document for the caller (Spec §7.6)\n- [Refusal] Composing the answer — enforcement: only the runner composes, and only behind the answer gate (§8.4) (Spec §7.6)\n- [Refusal] Fuzzy matching on codes — enforcement: conformance grep for no edit-distance/similarity library in `requirements.txt`, no `MatchText` in `serve/`, plus an I3 property test (Spec §7.6)\n\nInvariants / Failure Rows Touched:\n- I5 — the two-envelope-family design is attributed directly to I5 (§7.1 section title)\n- I8 — `verify` must check per `(claim, page)`, not per claim, so a citation spanning pages can't leak a neighbouring page's code (§7.2.4)\n- I2, I3 — an image query can find a candidate page but can never confirm a code; `lookup`/`verify` accept text labels only (§7.2.1 rule 3)\n- F8 — `effective_scope` is echoed back in every Family A response because the service is stateless (§7.1)\n- F18 — all caps in §7.3 are typed 400s by design, never clamps or silent truncation (§7.3 section title)\n\nDependencies Identified:\n- Ordering/aggregation ported from `impl/app/retrieve.py::rrf` (D2), ranks-only (§7.2.1)\n- Image-query embedding ported from `impl`'s `embed_query_image(image, text=query)` (D4, D12) (§7.2.1)\n- `GET /pages/{page_id}/image` ported from `impl`'s `/api/v1/page-image/{page_id}` (§7.4)\n- MCP server calls the identical tool implementations as the HTTP surface — no second code path (§7.5)\n- `read`'s pinned dpi 220 is tied into `read_key` (§4.2, §6.3)\n- In-process raster caching across turns depends on §4.2\n- `next.suggest` behavior ties to §12.3's phrasing-accident handling\n- `why`/`rank` fusion output feeds §8.2's auto-promote-exact-hits and why-as-signal logic\n- `POST /ask` prose output depends on the answer gate defined in §8.4\n- `fetch`'s `url` field is what M7's viewer renders\n- `effective_scope` echo-back depends on statelessness invariant referenced as F8/C11\n- Run/export routes (`GET /runs/{run_id}`, exports) depend on §6.8 and §6.9 definitions\n\nTechnical Constraints:\n- RRF: `rrf_k = 60`, weights `page 1.0 · lexical 1.0 · captions 0.4`; only ranks enter the arithmetic\n- `WEAK_ABS = 20` server constant; `weak = needs_scope = total > max(WEAK_ABS, 0.25 * scope_stats.pages)` — independent of caller-passed `cap`\n- `dpi` enum {36, 72, 150, 220, 300, 400}; `dpi > 220` requires `region`\n- `read`: ≤3 page images/call, pinned dpi 220 (uneditable)\n- `fetch`: ≤5 pages/call, ≤12 MP total, default dpi 150, `inline` default true\n- `lookup`: default `cap=20`; `present_instead` prefix-match capped at 5\n- `skim_pages`: `limit=10`, max 25; `skim_sections`/`skim_documents`: ≤10 rows\n- No field named `score` permitted anywhere in response models (conformance grep)\n- No edit-distance/similarity library in `requirements.txt`; no `MatchText` in `serve/` (conformance grep + I3 property test)\n\nSpec References:\n- Spec §7.1, §7.2 (intro), §7.2.1, §7.2.2, §7.2.3, §7.2.4, §7.2.5, §7.2.6, §7.3, §7.4, §7.5, §7.6\n- Cross-references touched within region: I2, I3, I5, I8, F8, F18, C11, P2, P4, D2, D4, D5, D12, §4.2, §6.3, §6.8, §6.9, §8.2, §8.4, §11.4, §12.3, §15.1\n\nContradictions Noticed (report only, do not resolve):\n- `fetch`'s free/paid status is unlabeled — §7.2.1–§7.2.4 headers each explicitly say \"(free)\" and §7.2.6 explicitly calls `read` \"the paid step,\" but §7.2.5's `fetch` header carries no such annotation, even though §7.4's audit-line requirement groups `fetch` with `read` (\"one append-only audit line per `read` and `fetch`\") and §7.3's quota is named specifically a \"read quota\" (not a fetch quota) — unclear whether `fetch` is free, paid, or partially metered.\n- `why` branch-label enum vs. actual fused branches — §7.2.1 states `why ∈ {\"dense\", \"lexical\"}` and every worked example of `why` (`[\"dense\"]`, `[\"lexical\"]`, `[\"dense\",\"lexical\"]`) uses only two labels, but the ordering rules describe three fused branches (`page`/dense, `lexical`, and `captions`, weighted 0.4) — it's unstated whether a `captions`-only or `captions`-contributing hit is ever surfaced as `\"captions\"` in `why`, or silently folded into `\"dense\"`.\n- \"`cap`\" terminology vs. actual parameter names — §7.1's general discussion of Family A behavior (\"`cap` controls how many hits come back... `lookup(\"3\")` unscoped matches most of the corpus, so it is `weak` at any `cap`\") speaks of `cap` as if it were common across Family A, and ties the `capped` envelope field to it (\"`cap` bounds the returned page of the set and sets `capped`\"), but only `lookup`'s actual signature has a `cap` parameter (§7.2.2) — `skim_pages` instead has a `limit` parameter (§7.2.1), and `skim_documents`/`skim_sections`/`resolve` have no bounding parameter named at all. It's unclear whether `capped`/`weak` on skim/resolve responses are driven by `limit` or some other implicit value.","usage":{"total_tokens":42500,"tool_uses":1,"duration_ms":167719},"uuid":"046410ec-de20-41bd-8685-d536727b2028","session_id":"4eefb16f-3989-4441-9cd3-d294cfccb11f"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LiRsJMSVY7pKE57tS6vS6t","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"### Agent 5: Tool Surface\n\nFocus:\n- §7.1–7.6 of the spec: the two response envelope families, six-value status enum, hit models, ImageRef rules, the eight tools (§7.2.1–7.2.6), caps/typed errors, HTTP surface/auth/audit, MCP server, and the four enforced refusals.\n\nRequirements Extracted:\n\n- [EnvelopeA] Family A (`skim_documents`, `skim_sections`, `skim_pages`, `lookup`, `resolve`) uses `SearchResponse[HitT]` with fields: `status`, `hits`, `unverified_hits`, `total`, `capped`, `weak`, `needs_scope`, `next`, `effective_scope`, `scope_stats`, `reads_remaining`, `provenance` (Spec §7.1)\n- [EnvelopeA] Validator `empty_is_never_ok`: asserts `hits` or `unverified_hits` non-empty, or `status != \"ok\"` — an empty result can never claim `ok` (Spec §7.1)\n- [EnvelopeA] `total` is `count(exact=True)` — the SET size, not `len(hits)` (Spec §7.1)\n- [EnvelopeA] `unverified_hits` is `vlm_codes`-only, `verified=False`, and is never merged into `hits` (Spec §7.1)\n- [EnvelopeB] Family B (`fetch`, `read`, `verify`) uses `ToolEnvelope[ResultT]` with fields: `status` (`ok`|`error`, describes whether the call ran, not what it found), `result`, `reads_remaining`, `provenance` (Spec §7.1)\n- [EnvelopeB] A `verify` where every claim is `absent` is still `status: ok` with three `absent` verdicts; a missing `page_id` is `404 page_not_found`; a backend failure is a 5xx — a failed call must never look like an empty successful call (Spec §7.1)\n- [Status] `ok` — hits/result present; agent proceeds normally (not itemized in the spec's action table, which only tabulates the five non-`ok` values) (Spec §7.1)\n- [Status] `not_found` (searched, genuinely absent) — agent action: abstain, but check `next.suggest` first (Spec §7.1)\n- [Status] `not_searchable` (candidate pages have no text layer) — agent action: escalate to vision (`fetch`/`read`) (Spec §7.1)\n- [Status] `out_of_scope` (no document matched filters) — agent action: re-orient, widen scope (Spec §7.1)\n- [Status] `found_only_in_superseded` — agent action: surface the revision and let the caller decide (Spec §7.1)\n- [Status] `error` — agent action: retry or report, never abstain (Spec §7.1)\n- [Status] `next.suggest` softens a `not_found`: e.g. `lookup(\"alarm 152\")` returns `status: not_found` with `next.suggest: [\"skim_pages\"]` plus tokens that did occur, so status stays honest while the affordance prevents abstention on a phrasing accident (Spec §7.1, §12.3)\n- [Status] `weak`/`needs_scope` are caller-independent: `WEAK_ABS = 20` (server constant), `weak = needs_scope = total > max(WEAK_ABS, 0.25 * scope_stats.pages)`; `cap` only bounds returned hits, never affects `weak` (Spec §7.1)\n- [HitModel] `ImageRef` = `{url, thumb_url, dpi, width, height}` — a reference, never bytes (Spec §7.1)\n- [HitModel] `Preview` = `{page_id, thumb_url}` — the group's best-ranked page (Spec §7.1)\n- [HitModel] `DocHit` = `{doc_id, title, doc_type, pages_matched, best_rank, searchable_ratio, summary, preview}` (Spec §7.1)\n- [HitModel] `SectionHit` = `{section_id, title, page_range, pages_matched, best_rank, preview}` (Spec §7.1)\n- [HitModel] `PageHit` = `{page_id, printed_page_no, summary, summary_lang, page_kind, why, rank, flags, grounded_rate, text_trust, image, next}` (Spec §7.1)\n- [HitModel] `LookupHit` = `{page_id, page_no, printed_page_no, page_kind, verified, text_trust, image, next}` (Spec §7.1)\n- [HitModel] `ResolveHit` = `{page_id, printed_page_no, label_verified, interpolated, image}` (Spec §7.1)\n- [ImageQuery] Every search result carries an `ImageRef`; no search result carries image bytes — the sharpened form of P2 (Spec §7.1)\n- [ImageQuery] `skim_pages`, `lookup`, `resolve` hand back `page_id` + ready-made `ImageRef`; caller never constructs a URL; URL is lazy so nothing renders until dereferenced (Spec §7.1)\n- [ImageQuery] `DocHit`/`SectionHit` carry no `page_id` (answer \"which binder/chapter\") but carry `preview` = `thumb_url` of the group's best-ranked matched page, falling back to page 1 when nothing matched (useful for `searchable_ratio: 0.00` binders) (Spec §7.1)\n- [ImageQuery] Image *bytes* in a triage row are refused — would let the agent answer from the search result instead of choosing then paying (the failure P2 prevents), at 1–2k tokens/row (Spec §7.1)\n- [HitModel] `verified` on `LookupHit` is a boolean about the surface (`text`=true, `vlm_codes`=false), distinct from the three-state `present|absent|unverifiable` vocabulary used by per-claim checks (Spec §7.1, §7.2.4, §7.2.6)\n- [Tool] `skim_documents(query, image=None, scope?, exclude?) → [DocHit]` — free — Family A — no milestone stated (Spec §7.2.1)\n- [Tool] `skim_sections(query, image=None, scope, exclude?) → [SectionHit]` — free — Family A — no milestone stated (Spec §7.2.1)\n- [Tool] `skim_pages(query, image=None, scope, exclude?, limit=10) → [PageHit]` — free — Family A — no milestone stated (Spec §7.2.1)\n- [Tool] `lookup(label, scope?, include_unverified=False, cap=20)` — free — Family A — no milestone stated (Spec §7.2.2)\n- [Tool] `resolve(printed_label, doc_id?)` — free — Family A — no milestone stated (Spec §7.2.3)\n- [Tool] `verify(claims, page_ids)` — free — Family B — no milestone stated (Spec §7.2.4)\n- [Tool] `fetch(page_ids, include=[\"image\",\"text\",\"summary\"], dpi=150, region=None, inline=True)` — free/paid label NOT stated in the tool header (unlike all other tools) — Family B — milestone: `url` field is \"what M7's viewer displays\" (Spec §7.2.5)\n- [Tool] `read(page_ids, question)` — explicitly **\"the paid step\"** — Family B — renders at pinned dpi 220, no milestone stated (Spec §7.2.6)\n- [Ordering] `query` optional when `image` given and vice versa; one implementation exposed as three tool names so the agent chooses between names, not a `granularity` enum (Spec §7.2.1)\n- [Ordering] `why ∈ {\"dense\", \"lexical\"}`; `lexical` = text-index phrase/token hit (no sparse vector, D2) (Spec §7.2.1)\n- [Ordering] Triage-row `summary` is in caller's requested `lang`, falling back to page's dominant language (D5); row states which language it returned (Spec §7.2.1)\n- [Ordering] No full text in a triage row (P2) (Spec §7.2.1)\n- [Ordering] `next: {expand: section_id, neighbours: [page_id,…], references: [printed labels]}` turns retrieval into navigation (P4) (Spec §7.2.1)\n- [Ordering] Three branches run inside `scope` minus `exclude`: `page` (dense), `lexical` (sparse over extracted text), `captions` (sparse over generated text); `decompose(query)` splits exact identifiers to `lookup`/phrase filter before embedding (Spec §7.2.1)\n- [Ordering] Branches fused client-side via reciprocal rank fusion at `rrf_k=60`, weights `page 1.0 · lexical 1.0 · captions 0.4`; only ranks enter the arithmetic — no score computed, stored, or returned (Spec §7.2.1, §7.6)\n- [Ordering] `rank` = 1-based ordinal of fused list; `why` names every contributing branch (e.g. `[\"dense\"]`, `[\"lexical\"]`, `[\"dense\",\"lexical\"]`), enabling §8.2's auto-promote-exact-hits and use-`why`-as-signal (Spec §7.2.1, §8.2)\n- [Ordering] `skim_pages` returns ≤10 rows (`limit`, max 25); `skim_sections`/`skim_documents` group same fused candidates: `pages_matched`=group size, `best_rank`=best page rank in group, rows ordered by `(best_rank, -pages_matched)`, ≤10 rows (Spec §7.2.1)\n- [Ordering] Fusion is deterministic given the same branches — identical `(query, image, scope, exclude)` yields identical order, required for E2E/L2 assertion stability (Spec §7.2.1)\n- [ImageQuery] Query vector for an image comes from `embed_query_image(image, text=query)`, fusing photo+words in one `types.Content` so both land in the same vector space as indexed page vectors (D4) (Spec §7.2.1, D12)\n- [ImageQuery] Rule 1: no instruction prefix when the query is multimodal — prefix applies only to a bare text query (impl's constraint, from Google's guidance) (Spec §7.2.1)\n- [ImageQuery] Rule 2: an image-only query runs the dense branch alone; `lexical`/`captions` (sparse, text-built) are skipped; RRF degenerates to dense ranking; every row's `why` = `[\"dense\"]`, stated not silent (Spec §7.2.1, §8.2)\n- [ImageQuery] Rule 3: an image can never reach the exact surface — `lookup` and `verify` take a text label only (I2, I3); a photo may find a candidate page but never confirm a code (Spec §7.2.1)\n- [Tool] `lookup` is exact, phrase-only, a set not a ranking; `total` = `count(exact=True)`, then `scroll` to `cap`; `cap` bounds the returned page of the set and sets `capped`, never affects `weak` (Spec §7.2.2, §7.1)\n- [Tool] `lookup(include_unverified=True)` repeats the query against `vlm_codes`, returning results in `unverified_hits` with `verified: false`; scores and lists are never merged (Spec §7.2.2)\n- [Tool] `lookup` on candidate pages with no text layer returns `not_searchable`, never a bare empty set (Spec §7.2.2)\n- [Tool] `resolve(printed_label, doc_id?) → page_id + interpolated + label_verified`; ambiguity returns every candidate (Spec §7.2.3)\n- [Tool] `verify(claims, page_ids)` checks per `(claim, page)`, not per claim — prevents a draft citing `p001–p002` from letting a code from the neighbouring page through (I8) (Spec §7.2.4)\n- [Tool] `VerifyResult` is a map of claim → verdict inside the Family B envelope; three states: `present`, `absent` (with `present_instead`), `unverifiable` (with `reason`) (Spec §7.2.4)\n- [Tool] Collapsing `unverifiable` into `absent` would falsely tell the agent \"not on the page\" about a page it couldn't examine (Spec §7.2.4)\n- [Tool] `present_instead` = prefix lookup over observed tokens, capped at 5, labelled \"different part\" — never a distance or nearest-match (Spec §7.2.4)\n- [Tool] `fetch` returns material, not an answer; `region` is normalised `[x0,y0,x1,y1]`; PyMuPDF renders the clip on demand with no new storage; rendered rasters cached in-process across turns (§4.2) (Spec §7.2.5)\n- [Tool] `fetch` result `url` is always present — a bearer-authenticated GET usable directly by a browser `<img>` or renderer; `bytes_b64` present only when `inline=true` (default true, since an agent needs pixels in context and an MCP client cannot follow a URL); `inline=false` returns reference only (used by the console to avoid moving megabytes through JSON twice) (Spec §7.2.5)\n- [Tool] `fetch`'s `include` controls parts returned; dropping `\"image\"` makes `fetch` a cheap text/summary read (Spec §7.2.5)\n- [Tool] `read` renders at pinned dpi 220 — caller cannot change it because dpi is part of `read_key` (§4.2, §6.3) (Spec §7.2.6)\n- [Tool] `ReadResult` fields: `extract`, `codes` (list of `{raw, status}` with `present_instead` when absent), `sufficient`, `flags`, `page_provenance` (list of `{page_id, text_trust}`) (Spec §7.2.6)\n- [Tool] Transcription correction is inside `read`, automatic and always (Loop 1): every emitted code is phrase-checked against page text and stamped with the same three states `verify` uses — one vocabulary, one meaning; a page with no text layer makes every code `unverifiable` (Spec §7.2.6, §7.2.4)\n- [Tool] `sufficient` is mandatory — without it the agent can't separate \"the answer is no\" from \"wrong page,\" and might compose an answer from a page that never contained one (Spec §7.2.6)\n- [Tool] Retrieval judgment never happens inside `read` — that would make the engine the answerer (Spec §7.2.6)\n- [Cap] `read` page images per call: ≤3 → `read_page_cap_exceeded` (Spec §7.3)\n- [Cap] `fetch` pages per call: ≤5 and ≤12 MP total → `fetch_budget_exceeded {limit, requested}` (Spec §7.3)\n- [Cap] `dpi` ∈ {36, 72, 150, 220, 300, 400} (36/72 = triage thumbnail tiers behind `thumb_url`, 150 = `fetch` default, 220 = `read`) → `dpi_not_allowed` (Spec §7.3)\n- [Cap] `dpi > 220` requires `region` → `dpi_requires_region` (Spec §7.3)\n- [Cap] unknown scope key → `filter_unknown_key {keys}` (Spec §7.3)\n- [Cap] per-caller `read` quota, server-side, surfaced as `reads_remaining` in every envelope → `429 budget_exhausted` (Spec §7.3)\n- [Cap] All caps are typed 400s, never a clamp, never a silent truncation (F18) (Spec §7.3)\n- [Route] `POST /tools/{tool_name}` — the eight tools of §7.2, one envelope each — bearer (Spec §7.4)\n- [Route] `POST /ask` — the runner; the only surface that may return prose (§8.4) — bearer (Spec §7.4)\n- [Route] `GET /pages/{page_id}/image?dpi=&region=` — the page raster, rendered on demand, browser-renderable half of `fetch`, same caps/typed 400s as §7.3, ported from `impl`'s `/api/v1/page-image/{page_id}` — bearer (Spec §7.4)\n- [Route] `GET /runs/{run_id}` — the run record of §6.9 — bearer (Spec §7.4)\n- [Route] `GET /runs/{run_id}/export/{labels,observed_tokens}.jsonl` — streamed exports of §6.8 — bearer (Spec §7.4)\n- [Route] `GET /health` — liveness, process up; MUST NOT fail on a backing-service outage (§15.1) — none (Spec §7.4)\n- [Route] `GET /ready` — readiness: boot self-check passed, Qdrant reachable, pinned index schema present — none (Spec §7.4)\n- [Route] `GET /metrics` — Prometheus (§11.4) — none (internal network) (Spec §7.4)\n- [Auth] Bearer token required on every tool call; `401` without one; identity is propagated, never client-supplied (Spec §7.4)\n- [Audit] One append-only audit line per `read` and `fetch`: `(user_id, run_id, session_id, tool, page_ids, dpi, input_tokens, output_tokens, cache_hit, latency_ms)` (Spec §7.4)\n- [Audit] Cost goes in the audit log, not the response body — agent gets one integer, `reads_remaining`; a `usd_estimate` beside verification stamps would be noise next to must-not-miss fields (Spec §7.4)\n- [MCP] `vision-segmentation-retriever` exposes the same eight tools over stdio + SSE, calling identical implementations — no second code path (Spec §7.5)\n- [MCP] MCP server is stateless: `scope` and `exclude` are parameters; `effective_scope` is echoed back (Spec §7.5)\n- [Refusal] Returning a similarity score — enforcement: conformance grep for no field named `score` in any response model; ordinal `rank`/`best_rank` permitted and required (§7.2.1) since a position is not a confidence (Spec §7.6)\n- [Refusal] Routing the query — enforcement: no tool picks the document for the caller (Spec §7.6)\n- [Refusal] Composing the answer — enforcement: only the runner composes, and only behind the answer gate (§8.4) (Spec §7.6)\n- [Refusal] Fuzzy matching on codes — enforcement: conformance grep for no edit-distance/similarity library in `requirements.txt`, no `MatchText` in `serve/`, plus an I3 property test (Spec §7.6)\n\nInvariants / Failure Rows Touched:\n- I5 — the two-envelope-family design is attributed directly to I5 (§7.1 section title)\n- I8 — `verify` must check per `(claim, page)`, not per claim, so a citation spanning pages can't leak a neighbouring page's code (§7.2.4)\n- I2, I3 — an image query can find a candidate page but can never confirm a code; `lookup`/`verify` accept text labels only (§7.2.1 rule 3)\n- F8 — `effective_scope` is echoed back in every Family A response because the service is stateless (§7.1)\n- F18 — all caps in §7.3 are typed 400s by design, never clamps or silent truncation (§7.3 section title)\n\nDependencies Identified:\n- Ordering/aggregation ported from `impl/app/retrieve.py::rrf` (D2), ranks-only (§7.2.1)\n- Image-query embedding ported from `impl`'s `embed_query_image(image, text=query)` (D4, D12) (§7.2.1)\n- `GET /pages/{page_id}/image` ported from `impl`'s `/api/v1/page-image/{page_id}` (§7.4)\n- MCP server calls the identical tool implementations as the HTTP surface — no second code path (§7.5)\n- `read`'s pinned dpi 220 is tied into `read_key` (§4.2, §6.3)\n- In-process raster caching across turns depends on §4.2\n- `next.suggest` behavior ties to §12.3's phrasing-accident handling\n- `why`/`rank` fusion output feeds §8.2's auto-promote-exact-hits and why-as-signal logic\n- `POST /ask` prose output depends on the answer gate defined in §8.4\n- `fetch`'s `url` field is what M7's viewer renders\n- `effective_scope` echo-back depends on statelessness invariant referenced as F8/C11\n- Run/export routes (`GET /runs/{run_id}`, exports) depend on §6.8 and §6.9 definitions\n\nTechnical Constraints:\n- RRF: `rrf_k = 60`, weights `page 1.0 · lexical 1.0 · captions 0.4`; only ranks enter the arithmetic\n- `WEAK_ABS = 20` server constant; `weak = needs_scope = total > max(WEAK_ABS, 0.25 * scope_stats.pages)` — independent of caller-passed `cap`\n- `dpi` enum {36, 72, 150, 220, 300, 400}; `dpi > 220` requires `region`\n- `read`: ≤3 page images/call, pinned dpi 220 (uneditable)\n- `fetch`: ≤5 pages/call, ≤12 MP total, default dpi 150, `inline` default true\n- `lookup`: default `cap=20`; `present_instead` prefix-match capped at 5\n- `skim_pages`: `limit=10`, max 25; `skim_sections`/`skim_documents`: ≤10 rows\n- No field named `score` permitted anywhere in response models (conformance grep)\n- No edit-distance/similarity library in `requirements.txt`; no `MatchText` in `serve/` (conformance grep + I3 property test)\n\nSpec References:\n- Spec §7.1, §7.2 (intro), §7.2.1, §7.2.2, §7.2.3, §7.2.4, §7.2.5, §7.2.6, §7.3, §7.4, §7.5, §7.6\n- Cross-references touched within region: I2, I3, I5, I8, F8, F18, C11, P2, P4, D2, D4, D5, D12, §4.2, §6.3, §6.8, §6.9, §8.2, §8.4, §11.4, §12.3, §15.1\n\nContradictions Noticed (report only, do not resolve):\n- `fetch`'s free/paid status is unlabeled — §7.2.1–§7.2.4 headers each explicitly say \"(free)\" and §7.2.6 explicitly calls `read` \"the paid step,\" but §7.2.5's `fetch` header carries no such annotation, even though §7.4's audit-line requirement groups `fetch` with `read` (\"one append-only audit line per `read` and `fetch`\") and §7.3's quota is named specifically a \"read quota\" (not a fetch quota) — unclear whether `fetch` is free, paid, or partially metered.\n- `why` branch-label enum vs. actual fused branches — §7.2.1 states `why ∈ {\"dense\", \"lexical\"}` and every worked example of `why` (`[\"dense\"]`, `[\"lexical\"]`, `[\"dense\",\"lexical\"]`) uses only two labels, but the ordering rules describe three fused branches (`page`/dense, `lexical`, and `captions`, weighted 0.4) — it's unstated whether a `captions`-only or `captions`-contributing hit is ever surfaced as `\"captions\"` in `why`, or silently folded into `\"dense\"`.\n- \"`cap`\" terminology vs. actual parameter names — §7.1's general discussion of Family A behavior (\"`cap` controls how many hits come back... `lookup(\"3\")` unscoped matches most of the corpus, so it is `weak` at any `cap`\") speaks of `cap` as if it were common across Family A, and ties the `capped` envelope field to it (\"`cap` bounds the returned page of the set and sets `capped`\"), but only `lookup`'s actual signature has a `cap` parameter (§7.2.2) — `skim_pages` instead has a `limit` parameter (§7.2.1), and `skim_documents`/`skim_sections`/`resolve` have no bounding parameter named at all. It's unclear whether `capped`/`weak` on skim/resolve responses are driven by `limit` or some other implicit value."},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: ac48122ec21c0694b (use SendMessage with to: 'ac48122ec21c0694b', summary: '<5-10 word recap>' to continue this agent)\n<usage>subagent_tokens: 46226\ntool_uses: 1\nduration_ms: 167721</usage>"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4eefb16f-3989-4441-9cd3-d294cfccb11f","uuid":"e8e766e4-175d-4650-b27c-bc0f49c5e5e5","timestamp":"2026-09-09T16:47:02.212Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"You are Extraction Agent 5 for a PLAN-ONLY implementation-planning task. Read ONLY this region of the spec:\n\n`sed -n '720,1031p' /Users/sabesonk/Documents/DILMAH/dilmah-engineering-solutioning/poc/vision_segmentation_index_and_retrieval/development/cr1/spec/spec.md`\n\n(That covers §7.1 the two response envelope families + the six-value status enum + hit models + ImageRef rules, §7.2.1–7.2.6 the eight tools, §7.3 caps and typed errors, §7.4 the HTTP surface + auth + audit, §7.5 the MCP server, §7.6 the four refusals.)\n\nDo NOT read any other file. Do NOT quote spec text — use pointers only.\n\nYour focus: every tool signature, every envelope field, every hit model's fields, the ordering/aggregation rules, the image-query rules, the caps table with each typed error code, the HTTP route table with auth, the audit line fields, and the four enforced refusals.\n\nOutput EXACTLY this format, structured lists only:\n\n### Agent 5: Tool Surface\n\nFocus:\n- <one line>\n\nRequirements Extracted:\n- [Category] Requirement description (Spec §X.Y)\n(Categories: EnvelopeA, EnvelopeB, Status, HitModel, Tool, Ordering, ImageQuery, Cap, Route, Auth, Audit, MCP, Refusal)\n(Emit one [Tool] line per tool: exact signature, free/paid, envelope family, and the milestone the spec attaches it to if stated.)\n(Emit one [HitModel] line per hit model naming every field.)\n(Emit one [Cap] line per row of the §7.3 table: bound, value, error code.)\n(Emit one [Route] line per row of the §7.4 table: method+path, purpose, auth.)\n(Emit one [Refusal] line per §7.6 row with its enforcement mechanism.)\n(Emit one [Status] line per each of the six status values with the agent action it implies.)\n\nInvariants / Failure Rows Touched:\n- I<n>, F<n> — <one line each>\n\nDependencies Identified:\n- <…>\n\nTechnical Constraints:\n- <…>\n\nSpec References:\n- Spec §<pointers>\n\nContradictions Noticed (report only, do not resolve):\n- <item> — <the two places that disagree>\n","agentId":"ac48122ec21c0694b","agentType":"general-purpose","harnessNoteCount":0,"harnessTailCount":0,"harnessSectionHash":"5f0202828d569c23","content":[{"type":"text","text":"### Agent 5: Tool Surface\n\nFocus:\n- §7.1–7.6 of the spec: the two response envelope families, six-value status enum, hit models, ImageRef rules, the eight tools (§7.2.1–7.2.6), caps/typed errors, HTTP surface/auth/audit, MCP server, and the four enforced refusals.\n\nRequirements Extracted:\n\n- [EnvelopeA] Family A (`skim_documents`, `skim_sections`, `skim_pages`, `lookup`, `resolve`) uses `SearchResponse[HitT]` with fields: `status`, `hits`, `unverified_hits`, `total`, `capped`, `weak`, `needs_scope`, `next`, `effective_scope`, `scope_stats`, `reads_remaining`, `provenance` (Spec §7.1)\n- [EnvelopeA] Validator `empty_is_never_ok`: asserts `hits` or `unverified_hits` non-empty, or `status != \"ok\"` — an empty result can never claim `ok` (Spec §7.1)\n- [EnvelopeA] `total` is `count(exact=True)` — the SET size, not `len(hits)` (Spec §7.1)\n- [EnvelopeA] `unverified_hits` is `vlm_codes`-only, `verified=False`, and is never merged into `hits` (Spec §7.1)\n- [EnvelopeB] Family B (`fetch`, `read`, `verify`) uses `ToolEnvelope[ResultT]` with fields: `status` (`ok`|`error`, describes whether the call ran, not what it found), `result`, `reads_remaining`, `provenance` (Spec §7.1)\n- [EnvelopeB] A `verify` where every claim is `absent` is still `status: ok` with three `absent` verdicts; a missing `page_id` is `404 page_not_found`; a backend failure is a 5xx — a failed call must never look like an empty successful call (Spec §7.1)\n- [Status] `ok` — hits/result present; agent proceeds normally (not itemized in the spec's action table, which only tabulates the five non-`ok` values) (Spec §7.1)\n- [Status] `not_found` (searched, genuinely absent) — agent action: abstain, but check `next.suggest` first (Spec §7.1)\n- [Status] `not_searchable` (candidate pages have no text layer) — agent action: escalate to vision (`fetch`/`read`) (Spec §7.1)\n- [Status] `out_of_scope` (no document matched filters) — agent action: re-orient, widen scope (Spec §7.1)\n- [Status] `found_only_in_superseded` — agent action: surface the revision and let the caller decide (Spec §7.1)\n- [Status] `error` — agent action: retry or report, never abstain (Spec §7.1)\n- [Status] `next.suggest` softens a `not_found`: e.g. `lookup(\"alarm 152\")` returns `status: not_found` with `next.suggest: [\"skim_pages\"]` plus tokens that did occur, so status stays honest while the affordance prevents abstention on a phrasing accident (Spec §7.1, §12.3)\n- [Status] `weak`/`needs_scope` are caller-independent: `WEAK_ABS = 20` (server constant), `weak = needs_scope = total > max(WEAK_ABS, 0.25 * scope_stats.pages)`; `cap` only bounds returned hits, never affects `weak` (Spec §7.1)\n- [HitModel] `ImageRef` = `{url, thumb_url, dpi, width, height}` — a reference, never bytes (Spec §7.1)\n- [HitModel] `Preview` = `{page_id, thumb_url}` — the group's best-ranked page (Spec §7.1)\n- [HitModel] `DocHit` = `{doc_id, title, doc_type, pages_matched, best_rank, searchable_ratio, summary, preview}` (Spec §7.1)\n- [HitModel] `SectionHit` = `{section_id, title, page_range, pages_matched, best_rank, preview}` (Spec §7.1)\n- [HitModel] `PageHit` = `{page_id, printed_page_no, summary, summary_lang, page_kind, why, rank, flags, grounded_rate, text_trust, image, next}` (Spec §7.1)\n- [HitModel] `LookupHit` = `{page_id, page_no, printed_page_no, page_kind, verified, text_trust, image, next}` (Spec §7.1)\n- [HitModel] `ResolveHit` = `{page_id, printed_page_no, label_verified, interpolated, image}` (Spec §7.1)\n- [ImageQuery] Every search result carries an `ImageRef`; no search result carries image bytes — the sharpened form of P2 (Spec §7.1)\n- [ImageQuery] `skim_pages`, `lookup`, `resolve` hand back `page_id` + ready-made `ImageRef`; caller never constructs a URL; URL is lazy so nothing renders until dereferenced (Spec §7.1)\n- [ImageQuery] `DocHit`/`SectionHit` carry no `page_id` (answer \"which binder/chapter\") but carry `preview` = `thumb_url` of the group's best-ranked matched page, falling back to page 1 when nothing matched (useful for `searchable_ratio: 0.00` binders) (Spec §7.1)\n- [ImageQuery] Image *bytes* in a triage row are refused — would let the agent answer from the search result instead of choosing then paying (the failure P2 prevents), at 1–2k tokens/row (Spec §7.1)\n- [HitModel] `verified` on `LookupHit` is a boolean about the surface (`text`=true, `vlm_codes`=false), distinct from the three-state `present|absent|unverifiable` vocabulary used by per-claim checks (Spec §7.1, §7.2.4, §7.2.6)\n- [Tool] `skim_documents(query, image=None, scope?, exclude?) → [DocHit]` — free — Family A — no milestone stated (Spec §7.2.1)\n- [Tool] `skim_sections(query, image=None, scope, exclude?) → [SectionHit]` — free — Family A — no milestone stated (Spec §7.2.1)\n- [Tool] `skim_pages(query, image=None, scope, exclude?, limit=10) → [PageHit]` — free — Family A — no milestone stated (Spec §7.2.1)\n- [Tool] `lookup(label, scope?, include_unverified=False, cap=20)` — free — Family A — no milestone stated (Spec §7.2.2)\n- [Tool] `resolve(printed_label, doc_id?)` — free — Family A — no milestone stated (Spec §7.2.3)\n- [Tool] `verify(claims, page_ids)` — free — Family B — no milestone stated (Spec §7.2.4)\n- [Tool] `fetch(page_ids, include=[\"image\",\"text\",\"summary\"], dpi=150, region=None, inline=True)` — free/paid label NOT stated in the tool header (unlike all other tools) — Family B — milestone: `url` field is \"what M7's viewer displays\" (Spec §7.2.5)\n- [Tool] `read(page_ids, question)` — explicitly **\"the paid step\"** — Family B — renders at pinned dpi 220, no milestone stated (Spec §7.2.6)\n- [Ordering] `query` optional when `image` given and vice versa; one implementation exposed as three tool names so the agent chooses between names, not a `granularity` enum (Spec §7.2.1)\n- [Ordering] `why ∈ {\"dense\", \"lexical\"}`; `lexical` = text-index phrase/token hit (no sparse vector, D2) (Spec §7.2.1)\n- [Ordering] Triage-row `summary` is in caller's requested `lang`, falling back to page's dominant language (D5); row states which language it returned (Spec §7.2.1)\n- [Ordering] No full text in a triage row (P2) (Spec §7.2.1)\n- [Ordering] `next: {expand: section_id, neighbours: [page_id,…], references: [printed labels]}` turns retrieval into navigation (P4) (Spec §7.2.1)\n- [Ordering] Three branches run inside `scope` minus `exclude`: `page` (dense), `lexical` (sparse over extracted text), `captions` (sparse over generated text); `decompose(query)` splits exact identifiers to `lookup`/phrase filter before embedding (Spec §7.2.1)\n- [Ordering] Branches fused client-side via reciprocal rank fusion at `rrf_k=60`, weights `page 1.0 · lexical 1.0 · captions 0.4`; only ranks enter the arithmetic — no score computed, stored, or returned (Spec §7.2.1, §7.6)\n- [Ordering] `rank` = 1-based ordinal of fused list; `why` names every contributing branch (e.g. `[\"dense\"]`, `[\"lexical\"]`, `[\"dense\",\"lexical\"]`), enabling §8.2's auto-promote-exact-hits and use-`why`-as-signal (Spec §7.2.1, §8.2)\n- [Ordering] `skim_pages` returns ≤10 rows (`limit`, max 25); `skim_sections`/`skim_documents` group same fused candidates: `pages_matched`=group size, `best_rank`=best page rank in group, rows ordered by `(best_rank, -pages_matched)`, ≤10 rows (Spec §7.2.1)\n- [Ordering] Fusion is deterministic given the same branches — identical `(query, image, scope, exclude)` yields identical order, required for E2E/L2 assertion stability (Spec §7.2.1)\n- [ImageQuery] Query vector for an image comes from `embed_query_image(image, text=query)`, fusing photo+words in one `types.Content` so both land in the same vector space as indexed page vectors (D4) (Spec §7.2.1, D12)\n- [ImageQuery] Rule 1: no instruction prefix when the query is multimodal — prefix applies only to a bare text query (impl's constraint, from Google's guidance) (Spec §7.2.1)\n- [ImageQuery] Rule 2: an image-only query runs the dense branch alone; `lexical`/`captions` (sparse, text-built) are skipped; RRF degenerates to dense ranking; every row's `why` = `[\"dense\"]`, stated not silent (Spec §7.2.1, §8.2)\n- [ImageQuery] Rule 3: an image can never reach the exact surface — `lookup` and `verify` take a text label only (I2, I3); a photo may find a candidate page but never confirm a code (Spec §7.2.1)\n- [Tool] `lookup` is exact, phrase-only, a set not a ranking; `total` = `count(exact=True)`, then `scroll` to `cap`; `cap` bounds the returned page of the set and sets `capped`, never affects `weak` (Spec §7.2.2, §7.1)\n- [Tool] `lookup(include_unverified=True)` repeats the query against `vlm_codes`, returning results in `unverified_hits` with `verified: false`; scores and lists are never merged (Spec §7.2.2)\n- [Tool] `lookup` on candidate pages with no text layer returns `not_searchable`, never a bare empty set (Spec §7.2.2)\n- [Tool] `resolve(printed_label, doc_id?) → page_id + interpolated + label_verified`; ambiguity returns every candidate (Spec §7.2.3)\n- [Tool] `verify(claims, page_ids)` checks per `(claim, page)`, not per claim — prevents a draft citing `p001–p002` from letting a code from the neighbouring page through (I8) (Spec §7.2.4)\n- [Tool] `VerifyResult` is a map of claim → verdict inside the Family B envelope; three states: `present`, `absent` (with `present_instead`), `unverifiable` (with `reason`) (Spec §7.2.4)\n- [Tool] Collapsing `unverifiable` into `absent` would falsely tell the agent \"not on the page\" about a page it couldn't examine (Spec §7.2.4)\n- [Tool] `present_instead` = prefix lookup over observed tokens, capped at 5, labelled \"different part\" — never a distance or nearest-match (Spec §7.2.4)\n- [Tool] `fetch` returns material, not an answer; `region` is normalised `[x0,y0,x1,y1]`; PyMuPDF renders the clip on demand with no new storage; rendered rasters cached in-process across turns (§4.2) (Spec §7.2.5)\n- [Tool] `fetch` result `url` is always present — a bearer-authenticated GET usable directly by a browser `<img>` or renderer; `bytes_b64` present only when `inline=true` (default true, since an agent needs pixels in context and an MCP client cannot follow a URL); `inline=false` returns reference only (used by the console to avoid moving megabytes through JSON twice) (Spec §7.2.5)\n- [Tool] `fetch`'s `include` controls parts returned; dropping `\"image\"` makes `fetch` a cheap text/summary read (Spec §7.2.5)\n- [Tool] `read` renders at pinned dpi 220 — caller cannot change it because dpi is part of `read_key` (§4.2, §6.3) (Spec §7.2.6)\n- [Tool] `ReadResult` fields: `extract`, `codes` (list of `{raw, status}` with `present_instead` when absent), `sufficient`, `flags`, `page_provenance` (list of `{page_id, text_trust}`) (Spec §7.2.6)\n- [Tool] Transcription correction is inside `read`, automatic and always (Loop 1): every emitted code is phrase-checked against page text and stamped with the same three states `verify` uses — one vocabulary, one meaning; a page with no text layer makes every code `unverifiable` (Spec §7.2.6, §7.2.4)\n- [Tool] `sufficient` is mandatory — without it the agent can't separate \"the answer is no\" from \"wrong page,\" and might compose an answer from a page that never contained one (Spec §7.2.6)\n- [Tool] Retrieval judgment never happens inside `read` — that would make the engine the answerer (Spec §7.2.6)\n- [Cap] `read` page images per call: ≤3 → `read_page_cap_exceeded` (Spec §7.3)\n- [Cap] `fetch` pages per call: ≤5 and ≤12 MP total → `fetch_budget_exceeded {limit, requested}` (Spec §7.3)\n- [Cap] `dpi` ∈ {36, 72, 150, 220, 300, 400} (36/72 = triage thumbnail tiers behind `thumb_url`, 150 = `fetch` default, 220 = `read`) → `dpi_not_allowed` (Spec §7.3)\n- [Cap] `dpi > 220` requires `region` → `dpi_requires_region` (Spec §7.3)\n- [Cap] unknown scope key → `filter_unknown_key {keys}` (Spec §7.3)\n- [Cap] per-caller `read` quota, server-side, surfaced as `reads_remaining` in every envelope → `429 budget_exhausted` (Spec §7.3)\n- [Cap] All caps are typed 400s, never a clamp, never a silent truncation (F18) (Spec §7.3)\n- [Route] `POST /tools/{tool_name}` — the eight tools of §7.2, one envelope each — bearer (Spec §7.4)\n- [Route] `POST /ask` — the runner; the only surface that may return prose (§8.4) — bearer (Spec §7.4)\n- [Route] `GET /pages/{page_id}/image?dpi=&region=` — the page raster, rendered on demand, browser-renderable half of `fetch`, same caps/typed 400s as §7.3, ported from `impl`'s `/api/v1/page-image/{page_id}` — bearer (Spec §7.4)\n- [Route] `GET /runs/{run_id}` — the run record of §6.9 — bearer (Spec §7.4)\n- [Route] `GET /runs/{run_id}/export/{labels,observed_tokens}.jsonl` — streamed exports of §6.8 — bearer (Spec §7.4)\n- [Route] `GET /health` — liveness, process up; MUST NOT fail on a backing-service outage (§15.1) — none (Spec §7.4)\n- [Route] `GET /ready` — readiness: boot self-check passed, Qdrant reachable, pinned index schema present — none (Spec §7.4)\n- [Route] `GET /metrics` — Prometheus (§11.4) — none (internal network) (Spec §7.4)\n- [Auth] Bearer token required on every tool call; `401` without one; identity is propagated, never client-supplied (Spec §7.4)\n- [Audit] One append-only audit line per `read` and `fetch`: `(user_id, run_id, session_id, tool, page_ids, dpi, input_tokens, output_tokens, cache_hit, latency_ms)` (Spec §7.4)\n- [Audit] Cost goes in the audit log, not the response body — agent gets one integer, `reads_remaining`; a `usd_estimate` beside verification stamps would be noise next to must-not-miss fields (Spec §7.4)\n- [MCP] `vision-segmentation-retriever` exposes the same eight tools over stdio + SSE, calling identical implementations — no second code path (Spec §7.5)\n- [MCP] MCP server is stateless: `scope` and `exclude` are parameters; `effective_scope` is echoed back (Spec §7.5)\n- [Refusal] Returning a similarity score — enforcement: conformance grep for no field named `score` in any response model; ordinal `rank`/`best_rank` permitted and required (§7.2.1) since a position is not a confidence (Spec §7.6)\n- [Refusal] Routing the query — enforcement: no tool picks the document for the caller (Spec §7.6)\n- [Refusal] Composing the answer — enforcement: only the runner composes, and only behind the answer gate (§8.4) (Spec §7.6)\n- [Refusal] Fuzzy matching on codes — enforcement: conformance grep for no edit-distance/similarity library in `requirements.txt`, no `MatchText` in `serve/`, plus an I3 property test (Spec §7.6)\n\nInvariants / Failure Rows Touched:\n- I5 — the two-envelope-family design is attributed directly to I5 (§7.1 section title)\n- I8 — `verify` must check per `(claim, page)`, not per claim, so a citation spanning pages can't leak a neighbouring page's code (§7.2.4)\n- I2, I3 — an image query can find a candidate page but can never confirm a code; `lookup`/`verify` accept text labels only (§7.2.1 rule 3)\n- F8 — `effective_scope` is echoed back in every Family A response because the service is stateless (§7.1)\n- F18 — all caps in §7.3 are typed 400s by design, never clamps or silent truncation (§7.3 section title)\n\nDependencies Identified:\n- Ordering/aggregation ported from `impl/app/retrieve.py::rrf` (D2), ranks-only (§7.2.1)\n- Image-query embedding ported from `impl`'s `embed_query_image(image, text=query)` (D4, D12) (§7.2.1)\n- `GET /pages/{page_id}/image` ported from `impl`'s `/api/v1/page-image/{page_id}` (§7.4)\n- MCP server calls the identical tool implementations as the HTTP surface — no second code path (§7.5)\n- `read`'s pinned dpi 220 is tied into `read_key` (§4.2, §6.3)\n- In-process raster caching across turns depends on §4.2\n- `next.suggest` behavior ties to §12.3's phrasing-accident handling\n- `why`/`rank` fusion output feeds §8.2's auto-promote-exact-hits and why-as-signal logic\n- `POST /ask` prose output depends on the answer gate defined in §8.4\n- `fetch`'s `url` field is what M7's viewer renders\n- `effective_scope` echo-back depends on statelessness invariant referenced as F8/C11\n- Run/export routes (`GET /runs/{run_id}`, exports) depend on §6.8 and §6.9 definitions\n\nTechnical Constraints:\n- RRF: `rrf_k = 60`, weights `page 1.0 · lexical 1.0 · captions 0.4`; only ranks enter the arithmetic\n- `WEAK_ABS = 20` server constant; `weak = needs_scope = total > max(WEAK_ABS, 0.25 * scope_stats.pages)` — independent of caller-passed `cap`\n- `dpi` enum {36, 72, 150, 220, 300, 400}; `dpi > 220` requires `region`\n- `read`: ≤3 page images/call, pinned dpi 220 (uneditable)\n- `fetch`: ≤5 pages/call, ≤12 MP total, default dpi 150, `inline` default true\n- `lookup`: default `cap=20`; `present_instead` prefix-match capped at 5\n- `skim_pages`: `limit=10`, max 25; `skim_sections`/`skim_documents`: ≤10 rows\n- No field named `score` permitted anywhere in response models (conformance grep)\n- No edit-distance/similarity library in `requirements.txt`; no `MatchText` in `serve/` (conformance grep + I3 property test)\n\nSpec References:\n- Spec §7.1, §7.2 (intro), §7.2.1, §7.2.2, §7.2.3, §7.2.4, §7.2.5, §7.2.6, §7.3, §7.4, §7.5, §7.6\n- Cross-references touched within region: I2, I3, I5, I8, F8, F18, C11, P2, P4, D2, D4, D5, D12, §4.2, §6.3, §6.8, §6.9, §8.2, §8.4, §11.4, §12.3, §15.1\n\nContradictions Noticed (report only, do not resolve):\n- `fetch`'s free/paid status is unlabeled — §7.2.1–§7.2.4 headers each explicitly say \"(free)\" and §7.2.6 explicitly calls `read` \"the paid step,\" but §7.2.5's `fetch` header carries no such annotation, even though §7.4's audit-line requirement groups `fetch` with `read` (\"one append-only audit line per `read` and `fetch`\") and §7.3's quota is named specifically a \"read quota\" (not a fetch quota) — unclear whether `fetch` is free, paid, or partially metered.\n- `why` branch-label enum vs. actual fused branches — §7.2.1 states `why ∈ {\"dense\", \"lexical\"}` and every worked example of `why` (`[\"dense\"]`, `[\"lexical\"]`, `[\"dense\",\"lexical\"]`) uses only two labels, but the ordering rules describe three fused branches (`page`/dense, `lexical`, and `captions`, weighted 0.4) — it's unstated whether a `captions`-only or `captions`-contributing hit is ever surfaced as `\"captions\"` in `why`, or silently folded into `\"dense\"`.\n- \"`cap`\" terminology vs. actual parameter names — §7.1's general discussion of Family A behavior (\"`cap` controls how many hits come back... `lookup(\"3\")` unscoped matches most of the corpus, so it is `weak` at any `cap`\") speaks of `cap` as if it were common across Family A, and ties the `capped` envelope field to it (\"`cap` bounds the returned page of the set and sets `capped`\"), but only `lookup`'s actual signature has a `cap` parameter (§7.2.2) — `skim_pages` instead has a `limit` parameter (§7.2.1), and `skim_documents`/`skim_sections`/`resolve` have no bounding parameter named at all. It's unclear whether `capped`/`weak` on skim/resolve responses are driven by `limit` or some other implicit value."}],"resolvedModel":"claude-sonnet-5","totalDurationMs":167721,"totalTokens":46226,"totalToolUseCount":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8385,"cache_read_input_tokens":18811,"output_tokens":19028,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":10740},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":8385},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":19028,"cache_read_input_tokens":18811,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8385,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":8385,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"toolStats":{"readCount":0,"searchCount":0,"bashCount":1,"editFileCount":0,"linesAdded":0,"linesRemoved":0,"otherToolCount":0}}}
