{"type":"system","subtype":"task_notification","task_id":"a4cf917ad5577bf41","tool_use_id":"toolu_01GiCUet7yFxooAE2czdaAQK","status":"completed","output_file":"/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-sabesonk-Documents-DILMAH-dilmah-engineering-solutioning-poc-vision-segmentation-index-and-retrieval/4eefb16f-3989-4441-9cd3-d294cfccb11f/tasks/a4cf917ad5577bf41.output","summary":"### Agent 8: Tests, Milestones, Acceptance Criteria\n\nFocus:\n- The test pyramid (fixtures → L0–L5/E2E → conformance greps → corpus eval) as plannable work, paired with the M0–M8 milestone ladder and the sixteen top-level acceptance criteria that gate it.\n\nRequirements Extracted:\n\n- [Fixture] `impl/data/raw/<doc_id>/<sha256>.json` — content-addressable S2 responses (old schema) for 7 docs (`TC1E-SF` 2 windows/64KB, `LTC1AV81` 12 windows, `CE-TC1AV8`, `DS-2611-SICK`, `DS-5549-EATON`, `TC1E-PERIODIC`, `TC1AV8M2-LIFTING`) — good immediately for real-data L1 derivation, offset proof (I4/F7), stitching, at zero spend — exists now (already paid, ported from `impl`); missing new-schema fields (`summaries`, `topics`, `codes`, `sections`) until M2b's re-bill (Spec §12.1)\n- [Fixture] `impl/data/exports/r-poc-*/labels.jsonl` — the `lookup` parity baseline (every identifier the old `entity_keys` gate accepted must still be findable by phrase) — exists now, ported from `impl`, used from M2b onward (Spec §12.1, §12.3)\n- [Fixture] `impl/data/exports/r-poc-*/withheld.jsonl` — the negative set: model-emitted codes the text layer never backed, must be unfindable except via `include_unverified` (I2, F14) — exists now, ported from `impl` (Spec §12.1, §12.3)\n- [Fixture] `data/fixtures/synthetic_3window/` — generated, checked in, no PDF corpus, no spend — exists from M2a; used by all fixture-consuming levels until M2b lands (Spec §12.1)\n- [Fixture] `data/fixtures/TC1E-SF/raw_window_1.json` — verbatim `WindowOut`, pages 1–30 — generated by freezing a real M2b ingest, exists from M2b (Spec §12.1)\n- [Fixture] `data/fixtures/TC1E-SF/raw_window_2.json` — pages 31–55 — generated/frozen at M2b (Spec §12.1)\n- [Fixture] `data/fixtures/TC1E-SF/text.json` — PyMuPDF text per page, pinned extractor — generated/frozen at M2b (Spec §12.1)\n- [Fixture] `data/fixtures/TC1E-SF/expected.json` — the §12.3 acceptance table — generated/frozen at M2b (Spec §12.1)\n- [Level] L0 — pure functions: `tok`, `variants`, offset, label normalisation, stitching; needs nothing; runtime < 1s; script `scripts/test-unit.sh` (Spec §12.2)\n- [Level] L1 — derivation over frozen `raw_window_*.json` (synthetic fixture pre-M2b, `TC1E-SF`'s 55 pages post-M2b); needs fixture; runtime < 5s; script `scripts/test-unit.sh` (Spec §12.2)\n- [Level] L2 — index contract: the §12.3 acceptance table against an ephemeral Qdrant; needs docker; runtime < 30s; script `scripts/test-api.sh` (Spec §12.2)\n- [Level] L3 — adversarial abstention, the safety test; needs docker; runtime < 60s; script `scripts/test-api.sh` (Spec §12.2)\n- [Level] L4 — worked trace + failure branch, end to end; needs docker + Gemini; runtime minutes; script `scripts/test-paid.sh` (requires `VSIR_ALLOW_PAID=1`) — the only level permitted to spend (Spec §12.2)\n- [Level] L5 — canary on a held-out document nobody tuned against; needs full stack; runtime manual; script `vsir eval corpus` (Spec §12.2)\n- [Level] E2E — console drives the loop against fixture-backed data; needs docker; runtime minutes; script `scripts/test-e2e.sh` (Spec §12.2)\n- [AbstentionEval] `test_near_miss_codes_never_answer` — `near_misses(n=100)` mutates one char of codes from the observed-token inventory of whichever corpus is indexed (§6.8: synthetic seed at M1, real fixture after M2b); asserts `r.hits == []`, `r.status in (\"not_found\",\"not_searchable\")`, and no `present_instead` value equals the fake; runs in CI on every commit from M1 on (Spec §12.4)\n- [AcceptanceTable] `lookup(\"SF 1.1A\")` → exactly 1 page (any-order matching would give 3) (Spec §12.3)\n- [AcceptanceTable] `lookup(\"SF 5.5b\")` → exactly 1 page (any-order would give 2) (Spec §12.3)\n- [AcceptanceTable] `lookup(\"SF 121.1\")` → 1 page (the compact-label variant) (Spec §12.3)\n- [AcceptanceTable] `lookup(\"EAO 84-5140.0020\")` → total 10 (hits capped at cap, capped:true) (Spec §12.3)\n- [AcceptanceTable] `lookup(\"B&R X20SI4100\")` → total 54 (capped:true at cap=20) (Spec §12.3)\n- [AcceptanceTable] `lookup(\"3\")` unscoped → weak:true, needs_scope:true (at ANY cap — §7.1) (Spec §12.3)\n- [AcceptanceTable] `lookup(\"alarm 152\")` → not_found + next.suggest:[\"skim_pages\"]; never a wrong page, never a bare empty 200 (Spec §12.3)\n- [AcceptanceTable] `verify(\"SF 1.1A\", [p008])` → absent (tokens present, phrase not) (Spec §12.3)\n- [AcceptanceTable] scanned document → not_searchable, never not_found (Spec §12.3)\n- [AcceptanceTable] PARITY (against `impl/data/exports/r-poc-*/labels.jsonl`): every identifier the old `entity_keys` gate accepted → still findable by phrase (Spec §12.3)\n- [AcceptanceTable] PARITY: every raw in `withheld.jsonl` → NOT findable in `text` (only via `include_unverified`) (Spec §12.3)\n- [Grep] Scope: `backend/vsir/**` and `requirements*.txt` only — never markdown, never the conformance test itself (must exclude its own file) (Spec §12.5)\n- [Grep] `MatchText` or `MatchTextAny` under `serve/` — banned; scope as above (Spec §12.5)\n- [Grep] any fuzzy / similarity / edit-distance library in `requirements*.txt` — banned (Spec §12.5)\n- [Grep] any field named `score` in a response model — banned (Spec §12.5)\n- [Grep] a model id ending `-latest` — banned (Spec §12.5)\n- [Grep] `alembic` or `sqlalchemy` anywhere — banned (Spec §12.5)\n- [Grep] `get_text(` outside `ingest/probe.py` — banned; probe is the only module allowed to derive text, pipeline may only carry it unmodified (paired with the I2 L1 assertion `record.text == probe_text[page_no]` for every fixture page, since grepping `\"text\"` in `ingest/index.py` would be a false positive) (Spec §12.5)\n- [Grep] struck legacy names `SCHEMA_CARD`, `IdClass`, `entity_keys`, `classify(` — banned (C1) (Spec §12.5)\n- [Grep] Cloud-native set (§15), same scope plus `Dockerfile*` and `docker-compose*.yml`: no `logging.FileHandler` — banned (Spec §12.5)\n- [Grep] Cloud-native set: no container image tagged `latest` — banned (Spec §12.5)\n- [Grep] Cloud-native set: no credential literal (`api_key=`, `token=`, `Bearer ` followed by a string literal) — banned (Spec §12.5)\n- [Grep] Cloud-native set: no test-only branch (`if TESTING`, `if os.environ.get(\"TESTING\")`) inside `backend/vsir/**` — banned (Spec §12.5)\n- [Grep] Cloud-native set: no `RetrievalState`-style module-level mutable session store (C11) — banned (Spec §12.5)\n- [CorpusEval] Component register (E pp. 59–125) | ground truth: 2,053 rows · 748 tags · 484 codes | metric `code_precision` (a code `lookup` returns is the printed code) | gate = 1.00, any miss is P0 stop (Spec §12.6)\n- [CorpusEval] Component register (same set) | ground truth: same | metric `code_recall` (printed codes findable by `lookup`) | gate ≥ 0.95; block below 0.90 (Spec §12.6)\n- [CorpusEval] Near-miss sample (§12.4) | ground truth: 100 mutated codes | metric `abstention_correctness` | gate = 1.00 (Spec §12.6)\n- [CorpusEval] Alarm catalogue | ground truth: numbers 0–539, ~494 records | metric `alarm_label_hit` (each number lands its record's page) | gate ≥ 0.99 (Spec §12.6)\n- [CorpusEval] Cross-references | ground truth: 6,880 tokens, 99.97% resolvable | metric `xref_resolve` (`resolve` returns the right page) | gate ≥ 0.99 (Spec §12.6)\n- [Milestone] `M0 | depends-on: nothing | spend: none | demo: vsir doctor && bash scripts/test-unit.sh | deliverable: repo skeleton (backend/vsir/, cli.py→vsir doctor, §4.1 dirs, modules created only by implementing milestone), pinned requirements.txt+lock, docker-compose.test.yml Postgres→Qdrant rewrite, scripts/test-*.sh extended (test-paid.sh added), AGENTS.md filled, vsir doctor per §4.3, §12.5 conformance greps as a test, twelve-factor runtime skeleton §15 (Dockerfile non-root/digest-pinned/read-only rootfs+tmpfs, .env.example, GET /health+/ready, structured JSON logs, SIGTERM handler, release_id stamping) | acceptance: doctor refuses -latest model id and missing payload index naming reason; conformance greps (incl. cloud-native set) pass; /health green while Qdrant stopped, /ready red; doctor prints release_id/model ids/index fingerprint; D1–D7 restated in README` (Spec §13)\n- [Milestone] `M1 | depends-on: M0 (ports sparse.py + rrf() from impl §2.4, D2) | spend: none | demo: vsir demo exact --synthetic | deliverable: record, both envelope families (§7.1), INDEXED, tok, variants, exact_filter, core/verify.py::verify_claims, §12.4 near-miss generator, collection+index creation, lookup against ephemeral Qdrant seeded with 3 hand-written synthetic pages (SF 1.1A; scattered tokens sf/1/1a; SF121.1)) plus a K999-claiming page with no backing text, observed-token inventory §6.8 | acceptance: F1, F2(core), F3, F10, F14, F16 closed; I2, I3, I5, I6 asserted; §7.3 cap validators reject over-budget args as typed 400s; L3 abstention eval runs here on synthetic near-misses; L0+L2+L3 green` (Spec §13)\n- [Milestone] `M2a | depends-on: M1 | spend: none | demo: vsir ingest data/source/synthetic_3window.pdf --vlm stub && vsir runs show <run_id> | deliverable: steps 01–12 wired end to end incl. vsir_runs control collection + §6.7 retirement rule, generated 3-window PDF in data/source/ with off-by-one and crop traps, stub VLM, run record, publish gating | acceptance: I1, I4, I7 hold; F6, F7, F12, F13, F15, F17 closed + F8's stitching half; killed mid-run leaves 0 queryable pages + state:stopped; re-run twice yields same point count; text-free doc publishes and answers only not_searchable (A1/§11.1)` (Spec §13)\n- [Milestone] `M2b | depends-on: M2a (OQ-1/OQ-2 only for the re-bill) | spend: S2+embed, once | demo: VSIR_ALLOW_PAID=1 vsir ingest data/source/TC1E-SF.pdf && vsir runs show <run_id> | deliverable: port impl/data/raw/* → data/fixtures/ as old-schema baseline + labels.jsonl/withheld.jsonl as parity/negative sets; one real ingest of TC1E-SF (55 pages) under new S2 schema only; data/fixtures/TC1E-SF/* frozen; grounded_rate distribution reported, gate threshold set | acceptance: 55 points published; window_coverage==1.0; offset_check all pass; parity check against impl's labels.jsonl passes and every withheld.jsonl raw unfindable (§12.3); acceptance table reconciled against C10, discrepancies recorded` (Spec §13)\n- [Milestone] `M3 | depends-on: M2a (real-corpus half of acceptance additionally needs M2b) | spend: none | demo: vsir serve & then vsir lookup \"SF 1.1A\" && vsir verify --claims K73 --pages … , same two tools via MCP client | deliverable: six-value status enum with all four absences, next.suggest, present_instead, unverifiable, bearer auth, audit log, reads_remaining, MCP server exposing both tools, vsir eval acceptance/abstention | acceptance-always: acceptance table + L3 eval pass on synthetic corpus; 401 without token; not_found carries next.suggest; text-free page → not_searchable (F4) | acceptance-once-M2b: same table passes on real text reconciled per C10, F16 demonstrated on real near-miss pair` (Spec §13)\n- [Milestone] `M4 | depends-on: M3 | spend: none | demo: vsir demo narrow | deliverable: triage rows with ImageRef on every page-level hit (§7.1), deterministic ordering §7.2.1, exclude, next affordances, region/dpi budgets incl. 36/72 thumbnail tiers, GET /pages/{page_id}/image, in-process raster cache, image queries (D12), resolve with interpolated | acceptance: F5 closed; every page-level hit has dereferenceable image.url, every aggregate row a preview.thumb_url, no triage row contains bytes_b64 (asserted test); image-only skim_pages rows have why exactly [\"dense\"]; F8's stateless half (effective_scope echoed, no server session); F18 for fetch (fetch_budget_exceeded naming bound; dpi=400 without region is typed