erifiable badge renders, rejected code absent from rendered answer, abstention text names unread image-only pages; assertions fixture-independent, pass on synthetic too` (Spec §13)\n- [Milestone] `M8 | depends-on: M6 (and M2b for real-corpus numbers) | spend: ingest | demo: vsir ingest --resume <run_id> after a deliberate kill, then vsir eval corpus | deliverable: is_current lifecycle, found_only_in_superseded, series_id across revisions, resumable/--resume ingest with per-window checkpoints, graceful-shutdown checkpointing (§15 Factor IX), §12.6 corpus evaluation report | acceptance: F9 closed + F12's revision half (1.4 retires 1.3 to is_current=false without deleting; lookup satisfied only by 1.3 returns found_only_in_superseded); F8's series_id half; SIGTERM mid-window loses ≤1 window, publishes nothing partial; ≥700-window generated large PDF (not the excluded 1,440-page Level-2 manual, §6.2) survives kill at window 700 and resumes without re-billing; Level-2 document attempt fails typed ladder_level_2_required; report states code exactness and abstention correctness per set` (Spec §13)\n- [AC] AC-001: Model-claimed-but-textless code is unfindable via lookup, appears only in unverified_hits when opted in. (I2, F14) (Spec §14)\n- [AC] AC-002: Exact matching is phrase-only; no label variant differs by more than whitespace. (I3, F1, F3) (Spec §14)\n- [AC] AC-003: Six-value status enum (ok + four distinct absences + error); no Family A tool returns empty ok. (I5, F4, §7.1) (Spec §14)\n- [AC] AC-004: A scanned document answers not_searchable, never not_found. (F4) (Spec §14)\n- [AC] AC-005: verify distinguishes present/absent/unverifiable per (claim,page); near-misses offered only as labelled different parts. (F2, F16, I8) (Spec §14)\n- [AC] AC-006: Every page number proved by two independent checks; offset failure bisects and re-bills instead of publishing. (I4, F7) (Spec §14)\n- [AC] AC-007: A run that hasn't passed its gates has zero queryable pages. (I7, F17) (Spec §14)\n- [AC] AC-008: Every §7.3 cap is a typed 400 naming its bound; no silent clamp exists. (F18) (Spec §14)\n- [AC] AC-009: Worked-trace answer costs exactly one paid read with citations; ceiling is VSIR_READS_PER_QUESTION. (§8.4, no I/F cited) (Spec §14)\n- [AC] AC-010: Failure branch abstains with coverage numbers, never claims absence while unread image-only pages remain. (§8.5, no I/F cited) (Spec §14)\n- [AC] AC-011: L3 abstention eval passes on 100 near-miss codes, in CI, on every commit. (no I/F cited) (Spec §14)\n- [AC] AC-012: Boot self-check refuses to serve on schema drift, fingerprint mismatch, or a -latest model id. (§4.3, F11) (Spec §14)\n- [AC] AC-013: labels.jsonl delivers per-page codes_in_text, page_range, sections[], summaries[], safety_flag to Part A. (D1, C8) (Spec §14)\n- [AC] AC-014: Every milestone's demo command in §0 runs green on a clean checkout. (no I/F cited) (Spec §14)\n- [AC] AC-015: One image runs every process type; deployment-varying values from environment; no correctness-bearing state in process/local disk. (§15 Factors III,V,VI,VIII,XII; C11) (Spec §14)\n- [AC] AC-016: SIGTERM at any instant leaves no queryable half-document; --resume completes the run; /health and /ready behave per §15.1 during a Qdrant outage. (no I/F cited) (Spec §14)\n\nInvariants / Failure Rows Touched:\n- I1 — ingest publish gating holds, claimed at M2a (\"I1, I4, I7 hold\"); no further elaboration in this region\n- I2 — model-claimed-but-textless codes unfindable via lookup; explicitly enforced by an L1 test (not a `\"text\"` grep) per §12.5, asserted at M1 (AC-001)\n- I3 — exact/phrase-matching invariant, asserted at M1 (AC-002)\n- I4 — page-number offset proof via two independent checks, holds at M2a, closed with F7 (AC-006)\n- I5 — six-value status enum / no empty `ok` for Family A, asserted at M1 (AC-003)\n- I6 — asserted at M1; no further detail given in this region\n- I7 — an ungated run has zero queryable pages, holds at M2a (AC-007)\n- I8 — a