 The §12.4 near-miss generator depends on the observed-token inventory (§6.8) of whatever corpus is currently indexed\n- M1 ports `sparse.py` and `rrf()` from `impl` (§2.4, D2)\n\nTechnical Constraints:\n- L0–L3 and E2E must never call Gemini; they run in replay mode (D10): `VSIR_VLM=stub` + `VSIR_FIXTURE=<dir>`, with a fixture miss surfaced as a typed `fixture_miss`\n- L4 is the only level permitted to spend, and only under `VSIR_ALLOW_PAID=1`\n- No level ever requires a new paid call until M2b lands (D10, OQ-1)\n- Conformance greps (§12.5) scope to `backend/vsir/**` + `requirements*.txt` only (cloud-native set also covers `Dockerfile*`/`docker-compose*.yml`), excluding markdown and the conformance test's own file\n- Corpus-eval precision must be exactly 1.00 (a safety property, any miss is P0); recall is a measured target (§12.6)\n- Corpus-eval numbers are re-baselined exactly once, from the M2b measurement, with a recorded rationale (C10)\n- Modules are created only by the milestone that implements them, never as empty placeholders (M0)\n\nSpec References:\n- Spec §12.1, §12.2, §12.3, §12.4, §12.5, §12.6, §13 (M0–M8), §14 (AC-001–AC-016)\n- Cross-referenced (not read): §2.4, D2, §4.1, §4.3, §6.2, §6.7, §6.8, §7.1, §7.2.1, §7.3, §8, §8.4, §8.5, §11.1, §15, §15.1, A1, C1, C8, C10, C11, D1, D10, D11, D12, OQ-1, OQ-2\n\nContradictions Noticed (report only, do not resolve):\n- F8 is described as having three separate \"halves\" — \"stitching half\" (M2a), \"stateless half\" (M4), \"series_id half\" (M8) — which is numerically inconsistent with the word \"half\" (implies two parts, not three).\n- F12 is listed as fully \"closed\" at M2a (in the group \"F6, F7, F12, F13, F15, F17 closed\") yet M8's acceptance separately delivers \"F12's revision half\" (`found_only_in_superseded`), suggesting F12 was not actually complete at M2a despite being labelled closed there.\n- The §12.3 acceptance table shows `lookup(\"EAO 84-5140.0020\") → total 10 (hits capped at cap, capped:t