E must never call Gemini; they run in replay mode (D10): `VSIR_VLM=stub` + `VSIR_FIXTURE=<dir>`, with a fixture miss surfaced as a typed `fixture_miss`\n- L4 is the only level permitted to spend, and only under `VSIR_ALLOW_PAID=1`\n- No level ever requires a new paid call until M2b lands (D10, OQ-1)\n- Conformance greps (§12.5) scope to `backend/vsir/**` + `requirements*.txt` only (cloud-native set also covers `Dockerfile*`/`docker-compose*.yml`), excluding markdown and the conformance test's own file\n- Corpus-eval precision must be exactly 1.00 (a safety property, any miss is P0); recall is a measured target (§12.6)\n- Corpus-eval numbers are re-baselined exactly once, from the M2b measurement, with a recorded rationale (C10)\n- Modules are created only by the milestone that implements them, never as empty placeholders (M0)\n\nSpec References:\n- Spec §12.1, §12.2, §12.3, §12.4, §12.5, §12.6, §13 (M0–M8), §14 (AC-001–AC-016)\n- Cross-referenced (not read): §2.4, D2, §4.1, §4.3, §6.2, §6.7, §6.8, §7.1, §7.2.1, §7.3, §8, §8.4, §8.5, §11.1, §15, §15.1, A1, C1, C8, C10, C11, D1, D10, D11, D12, OQ-1, OQ-2\n\nContradictions Noticed (report only, do not resolve):\n- F8 is described as having three separate \"halves\" — \"stitching half\" (M2a), \"stateless half\" (M4), \"series_id half\" (M8) — which is numerically inconsistent with the word \"half\" (implies two parts, not three).\n- F12 is listed as fully \"closed\" at M2a (in the group \"F6, F7, F12, F13, F15, F17 closed\") yet M8's acceptance separately delivers \"F12's revision half\" (`found_only_in_superseded`), suggesting F12 was not actually complete at M2a despite being labelled closed there.\n- The §12.3 acceptance table shows `lookup(\"EAO 84-5140.0020\") → total 10 (hits capped at cap, capped:true)` alongside `lookup(\"B&R X20SI4100\") → total 54 (capped:true at cap=20)` — the two lines use \"total\" inconsistently (one apparently post-cap, the other explicitly pre-cap with an overridden cap value) without this region defining what \"total\" means, so the two examples cannot be reconciled from this text alone."},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: a4cf917ad5577bf41 (use SendMessage with to: 'a4cf917ad5577bf41', summary: '<5-10 word recap>' to continue this agent)\n<usage>subagent_tokens: 54193\ntool_uses: 1\nduration_ms: 219009</usage>"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4eefb16f-3989-4441-9cd3-d294cfccb11f","uuid":"1103c4c1-663c-469f-b234-ea6f4bff0c3e","timestamp":"2026-09-09T16:48:22.484Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"You are Extraction Agent 8 for a PLAN-ONLY implementation-planning task. Read ONLY this region of the spec:\n\n`sed -n '1230,1556p' /Users/sabesonk/Documents/DILMAH/dilmah-engineering-solutioning/poc/vision_segmentation_index_and_retrieval/development/cr1/spec/spec.md`\n\n(That covers §12.1 fixtures, §12.2 the L0–L5/E2E level table, §12.3 the L2 acceptance table, §12.4 the L3 adversarial abstention eval, §12.5 the conformance greps, §12.6 corpus evaluation, §13 milestones M0–M8, §14 acceptance criteria AC-001…AC-016.)\n\nDo NOT read any other file. Do NOT quote spec text — use pointers only, except that you MUST transcribe the §12.3 acceptance-table assertions and the §12.5 grep target strings literally, because they are executable.\n\nYour focus: the test pyramid as plannable work, the fixture inventory and which fixture exists when, the milestone table (deliverable / demo command / depends-on / acceptance bullets, per milestone), and the sixteen top-level acceptance criteria.\n\nOutput EXACTLY this format, structured lists only:\n\n### Agent 8: Tests, Milestones, Acceptance Criteria\n\nFocus:\n- <one line>\n\nRequirements Extracted:\n- [Category] Requirement description (Spec §X.Y)\n(Categories: Fixture, Level, AcceptanceTable, AbstentionEval, Grep, CorpusEval, Milestone, AC)\n(Emit one [Fixture] line per fixture artefact: path, what it is good for, when it exists, whether it is ported from `impl` or generated.)\n(Emit one [Level] line per L0/L1/L2/L3/L4/L5/E2E: what it tests, what it needs, runtime budget, script.)\n(Emit one [AcceptanceTable] line per assertion in §12.3, transcribed exactly, including the parity rows.)\n(Emit one [Grep] line per banned string / pattern in §12.5, including the cloud-native set, with its scope and its exclusions.)\n(Emit one [Milestone] line per M0…M8 in this shape: `M<x> | depends-on: <…> | spend: <…> | demo: <exact command> | deliverable: <compact list> | acceptance: <compact list of the acceptance bullets, preserving which I/F ids each milestone claims>`)\n(Emit one [AC] line per AC-001…AC-016: the assertion in ≤20 words plus the I/F ids it cites.)\n(Emit one [CorpusEval] line per §12.6 row: set, ground truth, metric, gate number.)\n\nInvariants / Failure Rows Touched:\n- I<n>, F<n> — <one line each, only those this region names>\n\nDependencies Identified:\n- <…>\n\nTechnical Constraints:\n- <…>\n\nSpec References:\n- Spec §<pointers>\n\nContradictions Noticed (report only, do not resolve):\n- <item> — <the two places that disagree>\n","agentId":"a4cf917ad5577bf41","agentType":"general-purpose","harnessNoteCount":0,"harnessTailCount":0,"harnessSectionHash":"6a4fd4c0abde0bf1","content":[{"type":"text","text":"### Agent 8: Tests, Milestones, Acceptance Criteria\n\nFocus:\n- The test pyramid (fixtures → L0–L5/E2E → conformance greps → corpus eval) as plannable work, paired with the M0–M8 milestone ladder and the sixteen top-level acceptance criteria that gate it.\n\nRequirements Extracted:\n\n- [Fixture] `impl/data/raw/<doc_id>/<sha256>.json` — content-addressable S2 responses (old schema) for 7 docs (`TC1E-SF` 2 windows/64KB, `LTC1AV81` 12 windows, `CE-TC1AV8`, `DS-2611-SICK`, `DS-5549-EATON`, `TC1E-PERIODIC`, `TC1AV8M2-LIFTING`) — good immediately for real-data L1 derivation, offset proof (I4/F7), stitching, at zero spend — exists now (already paid, ported from `impl`); missing new-schema fields (`summaries`, `topics`, `codes`, `sections`) until M2b's re-bill (Spec §12.1)\n- [Fixture] `impl/data/exports/r-poc-*/labels.jsonl` — the `lookup` parity baseline (every identifier the old `entity_keys` gate accepted must still be findable by phrase) — exists now, ported from `impl`, used from M2b onward (Spec §12.1, §12.3)\n- [Fixture] `impl/data/exports/r-poc-*/withheld.jsonl` — the negative set: model-emitted codes the text layer never backed, must be unfindable except via `include_unverified` (I2, F14) — exists now, ported from `impl` (Spec §12.1, §12.3)\n- [Fixture] `data/fixtures/synthetic_3window/` — generated, checked in, no PDF corpus, no spend — exists from M2a; used by all fixture-consuming levels until M2b lands (Spec §12.1)\n- [Fixture] `data/fixtures/TC1E-SF/raw_window_1.json` — verbatim `WindowOut`, pages 1–30 — generated by freezing a real M2b ingest, exists from M2b (Spec §12.1)\n- [Fixture] `data/fixtures/TC1E-SF/raw_window_2.json` — pages 31–55 — generated/frozen at M2b (Spec §12.1)\n- [Fixture] `data/fixtures/TC1E-SF/text.json` — PyMuPDF text per page, pinned extractor — generated/frozen at M2b (Spec §12.1)\n- [Fixture] `data/fixtures/TC1E-SF/expected.json` — the §12.3 acceptance table — generated/frozen at M2b (Spec §12.1)\n- [Level] L0 — pure functions: `tok`, `variants`, offset, label normalisation, stitching; needs nothing; runtime < 1s; script `scripts/test-unit.sh` (Spec §12.2)\n- [Level] L1 — derivation over frozen `raw_window_*.json` (synthetic fixture pre-M2b, `TC1E-SF`'s 55 pages post-M2b); needs fixture; runtime < 5s; script `scripts/test-unit.sh` (Spec §12.2)\n- [Level] L2 — index contract: the §12.3 acceptance table against an ephemeral Qdrant; needs docker; runtime < 30s; script `scripts/test-api.sh` (Spec §12.2)\n- [Level] L3 — adversarial abstention, the safety test; needs docker; runtime < 60s; script `scripts/test-api.sh` (Spec §12.2)\n- [Level] L4 — worked trace + failure branch, end to end; needs docker + Gemini; runtime minutes; script `scripts/test-paid.sh` (requires `VSIR_ALLOW_PAID=1`) — the only level permitted to spend (Spec §12.2)\n- [Level] L5 — canary on a held-out document nobody tuned against; needs full stack; runtime manual; script `vsir eval corpus` (Spec §12.2)\n- [Level] E2E — console drives the loop against fixture-backed data; needs docker; runtime minutes; script `scripts/test-e2e.sh` (Spec §12.2)\n- [AbstentionEval] `test_near_miss_codes_never_answer` — `near_misses(n=100)` mutates one char of codes from the observed-token inventory of whichever corpus is indexed (§6.8: synthetic seed at M1, real fixture after M2b); asserts `r.hits == []`, `r.status in (\"not_found\",\"not_searchable\")`, and no `present_instead` value equals the fake; runs in CI on every commit from M1 on (Spec §12.4)\n- [AcceptanceTable] `lookup(\"SF 1.1A\")` → exactly 1 page (any-order matching would give 3) (Spec §12.3)\n- [AcceptanceTable] `lookup(\"SF 5.5b\")` → exactly 1 page (any-order would give 2) (Spec §12.3)\n- [AcceptanceTable] `lookup(\"SF 121.1\")` → 1 page (the compact-label variant) (Spec §12.3)\n- [AcceptanceTable] `lookup(\"EAO 84-5140.0020\")` → total 10 (hits capped at cap, capped:true) (Spec §12.3)\n- [AcceptanceTable] `lookup(\"B&R X20SI4100\")` → total 54 (capped:true at cap=20) (Spec §12.3)\n- [AcceptanceTable] `lookup(\"3\")` unscoped → weak:true, needs_scope:true (at ANY cap — §7.1) (Spec §12.3)\n- [AcceptanceTable] `lookup(\"alarm 152\")` → not_found + next.suggest:[\"skim_pages\"]; never a wrong page, never a bare empty 200 (Spec §12.3)\n- [AcceptanceTable] `verify(\"SF 1.1A\", [p008])` → absent (tokens present, phrase not) (Spec §12.3)\n- [AcceptanceTable] scanned document → not_searchable, never not_found (Spec §12.3)\n- [AcceptanceTable] PARITY (against `impl/data/exports/r-poc-*/labels.jsonl`): every identifier the old `entity_keys` gate accepted → still findable by phrase (Spec §12.3)\n- [AcceptanceTable] PARITY: every raw in `withheld.jsonl` → NOT findable in `text` (only via `include_unverified`) (Spec §12.3)\n- [Grep] Scope: `backend/vsir/**` and `requirements*.txt` only — never markdown, never the conformance test itself (must exclude its own file) (Spec §12.5)\n- [Grep] `MatchText` or `MatchTextAny` under `serve/` — banned; scope as above (Spec §12.5)\n- [Grep] any fuzzy / similarity / edit-distance library in `requirements*.txt` — banned (Spec §12.5)\n- [Grep] any field named `score` in a response model — banned (Spec §12.5)\n- [Grep] a model id ending `-latest` — banned (Spec §12.5)\n- [Grep] `alembic` or `sqlalchemy` anywhere — banned (Spec §12.5)\n- [Grep] `get_text(` outside `ingest/probe.py` — banned; probe is the only module allowed to derive text, pipeline may only carry it unmodified (paired with the I2 L1 assertion `record.text == probe_text[page_no]` for every fixture page, since grepping `\"text\"` in `ingest/index.py` would be a false positive) (Spec §12.5)\n- [Grep] struck legacy names `SCHEMA_CARD`, `IdClass`, `entity_keys`, `classify(` — banned (C1) (Spec §12.5)\n- [Grep] Cloud-native set (§15), same scope plus `Dockerfile*` and `docker-compose*.yml`: no `logging.FileHandler` — banned (Spec §12.5)\n- [Grep] Cloud-native set: no container image tagged `latest` — banned (Spec §12.5)\n- [Grep] Cloud-native set: no credential literal (`api_key=`, `token=`, `Bearer ` followed by a string literal) — banned (Spec §12.5)\n- [Grep] Cloud-native set: no test-only branch (`if TESTING`, `if os.environ.get(\"TESTING\")`) inside `backend/vsir/**` — banned (Spec §12.5)\n- [Grep] Cloud-native set: no `RetrievalState`-style module-level mutable session store (C11) — banned (Spec §12.5)\n- [CorpusEval] Component register (E pp. 59–125) | ground truth: 2,053 rows · 748 tags · 484 codes | metric `code_precision` (a code `lookup` returns is the printed code) | gate = 1.00, any miss is P0 stop (Spec §12.6)\n- [CorpusEval] Component register (same set) | ground truth: same | metric `code_recall` (printed codes findable by `lookup`) | gate ≥ 0.95; block below 0.90 (Spec §12.6)\n- [CorpusEval] Near-miss sample (§12.4) | ground truth: 100 mutated codes | metric `abstention_correctness` | gate = 1.00 (Spec §12.6)\n- [CorpusEval] Alarm catalogue | ground truth: numbers 0–539, ~494 records | metric `alarm_label_hit` (each number lands its record's page) | gate ≥ 0.99 (Spec §12.6)\n- [CorpusEval] Cross-references | ground truth: 6,880 tokens, 99.97% resolvable | metric `xref_resolve` (`resolve` returns the right page) | gate ≥ 0.99 (Spec §12.6)\n- [Milestone] `M0 | depends-on: nothing | spend: none | demo: vsir doctor && bash scripts/test-unit.sh | deliverable: repo skeleton (backend/vsir/, cli.py→vsir doctor, §4.1 dirs, modules created only by implementing milestone), pinned requirements.txt+lock, docker-compose.test.yml Postgres→Qdrant rewrite, scripts/test-*.sh extended (test-paid.sh added), AGENTS.md filled, vsir doctor per §4.3, §12.5 conformance greps as a test, twelve-factor runtime skeleton §15 (Dockerfile non-root/digest-pinned/read-only rootfs+tmpfs, .env.example, GET /health+/ready, structured JSON logs, SIGTERM handler, release_id stamping) | acceptance: doctor refuses -latest model id and missing payload index naming reason; conformance greps (incl. cloud-native set) pass; /health green while Qdrant stopped, /ready red; doctor prints release_id/model ids/index fingerprint; D1–D7 restated in README` (Spec §13)\n- [Milestone] `M1 | depends-on: M0 (ports sparse.py + rrf() from impl §2.4, D2) | spend: none | demo: vsir demo exact --synthetic | deliverable: record, both envelope families (§7.1), INDEXED, tok, variants, exact_filter, core/verify.py::verify_claims, §12.4 near-miss generator, collection+index creation, lookup against ephemeral Qdrant seeded with 3 hand-written synthetic pages (SF 1.1A; scattered tokens sf/1/1a; SF121.1)) plus a K999-claiming page with no backing text, observed-token inventory §6.8 | acceptance: F1, F2(core), F3, F10, F14, F16 closed; I2, I3, I5, I6 asserted; §7.3 cap validators reject over-budget args as typed 400s; L3 abstention eval runs here on synthetic near-misses; L0+L2+L3 green` (Spec §13)\n- [Milestone] `M2a | depends-on: M1 | spend: none | demo: vsir ingest data/source/synthetic_3window.pdf --vlm stub && vsir runs show <run_id> | deliverable: steps 01–12 wired end to end incl. vsir_runs control collection + §6.7 retirement rule, generated 3-window PDF in data/source/ with off-by-one and crop traps, stub VLM, run record, publish gating | acceptance: I1, I4, I7 hold; F6, F7, F12, F13, F15, F17 closed + F8's stitching half; killed mid-run leaves 0 queryable pages + state:stopped; re-run twice yields same point count; text-free doc publishes and answers only not_searchable (A1/§11.1)` (Spec §13)\n- [Milestone] `M2b | depends-on: M2a (OQ-1/OQ-2 only for the re-bill) | spend: S2+embed, once | demo: VSIR_ALLOW_PAID=1 vsir ingest data/source/TC1E-SF.pdf && vsir runs show <run_id> | deliverable: port impl/data/raw/* → data/fixtures/ as old-schema baseline + labels.jsonl/withheld.jsonl as parity/negative sets; one real ingest of TC1E-SF (55 pages) under new S2 schema only; data/fixtures/TC1E-SF/* frozen; grounded_rate distribution reported, gate threshold set | acceptance: 55 points published; window_coverage==1.0; offset_check all pass; parity check against impl's labels.jsonl passes and every withheld.jsonl raw unfindable (§12.3); acceptance table reconciled against C10, discrepancies recorded` (Spec §13)\n- [Milestone] `M3 | depends-on: M2a (real-corpus half of acceptance additionally needs M2b) | spend: none | demo: vsir serve & then vsir lookup \"SF 1.1A\" && vsir verify --claims K73 --pages … , same two tools via MCP client | deliverable: six-value status enum with all four absences, next.suggest, present_instead, unverifiable, bearer auth, audit log, reads_remaining, MCP server exposing both tools, vsir eval acceptance/abstention | acceptance-always: acceptance table + L3 eval pass on synthetic corpus; 401 without token; not_found carries next.suggest; text-free page → not_searchable (F4) | acceptance-once-M2b: same table passes on real text reconciled per C10, F16 demonstrated on real near-miss pair` (Spec §13)\n- [Milestone] `M4 | depends-on: M3 | spend: none | demo: vsir demo narrow | deliverable: triage rows with ImageRef on every page-level hit (§7.1), deterministic ordering §7.2.1, exclude, next affordances, region/dpi budgets incl. 36/72 thumbnail tiers, GET /pages/{page_id}/image, in-process raster cache, image queries (D12), resolve with interpolated | acceptance: F5 closed; every page-level hit has dereferenceable image.url, every aggregate row a preview.thumb_url, no triage row contains bytes_b64 (asserted test); image-only skim_pages rows have why exactly [\"dense\"]; F8's stateless half (effective_scope echoed, no server session); F18 for fetch (fetch_budget_exceeded naming bound; dpi=400 without region is typed 400); read's F18 share → M5, series_id → M8, not claimed here` (Spec §13)\n- [Milestone] `M5 | depends-on: M4 (paid assertions additionally need M2b/OQ-2) | spend: read | demo: VSIR_ALLOW_PAID=1 vsir read --pages TC1E-SF@1.3#p001,…#p002 --question \"…\" | deliverable: skim_documents/skim_sections with searchable_ratio, read with per-code verified stamps, sufficient, page_provenance, ≤3-page cap, question-keyed cache | acceptance: Loop 1 stamps a deliberately misread code status:absent with present_instead; F19 verified (same pages+new question=cache miss); F18 for read (4-page call typed 400); every code on a text-free page returns unverifiable` (Spec §13)\n- [Milestone] `M6 | depends-on: M5 | spend: read | demo: VSIR_ALLOW_PAID=1 vsir ask \"the carton discharge won't restart after an E-stop reset\" | deliverable: runner/ implementing §8 (tri-state triage with exclude, six correction loops, system prompt, server-side answer gate, constrained abstention wording), POST /ask, vsir ask | acceptance: worked-trace fixture answer costs exactly one paid read, cites p001–p002, VSIR_READS_PER_QUESTION (default 3) as hard ceiling generally; failure branch abstains with coverage numbers and never says \"not in these documents\" while unread image-only pages remain; draft with unverified code rejected, not rendered (I8)` (Spec §13)\n- [Milestone] `M7 | depends-on: M6 | spend: none (fixture-backed) | demo: bash scripts/test-e2e.sh then browse http://localhost:5174 | deliverable: React+TS+Vite console, replay mode (D10, no Gemini/key/spend) against TC1E-SF (if OQ-1 answered) or synthetic_3window; consumes image.url/preview.thumb_url directly (inline=false, no extra endpoint); left: zoom-ladder breadcrumbs, high-res viewer, region zoom; right: collapsible agent moves, tri-state triage panel, draft answer with trust badges (verified/read from image/unverifiable) + amber warnings; click-to-scroll citations | acceptance: Playwright test drives worked trace in replay mode, asserts unverifiable badge renders, rejected code absent from rendered answer, abstention text names unread image-only pages; assertions fixture-independent, pass on synthetic too` (Spec §13)\n- [Milestone] `M8 | depends-on: M6 (and M2b for real-corpus numbers) | spend: ingest | demo: vsir ingest --resume <run_id> after a deliberate kill, then vsir eval corpus | deliverable: is_current lifecycle, found_only_in_superseded, series_id across revisions, resumable/--resume ingest with per-window checkpoints, graceful-shutdown checkpointing (§15 Factor IX), §12.6 corpus evaluation report | acceptance: F9 closed + F12's revision half (1.4 retires 1.3 to is_current=false without deleting; lookup satisfied only by 1.3 returns found_only_in_superseded); F8's series_id half; SIGTERM mid-window loses ≤1 window, publishes nothing partial; ≥700-window generated large PDF (not the excluded 1,440-page Level-2 manual, §6.2) survives kill at window 700 and resumes without re-billing; Level-2 document attempt fails typed ladder_level_2_required; report states code exactness and abstention correctness per set` (Spec §13)\n- [AC] AC-001: Model-claimed-but-textless code is unfindable via lookup, appears only in unverified_hits when opted in. (I2, F14) (Spec §14)\n- [AC] AC-002: Exact matching is phrase-only; no label variant differs by more than whitespace. (I3, F1, F3) (Spec §14)\n- [AC] AC-003: Six-value status enum (ok + four distinct absences + error); no Family A tool returns empty ok. (I5, F4, §7.1) (Spec §14)\n- [AC] AC-004: A scanned document answers not_searchable, never not_found. (F4) (Spec §14)\n- [AC] AC-005: verify distinguishes present/absent/unverifiable per (claim,page); near-misses offered only as labelled different parts. (F2, F16, I8) (Spec §14)\n- [AC] AC-006: Every page number proved by two independent checks; offset failure bisects and re-bills instead of publishing. (I4, F7) (Spec §14)\n- [AC] AC-007: A run that hasn't passed its gates has zero queryable pages. (I7, F17) (Spec §14)\n- [AC] AC-008: Every §7.3 cap is a typed 400 naming its bound; no silent clamp exists. (F18) (Spec §14)\n- [AC] AC-009: Worked-trace answer costs exactly one paid read with citations; ceiling is VSIR_READS_PER_QUESTION. (§8.4, no I/F cited) (Spec §14)\n- [AC] AC-010: Failure branch abstains with coverage numbers, never claims absence while unread image-only pages remain. (§8.5, no I/F cited) (Spec §14)\n- [AC] AC-011: L3 abstention eval passes on 100 near-miss codes, in CI, on every commit. (no I/F cited) (Spec §14)\n- [AC] AC-012: Boot self-check refuses to serve on schema drift, fingerprint mismatch, or a -latest model id. (§4.3, F11) (Spec §14)\n- [AC] AC-013: labels.jsonl delivers per-page codes_in_text, page_range, sections[], summaries[], safety_flag to Part A. (D1, C8) (Spec §14)\n- [AC] AC-014: Every milestone's demo command in §0 runs green on a clean checkout. (no I/F cited) (Spec §14)\n- [AC] AC-015: One image runs every process type; deployment-varying values from environment; no correctness-bearing state in process/local disk. (§15 Factors III,V,VI,VIII,XII; C11) (Spec §14)\n- [AC] AC-016: SIGTERM at any instant leaves no queryable half-document; --resume completes the run; /health and /ready behave per §15.1 during a Qdrant outage. (no I/F cited) (Spec §14)\n\nInvariants / Failure Rows Touched:\n- I1 — ingest publish gating holds, claimed at M2a (\"I1, I4, I7 hold\"); no further elaboration in this region\n- I2 — model-claimed-but-textless codes unfindable via lookup; explicitly enforced by an L1 test (not a `\"text\"` grep) per §12.5, asserted at M1 (AC-001)\n- I3 — exact/phrase-matching invariant, asserted at M1 (AC-002)\n- I4 — page-number offset proof via two independent checks, holds at M2a, closed with F7 (AC-006)\n- I5 — six-value status enum / no empty `ok` for Family A, asserted at M1 (AC-003)\n- I6 — asserted at M1; no further detail given in this region\n- I7 — an ungated run has zero queryable pages, holds at M2a (AC-007)\n- I8 — a draft containing an unverified code is rejected, not rendered, at M6 (AC-005)\n- F1 — exact/phrase match, closed at M1 core level (AC-002)\n- F2 — verify's present/absent distinction, closed at M1 core level (AC-005)\n- F3 — label-variant whitespace-only rule, closed at M1 (AC-002)\n- F4 — not_searchable for scanned/text-free documents, asserted at M3 (AC-004)\n- F5 — closed at M4 (triage/image affordances)\n- F6 — closed at M2a (ingest pipeline)\n- F7 — offset-check bisect-and-rebill, closed at M2a (AC-006)\n- F8 — split across three \"halves\": stitching (M2a), stateless/effective_scope (M4), series_id (M8)\n- F9 — closed at M8 (resumable ingest)\n- F10 — closed at M1\n- F11 — `-latest` model id refusal at boot self-check (AC-012)\n- F12 — closed at M2a; a further \"revision half\" (found_only_in_superseded) delivered at M8\n- F13 — closed at M2a\n- F14 — unverified_hits opt-in, closed at M1 (AC-001)\n- F15 — closed at M2a\n- F16 — closed at M1; demonstrated on a real near-miss pair once M2b exists, at M3 (AC-005)\n- F17 — zero queryable pages until gates pass, closed at M2a (AC-007)\n- F18 — typed-400 cap