{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MCc7Ehn3EbjWkupwpy9Gv1","type":"tool_result","content":"14:## 0. Deliverable ledger\n39:## 1. Overview\n41:### 1.1 The guarantee\n50:### 1.2 The one rule\n59:### 1.3 What this CR builds\n70:## 2. Scope\n72:### 2.1 In scope\n85:### 2.2 Out of scope\n97:### 2.3 Corrections to plan2 (normative)\n114:### 2.4 Inheritance from the previous implementation\n162:### 2.5 Features in the first implementation that this CR does **not** include\n225:## 3. Closed decisions\n252:## 4. Repository and runtime\n254:### 4.1 Layout (normative)\n301:### 4.2 Pinned dependencies and configuration\n322:### 4.3 Boot self-check (`vsir doctor`, and on server start)\n329:### 4.4 The `vsir` CLI — the only supported operational surface (§15 Factor XII)\n349:## 5. Data contracts\n351:### 5.1 Identifiers\n363:### 5.2 The S2 response schema (the only VLM extraction schema)\n399:### 5.3 The page record\n437:### 5.4 `INDEXED` — one dict, three jobs (I6)\n456:### 5.5 Text index configuration\n475:### 5.6 Tokenisation, variants, and the single exact code path\n496:### 5.7 Health signals\n522:## 6. Ingestion pipeline\n524:### 6.1 Steps\n541:### 6.2 Windowing and bisection\n567:### 6.3 Cache keys (deterministic, content-addressable)\n594:### 6.4 The offset proof (I4)\n611:### 6.5 Printed labels and code attribution\n624:### 6.6 Embedding fingerprint\n629:### 6.7 Publish gating (I7)\n658:### 6.8 Exports (the Part A contract — D1, C8)\n708:### 6.9 Run record\n720:## 7. Tool surface\n722:### 7.1 The response envelopes (I5)\n840:### 7.2 The eight tools\n982:### 7.3 Caps and typed errors (F18)\n995:### 7.4 HTTP surface, auth, audit and cost\n1015:### 7.5 MCP server\n1021:### 7.6 Refusals (all four, enforced)\n1032:## 8. The agentic runner\n1034:### 8.1 The loop\n1053:### 8.1a Where the answer comes from — the image, by one of two routes\n1085:### 8.2 Tri-state triage (Loop 0 — the cheapest correction)\n1105:### 8.3 The six correction loops\n1116:### 8.4 The answer gate (I8, server-side)\n1135:### 8.5 Abstention wording\n1146:## 9. Invariants (each enforced by an assertion, each with a test)\n1161:## 10. Failure catalogue — **this table is the definition of done**\n1192:## 11. Gates, degradation, observability\n1194:### 11.1 Publish gates (a document is published atomically or quarantined)\n1204:### 11.2 Answer gates\n1210:### 11.3 Runtime degradation — each row is a refusal, not a best-effort fallback\n1223:### 11.4 Observability\n1230:## 12. Test strategy\n1232:### 12.1 The fixture that makes it cheap\n1260:### 12.2 Levels\n1276:### 12.3 L2 · The acceptance table (absolute, not comparative — see C10)\n1301:### 12.4 L3 · The adversarial abstention eval (runs in CI on every commit)\n1322:### 12.5 Conformance greps (the mistakes a well-meaning contributor makes)\n1344:### 12.6 Corpus evaluation (M8)\n1360:## 13. Milestones\n1366:### M0 · Skeleton, pins, harness — *spend: none*\n1386:### M1 · `core/` + the exact surface on synthetic text — *spend: none* — **the whole proof**\n1402:### M2a · Ingest a generated PDF with a stubbed VLM — *spend: none*\n1415:### M2b · Ingest the pilot PDF; freeze the fixture — *spend: S2 + embed, once*\n1430:### M3 · `lookup` + `verify`, over HTTP and MCP — *spend: none*\n1445:### M4 · `skim_pages`, `fetch`, `resolve` — *spend: none*\n1462:### M5 · The ladder rungs + `read` — *spend: read*\n1474:### M6 · The runner, the loop, the answer gate — *spend: read*\n1488:### M7 · Operator console — *spend: none (fixture-backed)*\n1505:### M8 · Revisions, resumable ingest, scale-out — *spend: ingest*\n1524:## 14. Top-level acceptance criteria\n1557:## 15. Cloud-native delivery — the twelve factors, applied\n1580:### 15.1 What the orchestrator needs beyond the twelve\n1592:### 15.2 Explicitly banned\n1604:## 16. Non-functional requirements\n1623:## 17. Open questions\n1637:## 18. Residual risks (stated, not solved)\n1651:## 19. Traceability to plan2\n1671:## 20. Document map — progressive disclosure\n1677:### Tier 1 · Design rationale — `plan2/` (this repo)\n1687:### Tier 2 · The previous implementation — `impl/` (≈ 9,600 lines of prose)\n1712:### Tier 3 · Programme context\n1722:### 20.1 The known-defect register, and what this spec does with it","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01R7TMF5jmiorZcKXFYHK85U","session_id":"4eefb16f-3989-4441-9cd3-d294cfccb11f","uuid":"58fa3169-e8b5-4780-a3ab-d92085fad5c6","timestamp":"2026-09-09T16:49:36.906Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Gap analysis and validation"}
