{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CetCzaxdYKbmkZnh6jsx4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_011S1UJFiq6JPtip8C4TUM79","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Unit decomposition","subagent_type":"general-purpose","model":"sonnet","run_in_background":false,"prompt":"You are Synthesis Agent S2 (unit decomposition) for a PLAN-ONLY implementation-planning task. Spec: `development/cr1/spec/spec.md` in /Users/sabesonk/Documents/DILMAH/dilmah-engineering-solutioning/poc/vision_segmentation_index_and_retrieval. DO NOT WRITE ANY FILES. DO NOT IMPLEMENT CODE. Output your decomposition as your final message only.\n\nYou may read the spec with `sed -n` for detail, but the brief below already contains the authoritative structure. Read at most 2–3 targeted ranges; do not read the whole file.\n\n## Your task\nProduce **22–26 atomic, PR-sized (1–3 day) implementation units**, each belonging to exactly ONE milestone, each with a runnable Working Deliverable and a Demo Command.\n\n## Hard rules\n1. Every unit belongs to exactly one milestone from M0, M1, M2a, M2b, M3, M4, M5, M6, M7, M8 and inherits its spend class. Never merge across milestones. Never reorder milestones.\n2. Every unit must have a **Working Deliverable** (a runnable artefact: CLI subcommand, HTTP endpoint, MCP tool, script, page) and a **Demo Command** a reviewer can run and read the output of. A unit whose only output is a document, a schema file or a refactor is INVALID — fold it into the unit that makes it runnable.\n3. A unit may only claim invariants/failure rows its milestone owns (ownership table below is authoritative).\n4. Order units so nothing depends on an unbuilt paid dependency. Everything provable without a model call comes before anything that spends.\n5. Twelve-factor compliance (Spec §15) for any unit adding a process/endpoint/tool/worker: new config is an env var in `.env.example` (never a literal, never a committed config file); NO process-local or on-disk correctness-bearing state (C11 — no `RetrievalState`, no persisted rasters, no local run state); JSON logs to stdout; long-running work checkpointed so SIGTERM loses at most one window; stub-vs-real VLM is config (`VSIR_VLM=stub`), never a code branch or `if TESTING`.\n6. Units under half a day must be merged with a neighbour INSIDE the same milestone.\n\n## Port discipline (Spec §2.3 C1, §2.4, §4.1)\nThis is a **restructured port of a working implementation at `impl/` outside this repo**, not greenfield. Every unit that builds a module marked `←` (port) or `≈` (port with changes) in §4.1 MUST list **\"read `impl/app/<module>.py` first\"** as its first Core Requirement, and its Deliverables must state what is ported vs written. `+` = net new.\n\n§4.1 layout with markers and impl ancestors:\n- core/record.py ≈ pagemodel.py (record shape only); core/ids.py ≈ pagemodel.py::make_page_id; core/tok.py, variants.py, exact.py + net new; core/verify.py, status.py, indexed.py + net new; core/health.py + net new (grounded_rate)\n- ingest/manifest.py ≈ pipeline.py; probe.py ← textlayer.py::probe/page_texts/content_hash; render.py ← render.py; window.py ← windows.py (+ bisection ladder F13); extract.py ≈ segment.py (new S2 schema); derive.py ≈ segment.py (no gate); stitch.py ← stitch.py (sections, + series_id); embed.py ← embedder.py (interleaved D4); sparse.py ← sparse.py (D2); index.py ≈ segstore.py (+ text indexes, is_current); gates.py ≈ pipeline.py (grounded_rate not allowlist); export.py, run.py ≈ pipeline.py / segjobs.py\n- vlm/client.py, cache.py, stub.py ≈ segment.py's Gemini calls; vlm/prompts/{s1.md,s2.md,read.md}\n- serve/app.py ≈ main.py; serve/envelope.py ≈ api_models.py; serve/auth.py, audit.py, budget.py + net new; serve/tools/skim.py ≈ retrieve.py::search+rrf+decompose; lookup.py ≈ retrieve.py::lookup (rewritten as phrase filter); resolve.py ← retrieve.py::resolve; read.py ≈ retrieve.py::read; fetch.py, verify.py + net new\n- mcp/server.py + net new; runner/{loop,prompt,triage,answer}.py + net new; cli.py ≈ scripts/interfaces_demo.py\n- backend/tests/{unit,api,paid}/; frontend/ (M7 only); e2e/ (exists); data/source/, data/fixtures/; scripts/test-{unit,api,e2e,paid}.sh\nNote: modules are created by the milestone that implements them, never as empty M0 placeholders.\n\nRequired reading per unit (Spec §20 Tier 2 — name the doc, don't read it now): `impl/pipeline-guide/01-entry.md` (step01), `02-probe-and-render.md` (02,03), `03-document-facts.md` (04), `04-windowing-and-keys.md` (05), `05-extraction.md`+`../SEGMENTATION.md` (06), `06-derivation-and-gate.md` (07 — ⚠ documents the DELETED allowlist gate), `07-stitch-and-numbering.md` (08), `08-embedding.md` (09), `09-indexing.md` (10 — ⚠ entity_keys index deleted), `10-gates-and-publish.md` (11 — ⚠ allowlist/class_totality replaced by grounded_rate), `11-export.md` (12 — ⚠ withheld.jsonl dropped), `12-reproducibility.md` (§6.3/§6.6), `pipeline-guide/METADATA-CONTRACT.md` (§5.3), `impl/README.md §3` (§7.2), `impl/INGESTION_WALKTHROUGH.md` (M2a/M2b debugging), `pipeline-guide/IMPROVEMENTS.md` (read BEFORE porting anything — the known-defect register; §20.1 lists defects that must NOT be reproduced: A1 always-extract-text, A5 image_path, B6 pin the model, B1/B4 provenance, B5 cache embeddings, D3 captions never written, E2 job state on daemon threads, E3 rendering never collected, E4 no cost observability, E5 no auth, E6 no tests, E7 orphan points, E9 scroll-4096-and-filter-in-Python).\n\n## Milestone ledger (Spec §0 + §13) — deliverable, demo, spend, depends-on\n- M0 | none | depends: nothing | demo `vsir doctor && bash scripts/test-unit.sh` | repo skeleton, backend/vsir/ package, cli.py→`vsir doctor`, pinned requirements.txt + lock, docker-compose.test.yml REWRITTEN Postgres→Qdrant, scripts/test-*.sh extended + test-paid.sh added, AGENTS.md filled with real commands, `vsir doctor` per §4.3, §12.5 conformance greps as a runnable test, twelve-factor runtime skeleton §15 (Dockerfile non-root + digest-pinned base + read-only rootfs + tmpfs raster cache, `.env.example` with every Factor III var, GET /health + GET /ready per §15.1, structured JSON logs to stdout, SIGTERM handler, release_id stamping), D1–D7 restated in README.\n- M1 | none | depends M0 | demo `vsir demo exact --synthetic` | **the whole correctness proof, zero spend**: core/record, both envelope families §7.1, INDEXED, tok, variants, exact_filter, core/verify.py::verify_claims (per (claim,page); tool wrapper comes at M3), the §12.4 near-miss generator, collection + text-index creation §5.5, `lookup` against an ephemeral Qdrant seeded with HAND-WRITTEN page text (no PDF): three synthetic pages (one containing `SF 1.1A`; one with tokens `sf`,`1`,`1a` scattered; one printing `SF121.1)`) plus a page whose `codes` claim `K999` its text lacks; the observed-token inventory §6.8 built from the seeded pages so `present_instead` works before any PDF exists; §7.3 cap validators as typed 400s. Ports `sparse.py` and `rrf()` from impl.\n- M2a | none | depends M1 | demo `vsir ingest data/source/synthetic_3window.pdf --vlm stub && vsir runs show <run_id>` | steps 01–12 end to end incl. `vsir_runs` control collection and the §6.7 three-clause retirement rule; a GENERATED 3-window PDF checked into data/source/ with known printed labels, a deliberate off-by-one trap and a crop trap; the stub VLM; run record; publish gating.\n- M2b | paid (S2 + embed, once) | depends M2a | demo `VSIR_ALLOW_PAID=1 vsir ingest data/source/TC1E-SF.pdf && vsir runs show <run_id>` | FIRST port what is already paid for: `impl/data/raw/*` → data/fixtures/ as the old-schema baseline, and `impl/data/exports/r-poc-*/labels.jsonl` + `withheld.jsonl` as the parity and negative sets; THEN one real ingest of TC1E-SF (55 pages) under the new S2 schema; freeze data/fixtures/TC1E-SF/{raw_window_1.json,raw_window_2.json,text.json,expected.json}; report the grounded_rate distribution and set the gate