y rootfs + tmpfs raster cache, `.env.example` with every Factor III var, GET /health + GET /ready per §15.1, structured JSON logs to stdout, SIGTERM handler, release_id stamping), D1–D7 restated in README.\n- M1 | none | depends M0 | demo `vsir demo exact --synthetic` | **the whole correctness proof, zero spend**: core/record, both envelope families §7.1, INDEXED, tok, variants, exact_filter, core/verify.py::verify_claims (per (claim,page); tool wrapper comes at M3), the §12.4 near-miss generator, collection + text-index creation §5.5, `lookup` against an ephemeral Qdrant seeded with HAND-WRITTEN page text (no PDF): three synthetic pages (one containing `SF 1.1A`; one with tokens `sf`,`1`,`1a` scattered; one printing `SF121.1)`) plus a page whose `codes` claim `K999` its text lacks; the observed-token inventory §6.8 built from the seeded pages so `present_instead` works before any PDF exists; §7.3 cap validators as typed 400s. Ports `sparse.py` and `rrf()` from impl.\n- M2a | none | depends M1 | demo `vsir ingest data/source/synthetic_3window.pdf --vlm stub && vsir runs show <run_id>` | steps 01–12 end to end incl. `vsir_runs` control collection and the §6.7 three-clause retirement rule; a GENERATED 3-window PDF checked into data/source/ with known printed labels, a deliberate off-by-one trap and a crop trap; the stub VLM; run record; publish gating.\n- M2b | paid (S2 + embed, once) | depends M2a | demo `VSIR_ALLOW_PAID=1 vsir ingest data/source/TC1E-SF.pdf && vsir runs show <run_id>` | FIRST port what is already paid for: `impl/data/raw/*` → data/fixtures/ as the old-schema baseline, and `impl/data/exports/r-poc-*/labels.jsonl` + `withheld.jsonl` as the parity and negative sets; THEN one real ingest of TC1E-SF (55 pages) under the new S2 schema; freeze data/fixtures/TC1E-SF/{raw_window_1.json,raw_window_2.json,text.json,expected.json}; report the grounded_rate distribution and set the gate threshold from it (R4).\n- M3 | none | depends M2a (real-corpus acceptance also needs M2b) | demo `vsir serve &` then `vsir lookup \"SF 1.1A\" && vsir verify --claims K73 --pages …` plus the same two tools over MCP | six-value status enum with all four absences, `next.suggest`, `present_instead`, `unverifiable`, bearer auth, audit log, `reads_remaining`, MCP server exposing both tools through the SAME implementations, `vsir eval acceptance` + `vsir eval abstention`.\n- M4 | none | depends M3 | demo `vsir demo narrow` | triage rows (no full text, but an ImageRef on EVERY page-level hit), deterministic §7.2.1 ordering (RRF ranks-only, rrf_k=60, weights page 1.0/lexical 1.0/captions 0.4), `exclude`, `next` affordances, region/dpi budgets incl. the 36/72 thumbnail tiers, `GET /pages/{page_id}/image`, the in-process raster LRU cache, image queries (D12, `embed_query_image`), `resolve` with `interpolated`.\n- M5 | paid (read) | depends M4 (paid assertions also need M2b/OQ-2) | demo `VSIR_ALLOW_PAID=1 vsir read --pages TC1E-SF@1.3#p001,…#p002 --question \"…\"` | `skim_documents`/`skim_sections` with `searchable_ratio` on every document row; `read` with per-code present/absent/unverifiable stamps, `sufficient`, `page_provenance`, the ≤3-page cap, the question-keyed cache.\n- M6 | paid (read) | depends M5 | demo `VSIR_ALLOW_PAID=1 vsir ask \"the carton discharge won't restart after an E-stop reset\"` | runner/ implementing §8: tri-state triage with `exclude`, the six correction loops, the system prompt, the SERVER-SIDE answer gate, constrained abstention wording; `POST /ask`; `vsir ask`.\n- M7 | none (fixture-backed replay) | depends M6 | demo `bash scripts/test-e2e.sh` then browse http://localhost:5174 | React + TypeScript + Vite, two zones. Consumes `image.url`/`preview.thumb_url` directly with `inline=false`. LEFT: zoom-ladder breadcrumbs, high-res page viewer, region zoom at escalated dpi. RIGHT: collapsible agent moves (skim/read/verify), tri-state triage panel, draft answer with trust badges (verified / read-from-image / unverifiable) and amber verification warnings; clicking a code scrolls the viewer to its cited page. Playwright drives the worked trace in replay mode; assertions must be fixture-independent (pass on synthetic_3window too).\n- M8 | paid (ingest) | depends M6 (and M2b for real-corpus numbers) | demo `vsir ingest --resume <run_id>` after a deliberate kill, then `vsir eval corpus` | `is_current` lifecycle, `found_only_in_superseded`, `series_id` across revisions, resumable `--resume` ingest with per-window checkpoints, graceful-shutdown checkpointing (§15 Factor IX), the §12.6 corpus evaluation report. Note §6.2: the resume test runs on a GENERATED large PDF, not the excluded 1,440-page manual; attempting a Level-2 document must fail typed `ladder_level_2_required`.\n\n## Invariant ownership (Spec §9 \"Asserted from\") — AUTHORITATIVE, a unit may not claim outside it\nI1 M2a | I2 M1 | I3 M1 | I4 M2a | I5 M1 | I6 M1 | I7 M2a | I8 M6\n\n## Failure-row ownership (Spec §10 \"Closed at\") — AUTHORITATIVE\nF1 M1 | F2 M1(core) + M3(tool) | F3 M1 | F4 M2a + M3 | F5 M2a + M4 | F6 M2a | F7 M2a | F8 M2a(stitching) + M4(stateless scope) + M8(series_id) | F9 M8 | F10 M1 | F11 M0(boot) + M2a(key) | F12 M2a (+ M8 revision half) | F13 M2a | F14 M1 | F15 M2a | F16 M1 | F17 M2a | F18 M4(fetch) + M5(read) | F19 M5\nA row split across milestones needs ONE OWNING UNIT PER PART.\n\n## Key technical content the units must cover (spec pointers only)\n- §5.1 ids (page_id/section_id/series_id/point_id=uuid5/run_id=ULID); §5.2 S2 schema (PageOut/SectionRef/Summary/WindowOut; **Prohibited**: any identifier grammar, classification enum, regex taxonomy or per-corpus keyword list); §5.3 record (facets / text+vlm_codes / three vectors dense+lexical+captions / nested `content` never filtered / provenance; NO image_path); §5.4 INDEXED dict — one dict creates, gates and is asserted at boot (I6), scope keys = INDEXED minus text and vlm_codes; §5.5 TextIndexParams WORD tokenizer, lowercase, phrase_matching=True, min_token_len=1, collection name carries dim (pages_1536); §5.6 tok() mirrors Qdrant WORD (NOT impl's TOKEN_RE — porting hazard), variants() = exactly 3 spellings of the same characters, exact_filter is the ONLY exact-match path; §5.7 grounded_rate is None where has_text is false, text_trust enum, searchable_ratio.\n- §6.1 steps 01–12; §6.2 windowing target 30 pages + bisect-and-re-bill on MAX_TOKENS/truncation/offset-failure, `window_unsplittable`, and **v1 is Level 0/1 + bisection only — a Level-2 document must fail typed `ladder_level_2_required`**; §6.3 four cache keys facts_key/extract_key/read_key/embed_key (VSIR_VLM_TIER is NOT part of extract_key) + replay mode `VSIR_VLM=stub` + `VSIR_FIXTURE=<dir>` with a typed `fixture_miss`; §6.4 the two independent offset checks; §6.5 label precedence + ambiguity→list + code reattribution with `moved_from`; §6.6 fingerprint {embed_model,dim,distance,composition_version} → refuse to upsert on mismatch; §6.7 publish gating + the THREE-CLAUSE retirement (delete same doc+revision earlier run_id → F12; set prior *other* revision is_current=False and KEEP → F9; never touch other documents) + `vsir_runs` run/window points + advisory lease + `--steal`; §6.8 exports labels.jsonl + observed_tokens.jsonl streamed over HTTP, `safety_flag` from manifest doc_type + model topics (never a keyword list), observed-token inventory display-only and unreachable from lookup/verify; §6.9 run record + state enum {queued,running,stopped,gated,published,failed}.\n- §7.1 two envelope families + six-value status + `empty_is_never_ok` validator + WEAK_ABS=20 server constant + hit models DocHit/SectionHit/PageHit/LookupHit/ResolveHit + ImageRef/Preview (references never bytes; bytes_b64 only in fetch); §7.2 the eight tools; §7.3 caps as typed 400s (read ≤3 `read_page_cap_exceeded`; fetch ≤5 and ≤12MP `fetch_budget_exceeded`; dpi ∈ {36,72,150,220,300,400} `dpi_not_allowed`; dpi>220 requires region `dpi_requires_region`; unknown scope key `filter_unknown_key`; 429 `budget_exhausted`); §7.4 routes + bearer + the ten-field audit line + cost-in-audit-not-body; §7.5 MCP stdio+SSE same implementations, stateless; §7.6 four refusals (no `score` field, no routing, no composing outside the runner, no fuzzy matching).\n- §8 the runner: loop, fetch-vs-read routing (default fetch), tri-state triage + five safeguards, six correction loops, server-side answer gate with three branches, VSIR_READS_PER_QUESTION default 3, abstention wording forbidden while `pages_no_text_read < scope_stats.pages_no_text`.\n- §11.1 publish gates (window_coverage block; offset_check block; grounded_rate ≥0.8 provisional block with `vsir publish --override <gate> --reason` and `published_with_override`; text_coverage flag `mostly_scanned` never block, and AT 0.0 the grounded_rate gate is SKIPPED so a fully scanned doc publishes; label_monotonic flag `label_conflict`); §11.3 degradation rows (503 qdrant_unavailable, 503 vlm_unavailable, boot refusals, 429, typed 400s — never an empty result, never a clamp); §11.4 Prometheus gauges + audit + triage telemetry.\n- §12.5 conformance greps (scope `backend/vsir/**` + `requirements*.txt`, never markdown, never the test's own file): MatchText/MatchTextAny under serve/; fuzzy/similarity/edit-distance library in requirements*.txt; a field named `score` in a response model; a model id ending `-latest`; `alembic`/`sqlalchemy`; `get_text(` outside ingest/probe.py; SCHEMA_CARD, IdClass, entity_keys, `classify(`. Cloud-native set (same scope + Dockerfile* + docker-compose*.yml): `logging.FileHandler`; an image tagged `latest`; credential literals (`api_key=`, `token=`, `Bearer ` + literal); test-only branches (`if TESTING`, `if os.environ.get(\"TESTING\")`) inside backend/vsir/**; a `RetrievalState`-style module-level mutable session store.\n- §4.2 pins: python 3.11; fastapi==0.141.1, uvicorn[standard]==0.52.4, python-multipart==0.0.32, google-genai==2.22.0, qdrant-client==1.19.0, PyMuPDF==1.28.2, pillow==12.3.0; qdrant/qdrant:v1.19.0; ports backend dev 8000 / test 8001, Qdrant dev 6333 REST + 6334 gRPC so test takes 6335 (never 6334), frontend dev 5173 / test 5174; dpi_index=150 (embedded) / dpi_answer=220 (read, pinned, part of read_key); dim ∈ {768,1536,3072}, concurrency=8, batch_size=8, max_edge_px=1568; rrf_k=60, weights page 1.0/lexical 1.0/captions 0.4, cap_pages_per_window=30, lookup_cap=20. Store is **Qdrant only**, two collections `vsir_pages` + `vsir_runs`. No relational DB, ORM, migration tool or queue service.\n- §4.4 CLI: doctor (M0), demo exact --synthetic (M1), ingest [--vlm stub|--resume|--steal] (M2a), runs show (M2a), gates rerun (M2a), publish --override --reason (M2b), serve (M3), mcp [--stdio|--sse] (M3), lookup/verify/resolve/skim/fetch/read one-shots (M3–M5), demo narrow (M4), ask (M6), eval acceptance|abstention|corpus (M3, M8), retire <doc_id> [--revision] (M8).\n- §17 open questions: OQ-1 pilot PDF location (blocks ONLY the M2b re-bill — the S2 responses are already in impl/data/raw/); OQ-2 Gemini key (blocks M2b/M5/M6 paid paths only — replay mode covers the rest); OQ-3/OQ-7 Part A export sign-off (M8); OQ-4 resolved by design; OQ-5 one collection.\n\n## Output format — repeat this block for EVERY unit, in milestone order\n### Synthesis Agent 2: Unit Decomposition\n\nUnit ID: U001 (sequential, zero-padded, never reused)\nName: <short descriptive name>\nMilestone: <M0|M1|M2a|M2b|M3|M4|M5|M6|M7|M8>\nType: <core|ingest|tool|mcp|runner|frontend|harness|eval>\nPriority: <P0-Critical|P1-High|P2-Medium|P3-Low>\nSize Estimate: <Small|Medium|Large>\nSpend: <none|paid>\nDepends On: [<unit IDs>]\nEnables: [<unit IDs>]\nSpec References: [Spec §X.Y, …]\nInvariants Enforced: [I<n>… — only ones this milestone owns, or empty]\nFailure Rows Closed: [F<n>… — only ones this milestone owns; say \"(fetch half)\" etc. for split rows, or empty]\nRequired Reading: [`impl/app/<module>.py` for every ← or ≈ module; the `impl/pipeline-guide/NN-*.md` for every ported step; `IMPROVEMENTS.md` register items it must not reproduce]\n\nDescription:\n- <one sentence goal>\n\nCore Requirements:\n- <bullets, spec pointers only; the FIRST bullet must be \"read `impl/app/<module>.py` first\" for any ←/≈ module>\n\nWorking Deliverable:\n- <the runnable artefact>\n\nDemo Command:\n- <exact command> — <what a reviewer should see>\n\nDeliverables (files):\n- <concrete paths under backend/vsir/…, backend/tests/…, frontend/…, scripts/…, data/…; state ported vs written for each ←/≈ file>\n\nTwelve-Factor Notes:\n- <the env vars this unit adds to .env.example; any statelessness/SIGTERM/log obligation; \"N/A — adds no process, endpoint, tool or worker\" if truly none>\n\n---\n\nEnd with:\n\nCoverage Self-Check:\n- Units per milestone: M0=<n>, M1=<n>, M2a=<n>, M2b=<n>, M3=<n>, M4=<n>, M5=<n>, M6=<n>, M7=<n>, M8=<n>, TOTAL=<n>\n- Every I1–I8 owned: <I → unit id, all eight>\n- Every F1–F19 owned (name the unit per part for split rows): <F → unit id(s), all nineteen>\n- Any unit without a runnable Demo Command: <must be \"none\">\n","uuid":"b3c77e8e-a935-4167-bfe9-6ec8304f8398","session_id":"4eefb16f-3989-4441-9cd3-d294cfccb11f"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"You are Synthesis Agent S2 (unit decomposition) for a PLAN-ONLY implementation-planning task. Spec: `development/cr1/spec/spec.md` in /Users/sabesonk/Documents/DILMAH/dilmah-engineering-solutioning/poc/vision_segmentation_index_and_retrieval. DO NOT WRITE ANY FILES. DO NOT IMPLEMENT CODE. Output your decomposition as your final message only.\n\nYou may read the spec with `sed -n` for detail, but the brief below already contains the authoritative structure. Read at most 2–3 targeted ranges; do not read the whole file.\n\n## Your task\nProduce **22–26 atomic, PR-sized (1–3 day) implementation units**, each belonging to exactly ONE milestone, each with a runnable Working Deliverable and a Demo Command.\n\n## Hard rules\n1. Every unit belongs to exactly one milestone from M0, M1, M2a, M2b, M3, M4, M5, M6, M7, M8 and inherits its spend class. Never merge across milestones. Never reorder milestones.\n2. Every unit must have a **Working Deliverable** (a runnable artefact: CLI subcommand, HTTP endpoint, MCP tool, script, page) and a **Demo Command** a reviewer can run and read the output of. A unit whose only output is a document, a schema file or a refactor is INVALID — fold it into the unit that makes it runnable.\n3. A unit may only claim invariants/failure rows its milestone owns (ownership table below is authoritative).\n4. Order units so nothing depends on an unbuilt paid dependency. Everything provable without a model call comes before anything that spends.\n5. Twelve-factor compliance (Spec §15) for any unit adding a process/endpoint/tool/worker: new config is an env var in `.env.example` (never a literal, never a committed config file); NO process-local or on-disk correctness-bearing state (C11 — no `RetrievalState`, no persisted rasters, no local run state); JSON logs to stdout; long-running work checkpointed so SIGTERM loses at most one window; stub-vs-real VLM is config (`VSIR_VLM=stub`), never a code branch or `if TESTING`.\n6. Units under half a day must be merged with a neighbour INSIDE the same milestone.\n\n## Port discipline (Spec §2.3 C1, §2.4, §4.1)\nThis is a **restructured port of a working implementation at `impl/` outside this repo**, not greenfield. Every unit that builds a module marked `←` (port) or `≈` (port with changes) in §4.1 MUST list **\"read `impl/app/<module>.py` first\"** as its first Core Requirement, and its Deliverables must state what is ported vs written. `+` = net new.\n\n§4.1 layout with markers and impl ancestors:\n- core/record.py ≈ pagemodel.py (record shape only); core/ids.py ≈ pagemodel.py::make_page_id; core/tok.py, variants.py, exact.py + net new; core/verify.py, status.py, indexed.py + net new; core/health.py + net new (grounded_rate)\n- ingest/manifest.py ≈ pipeline.py; probe.py ← textlayer.py::probe/page_texts/content_hash; render.py ← render.py; window.py ← windows.py (+ bisection ladder F13); extract.py ≈ segment.py (new S2 schema); derive.py ≈ segment.py (no gate); stitch.py ← stitch.py (sections, + series_id); embed.py ← embedder.py (interleaved D4); sparse.py ← sparse.py (D2); index.py ≈ segstore.py (+ text indexes, is_current); gates.py ≈ pipeline.py (grounded_rate not allowlist); export.py, run.py ≈ pipeline.py / segjobs.py\n- vlm/client.py, cache.py, stub.py ≈ segment.py's Gemini calls; vlm/prompts/{s1.md,s2.md,read.md}\n- serve/app.py ≈ main.py; serve/envelope.py ≈ api_models.py; serve/auth.py, audit.py, budget.py + net new; serve/tools/skim.py ≈ retrieve.py::search+rrf+decompose; lookup.py ≈ retrieve.py::lookup (rewritten as phrase filter); resolve.py ← retrieve.py::resolve; read.py ≈ retrieve.py::read; fetch.py, verify.py + net new\n- mcp/server.py + net new; runner/{loop,prompt,triage,answer}.py + net new; cli.py ≈ scripts/interfaces_demo.py\n- backend/tests/{unit,api,paid}/; frontend/ (M7 only); e2e/ (exists); data/source/, data/fixtures/; scripts/test-{unit,api,e2e,paid}.sh\nNote: modules are created by the milestone that implements them, never as empty M0 placeholders.\n\nRequired reading per unit (Spec §20 Tier 2 — name the doc, don't read it now): `impl/pipeline-guide/01-entry.md` (step01), `02-probe-and-render.md` (02,03), `03-document-facts.md` (04), `04-windowing-and-keys.md` (05), `05-extraction.md`+`../SEGMENTATION.md` (06), `06-derivation-and-gate.md` (07 — ⚠ documents the DELETED allowlist gate), `07-stitch-and-numbering.md` (08), `08-embedding.md` (09), `09-indexing.md` (10 — ⚠ entity_keys index deleted), `10-gates-and-publish.md` (11 — ⚠ allowlist/class_totality replaced by grounded_rate), `11-export.md` (12 — ⚠ withheld.jsonl dropped), `12-reproducibility.md` (§6.3/§6.6), `pipeline-guide/METADATA-CONTRACT.md` (§5.3), `impl/README.md §3` (§7.2), `impl/INGESTION_WALKTHROUGH.md` (M2a/M2b debugging), `pipeline-guide/IMPROVEMENTS.md` (read BEFORE porting anything — the known-defect register; §20.1 lists defects that must NOT be reproduced: A1 always-extract-text, A5 image_path, B6 pin the model, B1/B4 provenance, B5 cache embeddings, D3 captions never written, E2 job state on daemon threads, E3 rendering never collected, E4 no cost observability, E5 no auth, E6 no tests, E7 orphan points, E9 scroll-4096-and-filter-in-Python).\n\n## Milestone ledger (Spec §0 + §13) — deliverable, demo, spend, depends-on\n- M0 | none | depends: nothing | demo `vsir doctor && bash scripts/test-unit.sh` | repo skeleton, backend/vsir/ package, cli.py→`vsir doctor`, pinned requirements.txt + lock, docker-compose.test.yml REWRITTEN Postgres→Qdrant, scripts/test-*.sh extended + test-paid.sh added, AGENTS.md filled with real commands, `vsir doctor` per §4.3, §12.5 conformance greps as a runnable test, twelve-factor runtime skeleton §15 (Dockerfile non-root + digest-pinned base + read-only rootfs + tmpfs raster cache, `.env.example` with every Factor III var, GET /health + GET /ready per §15.1, structured JSON logs to stdout, SIGTERM handler, release_id stamping), D1–D7 restated in README.\n- M1 | none | depends M0 | demo `vsir demo exact --synthetic` | **the whole correctness proof, zero spend**: core/record, both envelope families §7.1, INDEXED, tok, variants, exact_filter, core/verify.py::verify_claims (per (claim,page); tool wrapper comes at M3), the §12.4 near-miss generator, collection + text-index creation §5.5, `lookup` against an ephemeral Qdrant seeded with HAND-WRITTEN page text (no PDF): three synthetic pages (one containing `SF 1.1A`; one with tokens `sf`,`1`,`1a` scattered; one printing `SF121.1)`) plus a page whose `codes` claim `K999` its text lacks; the observed-token inventory §6.8 built from the seeded pages so `present_instead` works before any PDF exists; §7.3 cap validators as typed 400s. Ports `sparse.py` and `rrf()` from impl.\n- M2a | none | depends M1 | demo `vsir ingest data/source/synthetic_3window.pdf --vlm stub && vsir runs show <run_id>` | steps 01–12 end to end incl. `vsir_runs` control collection and the §6.7 three-clause retirement rule; a GENERATED 3-window PDF checked into data/source/ with known printed labels, a deliberate off-by-one trap and a crop trap; the stub VLM; run record; publish gating.\n- M2b | paid (S2 + embed, once) | depends M2a | demo `VSIR_ALLOW_PAID=1 vsir ingest data/source/TC1E-SF.pdf && vsir runs show <run_id>` | FIRST port what is already paid for: `impl/data/raw/*` → data/fixtures/ as the old-schema baseline, and `impl/data/exports/r-poc-*/labels.jsonl` + `withheld.jsonl` as the parity and negative sets; THEN one real ingest of TC1E-SF (55 pages) under the new S2 schema; freeze data/fixtures/TC1E-SF/{raw_window_1.json,raw_window_2.json,text.json,expected.json}; report the grounded_rate distribution and set the gate threshold from it (R4).\n- M3 | none | depends M2a (real-corpus acceptance also needs M2b) | demo `vsir serve &` then `vsir lookup \"SF 1.1A\" && vsir verify --claims K73 --pages …` plus the same two tools over MCP | six-value status enum with all four absences, `next.suggest`, `present_instead`, `unverifiable`, bearer auth, audit log, `reads_remaining`, MCP server exposing both tools through the SAME implementations, `vsir eval acceptance` + `vsir eval abstention`.\n- M4 | none | depends M3 | demo `vsir demo narrow` | triage rows (no full text, but an ImageRef on EVERY page-level hit), deterministic §7.2.1 ordering (RRF ranks-only, rrf_k=60, weights page 1.0/lexical 1.0/captions 0.4), `exclude`, `next` affordances, region/dpi budgets incl. the 36/72 thumbnail tiers, `GET /pages/{page_id}/image`, the in-process raster LRU cache, image queries (D12, `embed_query_image`), `resolve` with `interpolated`.\n- M5 | paid (read) | depends M4 (paid assertions also need M2b/OQ-2) | demo `VSIR_ALLOW_PAID=1 vsir read --pages TC1E-SF@1.3#p001,…#p002 --question \"…\"` | `skim_documents`/`skim_sections` with `searchable_ratio` on every document row; `read` with per-code present/absent/unverifiable stamps, `sufficient`, `page_provenance`, the ≤3-page cap, the question-keyed cache.\n- M6 | paid (read) | depends M5 | demo `VSIR_ALLOW_PAID=1 vsir ask \"the carton discharge won't restart after an E-stop reset\"` | runner/ implementing §8: tri-state triage with `exclude`, the six correction loops, the system prompt, the SERVER-SIDE answer gate, constrained abstention wording; `POST /ask`; `vsir ask`.\n- M7 | none (fixture-backed replay) | depends M6 | demo `bash scripts/test-e2e.sh` then browse http://localhost:5174 | React + TypeScript + Vite, two zones. Consumes `image.url`/`preview.thumb_url` directly with `inline=false`. LEFT: zoom-ladder breadcrumbs, high-res page viewer, region zoom at escalated dpi. RIGHT: collapsible agent moves (skim/read/verify), tri-state triage panel, draft answer with trust badges (verified / read-from-image / unverifiable) and amber verification warnings; clicking a code scrolls the viewer to its cited page. Playwright drives the worked trace in replay mode; assertions must be fixture-independent (pass on synthetic_3window too).\n- M8 | paid (ingest) | depends M6 (and M2b for real-corpus numbers) | demo `vsir ingest --resume <run_id>` after a deliberate kill, then `vsir eval corpus` | `is_current` lifecycle, `found_only_in_superseded`, `series_id` across revisions, resumable `--resume` ingest with per-window checkpoints, graceful-shutdown checkpointing (§15 Factor IX), the §12.6 corpus evaluation report. Note §6.2: the resume test runs on a GENERATED large PDF, not the excluded 1,440-page manual; attempting a Level-2 document must fail typed `ladder_level_2_required`.\n\n## Invariant ownership (Spec §9 \"Asserted from\") — AUTHORITATIVE, a unit may not claim outside it\nI1 M2a | I2 M1 | I3 M1 | I4 M2a | I5 M1 | I6 M1 | I7 M2a | I8 M6\n\n## Failure-row ownership (Spec §10 \"Closed at\") — AUTHORITATIVE\nF1 M1 | F2 M1(core) + M3(tool) | F3 M1 | F4 M2a + M3 | F5 M2a + M4 | F6 M2a | F7 M2a | F8 M2a(stitching) + M4(stateless scope) + M8(series_id) | F9 M8 | F10 M1 | F11 M0(boot) + M2a(key) | F12 M2a (+ M8 revision half) | F13 M2a | F14 M1 | F15 M2a | F16 M1 | F17 M2a | F18 M4(fetch) + M5(read) | F19 M5\nA row split across milestones needs ONE OWNING UNIT PER PART.\n\n## Key technical content the units must cover (spec pointers only)\n- §5.1 ids (page_id/section_id/series_id/point_id=uuid5/run_id=ULID); §5.2 S2 schema (PageOut/SectionRef/Summary/WindowOut; **Prohibited**: any identifier grammar, classification enum, regex taxonomy or per-corpus keyword list); §5.3 record (facets / text+vlm_codes / three vectors dense+lexical+captions / nested `content` never filtered / provenance; NO image_path); §5.4 INDEXED dict — one dict creates, gates and is asserted at boot (I6), scope keys = INDEXED minus text and vlm_codes; §5.5 TextIndexParams WORD tokenizer, lowercase, phrase_matching=True, min_token_len=1, collection name carries dim (pages_1536); §5.6 tok() mirrors Qdrant WORD (NOT impl's TOKEN_RE — porting hazard), variants() = exactly 3 spellings of the same characters, exact_filter is the ONLY exact-match path; §5.7 grounded_rate is None where has_text is false, text_trust enum, searchable_ratio.\n- §6.1 steps 01–12; §6.2 windowing target 30 pages + bisect-and-re-bill on MAX_TOKENS/truncation/offset-failure, `window_unsplittable`, and **v1 is Level 0/1 + bisection only — a Level-2 document must fail typed `ladder_level_2_required`**; §6.3 four cache keys facts_key/extract_key/read_key/embed_key (VSIR_VLM_TIER is NOT part of extract_key) + replay mode `VSIR_VLM=stub` + `VSIR_FIXTURE=<dir>` with a typed `fixture_miss`; §6.4 the two independent offset checks; §6.5 label precedence + ambiguity→list + code reattribution with `moved_from`; §6.6 fingerprint {embed_model,dim,distance,composition_version} → refuse to upsert on mismatch; §6.7 publish gating + the THREE-CLAUSE retirement (delete same doc+revision earlier run_id → F12; set prior *other* revision is_current=False and KEEP → F9; never touch other documents) + `vsir_runs` run/window points + advisory lease + `--steal`; §6.8 exports labels.jsonl + observed_tokens.jsonl streamed over HTTP, `safety_flag` from manifest doc_type + model topics (never a keyword list), observed-token inventory display-only and unreachable from lookup/verify; §6.9 run record + state enum {queued,running,stopped,gated,published,failed}.\n- §7.1 two envelope families + six-value status + `empty_is_never_ok` validator + WEAK_ABS=20 server constant + hit models DocHit/SectionHit/PageHit/LookupHit/ResolveHit + ImageRef/Preview (references never bytes; bytes_b64 only in fetch); §7.2 the eight tools; §7.3 caps as typed 400s (read ≤3 `read_page_cap_exceeded`; fetch ≤5 and ≤12MP `fetch_budget_exceeded`; dpi ∈ {36,72,150,220,300,400} `dpi_not_allowed`; dpi>220 requires region `dpi_requires_region`; unknown scope key `filter_unknown_key`; 429 `budget_exhausted`); §7.4 routes + bearer + the ten-field audit line + cost-in-audit-not-body; §7.5 MCP stdio+SSE same implementations, stateless; §7.6 four refusals (no `score` field, no routing, no composing outside the runner, no fuzzy matching).\n- §8 the runner: loop, fetch-vs-read routing (default fetch), tri-state triage + five safeguards, six correction loops, server-side answer gate with three branches, VSIR_READS_PER_QUESTION default 3, abstention wording forbidden while `pages_no_text_read < scope_stats.pages_no_text`.\n- §11.1 publish gates (window_coverage block; offset_check block; grounded_rate ≥0.8 provisional block with `vsir publish --override <gate> --reason` and `published_with_override`; text_coverage flag `mostly_scanned` never block, and AT 0.0 the grounded_rate gate is SKIPPED so a fully scanned doc publishes; label_monotonic flag `label_conflict`); §11.3 degradation rows (503 qdrant_unavailable, 503 vlm_unavailable, boot refusals, 429, typed 400s — never an empty result, never a clamp); §11.4 Prometheus gauges + audit + triage telemetry.\n- §12.5 conformance greps (scope `backend/vsir/**` + `requirements*.txt`, never markdown, never the test's own file): MatchText/MatchTextAny under serve/; fuzzy/similarity/edit-distance library in requirements*.txt; a field named `score` in a response model; a model id ending `-latest`; `alembic`/`sqlalchemy`; `get_text(` outside ingest/probe.py; SCHEMA_CARD, IdClass, entity_keys, `classify(`. Cloud-native set (same scope + Dockerfile* + docker-compose*.yml): `logging.FileHandler`; an image tagged `latest`; credential literals (`api_key=`, `token=`, `Bearer ` + literal); test-only branches (`if TESTING`, `if os.environ.get(\"TESTING\")`) inside backend/vsir/**; a `RetrievalState`-style module-level mutable session store.\n- §4.2 pins: python 3.11; fastapi==0.141.1, uvicorn[standard]==0.52.4, python-multipart==0.0.32, google-genai==2.22.0, qdrant-client==1.19.0, PyMuPDF==1.28.2, pillow==12.3.0; qdrant/qdrant:v1.19.0; ports backend dev 8000 / test 8001, Qdrant dev 6333 REST + 6334 gRPC so test takes 6335 (never 6334), frontend dev 5173 / test 5174; dpi_index=150 (embedded) / dpi_answer=220 (read, pinned, part of read_key); dim ∈ {768,1536,3072}, concurrency=8, batch_size=8, max_edge_px=1568; rrf_k=60, weights page 1.0/lexical 1.0/captions 0.4, cap_pages_per_window=30, lookup_cap=20. Store is **Qdrant only**, two collections `vsir_pages` + `vsir_runs`. No relational DB, ORM, migration tool or queue service.\n- §4.4 CLI: doctor (M0), demo exact --synthetic (M1), ingest [--vlm stub|--resume|--steal] (M2a), runs show (M2a), gates rerun (M2a), publish --override --reason (M2b), serve (M3), mcp [--stdio|--sse] (M3), lookup/verify/resolve/skim/fetch/read one-shots (M3–M5), demo narrow (M4), ask (M6), eval acceptance|abstention|corpus (M3, M8), retire <doc_id> [--revision] (M8).\n- §17 open questions: OQ-1 pilot PDF location (blocks ONLY the M2b re-bill — the S2 responses are already in impl/data/raw/); OQ-2 Gemini key (blocks M2b/M5/M6 paid paths only — replay mode covers the rest); OQ-3/OQ-7 Part A export sign-off (M8); OQ-4 resolved by design; OQ-5 one collection.\n\n## Output format — repeat this block for EVERY unit, in milestone order\n### Synthesis Agent 2: Unit Decomposition\n\nUnit ID: U001 (sequential, zero-padded, never reused)\nName: <short descriptive name>\nMilestone: <M0|M1|M2a|M2b|M3|M4|M5|M6|M7|M8>\nType: <core|ingest|tool|mcp|runner|frontend|harness|eval>\nPriority: <P0-Critical|P1-High|P2-Medium|P3-Low>\nSize Estimate: <Small|Medium|Large>\nSpend: <none|paid>\nDepends On: [<unit IDs>]\nEnables: [<unit IDs>]\nSpec References: [Spec §X.Y, …]\nInvariants Enforced: [I<n>… — only ones this milestone owns, or empty]\nFailure Rows Closed: [F<n>… — only ones this milestone owns; say \"(fetch half)\" etc. for split rows, or empty]\nRequired Reading: [`impl/app/<module>.py` for every ← or ≈ module; the `impl/pipeline-guide/NN-*.md` for every ported step; `IMPROVEMENTS.md` register items it must not reproduce]\n\nDescription:\n- <one sentence goal>\n\nCore Requirements:\n- <bullets, spec pointers only; the FIRST bullet must be \"read `impl/app/<module>.py` first\" for any ←/≈ module>\n\nWorking Deliverable:\n- <the runnable artefact>\n\nDemo Command:\n- <exact command> — <what a reviewer should see>\n\nDeliverables (files):\n- <concrete paths under backend/vsir/…, backend/tests/…, frontend/…, scripts/…, data/…; state ported vs written for each ←/≈ file>\n\nTwelve-Factor Notes:\n- <the env vars this unit adds to .env.example; any statelessness/SIGTERM/log obligation; \"N/A — adds no process, endpoint, tool or worker\" if truly none>\n\n---\n\nEnd with:\n\nCoverage Self-Check:\n- Units per milestone: M0=<n>, M1=<n>, M2a=<n>, M2b=<n>, M3=<n>, M4=<n>, M5=<n>, M6=<n>, M7=<n>, M8=<n>, TOTAL=<n>\n- Every I1–I8 owned: <I → unit id, all eight>\n- Every F1–F19 owned (name the unit per part for split rows): <F → unit id(s), all nineteen>\n- Any unit without a runnable Demo Command: <must be \"none\">\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_011S1UJFiq6JPtip8C4TUM79","session_id":"4eefb16f-3989-4441-9cd3-d294cfccb11f","uuid":"b5968551-7f24-43fb-b981-fd2e6613aaec","timestamp":"2026-09-09T16:51:00.368Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Unit decomposition"}
