{"type":"system","subtype":"task_notification","task_id":"a08a24a5168b021fd","tool_use_id":"toolu_011S1UJFiq6JPtip8C4TUM79","status":"completed","output_file":"/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-sabesonk-Documents-DILMAH-dilmah-engineering-solutioning-poc-vision-segmentation-index-and-retrieval/4eefb16f-3989-4441-9cd3-d294cfccb11f/tasks/a08a24a5168b021fd.output","summary":"### Synthesis Agent 2: Unit Decomposition\n\nUnit ID: U001\nName: Repo skeleton, CLI doctor, and twelve-factor runtime shell\nMilestone: M0\nType: harness\nPriority: P0-Critical\nSize Estimate: Large\nSpend: none\nDepends On: []\nEnables: [U002, U003]\nSpec References: [Spec §4.1, §4.2, §4.3, §4.4, §15, §15.1, §15.2]\nInvariants Enforced: []\nFailure Rows Closed: [F11 (boot half — alias/`-latest` model id refused at boot)]\nRequired Reading: [`impl/README.md §3` (§7.2 twelve-factor precedent); `pipeline-guide/IMPROVEMENTS.md` items E5 (no auth — do not reproduce, stub it out now so M3 has a hook), E4 (no cost observability — plan gauge hooks now)]\n\nDescription:\n- Stand up the installable `backend/vsir/` package, the `vsir` CLI entrypoint, and a self-checking, twelve-factor-compliant runtime shell with nothing paid or ingest-specific in it yet.\n\nCore Requirements:\n- §4.1 repo layout skeleton: `backend/vsir/{core,ingest,vlm,serve,mcp,runner}/__init__.py` placeholders only where a later milestone owns the first real module (never populate a module ahead of its owning milestone).\n- `cli.py` ≈ `impl/scripts/interfaces_demo.py` (read first) — port the argument-parsing skeleton only; wire the `vsir` entrypoint and register `doctor` as the first real subcommand.\n- §4.3 boot self-check: Qdrant reachable, pinned model id does not end in `-latest` (refuse to start — F11 boot half), release_id resolvable.\n- §4.2 pin python 3.11, fastapi==0.141.1, uvicorn[standard]==0.52.4, python-multipart==0.0.32, google-genai==2.22.0, qdrant-client==1.19.0, PyMuPDF==1.28.2, pillow==12.3.0 in `requirements.txt` + generate a lock file.\n- REWRITE `docker-compose.test.yml` from any Postgres service to `qdrant/qdrant:v1.19.0` on test ports (backend 8001, Qdrant REST 6335 gRPC — never reuse dev 6334).\n- §15 Dockerfile: non-root user, digest-pinned base image, read-only rootfs, tmpfs mount for the raster cache; `.env.example` with every Factor III var used so far (`VSIR_ENV`, `VSIR_QDRANT_URL`, `VSIR_RELEASE_ID`, `VSIR_LOG_LEVEL`, `VSIR_PORT`).\n- `GET /health` (always green if process is up) and `GET /ready` (red if Qdrant unreachable) per §15.1, minimal FastAPI app.\n- Structured JSON logs to stdout (no `logging.FileHandler` — §12.5 cloud-native grep); SIGTERM handler that exits cleanly (no in-flight work yet, so this is just the hook).\n- §0/§13 D1–D7 restated in README.\n\nWorking Deliverable:\n- `vsir` CLI binary with a working `doctor` subcommand and a minimal FastAPI process exposing `/health` and `/ready`.\n\nDemo Command:\n- `vsir doctor` — prints PASS/FAIL per boot check (Qdrant reachable, model id not `-latest`, release_id set) and exits non-zero on any FAIL.\n\nDeliverables (files):\n- `backend/vsir/cli.py` (written; skeleton only, ≈ `impl/scripts/interfaces_demo.py` for arg-parsing shape)\n- `backend/vsir/core/health.py` (written — boot checks only; `grounded_rate` logic is M2a's)\n- `backend/vsir/serve/app.py` (written — health/ready only; full app is M3's)\n- `Dockerfile`, `docker-compose.test.yml` (rewritten), `.env.example`, `requirements.txt`, `requirements.lock`\n- `README.md` (D1–D7 section)\n\nTwelve-Factor Notes:\n- Adds `.env.example` vars: `VSIR_ENV`, `VSIR_QDRANT_URL`, `VSIR_RELEASE_ID`, `VSIR_LOG_LEVEL`, `VSIR_PORT`.\n- JSON logs to stdout from process start; SIGTERM handler stub; no process-local correctness-bearing state introduced.\n\n---\n\nUnit ID: U002\nName: Test harness, conformance greps, and AGENTS.md\nMilestone: M0\nType: harness\nPriority: P0-Critical\nSize Estimate: Medium\nSpend: none\nDepends On: [U001]\nEnables: [U003]\nSpec References: [Spec §12.5, §4.4]\nInvariants Enforced: []\nFailure Rows Closed: []\nRequired Reading: [`pipeline-guide/IMPROVEMENTS.md` E6 (no tests — the register item this unit exists to not reproduce)]\n\nDescription:\n- Give every later unit a runnable, growing test/CI surface and turn the §12.5 conformance rules into an executable gate instead of a checklist.\n\nCore Requirements:\n- §12.5 conformance greps as a pytest module scoped to `backend/vsir/**` + `requirements*.txt` (never markdown, never the test's own file): no `MatchText`/`MatchTextAny` under `serve/`; no fuzzy/similarity/edit-distance library in requirements; no field named `score` in a response model; no model id ending `-latest`; no `alembic`/`sqlalchemy`; no `get_text(` outside `ingest/probe.py`; no `SCHEMA_CARD`/`IdClass`/`entity_keys`/`classify(`.\n- Cloud-native grep set, same scope + `Dockerfile*` + `docker-compose*.yml`: no `logging.FileHandler`; no image tagged `latest`; no credential literals (`api_key=`, `token=`, `Bearer ` + literal); no `if TESTING` / `if os.environ.get(\"TESTING\")` branches in `backend/vsir/**`; no `RetrievalState`-style module-level mutable session store.\n- `scripts/test-unit.sh`, `scripts/test-api.sh`, `scripts/test-e2e.sh` extended to run against this repo's actual layout (not placeholders); `scripts/test-paid.sh` added, gated on `VSIR_ALLOW_PAID=1`, refuses to run otherwise.\n- `AGENTS.md` filled with the real, working commands (not aspirational ones) for doctor/test-unit/test-api/test-paid.\n\nWorking Deliverable:\n- Runnable conformance-grep pytest module wired into `scripts/test-unit.sh`.\n\nDemo Command:\n- `bash scripts/test-unit.sh` — runs `vsir doctor`'s underlying checks plus the conformance-grep suite and prints PASS; introducing a `score` field or a `logging.FileHandler` anywhere in scope should be shown failing it once (reviewer can `git stash`/inject to see the red).\n\nDeliverables (files):\n- `backend/tests/unit/test_conformance.py` (written, net new)\n- `scripts/test-unit.sh`, `scripts/test-api.sh`, `scripts/test-e2e.sh`, `scripts/test-paid.sh` (written)\n- `AGENTS.md` (written)\n\nTwelve-Factor Notes:\n- N/A — adds no process, endpoint, tool or worker; it is test tooling only.\n\n---\n\nUnit ID: U003\nName: core/record, ids, and the INDEXED bootstrap\nMilestone: M1\nType: core\nPriority: P0-Critical\nSize Estimate: Medium\nSpend: none\nDepends On: [U001, U002]\nEnables: [U004]\nSpec References: [Spec §5.1, §5.3, §5.4, §5.5]\nInvariants Enforced: [I6]\nFailure Rows Closed: []\nRequired Reading: [`impl/app/pagemodel.py` (record shape and `make_page_id` — read first); `pipeline-guide/METADATA-CONTRACT.md` (§5.3); `IMPROVEMENTS.md` A5 (`image_path` — must NOT be reproduced in the record) and B1/B4 (provenance gaps — provenance must be a first-class field here)]\n\nDescription:\n- Port the page record shape and identifier scheme from `impl/app/pagemodel.py`, and stand up the single `INDEXED` dict that creates and will later gate the Qdrant schema.\n\nCore Requirements:\n- Read `impl/app/pagemodel.py` first.\n- `core/record.py` ≈ `pagemodel.py` (record shape only, no new business logic): facets / text+vlm_codes / three vectors dense+lexical+captions / nested `content` never filtered / provenance — explicitly NO `image_path` field (A5).\n- `core/ids.py` ≈ `pagemodel.py::make_page_id`: `page_id`/`section_id`/`series_id`/`point_id=uuid5(page_id)`/`run_id=ULID` per §5.1.\n- `core/indexed.py` (net new): the one `INDEXED` dict that will create, gate (M2a/M8) and be asserted at boot (I6); scope keys = INDEXED minus `text` and `vlm_codes`.\n- §5.5 `TextIndexParams`: WORD tokenizer, lowercase, `phrase_matching=True`, `min_token_len=1`; collection name carries dim (`pages_1536`).\n- Qdrant collection + text-index creation using an ephemeral/in-memory client for self-test.\n\nWorking Deliverable:\n- `vsir index selftest` CLI subcommand: creates an ephemeral Qdrant collection from `INDEXED`, builds one `core/record.py` record via `core/ids.py`, upserts and reads it back.\n\nDemo Command:\n- `vsir index selftest` — prints the created collection's schema (vector configs, text-index params) next to the round-tripped record, proving `INDEXED` and the record shape agree and that no `image_path` field exists anywhere in the payload.\n\nDeliverables (files):\n- `backend/vsir/core/record.py` (ported from `impl/app/pagemodel.py`, record-shape subset only)\n- `backend/vsir/core/ids.py` (ported from `impl/app/pagemodel.py::make_page_id`)\n- `backend/vsir/core/indexed.py` (written, net new)\n- `backend/tests/unit/test_record.py`, `backend/tests/unit/test_indexed.py` (written)\n\nTwelve-Factor Notes:\n- N/A for new env vars. The ephemeral Qdrant client used by `selftest` is in-process and disposable — not correctness-bearing state (no C11 violation).\n\n---\n\nUnit ID: U004\nName: tok/variants/exact_filter, Family A envelope, and rrf/sparse ports\nMilestone: M1\nType: core\nPriority: P0-Critical\nSize Estimate: Large\nSpend: none\nDepends On: [U003]\nEnables: [U005, U006]\nSpec References: [Spec §5.6, §7.1, §7.2.1 (ordering), §7.3]\nInvariants Enforced: [I3, I5]\nFailure Rows Closed: [F10]\nRequired Reading: [`impl/app/sparse.py` (read first — D2, ported verbatim where possible); `impl/app/retrieve.py` (read first — `rrf()` is ranks-only, decompose()); `IMPROVEMENTS.md` E9 (scroll-4096-and-filter-in-Python — the exact_filter and scope-key check must use a real Qdrant filter, never scroll+Python filtering)]\n\nDescription:\n- Build the single exact-match path, the Family A search/absence envelope, and port the deterministic ranks-only fusion machinery that every retrieval tool will reuse from M3 onward.\n\nCore Requirements:\n- Read `impl/app/sparse.py` and `impl/app/retrieve.py` first.\n- `core/tok.py`: mirrors Qdrant's WORD tokenizer exactly — NOT `impl`'s `TOKEN_RE` (named porting hazard, §5.6).\n- `core/variants.py`: exactly 3 spellings of the same characters (whitespace variants only).\n- `core/exact.py::exact_filter`: the ONLY exact-match path in the system; no `MatchText`/`MatchTextAny` anywhere else (I3).\n- §7.1 Family A envelope (`SearchResponse[HitT]`): six-value status enum scaffold (`ok`/four absences/`error` — full absence semantics land in M2a–M4 as data becomes available), `empty_is_never_ok` validator, `WEAK_ABS=20` server constant, `weak`/`needs_scope` formula, hit models `DocHit`/`SectionHit`/`PageHit`/`LookupHit`/`ResolveHit`, `ImageRef`/`Preview` types (references only, no bytes).\n- §7.3 cap validators as typed 400s: `dpi_not_allowed`, `dpi_requires_region`, `filter_unknown_key {keys}` — the last one is what closes F10 using `core/indexed.py`'s scope-key set from U003.\n- Port `sparse.py` (D2) and `rrf()` (ranks-only fusion, `rrf_k=60`, weights page 1.0/lexical 1.0/captions 0.4) verbatim as `core` utilities for reuse by M3's/M4's tools.\n\nWorking Deliverable:\n- `vsir index selftest --query <text>` extension: runs `tok`/`variants`/`exact_filter` against the seeded collection and prints a Family A envelope.\n\nDemo Command:\n- `vsir index selftest --query \"SF 1.1A\"` — prints the 3 whitespace variants generated, the exact_filter Qdrant filter used, and a valid `SearchResponse` JSON; then `vsir index selftest --query \"\" --unknown-scope-key foo` to show `filter_unknown_key` as a typed 400 (F10).\n\nDeliverables (files):\n- `backend/vsir/core/tok.py`, `backend/vsir/core/variants.py`, `backend/vsir/core/exact.py` (written, net new)\n- `backend/vsir/core/envelope.py` (written, net new — Family A only; Family B in U006)\n- `backend/vsir/core/sparse.py` (ported from `impl/app/sparse.py`)\n- `backend/vsir/core/rrf.py` (ported from `impl/app/retrieve.py::rrf`)\n- `backend/tests/unit/test_exact.py`, `backend/tests/unit/test_envelope.py`, `backend/tests/unit/test_rrf.py` (written)\n\nTwelve-Factor Notes:\n- N/A — adds no process, endpoint, tool or worker; pure library code exercised through the existing `selftest` CLI.\n\n---\n\nUnit ID: U005\nName: Synthetic fixtures, observed-token inventory, and `vsir demo exact`\nMilestone: M1\nType: core\nPriority: P0-Critical\nSize Estimate: Medium\nSpend: none\nDepends On: [U004]\nEnables: [U006]\nSpec References: [Spec §6.8 (observed-token inventory subset), §12.4, §7.2.2]\nInvariants Enforced: [I2]\nFailure Rows Closed: [F1, F3, F14]\nRequired Reading: [`impl/app/retrieve.py::lookup` (read first — being rewritten as a phrase filter per §5.6); `IMPROVEMENTS.md` A1 (always-extract-text — not relevant to hand-written fixtures, but the pattern this unit must avoid once probe.py exists in M2a)]\n\nDescription:\n- Seed an ephemeral Qdrant with four hand-written pages (no PDF) and wire `lookup` end to end as the flagship, zero-spend M1 proof.\n\nCore Requirements:\n- Hand-write four synthetic pages' `text` fields directly into `core/record.py` records (bypassing any VLM/probe step, since none exists yet): (1) a page containing the literal string `SF 1.1A`; (2) a page with tokens `sf`, `1`, `1a` scattered non-adjacently; (3) a page printing `SF121.1)`; (4) a page whose `vlm_codes` claims `K999` but whose `text` does not contain it.\n- `serve/tools/lookup.py`'s core logic lives here as `core`-level function (the HTTP/MCP wrapper comes in M3): `lookup(label, scope?, include_unverified=False, cap=20)` — exact, phrase-only, a set not a ranking, using `exact_filter` from U004.\n- Build the observed-token inventory (§6.8 subset only — display data, not the full export pipeline) from the four seeded pages so `present_instead` (U006) works before any PDF exists.\n- `lookup(\"K999\")` on the hallucinated-claim page → `not_found` (I2); `include_unverified=True` returns it separately in `unverified_hits`, `verified: false`, never merged into `hits`.\n- §12.4's 8 compact-label variants exercised against page (2)/(3) to prove I3's variant matching in practice (F3).\n\nWorking Deliverable:\n- `vsir demo exact --synthetic` CLI subcommand — the milestone's official demo.\n\nDemo Command:\n- `vsir demo exact --synthetic` — seeds the four pages into an ephemeral Qdrant, then runs `lookup(\"SF 1.1A\")` (exactly 1 hit — F1), `lookup(\"sf1.1a\")`/7 other compact spellings (all resolve to the same page — F3), and `lookup(\"K999\")` (→ `not_found`, `unverified_hits` only with `include_unverified=True` — F14/I2).\n\nDeliverables (files):\n- `backend/vsir/core/lookup.py` (written — core lookup logic; tool wrapper is M3's `serve/tools/lookup.py`)\n- `backend/vsir/core/observed_tokens.py` (written, net new — §6.8 subset)\n- `data/fixtures/synthetic_pages/*.json` (written — 4 hand-written page records)\n- `backend/tests/unit/test_lookup.py`, `backend/tests/unit/test_observed_tokens.py` (written)\n\nTwelve-Factor Notes:\n- N/A — adds no process, endpoint, tool or worker.\n\n---\n\nUnit ID: U006\nName: core/verify.py, present_instead, and Family B envelope\nMilestone: M1\nType: core\nPriority: P0-Critical\nSize Estimate: Medium\nSpend: none\nDepends On: [U004, U005]\nEnables: [U007]\nSpec References: [Spec §7.1 (Family B), §7.2.4, §12.4]\nInvariants Enforced: []\nFailure Rows Closed: [F2 (core), F16]\nRequired Reading: [`impl/app/retrieve.py` (verify-adjacent logic, read first — no direct `verify` predecessor, this is mostly net new per layout note); `IMPROVEMENTS.md` — confirms `present_instead` must never become a distance/similarity function (guards against reintroducing a fuzzy-match library, which U002's conformance grep also catches)]\n\nDescription:\n- Implement per-`(claim, page)` verification and the deterministic near-miss generator, and define the Family B envelope used by `verify`/`fetch`/`read`.\n\nCore Requirements:\n- `core/verify.py::verify_claims`: per `(claim, page)` — not per claim — so a draft citing `p001–p002` cannot let a code from the neighbouring page through (this is the mechanism I8 will later gate on; the tool wrapper comes at M3).\n- Three states only: `present | absent | unverifiable` — same vocabulary `read` will reuse later (§7.2.6).\n- `present_instead`: a prefix lookup over U005's observed-token inventory, capped at 5, labelled \"different part\" — never a distance (F16).\n- §12.4 near-miss generator: produces the adversarial near-miss set (e.g. `K73` on a page only containing `K78`) used both here and later by M3's `vsir eval abstention`.\n- Family B envelope (`ToolEnvelope[ResultT]`, `VerifyResult`): `status: ok|error` describes whether the call ran, not what it found; a page with every claim `absent` is still `status: ok`.\n\nWorking Deliverable:\n- `vsir demo exact --synthetic --verify <claims>` extension to U005's CLI.\n\nDemo Command:\n- `vsir demo exact --synthetic --verify K73,K158,K999` — prints a `VerifyResult` map showing `K158: present`, `K73: absent` with `present_instead` from the near-miss fixture, and `K999: absent` with `present_instead: []` (F2 core, F16).\n\nDeliverables (files):\n- `backend/vsir/core/verify.py` (written, net new)\n- `backend/vsir/core/nearmiss.py` (written, net new — §12.4 generator)\n- `backend/vsir/core/envelope.py` (extended — Family B added alongside U004's Family A)\n- `backend/tests/unit/test_verify.py`, `backend/tests/unit/test_nearmiss.py` (written)\n\nTwelve-Factor Notes:\n- N/A — adds no process, endpoint, tool or worker.\n\n---\n\nUnit ID: U007\nName: manifest, probe, render, doc-facts, and windowing\nMilestone: M2a\nType: ingest\nPriority: P0-Critical\nSize Estimate: Large\nSpend: none\nDepends On: [U001, U006]\nEnables: [U008]\nSpec References: [Spec §6.1 (steps 01–05), §6.2, §6.4]\nInvariants Enforced: []\nFailure Rows Closed: [F4 (M2a half), F13, F15]\nRequired Reading: [`impl/app/textlayer.py` (read first — `probe`/`page_texts`/`content_hash`); `impl/app/render.py` (read first); `impl/app/windows.py` (read first); `impl/pipeline-guide/01-entry.md`, `02-probe-and-render.md`, `03-document-facts.md`, `04-windowing-and-keys.md`; `IMPROVEMENTS.md` A1 (always-extract-text — probe.py must gate on actual text presence, not extract unconditionally) and E3 (rendering never collected — render outputs must be eligible for cache eviction, not accumulate unbounded)]\n\nDescription:\n- Port the entry manifest, text-layer probing, page rendering, document facts, and the bisecting windowing ladder, and generate the checked-in 3-window synthetic PDF fixture with its off-by-one and crop traps.\n\nCore Requirements:\n- Read `impl/app/textlayer.py`, `impl/app/render.py`, `impl/app/windows.py` first.\n- `ingest/manifest.py` ≈ `impl/app/pipeline.py` (entry/manifest only — step 01).\n- `ingest/probe.py` ← `textlayer.py::probe/page_texts/content_hash` (steps 02–04: `has_text` facet, full-page text extraction, `content_hash`, doc facts/`doc_type`).\n- `ingest/render.py` ← `render.py`, rendering at `dpi_index=150` (§4.2).\n- `ingest/window.py` ← `windows.py` (+ bisection ladder, F13): target 30 pages/window; bisect-and-re-bill on `MAX_TOKENS`/truncation/offset-failure; typed `window_unsplittable`; v1 is Level 0/1 + bisection only — a Level-2 document fails typed `ladder_level_2_required` (this unit defines the check; M8 exercises it against a real Level-2-marked fixture).\n- §6.4 the two independent offset checks (mechanism only here; the gate that gates on them is M2a's `gates.py`, U011).\n- Generate `data/source/synthetic_3window.pdf`: known printed labels, a deliberate off-by-one trap (printed page numbers vs. physical index diverge), and a crop trap (a code visually cropped at render time but present in the underlying full-page text) — proves `text` always comes from the full page (F15), independent of any render crop.\n\nWorking Deliverable:\n- `vsir ingest <pdf> --vlm stub --until window` (the `--until` debug flag is added here and reused by U008–U010).\n\nDemo Command:\n- `vsir ingest data/source/synthetic_3window.pdf --vlm stub --until window` — prints per-page `has_text`/`content_hash`/doc facts and the resulting window plan (3 windows), and confirms the crop-trap page's indexed `text` contains the full label despite the render crop.\n\nDeliverables (files):\n- `backend/vsir/ingest/manifest.py` (ported from `impl/app/pipeline.py`, entry subset)\n- `backend/vsir/ingest/probe.py` (ported from `impl/app/textlayer.py`)\n- `backend/vsir/ingest/render.py` (ported from `impl/app/render.py`)\n- `backend/vsir/ingest/window.py` (ported from `impl/app/windows.py`, + bisection ladder written net new)\n- `data/source/synthetic_3window.pdf` (written, generated fixture, checked in)\n- `backend/tests/unit/test_probe.py`, `test_render.py`, `test_window.py` (written)\n\nTwelve-Factor Notes:\n- Adds `.env.example` vars: `VSIR_RASTER_CACHE_DIR` (tmpfs path from U001's Dockerfile, not correctness-bearing — rasters are always re-derivable from the PDF, C11-safe).\n- No process-local correctness state: window plans and facts are recomputed from the PDF + content_hash, never cached to disk outside the ephemeral raster cache.\n\n---\n\nUnit ID: U008\nName: VLM stub/client/cache and S2 extraction\nMilestone: M2a\nType: ingest\nPriority: P0-Critical\nSize Estimate: Large\nSpend: none\nDepends On: [U007]\nEnables: [U009]\nSpec References: [Spec §5.2, §6.1 (step 06), §6.3]\nInvariants Enforced: []\nFailure Rows Closed: [F11 (M2a key half)]\nRequired Reading: [`impl/app/segment.py` (read first — Gemini call shape and the old S1 schema being replaced); `impl/pipeline-guide/05-extraction.md`, `../SEGMENTATION.md`; `IMPROVEMENTS.md` B6 (pin the model — `vlm/client.py` must hard-fail on an alias id, reusing U001's boot check pattern) and D3 (captions never written — this unit must actually populate the captions field this VLM call produces, since M1's `rrf` already expects a captions branch)]\n\nDescription:\n- Build the VLM abstraction (stub and real client scaffolding, cache, prompts) and the S2 window extraction step, with `VSIR_VLM=stub` selected purely by config.\n\nCore Requirements:\n- Read `impl/app/segment.py` first.\n- `vlm/client.py` (net new): thin Gemini wrapper; pinned model id only (never `-latest`, reuses U001's boot check).\n- `vlm/stub.py` (net new): deterministic, fixture-driven fake VLM responses selected by `VSIR_VLM=stub` — config, never a code branch or `if TESTING` (rule 5).\n- `vlm/cache.py` (net new): §6.3 cache keys — `facts_key`, `extract_key` (model id + prompt version; `VSIR_VLM_TIER` is explicitly NOT part of `extract_key`).\n- `vlm/prompts/s1.md`, `s2.md` (net new prompt text, versioned).\n- `ingest/extract.py` ≈ `impl/app/segment.py` (new S2 schema per §5.2: `PageOut`/`SectionRef`/`Summary`/`WindowOut`; **Prohibited**: any identifier grammar, classification enum, regex taxonomy, or per-corpus keyword list).\n- Replay mode: `VSIR_VLM=stub` + `VSIR_FIXTURE=<dir>` with a typed `fixture_miss` when the fixture directory lacks the requested key.\n\nWorking Deliverable:\n- `vsir ingest <pdf> --vlm stub --until extract`.\n\nDemo Command:\n- `vsir ingest data/source/synthetic_3window.pdf --vlm stub --until extract` — prints the raw S2 `WindowOut` JSON per window from the stub VLM, and re-running with a changed prompt version shows a different `extract_key` (F11 key half).\n\nDeliverables (files):\n- `backend/vsir/vlm/client.py`, `vlm/stub.py`, `vlm/cache.py` (written, net new)\n- `backend/vsir/vlm/prompts/s1.md`, `vlm/prompts/s2.md` (written, net new)\n- `backend/vsir/ingest/extract.py` (ported from `impl/app/segment.py`, schema rewritten to S2)\n- `backend/tests/unit/test_extract.py`, `test_vlm_cache.py` (written)\n\nTwelve-Factor Notes:\n- Adds `.env.example` vars: `VSIR_VLM` (`stub|real`), `VSIR_VLM_MODEL`, `VSIR_VLM_TIER`, `VSIR_FIXTURE`, `GEMINI_API_KEY` (unused until real path, but declared here since the client scaffold reads it).\n- Stub-vs-real is purely `VSIR_VLM` config, no code branch; no VLM output cached to local disk outside the declared `VSIR_FIXTURE` path (which is itself read-only, checked-in fixture data, not runtime state).\n\n---\n\nUnit ID: U009\nName: Derivation, gating removal, and stitching\nMilestone: M2a\nType: ingest\nPriority: P0-Critical\nSize Estimate: Large\nSpend: none\nDepends On: [U008]\nEnables: [U010]\nSpec References: [Spec §6.1 (steps 07–08), §6.5, §5.7]\nInvariants Enforced: []\nFailure Rows Closed: [F5 (M2a half), F6, F8 (M2a stitching half)]\nRequired Reading: [`impl/app/segment.py` (read first — derivation logic being carried without the allowlist gate); `impl/app/stitch.py` (read first); `impl/pipeline-guide/06-derivation-and-gate.md` (⚠ documents the DELETED allowlist gate — do not port it), `07-stitch-and-numbering.md`; `IMPROVEMENTS.md` — confirms the allowlist/`classify()` pattern must not reappear (also enforced mechanically by U002's conformance grep)]\n\nDescription:\n- Port per-page derivation (grounded_rate, no allowlist gate) and section stitching with cross-window carry-in and code reattribution.\n\nCore Requirements:\n- Read `impl/app/segment.py` and `impl/app/stitch.py` first.\n- `ingest/derive.py` ≈ `segment.py` (derivation logic only, the allowlist/`classify()` gate is deleted — grounded_rate replaces it per §5.7: `None` where `has_text` is false).\n- Label precedence + ambiguity → list; code reattribution with `moved_from` when a code derived on one page actually belongs on its neighbour (F6, per-page `grounded_rate`).\n- `ingest/stitch.py` ← `stitch.py` (sections, + `series_id`): canonical section key + carry-in across window boundaries so a straddling section is not mistaken for a fully-searched chapter (F8, stitching half).\n\nWorking Deliverable:\n- `vsir ingest <pdf> --vlm stub --until stitch`.\n\nDemo Command:\n- `vsir ingest data/source/synthetic_3window.pdf --vlm stub --until stitch` — prints stitched `PageOut` records with `section_id`, per-page `grounded_rate`, and (on a fixture with a deliberately misattributed code) the `moved_from` field populated.\n\nDeliverables (files):\n- `backend/vsir/ingest/derive.py` (ported from `impl/app/segment.py`, gate removed)\n- `backend/vsir/ingest/stitch.py` (ported from `impl/app/stitch.py`, + `series_id` written net new)\n- `backend/tests/unit/test_derive.py`, `test_stitch.py` (written)\n\nTwelve-Factor Notes:\n- N/A — adds no process, endpoint, tool or worker.\n\n---\n\nUnit ID: U010\nName: Embedding and indexing\nMilestone: M2a\nType: ingest\nPriority: P0-Critical\nSize Estimate: Large\nSpend: none\nDepends On: [U009]\nEnables: [U011]\nSpec References: [Spec §6.1 (steps 09–10), §6.6, §4.2 (D4, D12)]\nInvariants Enforced: []\nFailure Rows Closed: []\nRequired Reading: [`impl/app/embedder.py` (read first — D4 interleaved embedding); `impl/app/sparse.py` (read first, D2 — reused from U004's port); `impl/app/segstore.py` (read first); `pipeline-guide/08-embedding.md`, `09-indexing.md` (⚠ `entity_keys` index deleted — do not port it); `IMPROVEMENTS.md` B5 (cache embeddings — do not silently reuse stale embeddings across a fingerprint change) and D3 (captions never written — the captions vector must actually be populated and indexed here, completing what U008 started) and E7 (orphan points — index.py must never leave points without a valid run/publish linkage)]\n\nDescription:\n- Port dense/lexical/captions embedding and Qdrant upsert with the `is_current` flag and embedding-fingerprint protection.\n\nCore Requirements:\n- Read `impl/app/embedder.py`, `impl/app/sparse.py`, `impl/app/segstore.py` first.\n- `ingest/embed.py` ← `embedder.py` (D4 interleaved dense embedding: page image + text + captions in one call shape); reuses U004's ported `sparse.py` for the lexical branch.\n- `ingest/index.py` ≈ `segstore.py` (+ text indexes, `is_current`): Qdrant upsert using `point_id=uuid5(page_id)` from U003, `INDEXED` schema from U003, `is_current=False` at this stage (publish flips it — U011).\n- §6.6 embedding fingerprint `{embed_model, dim, distance, composition_version}`: refuse to upsert on mismatch; on mismatch, new collection + re-embed + alias swap (no in-place mutation).\n- dim ∈ {768, 1536, 3072}, concurrency=8, batch_size=8, max_edge_px=1568 per §4.2.\n\nWorking Deliverable:\n- `vsir ingest <pdf> --vlm stub --until index`.\n\nDemo Command:\n- `vsir ingest data/source/synthetic_3window.pdf --vlm stub --until index` — ingests into the ephemeral Qdrant with `is_current=False`; a follow-up raw scroll/count shows N points with correct `point_id`s and the fingerprint stamped in the collection's payload schema; re-running with a mutated `embed_model` shows the refusal.\n\nDeliverables (files):\n- `backend/vsir/ingest/embed.py` (ported from `impl/app/embedder.py`)\n- `backend/vsir/ingest/index.py` (ported from `impl/app/segstore.py`, + text indexes/`is_current` written net new)\n- `backend/tests/unit/test_embed.py`, `test_index.py` (written)\n\nTwelve-Factor Notes:\n- Adds `.env.example` vars: `VSIR_EMBED_MODEL`, `VSIR_EMBED_DIM`, `VSIR_EMBED_CONCURRENCY`, `VSIR_EMBED_BATCH_SIZE`.\n- No local embedding cache on disk; the fingerprint check is enforced against the Qdrant collection itself, never a local file (C11).\n\n---\n\nUnit ID: U011\nName: Gates, export, and run orchestration\nMilestone: M2a\nType: ingest\nPriority: P0-Critical\nSize Estimate: Large\nSpend: none\nDepends On: [U010]\nEnables: [U012, U014]\nSpec References: [Spec §6.1 (steps 11–12), §6.4, §6.7, §6.8, §6.9, §11.1, §4.4]\nInvariants Enforced: [I1, I4, I7]\nFailure Rows Closed: [F7, F12 (M2a half), F17]\nRequired Reading: [`impl/app/pipeline.py`, `impl/app/segjobs.py` (read first — run orchestration being restructured); `pipeline-guide/10-gates-and-publish.md` (⚠ allowlist/`class_totality` replaced by `grounded_rate`), `11-export.md` (⚠ `withheld.jsonl` dropped from this step — it lives only as a frozen M2b parity artefact); `12-reproducibility.md` (§6.3/§6.6); `IMPROVEMENTS.md` E2 (job state on daemon threads — run state must live in the `vsir_runs` Qdrant collection, never a Python thread/global) and E7 (orphan points — the three-clause retirement rule this unit implements exists specifically to prevent this)]\n\nDescription:\n- Close the pipeline: publish gating, the `vsir_runs` control collection, the three-clause retirement rule, exports, and the run record — the unit that makes `vsir ingest` a complete, gated, resumable-by-contract pipeline.\n\nCore Requirements:\n- Read `impl/app/pipeline.py` and `impl/app/segjobs.py` first.\n- `ingest/gates.py` ≈ `pipeline.py` (grounded_rate replaces the allowlist, §11.1): `window_coverage` (block, must be 1.0), `offset_check` (block, both §6.4 checks pass — I4), `grounded_rate ≥ 0.8` provisional (block, `vsir publish --override grounded_rate --reason \"…\"` records `published_with_override`), `text_coverage` (flag `mostly_scanned`, never block; **at 0.0 the grounded_rate gate is skipped entirely**), `label_monotonic` (flag `label_conflict`).\n- `ingest/export.py` (net new): `labels.jsonl` + `observed_tokens.jsonl` streamed over HTTP (§6.8); `safety_flag` derived from manifest `doc_type` + model topics — never a keyword list.\n- `ingest/run.py` ≈ `pipeline.py`/`segjobs.py`: `vsir_runs` control collection (run + window points, state enum `{queued,running,stopped,gated,published,failed}`), advisory lease + `--steal`, §6.7 three-clause retirement (delete same doc+revision earlier `run_id` → F12; set prior *other* revision `is_current=False` and KEEP → F9, owned by M8 since it needs a second revision; never touch other documents).\n- I1: `point_id` uniqueness + `count(doc,rev) == pdf.page_count` asserted after publish. I7: `is_current=False` until gates pass; every tool injects `is_current=True` by default (mechanism proven here, tool-level default enforced from M3 onward).\n- `vsir runs show <run_id>`, `vsir gates rerun <run_id>`, `vsir publish --override <gate> --reason` (§4.4).\n- F17 proof: kill an ingest mid-run (SIGKILL the process) → 0 pages queryable (because `is_current` never flipped).\n\nWorking Deliverable:\n- `vsir ingest <pdf> --vlm stub` (full pipeline, no `--until`) + `vsir runs show` + `vsir gates rerun` + `vsir publish --override`.\n\nDemo Command:\n- `vsir ingest data/source/synthetic_3window.pdf --vlm stub && vsir runs show <run_id>` — the milestone demo: run reaches `published`, gate results shown, F7's off-by-one trap fixture proven caught by `offset_check`, and a second identical ingest shown retiring the first run's points without touching anything else (F12).\n\nDeliverables (files):\n- `backend/vsir/ingest/gates.py` (ported from `impl/app/pipeline.py`, gate logic replaced per §11.1)\n- `backend/vsir/ingest/export.py` (written, net new)\n- `backend/vsir/ingest/run.py` (ported from `impl/app/pipeline.py` / `impl/app/segjobs.py`)\n- `backend/vsir/core/status.py` (written, net new — run state enum)\n- `backend/tests/unit/test_gates.py`, `test_export.py`, `test_run.py` (written)\n- `backend/tests/api/test_publish_gating.py` (written — F17 kill-mid-run proof)\n\nTwelve-Factor Notes:\n- Adds `.env.example` vars: `VSIR_GROUNDED_RATE_THRESHOLD` (provisional, 0.8 — reset by M2b's R4), `VSIR_LEASE_TTL_SECONDS`.\n- Run/window state lives entirely in the `vsir_runs` Qdrant collection — no daemon threads, no local job-state files (E2); SIGTERM during ingest leaves the run in `stopped` state, resumable, not `published` (full checkpoint granularity is M8's).\n\n---\n\nUnit ID: U012\nName: Port legacy fixtures and parity/negative sets\nMilestone: M2b\nType: eval\nPriority: P1-High\nSize Estimate: Medium\nSpend: none\nDepends On: [U011]\nEnables: [U013]\nSpec References: [Spec §6.8, §12.1, §17 (OQ-1)]\nInvariants Enforced: []\nFailure Rows Closed: []\nRequired Reading: [`impl/data/raw/*` (read first — old-schema baseline being ported as-is); `impl/data/exports/r-poc-*/labels.jsonl`, `withheld.jsonl` (read first — the parity and negative sets)]\n\nDescription:\n- Port already-paid-for legacy pipeline outputs into this repo as fixtures, before spending anything new, so the real M2b ingest (U013) has a parity baseline to check against.\n\nCore Requirements:\n- Copy `impl/data/raw/*` → `data/fixtures/legacy/` verbatim as the old-schema baseline (no reshaping — this is intentionally the *old* schema, kept for comparison).\n- Copy `impl/data/exports/r-poc-*/labels.jsonl` and `withheld.jsonl` → `data/fixtures/legacy/` as the parity set and the negative set respectively.\n- `vsir eval parity` (net new CLI subcommand): loads the legacy fixtures, reports counts and basic shape validation (labels present, withheld codes present) — pure read, no model call, so it can run before U013's real spend and before any new-schema data exists.\n- Note OQ-1 (pilot PDF location) blocks only U013's re-bill, not this unit — the S2 responses this unit ports are already paid for and sitting in `impl/data/raw/*`.\n\nWorking Deliverable:\n- `vsir eval parity` CLI subcommand.\n\nDemo Command:\n- `vsir eval parity --legacy data/fixtures/legacy` — prints row counts for the ported `labels.jsonl`/`withheld.jsonl` and confirms the legacy raw dump loads without error.\n\nDeliverables (files):\n- `data/fixtures/legacy/*` (ported verbatim from `impl/data/raw/*` and `impl/data/exports/r-poc-*/`)\n- `backend/vsir/cli.py` (extended — `eval parity` subcommand)\n- `backend/vsir/core/parity.py` (written, net new)\n- `backend/tests/unit/test_parity.py` (written)\n\nTwelve-Factor Notes:\n- N/A — adds no process, endpoint, tool or worker; pure fixture loading.\n\n---\n\nUnit ID: U013\nName: Real TC1E-SF ingest and grounded_rate threshold\nMilestone: M2b\nType: ingest\nPriority: P0-Critical\nSize Estimate: Large\nSpend: paid\nDepends On: [U012, U011]\nEnables: [U016, U019]\nSpec References: [Spec §6.7, §11.1 (R4), §17 (OQ-1, OQ-2)]\nInvariants Enforced: []\nFailure Rows Closed: []\nRequired Reading: [`impl/INGESTION_WALKTHROUGH.md` (M2a/M2b debugging); `IMPROVEMENTS.md` — reconfirm B6 (pinned model) applies to this, the first real Gemini call in the whole plan]\n\nDescription:\n- Run the one real, paid ingest of TC1E-SF (55 pages) under the new S2 schema, freeze the resulting fixtures, and set the `grounded_rate` publish threshold from the observed distribution.\n\nCore Requirements:\n- `VSIR_ALLOW_PAID=1 vsir ingest data/source/TC1E-SF.pdf` (real VLM path via U008's `vlm/client.py`, real embedding via U010's `ingest/embed.py`) — this is the FIRST real spend anywhere in the plan; refuses to run without `VSIR_ALLOW_PAID=1`.\n- Freeze `data/fixtures/TC1E-SF/{raw_window_1.json, raw_window_2.json, text.json, expected.json}` from this one run, for use as `VSIR_FIXTURE` replay data by every later paid unit (U019, U020, U022).\n- Report the `grounded_rate` distribution across the 55 pages and set `VSIR_GROUNDED_RATE_THRESHOLD` from it (R4), replacing U011's provisional 0.8.\n- Runs through the same `vsir ingest`/`vsir gates rerun`/`vsir publish` surface built in U011 — no new pipeline code, only real credentials and real data.\n\nWorking Deliverable:\n- The same `vsir ingest`/`vsir runs show` CLI from U011, now exercised against real data and a real Gemini key.\n\nDemo Command:\n- `VSIR_ALLOW_PAID=1 vsir ingest data/source/TC1E-SF.pdf && vsir runs show <run_id>` — shows a published run over 55 real pages, with the grounded_rate distribution report printed and the frozen fixture files written to `data/fixtures/TC1E-SF/`.\n\nDeliverables (files):\n- `data/fixtures/TC1E-SF/raw_window_1.json`, `raw_window_2.json`, `text.json`, `expected.json` (written, frozen from the real run)\n- `backend/vsir/core/grounded_rate_report.py` (written, net new — distribution report used to set R4)\n- `.env.example` updated with the resolved `VSIR_GROUNDED_RATE_THRESHOLD` documented as \"set by M2b, see report\"\n\nTwelve-Factor Notes:\n- Uses `GEMINI_API_KEY` (declared in U008's `.env.example`) and `VSIR_ALLOW_PAID` (declared here) — no literal credentials committed anywhere (per U002's conformance grep).\n- Blocked on OQ-1 (pilot PDF location) and OQ-2 (Gemini key) per §17 — this unit cannot run until both are resolved; everything upstream of it (U001–U012) is provable without either.\n\n---\n\nUnit ID: U014\nName: serve/app, auth, audit, and budget scaffolding\nMilestone: M3\nType: tool\nPriority: P0-Critical\nSize Estimate: Medium\nSpend: none\nDepends On: [U011, U002]\nEnables: [U015]\nSpec References: [Spec §7.4, §11.3, §15.1]\nInvariants Enforced: []\nFailure Rows Closed: []\nRequired Reading: [`impl/app/main.py` (read first — HTTP app shape being restructured); `IMPROVEMENTS.md` E5 (no auth — the defect this unit directly closes) and E4 (no cost observability — audit line must carry cost, never expose it in the response body)]\n\nDescription:\n- Build the real FastAPI serving app with bearer auth, the ten-field audit log, and request budget scaffolding, replacing U001's minimal health-only stub.\n\nCore Requirements:\n- Read `impl/app/main.py` first.\n- `serve/app.py` ≈ `main.py`: full app boot, reusing U001's `/health`/`/ready` and its boot self-check (INDEXED schema assertion — refuse to serve at boot if schema mismatches, per §11.3).\n- `serve/auth.py` (net new): bearer token auth on every route except `/health`.\n- `serve/audit.py` (net new): the ten-field audit line per request (§7.4) — cost recorded in the audit log, never in the response body.\n- `serve/budget.py` (net new): per-caller request budget scaffolding; `reads_remaining` computed and available for every envelope (actual `read` quota consumption is wired in M5).\n- §11.3 degradation rows relevant here: Qdrant unreachable → `503 qdrant_unavailable` (never an empty result); embedding-model/collection fingerprint mismatch → refuse to upsert (already built in U010, wired to a 503 here at the serving layer too).\n\nWorking Deliverable:\n- `vsir serve` CLI subcommand starting the full authenticated app.\n\nDemo Command:\n- `vsir serve &` then `curl localhost:8000/health` (200, no auth needed) vs. `curl localhost:8000/pages/x/image` (401 without a bearer token) — and the resulting audit log line printed to stdout showing the ten fields including cost=0.\n\nDeliverables (files):\n- `backend/vsir/serve/app.py` (ported from `impl/app/main.py`)\n- `backend/vsir/serve/auth.py`, `serve/audit.py`, `serve/budget.py` (written, net new)\n- `backend/tests/api/test_auth.py`, `test_audit.py` (written)\n\nTwelve-Factor Notes:\n- Adds `.env.example` vars: `VSIR_API_TOKEN` (bearer secret, never a literal in code), `VSIR_READ_QUOTA_PER_CALLER`.\n- Structured JSON audit lines to stdout (no file handler); stateless — auth/budget state derived per-request from the token, no session store.\n\n---\n\nUnit ID: U015\nName: lookup/verify HTTP+MCP tools\nMilestone: M3\nType: tool\nPriority: P0-Critical\nSize Estimate: Large\nSpend: none\nDepends On: [U014, U004, U006]\nEnables: [U016, U017]\nSpec References: [Spec §7.2.2, §7.2.4, §7.5, §7.6]\nInvariants Enforced: []\nFailure Rows Closed: [F2 (tool half), F4 (M3 half)]\nRequired Reading: [`impl/app/retrieve.py::lookup` (read first — being rewritten as a phrase filter per §5.6); `impl/app/api_models.py` (read first — envelope wiring precedent); `IMPROVEMENTS.md` E9 (scroll-4096-and-filter-in-Python — the HTTP layer must call U004's `exact_filter`, never re-implement filtering client-side)]\n\nDescription:\n- Wrap M1's core `lookup`/`verify` logic as the first two real tools, exposed identically over HTTP and MCP, closing the tool-layer halves of F2 and F4.\n\nCore Requirements:\n- Read `impl/app/retrieve.py::lookup` and `impl/app/api_models.py` first.\n- `serve/envelope.py` ≈ `api_models.py`: wires U004's Family A / U006's Family B pydantic models into actual HTTP response models, with the full six-value status enum surfaced (`not_found`, `not_searchable`, `out_of_scope`, `found_only_in_superseded`, `error`, `ok`) — `not_searchable` now reachable end-to-end against a real scanned candidate from M2a data (F4, M3 half).\n- `serve/tools/lookup.py` ≈ `retrieve.py::lookup` (rewritten as phrase filter): thin HTTP wrapper over `core/lookup.py`.\n- `serve/tools/verify.py` (net new): thin HTTP wrapper over `core/verify.py::verify_claims` — this is the tool-layer half of F2 (`verify` confirming a code not on the page must 400/absent, never silently pass).\n- `mcp/server.py` (net new): stdio + SSE transport, exposing `lookup` and `verify` through the exact SAME implementations as the HTTP routes (stateless, §7.5) — no second copy of the logic.\n- §7.6 refusals enforced at this boundary: no `score` field, no routing, no composing outside the runner, no fuzzy matching (all also caught mechanically by U002's conformance grep).\n- CLI one-shots: `vsir lookup`, `vsir verify` (§4.4).\n\nWorking Deliverable:\n- `vsir serve` with working `/lookup` and `/verify` routes, plus `vsir mcp --stdio`/`--sse` exposing the same two tools.\n\nDemo Command:\n- `vsir serve &` then `vsir lookup \"SF 1.1A\" && vsir verify --claims K73 --pages TC1E-SF@1.3#p008` — plus the same two calls issued over `vsir mcp --stdio` piped JSON-RPC, showing byte-identical envelope bodies (proving \"same implementations\").\n\nDeliverables (files):\n- `backend/vsir/serve/envelope.py` (ported from `impl/app/api_models.py`)\n- `backend/vsir/serve/tools/lookup.py` (ported from `impl/app/retrieve.py::lookup`)\n- `backend/vsir/serve/tools/verify.py` (written, net new)\n- `backend/vsir/mcp/server.py` (written, net new)\n- `backend/vsir/cli.py` (extended — `lookup`, `verify`, `serve`, `mcp` subcommands)\n- `backend/tests/api/test_lookup_route.py`, `test_verify_route.py`, `backend/tests/unit/test_mcp_server.py` (written)\n\nTwelve-Factor Notes:\n- MCP server is stateless like the HTTP app — no per-session state; SSE/stdio transport selectable via `.env.example` var `VSIR_MCP_TRANSPORT` (default `stdio`).\n\n---\n\nUnit ID: U016\nName: Acceptance and abstention eval harness\nMilestone: M3\nType: eval\nPriority: P1-High\nSize Estimate: Medium\nSpend: none\nDepends On: [U015]\nEnables: []\nSpec References: [Spec §12.3, §12.4]\nInvariants Enforced: []\nFailure Rows Closed: []\nRequired Reading: [`impl/pipeline-guide/12-reproducibility.md` (§6.3/§6.6 — determinism the eval relies on)]\n\nDescription:\n- Turn §12.3's absolute acceptance table and §12.4's adversarial abstention set into runnable CLI eval commands.\n\nCore Requirements:\n- `vsir eval acceptance` (net new): runs the §12.3 L2 acceptance table (absolute, not comparative — C10) against whatever corpus is currently indexed and published (M2a's synthetic doc now; M2b's TC1E-SF once U013 lands — this unit does not itself require U013, per the ledger note that real-corpus acceptance is a later concern).\n- `vsir eval abstention` (net new): runs the §12.4 L3 adversarial abstention eval (the 8 compact-label set from U005 plus the near-miss set from U006) — designed to run in CI on every commit.\n- Both commands print a pass/fail table, exit non-zero on any failure.\n\nWorking Deliverable:\n- `vsir eval acceptance` and `vsir eval abstention` CLI subcommands.\n\nDemo Command:\n- `vsir eval abstention` — runs the adversarial set against the currently published corpus and prints a pass/fail row per case (must all pass on the M2a synthetic doc with zero spend).\n\nDeliverables (files):\n- `backend/vsir/cli.py` (extended — `eval acceptance`, `eval abstention` subcommands)\n- `backend/vsir/core/eval_acceptance.py`, `core/eval_abstention.py` (written, net new)\n- `backend/tests/api/test_eval_abstention.py` (written — wired into CI)\n\nTwelve-Factor Notes:\n- N/A — adds no process, endpoint, tool or worker; a CLI eval harness only.\n\n---\n\nUnit ID: U017\nName: skim/resolve tools and image queries\nMilestone: M4\nType: tool\nPriority: P0-Critical\nSize Estimate: Large\nSpend: none\nDepends On: [U015]\nEnables: [U018]\nSpec References: [Spec §7.2.1, §7.2.3, D12]\nInvariants Enforced: []\nFailure Rows Closed: [F8 (M4 stateless-scope half), F5 (M4 half)]\nRequired Reading: [`impl/app/retrieve.py::search+rrf+decompose` (read first); `impl/app/retrieve.py::resolve` (read first); `IMPROVEMENTS.md` E9 (scroll-4096-and-filter-in-Python — skim's three branches must use proper Qdrant queries, not scroll+Python filtering, especially for the `scope`/`exclude` mechanics)]\n\nDescription:\n- Build the NARROW ladder (`skim_documents`/`skim_sections`/`skim_pages`) as one implementation exposed three times, plus FOLLOW (`resolve`) and image-query support.\n\nCore Requirements:\n- Read `impl/app/retrieve.py::search+rrf+decompose` and `impl/app/retrieve.py::resolve` first.\n- `serve/tools/skim.py` ≈ `retrieve.py::search+rrf+decompose`: one page query aggregated three ways (doc/section/page), using U004's ported `rrf()`/`sparse.py`; `decompose(query)` splits exact identifiers to `lookup` rather than blurring into the embedding; `why` names every contributing branch; `next: {expand, neighbours, references}`; no full text in a triage row (P2); `effective_scope` always echoed back — the service is stateless (F8, this half).\n- `serve/tools/resolve.py` ← `retrieve.py::resolve`: `printed_label` → `page_id` + `interpolated` + `label_verified`; ambiguity returns every candidate (F5, M4 half — flagged, never silent).\n- Image queries (D12): `embed_query_image(image, text=query)` in one `types.Content`; no instruction prefix on multimodal queries; image-only query runs the dense branch alone (`why: [\"dense\"]`), `lexical`/`captions` skipped since there is no query text.\n- An image can never reach the exact surface — `lookup`/`verify` remain text-only (I2/I3, already enforced upstream).\n- CLI one-shots: `vsir skim`, `vsir resolve` (§4.4).\n\nWorking Deliverable:\n- `vsir skim documents|sections|pages <query>` and `vsir resolve <label>` CLI subcommands + HTTP routes.\n\nDemo Command:\n- `vsir skim pages \"emergency stop reset\" --scope '{\"doc_id\":\"TC1E-SF\"}'` — prints ≤10 ranked triage rows with `why`/`rank`/`ImageRef`, deterministic across repeated calls; then `vsir resolve \"SF 1.1A\"` showing `interpolated: false`.\n\nDeliverables (files):\n- `backend/vsir/serve/tools/skim.py` (ported from `impl/app/retrieve.py::search+rrf+decompose`)\n- `backend/vsir/serve/tools/resolve.py` (ported from `impl/app/retrieve.py::resolve`)\n- `backend/vsir/core/embed_query.py` (written, net new — D12 image-query embedding)\n- `backend/tests/api/test_skim.py`, `test_resolve.py` (written)\n\nTwelve-Factor Notes:\n- N/A beyond U014's existing auth/audit — no new process; `effective_scope` echoed per-request, no server-side session state (C11).\n\n---\n\nUnit ID: U018\nName: Page image endpoint, raster cache, and fetch\nMilestone: M4\nType: tool\nPriority: P0-Critical\nSize Estimate: Large\nSpend: none\nDepends On: [U017]\nEnables: [U019]\nSpec References: [Spec §7.2.5, §7.3, §4.2]\nInvariants Enforced: []\nFailure Rows Closed: [F18 (M4 fetch half)]\nRequired Reading: [`impl/app/render.py` (read first — reused from U007's port for on-demand region rendering); `IMPROVEMENTS.md` E3 (rendering never collected — the in-process LRU cache added here must actually evict, closing the defect U007 flagged but didn't fully solve)]\n\nDescription:\n- Serve page rasters directly, with dpi/region budgets and an in-process LRU cache, and build `fetch` — the tool that returns material instead of an answer.\n\nCore Requirements:\n- `GET /pages/{page_id}/image` (net new route): bearer-authenticated, dpi ∈ {36, 72, 150, 220, 300, 400} (`dpi_not_allowed`), `dpi > 220` requires `region` (`dpi_requires_region`); 36/72 are the triage thumbnail tiers behind `thumb_url`.\n- In-process raster LRU cache (bounded by `VSIR_RASTER_CACHE_SIZE`): PyMuPDF renders the region clip on demand, no new storage — cache is a pure performance optimization, evictable, never correctness-bearing (C11, closes E3).\n- `serve/tools/fetch.py` (net new): `fetch(page_ids, include=[\"image\",\"text\",\"summary\"], dpi=150, region=None, inline=True)`; caps: ≤5 pages and ≤12MP total (`fetch_budget_exceeded {limit, requested}` — F18, fetch half); `url` always present, `bytes_b64` only when `inline=true` (default).\n- CLI one-shot: `vsir fetch` (§4.4); `vsir demo narrow` ties skim → fetch together as the milestone's official walkthrough.\n\nWorking Deliverable:\n- `GET /pages/{page_id}/image` route + `vsir fetch` CLI + `vsir demo narrow`.\n\nDemo Command:\n- `vsir demo narrow` — runs `skim_pages` → `fetch` over the synthetic doc, printing triage rows with `ImageRef` only, then the `fetch` result with `bytes_b64` present, then an over-budget `fetch` (6 pages) failing typed `fetch_budget_exceeded` (F18).\n\nDeliverables (files):\n- `backend/vsir/serve/app.py` (extended — `/pages/{page_id}/image` route)\n- `backend/vsir/serve/tools/fetch.py` (written, net new)\n- `backend/vsir/core/raster_cache.py` (written, net new — in-process LRU)\n- `backend/vsir/cli.py` (extended — `fetch`, `demo narrow` subcommands)\n- `backend/tests/api/test_fetch.py`, `test_page_image.py` (written)\n\nTwelve-Factor Notes:\n- Adds `.env.example` var: `VSIR_RASTER_CACHE_SIZE` (LRU entry count, process-local perf cache only — lost on restart with no correctness impact, satisfying C11).\n\n---\n\nUnit ID: U019\nName: read tool core logic (stub replay)\nMilestone: M5\nType: tool\nPriority: P0-Critical\nSize Estimate: Large\nSpend: none\nDepends On: [U018, U013]\nEnables: [U020]\nSpec References: [Spec §7.2.6, §6.3 (read_key), §7.3]\nInvariants Enforced: []\nFailure Rows Closed: [F19, F18 (M5 read half)]\nRequired Reading: [`impl/app/retrieve.py::read` (read first); `pipeline-guide/METADATA-CONTRACT.md` (§5.3, page_provenance shape); `IMPROVEMENTS.md` D3 (captions never written — `read` must not silently drop the captions channel it inherits from the page record) and B5 (cache embeddings — the read_key cache here must key on the actual question text, not a stale/generic key, which is exactly what closes F19)]\n\nDescription:\n- Build `read`'s core logic — transcription correction, `sufficient`, `page_provenance`, the ≤3-page cap, and the question-keyed cache — proved entirely through `VSIR_VLM=stub` replay against U013's frozen TC1E-SF fixtures, at zero spend.\n\nCore Requirements:\n- Read `impl/app/retrieve.py::read` first.\n- `serve/tools/read.py` ≈ `retrieve.py::read`: renders at pinned `dpi_answer=220` (caller cannot change it — part of `read_key`); every VLM-emitted code phrase-checked against that page's text and stamped `present | absent | unverifiable` — same vocabulary as `verify` (§7.2.4); on a page with no text layer, every code is `unverifiable`.\n- `sufficient` is mandatory in the result; retrieval judgment never happens inside `read` (§7.6).\n- §6.3 `read_key` cache: includes `page_ids` + the pinned dpi + the question text — a second question about the same pages is a cache miss (F19).\n- ≤3-page cap: `read_page_cap_exceeded` typed 400 (F18, read half).\n- `vlm/prompts/read.md` (net new prompt).\n- Proven via `VSIR_VLM=stub VSIR_FIXTURE=data/fixtures/TC1E-SF` replay — no real Gemini call in this unit.\n\nWorking Deliverable:\n- `vsir read --pages <ids> --question <q>` CLI + HTTP route, runnable in stub mode.\n\nDemo Command:\n- `VSIR_VLM=stub VSIR_FIXTURE=data/fixtures/TC1E-SF vsir read --pages TC1E-SF@1.3#p001,TC1E-SF@1.3#p002 --question \"is K158 energised?\"` — prints `ReadResult` with per-code stamps and `sufficient`; repeating the identical call shows a cache hit (instant); asking a *different* question about the same pages shows a cache miss (F19); requesting a 4th page → `read_page_cap_exceeded`.\n\nDeliverables (files):\n- `backend/vsir/serve/tools/read.py` (ported from `impl/app/retrieve.py::read`)\n- `backend/vsir/vlm/prompts/read.md` (written, net new)\n- `backend/vsir/core/read_cache.py` (written, net new — `read_key`)\n- `backend/vsir/cli.py` (extended — `read` subcommand)\n- `backend/tests/unit/test_read_core.py` (written)\n\nTwelve-Factor Notes:\n- Adds `.env.example` var: `VSIR_DPI_ANSWER=220` (pinned, documented as non-overridable at the API layer despite being config).\n- `read_key` cache is stored in Qdrant/keyed storage, not a local file (C11); stub replay via `VSIR_FIXTURE` is the same config-only mechanism from U008, not a code branch.\n\n---\n\nUnit ID: U020\nName: Real Gemini read path and searchable_ratio\nMilestone: M5\nType: tool\nPriority: P0-Critical\nSize Estimate: Medium\nSpend: paid\nDepends On: [U019]\nEnables: [U021]\nSpec References: [Spec §7.2.6, §7.2.1 (searchable_ratio), §17 (OQ-2)]\nInvariants Enforced: []\nFailure Rows Closed: []\nRequired Reading: [`IMPROVEMENTS.md` B6 (pin the model — this is the second real Gemini integration point after U013, re-verify the pinned id here)]\n\nDescription:\n- Wire U019's `read` to the real Gemini client for the first time, and finish `searchable_ratio` population on every `skim_documents` row against the real TC1E-SF corpus.\n\nCore Requirements:\n- Wire `vlm/client.py` (real path, from U008) into `serve/tools/read.py`; `VSIR_ALLOW_PAID=1` required or the call refuses.\n- Verify/complete `searchable_ratio` on every `DocHit` row (already scaffolded in U004's hit models) against the real, published TC1E-SF corpus from U013.\n- This is the FIRST real `read` call — confirms the pinned dpi 220, real transcription correction, and real cache behavior end to end.\n\nWorking Deliverable:\n- `vsir read` against the real Gemini backend.\n\nDemo Command:\n- `VSIR_ALLOW_PAID=1 vsir read --pages TC1E-SF@1.3#p001,TC1E-SF@1.3#p002 --question \"the carton discharge won't restart after an E-stop reset\"` — the milestone's official demo, plus `vsir skim documents \"carton discharge\"` showing a non-null `searchable_ratio` on the TC1E-SF row.\n\nDeliverables (files):\n- `backend/vsir/serve/tools/read.py` (extended — real client wiring, no new file)\n- `backend/vsir/serve/tools/skim.py` (extended — `searchable_ratio` finishing touch)\n- `backend/tests/paid/test_read_real.py` (written, gated by `scripts/test-paid.sh`)\n\nTwelve-Factor Notes:\n- Uses `GEMINI_API_KEY` and `VSIR_ALLOW_PAID` (both already declared); no new vars.\n\n---\n\nUnit ID: U021\nName: Runner triage and routing (stub)\nMilestone: M6\nType: runner\nPriority: P0-Critical\nSize Estimate: Medium\nSpend: none\nDepends On: [U018, U019]\nEnables: [U022]\nSpec References: [Spec §8.1, §8.2, §8.1a]\nInvariants Enforced: []\nFailure Rows Closed: []\nRequired Reading: [`impl/pipeline-guide/` runner precedent is none (net new per §4.1 layout note); `IMPROVEMENTS.md` — general reminder that the runner must never fabricate an abstention on a backend failure]\n\nDescription:\n- Build the tri-state triage stage and fetch-vs-read routing decision logic, provable against already-built free tools without spending on `read`.\n\nCore Requirements:\n- `runner/triage.py` (net new): tri-state triage (`relevant`/`maybe`/`irrelevant`) with `exclude` and the five §8.2 safeguards — auto-promote exact hits, use `why` as a signal, etc.\n- `runner/prompt.py` (net new): the system prompt (§8.1).\n- §8.1a fetch-vs-read routing: default `fetch`, escalate to `read` only when triage judges the page insufficiently searchable — routing decision itself makes no VLM call.\n- Demoed against U017/U018's free tools (`skim`, `fetch`) only — no `read` call in this unit.\n\nWorking Deliverable:\n- `vsir ask --explain <question>` (dry-run mode): runs triage/routing and prints the plan without calling `read`.\n\nDemo Command:\n- `vsir ask --explain \"the carton discharge won't restart after an E-stop reset\"` — prints the triage table (relevant/maybe/irrelevant per candidate page) and the fetch-vs-read routing decision per page, with zero spend.\n\nDeliverables (files):\n- `backend/vsir/runner/triage.py`, `runner/prompt.py` (written, net new)\n- `backend/vsir/cli.py` (extended — `ask --explain` flag)\n- `backend/tests/unit/test_triage.py` (written)\n\nTwelve-Factor Notes:\n- N/A — adds no process, endpoint, tool or worker; runner logic invoked synchronously from the CLI.\n\n---\n\nUnit ID: U022\nName: Runner loop, answer gate, and POST /ask\nMilestone: M6\nType: runner\nPriority: P0-Critical\nSize Estimate: Large\nSpend: paid\nDepends On: [U021, U020]\nEnables: [U023, U025]\nSpec References: [Spec §8.3, §8.4, §8.5, §7.4]\nInvariants Enforced: [I8]\nFailure Rows Closed: []\nRequired Reading: [`IMPROVEMENTS.md` — reconfirm no allowlist/keyword-taxonomy pattern leaks into the answer gate or abstention wording]\n\nDescription:\n- Complete the agentic loop with the six correction loops and the server-side answer gate, and expose it as `POST /ask` / `vsir ask` — the first unit where a full question-to-answer cycle runs for real.\n\nCore Requirements:\n- `runner/loop.py` (net new): the full loop (§8.1) driving U021's triage/routing through real `fetch`/`read`/`verify` calls; the six correction loops (§8.3), including Loop 1's automatic transcription correction (already inside `read` per U019) and the other five orchestrated here.\n- `runner/answer.py` (net new): server-side answer gate (I8) — every asserted code verified against the page it is cited on, per `(claim, page)` via `core/verify.py`; three branches (verified answer / read-from-image answer / abstain); constrained abstention wording (§8.5) — forbidden while `pages_no_text_read < scope_stats.pages_no_text`.\n- `VSIR_READS_PER_QUESTION` default 3 enforced.\n- `POST /ask` route + `vsir ask` CLI (§4.4).\n\nWorking Deliverable:\n- `POST /ask` + `vsir ask`.\n\nDemo Command:\n- `VSIR_ALLOW_PAID=1 vsir ask \"the carton discharge won't restart after an E-stop reset\"` — the milestone's official demo: prints the agent's move-by-move trace, then a gated answer with verified/read-from-image/unverifiable badges per cited code (I8).\n\nDeliverables (files):\n- `backend/vsir/runner/loop.py`, `runner/answer.py` (written, net new)\n- `backend/vsir/serve/app.py` (extended — `POST /ask` route)\n- `backend/vsir/cli.py` (extended — `ask` subcommand)\n- `backend/tests/paid/test_ask_real.py` (written, gated by `scripts/test-paid.sh`)\n\nTwelve-Factor Notes:\n- Adds `.env.example` var: `VSIR_READS_PER_QUESTION` (default 3).\n- Loop state lives entirely in the request/response cycle (agent-side per §7.6, \"state lives in the agent, not the service\") — no server-side session store (C11).\n\n---\n\nUnit ID: U023\nName: Operator console — viewer and agent panel\nMilestone: M7\nType: frontend\nPriority: P1-High\nSize Estimate: Large\nSpend: none\nDepends On: [U022]\nEnables: [U024]\nSpec References: [Spec §13 M7, §7.1 (image.url/preview.thumb_url)]\nInvariants Enforced: []\nFailure Rows Closed: []\nRequired Reading: [none in `impl/` — net new per §4.1 layout note (frontend is M7-only, no port)]\n\nDescription:\n- Build the two-zone React/TypeScript/Vite console: the page viewer on the left, the agent-moves/triage/answer panel on the right.\n\nCore Requirements:\n- Vite + React + TypeScript scaffold under `frontend/`.\n- LEFT zone: zoom-ladder breadcrumbs, high-res page viewer, region zoom at escalated dpi — consumes `image.url`/`preview.thumb_url` directly with `inline=false` (never requests `bytes_b64` from the browser).\n- RIGHT zone: collapsible agent moves (skim/read/verify), tri-state triage panel, draft answer with trust badges (verified / read-from-image / unverifiable) and amber verification warnings.\n- Clicking a cited code scrolls the LEFT viewer to its page.\n- Talks to the backend's real HTTP surface (`/ask`, `/pages/{id}/image`, etc.) built in U014–U022.\n\nWorking Deliverable:\n- Running Vite dev server serving the full two-zone console against a live (or replay-mode) backend.\n\nDemo Command:\n- `npm --prefix frontend run dev` then browse `http://localhost:5173` — LEFT shows a fixture page image with zoom breadcrumbs, RIGHT shows a replayed agent trace with a trust-badged draft answer; clicking a citation scrolls the viewer.\n\nDeliverables (files):\n- `frontend/` (written, net new — full Vite/React/TS app)\n- `frontend/src/components/Viewer/*`, `frontend/src/components/AgentPanel/*` (written)\n\nTwelve-Factor Notes:\n- Adds `.env.example` vars: `VSIR_FRONTEND_DEV_PORT=5173`, `VSIR_BACKEND_URL` (frontend config, not a literal).\n- No frontend-local persisted state beyond the current session's in-memory trace — nothing correctness-bearing survives a reload.\n\n---\n\nUnit ID: U024\nName: E2E replay suite\nMilestone: M7\nType: harness\nPriority: P1-High\nSize Estimate: Medium\nSpend: none\nDepends On: [U023]\nEnables: []\nSpec References: [Spec §13 M7, §12.2]\nInvariants Enforced: []\nFailure Rows Closed: []\nRequired Reading: [none — net new]\n\nDescription:\n- Drive the worked trace through Playwright in replay mode, with assertions independent of which fixture corpus is loaded.\n\nCore Requirements:\n- `e2e/` Playwright suite (extends the existing `e2e/` directory noted in the repo layout) driving the full worked trace against the console in replay mode (`VSIR_VLM=stub` backend + fixture-backed `/ask` responses).\n- Assertions must be fixture-independent — pass on `synthetic_3window` as well as TC1E-SF, per the spec's explicit requirement.\n- `scripts/test-e2e.sh` wires up: backend on test port 8001 in replay mode, Qdrant test instance on 6335, frontend built for test port 5174, then runs Playwright against it.\n\nWorking Deliverable:\n- `scripts/test-e2e.sh` running Playwright end to end.\n\nDemo Command:\n- `bash scripts/test-e2e.sh` then browse `http://localhost:5174` — Playwright report shows the worked trace passing; manually browsing the same URL shows the same console state Playwright asserted against.\n\nDeliverables (files):\n- `e2e/*.spec.ts` (written, extends existing `e2e/` directory)\n- `scripts/test-e2e.sh` (extended, ported from U002's earlier stub)\n\nTwelve-Factor Notes:\n- Confirms test ports from U001 (backend 8001, Qdrant 6335, frontend 5174) are actually used, never dev ports.\n\n---\n\nUnit ID: U025\nName: Revision lifecycle and resumable ingest\nMilestone: M8\nType: ingest\nPriority: P0-Critical\nSize Estimate: Large\nSpend: none\nDepends On: [U022, U011]\nEnables: [U026]\nSpec References: [Spec §6.2 (Level-2 refusal), §6.7 (F9 half), §15 Factor IX, §4.4]\nInvariants Enforced: []\nFailure Rows Closed: [F9, F8 (M8 series_id half), F12 (M8 revision half)]\nRequired Reading: [`impl/app/pipeline.py`, `impl/app/segjobs.py` (read first — resumability being added on top of U011's run orchestration); `IMPROVEMENTS.md` E2 (job state on daemon threads — resumability must checkpoint through `vsir_runs`, never an in-memory thread) and E7 (orphan points — a killed-and-resumed run must not leave duplicate or orphaned points)]\n\nDescription:\n- Extend U011's run orchestration with `is_current` multi-revision lifecycle, `series_id` propagation, resumable `--resume` ingest with per-window checkpoints, graceful-shutdown checkpointing, and the typed Level-2 refusal — proved on a generated large PDF, never the excluded 1,440-page manual.\n\nCore Requirements:\n- Read `impl/app/pipeline.py`/`impl/app/segjobs.py` first (resumability extension).\n- `is_current` lifecycle across revisions: ingesting a new revision of the same `(doc_id)` sets prior *other* revision `is_current=False` and KEEPS it (never deletes — F9, F12 revision half); `found_only_in_superseded` status surfaced through `lookup`/`skim` when a code exists only in a non-current revision.\n- `series_id` propagated across revisions (F8, M8 half) so a straddling-section scope stays correct across a revision boundary.\n- Generate `data/source/synthetic_large.pdf` (a GENERATED large multi-window PDF, per §6.2's explicit note — never the excluded 1,440-page manual) for resume testing.\n- `--resume <run_id>` with per-window checkpoints in `vsir_runs`; SIGTERM handler checkpoints so at most one window's work is lost (Factor IX); `--steal` interplay with U011's advisory lease.\n- Typed `ladder_level_2_required`: attempting to ingest a Level-2-marked document (per U007's ladder check) fails with this typed error, never silently degrades.\n- `vsir retire <doc_id> [--revision]` CLI (§4.4).\n\nWorking Deliverable:\n- `vsir ingest --resume <run_id>` + `vsir retire`.\n\nDemo Command:\n- Start `vsir ingest data/source/synthetic_large.pdf --vlm stub`, kill it mid-run (SIGTERM), then `vsir ingest --resume <run_id>` — completes, `vsir runs show <run_id>` shows `published` with no duplicated pages; separately, `vsir ingest data/source/level2_stub.pdf --vlm stub` fails typed `ladder_level_2_required`.\n\nDeliverables (files):\n- `backend/vsir/ingest/run.py` (extended — resume/checkpoint logic, no new file)\n- `backend/vsir/ingest/stitch.py` (extended — `series_id` revision propagation)\n- `data/source/synthetic_large.pdf` (written, generated fixture)\n- `backend/vsir/cli.py` (extended — `ingest --resume`, `retire` subcommands)\n- `backend/tests/api/test_resume.py`, `test_revision_lifecycle.py` (written)\n\nTwelve-Factor Notes:\n- SIGTERM handler checkpoints the in-flight window's state into `vsir_runs` before exiting — no local job-state file, resumability is entirely Qdrant-backed (C11, Factor IX).\n\n---\n\nUnit ID: U026\nName: Corpus evaluation report\nMilestone: M8\nType: eval\nPriority: P1-High\nSize Estimate: Small\nSpend: none\nDepends On: [U025]\nEnables: []\nSpec References: [Spec §12.6]\nInvariants Enforced: []\nFailure Rows Closed: []\nRequired Reading: [none new — reuses U013/U016's eval patterns]\n\nDescription:\n- Produce the §12.6 corpus-wide evaluation report over whatever is currently published, reading only from the already-indexed corpus (no new model spend).\n\nCore Requirements:\n- `vsir eval corpus` (net new): aggregates grounded_rate/coverage/`is_current` stats across the full published corpus, reusing U013's grounded_rate reporting utility and U011's Prometheus gauge sources.\n- Read-only against the existing index — no fresh ingest or VLM call triggered by this command itself.\n\nWorking Deliverable:\n- `vsir eval corpus` CLI subcommand.\n\nDemo Command:\n- `vsir eval corpus` — prints the corpus evaluation report table (per-document grounded_rate, coverage, current-vs-superseded counts) for everything currently published, run immediately after U025's resume demo.\n\nDeliverables (files):\n- `backend/vsir/cli.py` (extended — `eval corpus` subcommand)\n- `backend/vsir/core/eval_corpus.py` (written, net new)\n- `backend/tests/unit/test_eval_corpus.py` (written)\n\nTwelve-Factor Notes:\n- N/A — adds no process, endpoint, tool or worker; read-only reporting CLI.\n\n---\n\n## Coverage Self-Check\n\n- Units per milestone: M0=2, M1=4, M2a=5, M2b=2, M3=3, M4=2, M5=2, M6=2, M7=2, M8=2, TOTAL=26\n- Every I1–I8 owned: I1→U011, I2→U005, I3→U004, I4→U011, I5→U004, I6→U003, I7→U011, I8→U022\n- Every F1–F19 owned (split rows named per part):\n  - F1→U005\n  - F2→U006 (core) + U015 (tool)\n  - F3→U005\n  - F4→U007 (M2a) + U015 (M3)\n  - F5→U009 (M2a) + U017 (M4)\n  - F6→U009\n  - F7→U011\n  - F8→U009 (M2a stitching) + U017 (M4 stateless scope) + U025 (M8 series_id)\n  - F9→U025\n  - F10→U004\n  - F11→U001 (M0 boot) + U008 (M2a key)\n  - F12→U011 (M2a) + U025 (M8 revision half)\n  - F13→U007\n  - F14→U005\n  - F15→U007\n  - F16→U006\n  - F17→U011\n  - F18→U018 (M4 fetch) + U019 (M5 read)\n  - F19→U019\n- Any unit without a runnable Demo Command: none","usage":{"total_tokens":95979,"tool_uses":4,"duration_ms":679931},"uuid":"4f62c406-0d07-4298-85e6-af77fb36f113","session_id":"4eefb16f-3989-4441-9cd3-d294cfccb11f"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011S1UJFiq6JPtip8C4TUM79","type":"tool_result","content":"<persisted-output>\nOutput too large (67.3KB). Full output saved to: /Users/sabesonk/.claude/projects/-Users-sabesonk-Documents-DILMAH-dilmah-engineering-solutioning-poc-vision-segmentation-index-and-retrieval/4eefb16f-3989-4441-9cd3-d294cfccb11f/tool-results/toolu_011S1UJFiq6JPtip8C4TUM79.json\n\nPreview (first 2KB):\n[\n  {\n    \"type\": \"text\",\n    \"text\": \"### Synthesis Agent 2: Unit Decomposition\\n\\nUnit ID: U001\\nName: Repo skeleton, CLI doctor, and twelve-factor runtime shell\\nMilestone: M0\\nType: harness\\nPriority: P0-Critical\\nSize Estimate: Large\\nSpend: none\\nDepends On: []\\nEnables: [U002, U003]\\nSpec References: [Spec §4.1, §4.2, §4.3, §4.4, §15, §15.1, §15.2]\\nInvariants Enforced: []\\nFailure Rows Closed: [F11 (boot half — alias/`-latest` model id refused at boot)]\\nRequired Reading: [`impl/README.md §3` (§7.2 twelve-factor precedent); `pipeline-guide/IMPROVEMENTS.md` items E5 (no auth — do not reproduce, stub it out now so M3 has a hook), E4 (no cost observability — plan gauge hooks now)]\\n\\nDescription:\\n- Stand up the installable `backend/vsir/` package, the `vsir` CLI entrypoint, and a self-checking, twelve-factor-compliant runtime shell with nothing paid or ingest-specific in it yet.\\n\\nCore Requirements:\\n- §4.1 repo layout skeleton: `backend/vsir/{core,ingest,vlm,serve,mcp,runner}/__init__.py` placeholders only where a later milestone owns the first real module (never populate a module ahead of its owning milestone).\\n- `cli.py` ≈ `impl/scripts/interfaces_demo.py` (read first) — port the argument-parsing skeleton only; wire the `vsir` entrypoint and register `doctor` as the first real subcommand.\\n- §4.3 boot self-check: Qdrant reachable, pinned model id does not end in `-latest` (refuse to start — F11 boot half), release_id resolvable.\\n- §4.2 pin python 3.11, fastapi==0.141.1, uvicorn[standard]==0.52.4, python-multipart==0.0.32, google-genai==2.22.0, qdrant-client==1.19.0, PyMuPDF==1.28.2, pillow==12.3.0 in `requirements.txt` + generate a lock file.\\n- REWRITE `docker-compose.test.yml` from any Postgres service to `qdrant/qdrant:v1.19.0` on test ports (backend 8001, Qdrant REST 6335 gRPC — never reuse dev 6334).\\n- §15 Dockerfile: non-root user, digest-pinned base image, read-only rootfs, tmpfs mount for the raster cache; `.env.example` with every Factor III va\n...\n</persisted-output>"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4eefb16f-3989-4441-9cd3-d294cfccb11f","uuid":"ab82ca3c-2ac2-4b71-8010-879295c96a89","timestamp":"2026-09-09T17:02:20.316Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"You are Synthesis Agent S2 (unit decomposition) for a PLAN-ONLY implementation-planning task. Spec: `development/cr1/spec/spec.md` in /Users/sabesonk/Documents/DILMAH/dilmah-engineering-solutioning/poc/vision_segmentation_index_and_retrieval. DO NOT WRITE ANY FILES. DO NOT IMPLEMENT CODE. Output your decomposition as your final message only.\n\nYou may read the spec with `sed -n` for detail, but the brief below already contains the authoritative structure. Read at most 2–3 targeted ranges; do not read the whole file.\n\n## Your task\nProduce **22–26 atomic, PR-sized (1–3 day) implementation units**, each belonging to exactly ONE milestone, each with a runnable Working Deliverable and a Demo Command.\n\n## Hard rules\n1. Every unit belongs to exactly one milestone from M0, M1, M2a, M2b, M3, M4, M5, M6, M7, M8 and inherits its spend class. Never merge across milestones. Never reorder milestones.\n2. Every unit must have a **Working Deliverable** (a runnable artefact: CLI subcommand, HTTP endpoint, MCP tool, script, page) and a **Demo Command** a reviewer can run and read the output of. A unit whose only output is a document, a schema file or a refactor is INVALID — fold it into the unit that makes it runnable.\n3. A unit may only claim invariants/failure rows its milestone owns (ownership table below is authoritative).\n4. Order units so nothing depends on an unbuilt paid dependency. Everything provable without a model call comes before anything that spends.\n5. Twelve-factor compliance (Spec §15) for any unit adding a process/endpoint/tool/worker: new config is an env var in `.env.example` (never a literal, never a committed config file); NO process-local or on-disk correctness-bearing state (C11 — no `RetrievalState`, no persisted rasters, no local run state); JSON logs to stdout; long-running work checkpointed so SIGTERM loses at most one window; stub-vs-real VLM is config (`VSIR_VLM=stub`), never a code branch or `if TESTING`.\n6. Units under half a day must be merged with a neighbour INSIDE the same milestone.\n\n## Port discipline (Spec §2.3 C1, §2.4, §4.1)\nThis is a **restructured port of a working implementation at `impl/` outside this repo**, not greenfield. Every unit that builds a module marked `←` (port) or `≈` (port with changes) in §4.1 MUST list **\"read `impl/app/<module>.py` first\"** as its first Core Requirement, and its Deliverables must state what is ported vs written. `+` = net new.\n\n§4.1 layout with markers and impl ancestors:\n- core/record.py ≈ pagemodel.py (record shape only); core/ids.py ≈ pagemodel.py::make_page_id; core/tok.py, variants.py, exact.py + net new; core/verify.py, status.py, indexed.py + net new; core/health.py + net new (grounded_rate)\n- ingest/manifest.py ≈ pipeline.py; probe.py ← textlayer.py::probe/page_texts/content_hash; render.py ← render.py; window.py ← windows.py (+ bisection ladder F13); extract.py ≈ segment.py (new S2 schema); derive.py ≈ segment.py (no gate); stitch.py ← stitch.py (sections, + series_id); embed.py ← embedder.py (interleaved D4); sparse.py ← sparse.py (D2); index.py ≈ segstore.py (+ text indexes, is_current); gates.py ≈ pipeline.py (grounded_rate not allowlist); export.py, run.py ≈ pipeline.py / segjobs.py\n- vlm/client.py, cache.py, stub.py ≈ segment.py's Gemini calls; vlm/prompts/{s1.md,s2.md,read.md}\n- serve/app.py ≈ main.py; serve/envelope.py ≈ api_models.py; serve/auth.py, audit.py, budget.py + net new; serve/tools/skim.py ≈ retrieve.py::search+rrf+decompose; lookup.py ≈ retrieve.py::lookup (rewritten as phrase filter); resolve.py ← retrieve.py::resolve; read.py ≈ retrieve.py::read; fetch.py, verify.py + net new\n- mcp/server.py + net new; runner/{loop,prompt,triage,answer}.py + net new; cli.py ≈ scripts/interfaces_demo.py\n- backend/tests/{unit,api,paid}/; frontend/ (M7 only); e2e/ (exists); data/source/, data/fixtures/; scripts/test-{unit,api,e2e,paid}.sh\nNote: modules are created by the milestone that implements them, never as empty M0 placeholders.\n\nRequired reading per unit (Spec §20 Tier 2 — name the doc, don't read it now): `impl/pipeline-guide/01-entry.md` (step01), `02-probe-and-render.md` (02,03), `03-document-facts.md` (04), `04-windowing-and-keys.md` (05), `05-extraction.md`+`../SEGMENTATION.md` (06), `06-derivation-and-gate.md` (07 — ⚠ documents the DELETED allowlist gate), `07-stitch-and-numbering.md` (08), `08-embedding.md` (09), `09-indexing.md` (10 — ⚠ entity_keys index deleted), `10-gates-and-publish.md` (11 — ⚠ allowlist/class_totality replaced by grounded_rate), `11-export.md` (12 — ⚠ withheld.jsonl dropped), `12-reproducibility.md` (§6.3/§6.6), `pipeline-guide/METADATA-CONTRACT.md` (§5.3), `impl/README.md §3` (§7.2), `impl/INGESTION_WALKTHROUGH.md` (M2a/M2b debugging), `pipeline-guide/IMPROVEMENTS.md` (read BEFORE porting anything — the known-defect register; §20.1 lists defects that must NOT be reproduced: A1 always-extract-text, A5 image_path, B6 pin the model, B1/B4 provenance, B5 cache embeddings, D3 captions never written, E2 job state on daemon threads, E3 rendering never collected, E4 no cost observability, E5 no auth, E6 no tests, E7 orphan points, E9 scroll-4096-and-filter-in-Python).\n\n## Milestone ledger (Spec §0 + §13) — deliverable, demo, spend, depends-on\n- M0 | none | depends: nothing | demo `vsir doctor && bash scripts/test-unit.sh` | repo skeleton, backend/vsir/ package, cli.py→`vsir doctor`, pinned requirements.txt + lock, docker-compose.test.yml REWRITTEN Postgres→Qdrant, scripts/test-*.sh extended + test-paid.sh added, AGENTS.md filled with real commands, `vsir doctor` per §4.3, §12.5 conformance greps as a runnable test, twelve-factor runtime skeleton §15 (Dockerfile non-root + digest-pinned base + read-only rootfs + tmpfs raster cache, `.env.example` with every Factor III var, GET /health + GET /ready per §15.1, structured JSON logs to stdout, SIGTERM handler, release_id stamping), D1–D7 restated in README.\n- M1 | none | depends M0 | demo `vsir demo exact --synthetic` | **the whole correctness proof, zero spend**: core/record, both envelope families §7.1, INDEXED, tok, variants, exact_filter, core/verify.py::verify_claims (per (claim,page); tool wrapper comes at M3), the §12.4 near-miss generator, collection + text-index creation §5.5, `lookup` against an ephemeral Qdrant seeded with HAND-WRITTEN page text (no PDF): three synthetic pages (one containing `SF 1.1A`; one with tokens `sf`,`1`,`1a` scattered; one printing `SF121.1)`) plus a page whose `codes` claim `K999` its text lacks; the observed-token inventory §6.8 built from the seeded pages so `present_instead` works before any PDF exists; §7.3 cap validators as typed 400s. Ports `sparse.py` and `rrf()` from impl.\n- M2a | none | depends M1 | demo `vsir ingest data/source/synthetic_3window.pdf --vlm stub && vsir runs show <run_id>` | steps 01–12 end to end incl. `vsir_runs` control collection and the §6.7 three-clause retirement rule; a GENERATED 3-window PDF checked into data/source/ with known printed labels, a deliberate off-by-one trap and a crop trap; the stub VLM; run record; publish gating.\n- M2b | paid (S2 + embed, once) | depends M2a | demo `VSIR_ALLOW_PAID=1 vsir ingest data/source/TC1E-SF.pdf && vsir runs show <run_id>` | FIRST port what is already paid for: `impl/data/raw/*` → data/fixtures/ as the old-schema baseline, and `impl/data/exports/r-poc-*/labels.jsonl` + `withheld.jsonl` as the parity and negative sets; THEN one real ingest of TC1E-SF (55 pages) under the new S2 schema; freeze data/fixtures/TC1E-SF/{raw_window_1.json,raw_window_2.json,text.json,expected.json}; report the grounded_rate distribution and set the gate threshold from it (R4).\n- M3 | none | depends M2a (real-corpus acceptance also needs M2b) | demo `vsir serve &` then `vsir lookup \"SF 1.1A\" && vsir verify --claims K73 --pages …` plus the same two tools over MCP | six-value status enum with all four absences, `next.suggest`, `present_instead`, `unverifiable`, bearer auth, audit log, `reads_remaining`, MCP server exposing both tools through the SAME implementations, `vsir eval acceptance` + `vsir eval abstention`.\n- M4 | none | depends M3 | demo `vsir demo narrow` | triage rows (no full text, but an ImageRef on EVERY page-level hit), deterministic §7.2.1 ordering (RRF ranks-only, rrf_k=60, weights page 1.0/lexical 1.0/captions 0.4), `exclude`, `next` affordances, region/dpi budgets incl. the 36/72 thumbnail tiers, `GET /pages/{page_id}/image`, the in-process raster LRU cache, image queries (D12, `embed_query_image`), `resolve` with `interpolated`.\n- M5 | paid (read) | depends M4 (paid assertions also need M2b/OQ-2) | demo `VSIR_ALLOW_PAID=1 vsir read --pages TC1E-SF@1.3#p001,…#p002 --question \"…\"` | `skim_documents`/`skim_sections` with `searchable_ratio` on every document row; `read` with per-code present/absent/unverifiable stamps, `sufficient`, `page_provenance`, the ≤3-page cap, the question-keyed cache.\n- M6 | paid (read) | depends M5 | demo `VSIR_ALLOW_PAID=1 vsir ask \"the carton discharge won't restart after an E-stop reset\"` | runner/ implementing §8: tri-state triage with `exclude`, the six correction loops, the system prompt, the SERVER-SIDE answer gate, constrained abstention wording; `POST /ask`; `vsir ask`.\n- M7 | none (fixture-backed replay) | depends M6 | demo `bash scripts/test-e2e.sh` then browse http://localhost:5174 | React + TypeScript + Vite, two zones. Consumes `image.url`/`preview.thumb_url` directly with `inline=false`. LEFT: zoom-ladder breadcrumbs, high-res page viewer, region zoom at escalated dpi. RIGHT: collapsible agent moves (skim/read/verify), tri-state triage panel, draft answer with trust badges (verified / read-from-image / unverifiable) and amber verification warnings; clicking a code scrolls the viewer to its cited page. Playwright drives the worked trace in replay mode; assertions must be fixture-independent (pass on synthetic_3window too).\n- M8 | paid (ingest) | depends M6 (and M2b for real-corpus numbers) | demo `vsir ingest --resume <run_id>` after a deliberate kill, then `vsir eval corpus` | `is_current` lifecycle, `found_only_in_superseded`, `series_id` across revisions, resumable `--resume` ingest with per-window checkpoints, graceful-shutdown checkpointing (§15 Factor IX), the §12.6 corpus evaluation report. Note §6.2: the resume test runs on a GENERATED large PDF, not the excluded 1,440-page manual; attempting a Level-2 document must fail typed `ladder_level_2_required`.\n\n## Invariant ownership (Spec §9 \"Asserted from\") — AUTHORITATIVE, a unit may not claim outside it\nI1 M2a | I2 M1 | I3 M1 | I4 M2a | I5 M1 | I6 M1 | I7 M2a | I8 M6\n\n## Failure-row ownership (Spec §10 \"Closed at\") — AUTHORITATIVE\nF1 M1 | F2 M1(core) + M3(tool) | F3 M1 | F4 M2a + M3 | F5 M2a + M4 | F6 M2a | F7 M2a | F8 M2a(stitching) + M4(stateless scope) + M8(series_id) | F9 M8 | F10 M1 | F11 M0(boot) + M2a(key) | F12 M2a (+ M8 revision half) | F13 M2a | F14 M1 | F15 M2a | F16 M1 | F17 M2a | F18 M4(fetch) + M5(read) | F19 M5\nA row split across milestones needs ONE OWNING UNIT PER PART.\n\n## Key technical content the units must cover (spec pointers only)\n- §5.1 ids (page_id/section_id/series_id/point_id=uuid5/run_id=ULID); §5.2 S2 schema (PageOut/SectionRef/Summary/WindowOut; **Prohibited**: any identifier grammar, classification enum, regex taxonomy or per-corpus keyword list); §5.3 record (facets / text+vlm_codes / three vectors dense+lexical+captions / nested `content` never filtered / provenance; NO image_path); §5.4 INDEXED dict — one dict creates, gates and is asserted at boot (I6), scope keys = INDEXED minus text and vlm_codes; §5.5 TextIndexParams WORD tokenizer, lowercase, phrase_matching=True, min_token_len=1, collection name carries dim (pages_1536); §5.6 tok() mirrors Qdrant WORD (NOT impl's TOKEN_RE — porting hazard), variants() = exactly 3 spellings of the same characters, exact_filter is the ONLY exact-match path; §5.7 grounded_rate is None where has_text is false, text_trust enum, searchable_ratio.\n- §6.1 steps 01–12; §6.2 windowing target 30 pages + bisect-and-re-bill on MAX_TOKENS/truncation/offset-failure, `window_unsplittable`, and **v1 is Level 0/1 + bisection only — a Level-2 document must fail typed `ladder_level_2_required`**; §6.3 four cache keys facts_key/extract_key/read_key/embed_key (VSIR_VLM_TIER is NOT part of extract_key) + replay mode `VSIR_VLM=stub` + `VSIR_FIXTURE=<dir>` with a typed `fixture_miss`; §6.4 the two independent offset checks; §6.5 label precedence + ambiguity→list + code reattribution with `moved_from`; §6.6 fingerprint {embed_model,dim,distance,composition_version} → refuse to upsert on mismatch; §6.7 publish gating + the THREE-CLAUSE retirement (delete same doc+revision earlier run_id → F12; set prior *other* revision is_current=False and KEEP → F9; never touch other documents) + `vsir_runs` run/window points + advisory lease + `--steal`; §6.8 exports labels.jsonl + observed_tokens.jsonl streamed over HTTP, `safety_flag` from manifest doc_type + model topics (never a keyword list), observed-token inventory display-only and unreachable from lookup/verify; §6.9 run record + state enum {queued,running,stopped,gated,published,failed}.\n- §7.1 two envelope families + six-value status + `empty_is_never_ok` validator + WEAK_ABS=20 server constant + hit models DocHit/SectionHit/PageHit/LookupHit/ResolveHit + ImageRef/Preview (references never bytes; bytes_b64 only in fetch); §7.2 the eight tools; §7.3 caps as typed 400s (read ≤3 `read_page_cap_exceeded`; fetch ≤5 and ≤12MP `fetch_budget_exceeded`; dpi ∈ {36,72,150,220,300,400} `dpi_not_allowed`; dpi>220 requires region `dpi_requires_region`; unknown scope key `filter_unknown_key`; 429 `budget_exhausted`); §7.4 routes + bearer + the ten-field audit line + cost-in-audit-not-body; §7.5 MCP stdio+SSE same implementations, stateless; §7.6 four refusals (no `score` field, no routing, no composing outside the runner, no fuzzy matching).\n- §8 the runner: loop, fetch-vs-read routing (default fetch), tri-state triage + five safeguards, six correction loops, server-side answer gate with three branches, VSIR_READS_PER_QUESTION default 3, abstention wording forbidden while `pages_no_text_read < scope_stats.pages_no_text`.\n- §11.1 publish gates (window_coverage block; offset_check block; grounded_rate ≥0.8 provisional block with `vsir publish --override <gate> --reason` and `published_with_override`; text_coverage flag `mostly_scanned` never block, and AT 0.0 the grounded_rate gate is SKIPPED so a fully scanned doc publishes; label_monotonic flag `label_conflict`); §11.3 degradation rows (503 qdrant_unavailable, 503 vlm_unavailable, boot refusals, 429, typed 400s — never an empty result, never a clamp); §11.4 Prometheus gauges + audit + triage telemetry.\n- §12.5 conformance greps (scope `backend/vsir/**` + `requirements*.txt`, never markdown, never the test's own file): MatchText/MatchTextAny under serve/; fuzzy/similarity/edit-distance library in requirements*.txt; a field named `score` in a response model; a model id ending `-latest`; `alembic`/`sqlalchemy`; `get_text(` outside ingest/probe.py; SCHEMA_CARD, IdClass, entity_keys, `classify(`. Cloud-native set (same scope + Dockerfile* + docker-compose*.yml): `logging.FileHandler`; an image tagged `latest`; credential literals (`api_key=`, `token=`, `Bearer ` + literal); test-only branches (`if TESTING`, `if os.environ.get(\"TESTING\")`) inside backend/vsir/**; a `RetrievalState`-style module-level mutable session store.\n- §4.2 pins: python 3.11; fastapi==0.141.1, uvicorn[standard]==0.52.4, python-multipart==0.0.32, google-genai==2.22.0, qdrant-client==1.19.0, PyMuPDF==1.28.2, pillow==12.3.0; qdrant/qdrant:v1.19.0; ports backend dev 8000 / test 8001, Qdrant dev 6333 REST + 6334 gRPC so test takes 6335 (never 6334), frontend dev 5173 / test 5174; dpi_index=150 (embedded) / dpi_answer=220 (read, pinned, part of read_key); dim ∈ {768,1536,3072}, concurrency=8, batch_size=8, max_edge_px=1568; rrf_k=60, weights page 1.0/lexical 1.0/captions 0.4, cap_pages_per_window=30, lookup_cap=20. Store is **Qdrant only**, two collections `vsir_pages` + `vsir_runs`. No relational DB, ORM, migration tool or queue service.\n- §4.4 CLI: doctor (M0), demo exact --synthetic (M1), ingest [--vlm stub|--resume|--steal] (M2a), runs show (M2a), gates rerun (M2a), publish --override --reason (M2b), serve (M3), mcp [--stdio|--sse] (M3), lookup/verify/resolve/skim/fetch/read one-shots (M3–M5), demo narrow (M4), ask (M6), eval acceptance|abstention|corpus (M3, M8), retire <doc_id> [--revision] (M8).\n- §17 open questions: OQ-1 pilot PDF location (blocks ONLY the M2b re-bill — the S2 responses are already in impl/data/raw/); OQ-2 Gemini key (blocks M2b/M5/M6 paid paths only — replay mode covers the rest); OQ-3/OQ-7 Part A export sign-off (M8); OQ-4 resolved by design; OQ-5 one collection.\n\n## Output format — repeat this block for EVERY unit, in milestone order\n### Synthesis Agent 2: Unit Decomposition\n\nUnit ID: U001 (sequential, zero-padded, never reused)\nName: <short descriptive name>\nMilestone: <M0|M1|M2a|M2b|M3|M4|M5|M6|M7|M8>\nType: <core|ingest|tool|mcp|runner|frontend|harness|eval>\nPriority: <P0-Critical|P1-High|P2-Medium|P3-Low>\nSize Estimate: <Small|Medium|Large>\nSpend: <none|paid>\nDepends On: [<unit IDs>]\nEnables: [<unit IDs>]\nSpec References: [Spec §X.Y, …]\nInvariants Enforced: [I<n>… — only ones this milestone owns, or empty]\nFailure Rows Closed: [F<n>… — only ones this milestone owns; say \"(fetch half)\" etc. for split rows, or empty]\nRequired Reading: [`impl/app/<module>.py` for every ← or ≈ module; the `impl/pipeline-guide/NN-*.md` for every ported step; `IMPROVEMENTS.md` register items it must not reproduce]\n\nDescription:\n- <one sentence goal>\n\nCore Requirements:\n- <bullets, spec pointers only; the FIRST bullet must be \"read `impl/app/<module>.py` first\" for any ←/≈ module>\n\nWorking Deliverable:\n- <the runnable artefact>\n\nDemo Command:\n- <exact command> — <what a reviewer should see>\n\nDeliverables (files):\n- <concrete paths under backend/vsir/…, backend/tests/…, frontend/…, scripts/…, data/…; state ported vs written for each ←/≈ file>\n\nTwelve-Factor Notes:\n- <the env vars this unit adds to .env.example; any statelessness/SIGTERM/log obligation; \"N/A — adds no process, endpoint, tool or worker\" if truly none>\n\n---\n\nEnd with:\n\nCoverage Self-Check:\n- Units per milestone: M0=<n>, M1=<n>, M2a=<n>, M2b=<n>, M3=<n>, M4=<n>, M5=<n>, M6=<n>, M7=<n>, M8=<n>, TOTAL=<n>\n- Every I1–I8 owned: <I → unit id, all eight>\n- Every F1–F19 owned (name the unit per part for split rows): <F → unit id(s), all nineteen>\n- Any unit without a runnable Demo Command: <must be \"none\">\n","agentId":"a08a24a5168b021fd","agentType":"general-purpose","harnessNoteCount":0,"harnessTailCount":0,"harnessSectionHash":"feaf2a202e4f277e","content":[{"type":"text","text":"### Synthesis Agent 2: Unit Decomposition\n\nUnit ID: U001\nName: Repo skeleton, CLI doctor, and twelve-factor runtime shell\nMilestone: M0\nType: harness\nPriority: P0-Critical\nSize Estimate: Large\nSpend: none\nDepends On: []\nEnables: [U002, U003]\nSpec References: [Spec §4.1, §4.2, §4.3, §4.4, §15, §15.1, §15.2]\nInvariants Enforced: []\nFailure Rows Closed: [F11 (boot half — alias/`-latest` model id refused at boot)]\nRequired Reading: [`impl/README.md §3` (§7.2 twelve-factor precedent); `pipeline-guide/IMPROVEMENTS.md` items E5 (no auth — do not reproduce, stub it out now so M3 has a hook), E4 (no cost observability — plan gauge hooks now)]\n\nDescription:\n- Stand up the installable `backend/vsir/` package, the `vsir` CLI entrypoint, and a self-checking, twelve-factor-compliant runtime shell with nothing paid or ingest-specific in it yet.\n\nCore Requirements:\n- §4.1 repo layout skeleton: `backend/vsir/{core,ingest,vlm,serve,mcp,runner}/__init__.py` placeholders only where a later milestone owns the first real module (never populate a module ahead of its owning milestone).\n- `cli.py` ≈ `impl/scripts/interfaces_demo.py` (read first) — port the argument-parsing skeleton only; wire the `vsir` entrypoint and register `doctor` as the first real subcommand.\n- §4.3 boot self-check: Qdrant reachable, pinned model id does not end in `-latest` (refuse to start — F11 boot half), release_id resolvable.\n- §4.2 pin python 3.11, fastapi==0.141.1, uvicorn[standard]==0.52.4, python-multipart==0.0.32, google-genai==2.22.0, qdrant-client==1.19.0, PyMuPDF==1.28.2, pillow==12.3.0 in `requirements.txt` + generate a lock file.\n- REWRITE `docker-compose.test.yml` from any Postgres service to `qdrant/qdrant:v1.19.0` on test ports (backend 8001, Qdrant REST 6335 gRPC — never reuse dev 6334).\n- §15 Dockerfile: non-root user, digest-pinned base image, read-only rootfs, tmpfs mount for the raster cache; `.env.example` with every Factor III var used so far (`VSIR_ENV`, `VSIR_QDRANT_URL`, `VSIR_RELEASE_ID`, `VSIR_LOG_LEVEL`, `VSIR_PORT`).\n- `GET /health` (always green if process is up) and `GET /ready` (red if Qdrant unreachable) per §15.1, minimal FastAPI app.\n- Structured JSON logs to stdout (no `logging.FileHandler` — §12.5 cloud-native grep); SIGTERM handler that exits cleanly (no in-flight work yet, so this is just the hook).\n- §0/§13 D1–D7 restated in README.\n\nWorking Deliverable:\n- `vsir` CLI binary with a working `doctor` subcommand and a minimal FastAPI process exposing `/health` and `/ready`.\n\nDemo Command:\n- `vsir doctor` — prints PASS/FAIL per boot check (Qdrant reachable, model id not `-latest`, release_id set) and exits non-zero on any FAIL.\n\nDeliverables (files):\n- `backend/vsir/cli.py` (written; skeleton only, ≈ `impl/scripts/interfaces_demo.py` for arg-parsing shape)\n- `backend/vsir/core/health.py` (written — boot checks only; `grounded_rate` logic is M2a's)\n- `backend/vsir/serve/app.py` (written — health/ready only; full app is M3's)\n- `Dockerfile`, `docker-compose.test.yml` (rewritten), `.env.example`, `requirements.txt`, `requirements.lock`\n- `README.md` (D1–D7 section)\n\nTwelve-Factor Notes:\n- Adds `.env.example` vars: `VSIR_ENV`, `VSIR_QDRANT_URL`, `VSIR_RELEASE_ID`, `VSIR_LOG_LEVEL`, `VSIR_PORT`.\n- JSON logs to stdout from process start; SIGTERM handler stub; no process-local correctness-bearing state introduced.\n\n---\n\nUnit ID: U002\nName: Test harness, conformance greps, and AGENTS.md\nMilestone: M0\nType: harness\nPriority: P0-Critical\nSize Estimate: Medium\nSpend: none\nDepends On: [U001]\nEnables: [U003]\nSpec References: [Spec §12.5, §4.4]\nInvariants Enforced: []\nFailure Rows Closed: []\nRequired Reading: [`pipeline-guide/IMPROVEMENTS.md` E6 (no tests — the register item this unit exists to not reproduce)]\n\nDescription:\n- Give every later unit a runnable, growing test/CI surface and turn the §12.5 conformance rules into an executable gate instead of a checklist.\n\nCore Requirements:\n- §12.5 conformance greps as a pytest module scoped to `backend/vsir/**` + `requirements*.txt` (never markdown, never the test's own file): no `MatchText`/`MatchTextAny` under `serve/`; no fuzzy/similarity/edit-distance library in requirements; no field named `score` in a response model; no model id ending `-latest`; no `alembic`/`sqlalchemy`; no `get_text(` outside `ingest/probe.py`; no `SCHEMA_CARD`/`IdClass`/`entity_keys`/`classify(`.\n- Cloud-native grep set, same scope + `Dockerfile*` + `docker-compose*.yml`: no `logging.FileHandler`; no image tagged `latest`; no credential literals (`api_key=`, `token=`, `Bearer ` + literal); no `if TESTING` / `if os.environ.get(\"TESTING\")` branches in `backend/vsir/**`; no `RetrievalState`-style module-level mutable session store.\n- `scripts/test-unit.sh`, `scripts/test-api.sh`, `scripts/test-e2e.sh` extended to run against this repo's actual layout (not placeholders); `scripts/test-paid.sh` added, gated on `VSIR_ALLOW_PAID=1`, refuses to run otherwise.\n- `AGENTS.md` filled with the real, working commands (not aspirational ones) for doctor/test-unit/test-api/test-paid.\n\nWorking Deliverable:\n- Runnable conformance-grep pytest module wired into `scripts/test-unit.sh`.\n\nDemo Command:\n- `bash scripts/test-unit.sh` — runs `vsir doctor`'s underlying checks plus the conformance-grep suite and prints PASS; introducing a `score` field or a `logging.FileHandler` anywhere in scope should be shown failing it once (reviewer can `git stash`/inject to see the red).\n\nDeliverables (files):\n- `backend/tests/unit/test_conformance.py` (written, net new)\n- `scripts/test-unit.sh`, `scripts/test-api.sh`, `scripts/test-e2e.sh`, `scripts/test-paid.sh` (written)\n- `AGENTS.md` (written)\n\nTwelve-Factor Notes:\n- N/A — adds no process, endpoint, tool or worker; it is test tooling only.\n\n---\n\nUnit ID: U003\nName: core/record, ids, and the INDEXED bootstrap\nMilestone: M1\nType: core\nPriority: P0-Critical\nSize Estimate: Medium\nSpend: none\nDepends On: [U001, U002]\nEnables: [U004]\nSpec References: [Spec §5.1, §5.3, §5.4, §5.5]\nInvariants Enforced: [I6]\nFailure Rows Closed: []\nRequired Reading: [`impl/app/pagemodel.py` (record shape and `make_page_id` — read first); `pipeline-guide/METADATA-CONTRACT.md` (§5.3); `IMPROVEMENTS.md` A5 (`image_path` — must NOT be reproduced in the record) and B1/B4 (provenance gaps — provenance must be a first-class field here)]\n\nDescription:\n- Port the page record shape and identifier scheme from `impl/app/pagemodel.py`, and stand up the single `INDEXED` dict that creates and will later gate the Qdrant schema.\n\nCore Requirements:\n- Read `impl/app/pagemodel.py` first.\n- `core/record.py` ≈ `pagemodel.py` (record shape only, no new business logic): facets / text+vlm_codes / three vectors dense+lexical+captions / nested `content` never filtered / provenance — explicitly NO `image_path` field (A5).\n- `core/ids.py` ≈ `pagemodel.py::make_page_id`: `page_id`/`section_id`/`series_id`/`point_id=uuid5(page_id)`/`run_id=ULID` per §5.1.\n- `core/indexed.py` (net new): the one `INDEXED` dict that will create, gate (M2a/M8) and be asserted at boot (I6); scope keys = INDEXED minus `text` and `vlm_codes`.\n- §5.5 `TextIndexParams`: WORD tokenizer, lowercase, `phrase_matching=True`, `min_token_len=1`; collection name carries dim (`pages_1536`).\n- Qdrant collection + text-index creation using an ephemeral/in-memory client for self-test.\n\nWorking Deliverable:\n- `vsir index selftest` CLI subcommand: creates an ephemeral Qdrant collection from `INDEXED`, builds one `core/record.py` record via `core/ids.py`, upserts and reads it back.\n\nDemo Command:\n- `vsir index selftest` — prints the created collection's schema (vector configs, text-index params) next to the round-tripped record, proving `INDEXED` and the record shape agree and that no `image_path` field exists anywhere in the payload.\n\nDeliverables (files):\n- `backend/vsir/core/record.py` (ported from `impl/app/pagemodel.py`, record-shape subset only)\n- `backend/vsir/core/ids.py` (ported from `impl/app/pagemodel.py::make_page_id`)\n- `backend/vsir/core/indexed.py` (written, net new)\n- `backend/tests/unit/test_record.py`, `backend/tests/unit/test_indexed.py` (written)\n\nTwelve-Factor Notes:\n- N/A for new env vars. The ephemeral Qdrant client used by `selftest` is in-process and disposable — not correctness-bearing state (no C11 violation).\n\n---\n\nUnit ID: U004\nName: tok/variants/exact_filter, Family A envelope, and rrf/sparse ports\nMilestone: M1\nType: core\nPriority: P0-Critical\nSize Estimate: Large\nSpend: none\nDepends On: [U003]\nEnables: [U005, U006]\nSpec References: [Spec §5.6, §7.1, §7.2.1 (ordering), §7.3]\nInvariants Enforced: [I3, I5]\nFailure Rows Closed: [F10]\nRequired Reading: [`impl/app/sparse.py` (read first — D2, ported verbatim where possible); `impl/app/retrieve.py` (read first — `rrf()` is ranks-only, decompose()); `IMPROVEMENTS.md` E9 (scroll-4096-and-filter-in-Python — the exact_filter and scope-key check must use a real Qdrant filter, never scroll+Python filtering)]\n\nDescription:\n- Build the single exact-match path, the Family A search/absence envelope, and port the deterministic ranks-only fusion machinery that every retrieval tool will reuse from M3 onward.\n\nCore Requirements:\n- Read `impl/app/sparse.py` and `impl/app/retrieve.py` first.\n- `core/tok.py`: mirrors Qdrant's WORD tokenizer exactly — NOT `impl`'s `TOKEN_RE` (named porting hazard, §5.6).\n- `core/variants.py`: exactly 3 spellings of the same characters (whitespace variants only).\n- `core/exact.py::exact_filter`: the ONLY exact-match path in the system; no `MatchText`/`MatchTextAny` anywhere else (I3).\n- §7.1 Family A envelope (`SearchResponse[HitT]`): six-value status enum scaffold (`ok`/four absences/`error` — full absence semantics land in M2a–M4 as data becomes available), `empty_is_never_ok` validator, `WEAK_ABS=20` server constant, `weak`/`needs_scope` formula, hit models `DocHit`/`SectionHit`/`PageHit`/`LookupHit`/`ResolveHit`, `ImageRef`/`Preview` types (references only, no bytes).\n- §7.3 cap validators as typed 400s: `dpi_not_allowed`, `dpi_requires_region`, `filter_unknown_key {keys}` — the last one is what closes F10 using `core/indexed.py`'s scope-key set from U003.\n- Port `sparse.py` (D2) and `rrf()` (ranks-only fusion, `rrf_k=60`, weights page 1.0/lexical 1.0/captions 0.4) verbatim as `core` utilities for reuse by M3's/M4's tools.\n\nWorking Deliverable:\n- `vsir index selftest --query <text>` extension: runs `tok`/`variants`/`exact_filter` against the seeded collection and prints a Family A envelope.\n\nDemo Command:\n- `vsir index selftest --query \"SF 1.1A\"` — prints the 3 whitespace variants generated, the exact_filter Qdrant filter used, and a valid `SearchResponse` JSON; then `vsir index selftest --query \"\" --unknown-scope-key foo` to show `filter_unknown_key` as a typed 400 (F10).\n\nDeliverables (files):\n- `backend/vsir/core/tok.py`, `backend/vsir/core/variants.py`, `backend/vsir/core/exact.py` (written, net new)\n- `backend/vsir/core/envelope.py` (written, net new — Family A only; Family B in U006)\n- `backend/vsir/core/sparse.py` (ported from `impl/app/sparse.py`)\n- `backend/vsir/core/rrf.py` (ported from `impl/app/retrieve.py::rrf`)\n- `backend/tests/unit/test_exact.py`, `backend/tests/unit/test_envelope.py`, `backend/tests/unit/test_rrf.py` (written)\n\nTwelve-Factor Notes:\n- N/A — adds no process, endpoint, tool or worker; pure library code exercised through the existing `selftest` CLI.\n\n---\n\nUnit ID: U005\nName: Synthetic fixtures, observed-token inventory, and `vsir demo exact`\nMilestone: M1\nType: core\nPriority: P0-Critical\nSize Estimate: Medium\nSpend: none\nDepends On: [U004]\nEnables: [U006]\nSpec References: [Spec §6.8 (observed-token inventory subset), §12.4, §7.2.2]\nInvariants Enforced: [I2]\nFailure Rows Closed: [F1, F3, F14]\nRequired Reading: [`impl/app/retrieve.py::lookup` (read first — being rewritten as a phrase filter per §5.6); `IMPROVEMENTS.md` A1 (always-extract-text — not relevant to hand-written fixtures, but the pattern this unit must avoid once probe.py exists in M2a)]\n\nDescription:\n- Seed an ephemeral Qdrant with four hand-written pages (no PDF) and wire `lookup` end to end as the flagship, zero-spend M1 proof.\n\nCore Requirements:\n- Hand-write four synthetic pages' `text` fields directly into `core/record.py` records (bypassing any VLM/probe step, since none exists yet): (1) a page containing the literal string `SF 1.1A`; (2) a page with tokens `sf`, `1`, `1a` scattered non-adjacently; (3) a page printing `SF121.1)`; (4) a page whose `vlm_codes` claims `K999` but whose `text` does not contain it.\n- `serve/tools/lookup.py`'s core logic lives here as `core`-level function (the HTTP/MCP wrapper comes in M3): `lookup(label, scope?, include_unverified=False, cap=20)` — exact, phrase-only, a set not a ranking, using `exact_filter` from U004.\n- Build the observed-token inventory (§6.8 subset only — display data, not the full export pipeline) from the four seeded pages so `present_instead` (U006) works before any PDF exists.\n- `lookup(\"K999\")` on the hallucinated-claim page → `not_found` (I2); `include_unverified=True` returns it separately in `unverified_hits`, `verified: false`, never merged into `hits`.\n- §12.4's 8 compact-label variants exercised against page (2)/(3) to prove I3's variant matching in practice (F3).\n\nWorking Deliverable:\n- `vsir demo exact --synthetic` CLI subcommand — the milestone's official demo.\n\nDemo Command:\n- `vsir demo exact --synthetic` — seeds the four pages into an ephemeral Qdrant, then runs `lookup(\"SF 1.1A\")` (exactly 1 hit — F1), `lookup(\"sf1.1a\")`/7 other compact spellings (all resolve to the same page — F3), and `lookup(\"K999\")` (→ `not_found`, `unverified_hits` only with `include_unverified=True` — F14/I2).\n\nDeliverables (files):\n- `backend/vsir/core/lookup.py` (written — core lookup logic; tool wrapper is M3's `serve/tools/lookup.py`)\n- `backend/vsir/core/observed_tokens.py` (written, net new — §6.8 subset)\n- `data/fixtures/synthetic_pages/*.json` (written — 4 hand-written page records)\n- `backend/tests/unit/test_lookup.py`, `backend/tests/unit/test_observed_tokens.py` (written)\n\nTwelve-Factor Notes:\n- N/A — adds no process, endpoint, tool or worker.\n\n---\n\nUnit ID: U006\nName: core/verify.py, present_instead, and Family B envelope\nMilestone: M1\nType: core\nPriority: P0-Critical\nSize Estimate: Medium\nSpend: none\nDepends On: [U004, U005]\nEnables: [U007]\nSpec References: [Spec §7.1 (Family B), §7.2.4, §12.4]\nInvariants Enforced: []\nFailure Rows Closed: [F2 (core), F16]\nRequired Reading: [`impl/app/retrieve.py` (verify-adjacent logic, read first — no direct `verify` predecessor, this is mostly net new per layout note); `IMPROVEMENTS.md` — confirms `present_instead` must never become a distance/similarity function (guards against reintroducing a fuzzy-match library, which U002's conformance grep also catches)]\n\nDescription:\n- Implement per-`(claim, page)` verification and the deterministic near-miss generator, and define the Family B envelope used by `verify`/`fetch`/`read`.\n\nCore Requirements:\n- `core/verify.py::verify_claims`: per `(claim, page)` — not per claim — so a draft citing `p001–p002` cannot let a code from the neighbouring page through (this is the mechanism I8 will later gate on; the tool wrapper comes at M3).\n- Three states only: `present | absent | unverifiable` — same vocabulary `read` will reuse later (§7.2.6).\n- `present_instead`: a prefix lookup over U005's observed-token inventory, capped at 5, labelled \"different part\" — never a distance (F16).\n- §12.4 near-miss generator: produces the adversarial near-miss set (e.g. `K73` on a page only containing `K78`) used both here and later by M3's `vsir eval abstention`.\n- Family B envelope (`ToolEnvelope[ResultT]`, `VerifyResult`): `status: ok|error` describes whether the call ran, not what it found; a page with every claim `absent` is still `status: ok`.\n\nWorking Deliverable:\n- `vsir demo exact --synthetic --verify <claims>` extension to U005's CLI.\n\nDemo Command:\n- `vsir demo exact --synthetic --verify K73,K158,K999` — prints a `VerifyResult` map showing `K158: present`, `K73: absent` with `present_instead` from the near-miss fixture, and `K999: absent` with `present_instead: []` (F2 core, F16).\n\nDeliverables (files):\n- `backend/vsir/core/verify.py` (written, net new)\n- `backend/vsir/core/nearmiss.py` (written, net new — §12.4 generator)\n- `backend/vsir/core/envelope.py` (extended — Family B added alongside U004's Family A)\n- `backend/tests/unit/test_verify.py`, `backend/tests/unit/test_nearmiss.py` (written)\n\nTwelve-Factor Notes:\n- N/A — adds no process, endpoint, tool or worker.\n\n---\n\nUnit ID: U007\nName: manifest, probe, render, doc-facts, and windowing\nMilestone: M2a\nType: ingest\nPriority: P0-Critical\nSize Estimate: Large\nSpend: none\nDepends On: [U001, U006]\nEnables: [U008]\nSpec References: [Spec §6.1 (steps 01–05), §6.2, §6.4]\nInvariants Enforced: []\nFailure Rows Closed: [F4 (M2a half), F13, F15]\nRequired Reading: [`impl/app/textlayer.py` (read first — `probe`/`page_texts`/`content_hash`); `impl/app/render.py` (read first); `impl/app/windows.py` (read first); `impl/pipeline-guide/01-entry.md`, `02-probe-and-render.md`, `03-document-facts.md`, `04-windowing-and-keys.md`; `IMPROVEMENTS.md` A1 (always-extract-text — probe.py must gate on actual text presence, not extract unconditionally) and E3 (rendering never collected — render outputs must be eligible for cache eviction, not accumulate unbounded)]\n\nDescription:\n- Port the entry manifest, text-layer probing, page rendering, document facts, and the bisecting windowing ladder, and generate the checked-in 3-window synthetic PDF fixture with its off-by-one and crop traps.\n\nCore Requirements:\n- Read `impl/app/textlayer.py`, `impl/app/render.py`, `impl/app/windows.py` first.\n- `ingest/manifest.py` ≈ `impl/app/pipeline.py` (entry/manifest only — step 01).\n- `ingest/probe.py` ← `textlayer.py::probe/page_texts/content_hash` (steps 02–04: `has_text` facet, full-page text extraction, `content_hash`, doc facts/`doc_type`).\n- `ingest/render.py` ← `render.py`, rendering at `dpi_index=150` (§4.2).\n- `ingest/window.py` ← `windows.py` (+ bisection ladder, F13): target 30 pages/window; bisect-and-re-bill on `MAX_TOKENS`/truncation/offset-failure; typed `window_unsplittable`; v1 is Level 0/1 + bisection only — a Level-2 document fails typed `ladder_level_2_required` (this unit defines the check; M8 exercises it against a real Level-2-marked fixture).\n- §6.4 the two independent offset checks (mechanism only here; the gate that gates on them is M2a's `gates.py`, U011).\n- Generate `data/source/synthetic_3window.pdf`: known printed labels, a deliberate off-by-one trap (printed page numbers vs. physical index diverge), and a crop trap (a code visually cropped at render time but present in the underlying full-page text) — proves `text` always comes from the full page (F15), independent of any render crop.\n\nWorking Deliverable:\n- `vsir ingest <pdf> --vlm stub --until window` (the `--until` debug flag is added here and reused by U008–U010).\n\nDemo Command:\n- `vsir ingest data/source/synthetic_3window.pdf --vlm stub --until window` — prints per-page `has_text`/`content_hash`/doc facts and the resulting window plan (3 windows), and confirms the crop-trap page's indexed `text` contains the full label despite the render crop.\n\nDeliverables (files):\n- `backend/vsir/ingest/manifest.py` (ported from `impl/app/pipeline.py`, entry subset)\n- `backend/vsir/ingest/probe.py` (ported from `impl/app/textlayer.py`)\n- `backend/vsir/ingest/render.py` (ported from `impl/app/render.py`)\n- `backend/vsir/ingest/window.py` (ported from `impl/app/windows.py`, + bisection ladder written net new)\n- `data/source/synthetic_3window.pdf` (written, generated fixture, checked in)\n- `backend/tests/unit/test_probe.py`, `test_render.py`, `test_window.py` (written)\n\nTwelve-Factor Notes:\n- Adds `.env.example` vars: `VSIR_RASTER_CACHE_DIR` (tmpfs path from U001's Dockerfile, not correctness-bearing — rasters are always re-derivable from the PDF, C11-safe).\n- No process-local correctness state: window plans and facts are recomputed from the PDF + content_hash, never cached to disk outside the ephemeral raster cache.\n\n---\n\nUnit ID: U008\nName: VLM stub/client/cache and S2 extraction\nMilestone: M2a\nType: ingest\nPriority: P0-Critical\nSize Estimate: Large\nSpend: none\nDepends On: [U007]\nEnables: [U009]\nSpec References: [Spec §5.2, §6.1 (step 06), §6.3]\nInvariants Enforced: []\nFailure Rows Closed: [F11 (M2a key half)]\nRequired Reading: [`impl/app/segment.py` (read first — Gemini call shape and the old S1 schema being replaced); `impl/pipeline-guide/05-extraction.md`, `../SEGMENTATION.md`; `IMPROVEMENTS.md` B6 (pin the model — `vlm/client.py` must hard-fail on an alias id, reusing U001's boot check pattern) and D3 (captions never written — this unit must actually populate the captions field this VLM call produces, since M1's `rrf` already expects a captions branch)]\n\nDescription:\n- Build the VLM abstraction (stub and real client scaffolding, cache, prompts) and the S2 window extraction step, with `VSIR_VLM=stub` selected purely by config.\n\nCore Requirements:\n- Read `impl/app/segment.py` first.\n- `vlm/client.py` (net new): thin Gemini wrapper; pinned model id only (never `-latest`, reuses U001's boot check).\n- `vlm/stub.py` (net new): deterministic, fixture-driven fake VLM responses selected by `VSIR_VLM=stub` — config, never a code branch or `if TESTING` (rule 5).\n- `vlm/cache.py` (net new): §6.3 cache keys — `facts_key`, `extract_key` (model id + prompt version; `VSIR_VLM_TIER` is explicitly NOT part of `extract_key`).\n- `vlm/prompts/s1.md`, `s2.md` (net new prompt text, versioned).\n- `ingest/extract.py` ≈ `impl/app/segment.py` (new S2 schema per §5.2: `PageOut`/`SectionRef`/`Summary`/`WindowOut`; **Prohibited**: any identifier grammar, classification enum, regex taxonomy, or per-corpus keyword list).\n- Replay mode: `VSIR_VLM=stub` + `VSIR_FIXTURE=<dir>` with a typed `fixture_miss` when the fixture directory lacks the requested key.\n\nWorking Deliverable:\n- `vsir ingest <pdf> --vlm stub --until extract`.\n\nDemo Command:\n- `vsir ingest data/source/synthetic_3window.pdf --vlm stub --until extract` — prints the raw S2 `WindowOut` JSON per window from the stub VLM, and re-running with a changed prompt version shows a different `extract_key` (F11 key half).\n\nDeliverables (files):\n- `backend/vsir/vlm/client.py`, `vlm/stub.py`, `vlm/cache.py` (written, net new)\n- `backend/vsir/vlm/prompts/s1.md`, `vlm/prompts/s2.md` (written, net new)\n- `backend/vsir/ingest/extract.py` (ported from `impl/app/segment.py`, schema rewritten to S2)\n- `backend/tests/unit/test_extract.py`, `test_vlm_cache.py` (written)\n\nTwelve-Factor Notes:\n- Adds `.env.example` vars: `VSIR_VLM` (`stub|real`), `VSIR_VLM_MODEL`, `VSIR_VLM_TIER`, `VSIR_FIXTURE`, `GEMINI_API_KEY` (unused until real path, but declared here since the client scaffold reads it).\n- Stub-vs-real is purely `VSIR_VLM` config, no code branch; no VLM output cached to local disk outside the declared `VSIR_FIXTURE` path (which is itself read-only, checked-in fixture data, not runtime state).\n\n---\n\nUnit ID: U009\nName: Derivation, gating removal, and stitching\nMilestone: M2a\nType: ingest\nPriority: P0-Critical\nSize Estimate: Large\nSpend: none\nDepends On: [U008]\nEnables: [U010]\nSpec References: [Spec §6.1 (steps 07–08), §6.5, §5.7]\nInvariants Enforced: []\nFailure Rows Closed: [F5 (M2a half), F6, F8 (M2a stitching half)]\nRequired Reading: [`impl/app/segment.py` (read first — derivation logic being carried without the allowlist gate); `impl/app/stitch.py` (read first); `impl/pipeline-guide/06-derivation-and-gate.md` (⚠ documents the DELETED allowlist gate — do not port it), `07-stitch-and-numbering.md`; `IMPROVEMENTS.md` — confirms the allowlist/`classify()` pattern must not reappear (also enforced mechanically by U002's conformance grep)]\n\nDescription:\n- Port per-page derivation (grounded_rate, no allowlist gate) and section stitching with cross-window carry-in and code reattribution.\n\nCore Requirements:\n- Read `impl/app/segment.py` and `impl/app/stitch.py` first.\n- `ingest/derive.py` ≈ `segment.py` (derivation logic only, the allowlist/`classify()` gate is deleted — grounded_rate replaces it per §5.7: `None` where `has_text` is false).\n- Label precedence + ambiguity → list; code reattribution with `moved_from` when a code derived on one page actually belongs on its neighbour (F6, per-page `grounded_rate`).\n- `ingest/stitch.py` ← `stitch.py` (sections, + `series_id`): canonical section key + carry-in across window boundaries so a straddling section is not mistaken for a fully-searched chapter (F8, stitching half).\n\nWorking Deliverable:\n- `vsir ingest <pdf> --vlm stub --until stitch`.\n\nDemo Command:\n- `vsir ingest data/source/synthetic_3window.pdf --vlm stub --until stitch` — prints stitched `PageOut` records with `section_id`, per-page `grounded_rate`, and (on a fixture with a deliberately misattributed code) the `moved_from` field populated.\n\nDeliverables (files):\n- `backend/vsir/ingest/derive.py` (ported from `impl/app/segment.py`, gate removed)\n- `backend/vsir/ingest/stitch.py` (ported from `impl/app/stitch.py`, + `series_id` written net new)\n- `backend/tests/unit/test_derive.py`, `test_stitch.py` (written)\n\nTwelve-Factor Notes:\n- N/A — adds no process, endpoint, tool or worker.\n\n---\n\nUnit ID: U010\nName: Embedding and indexing\nMilestone: M2a\nType: ingest\nPriority: P0-Critical\nSize Estimate: Large\nSpend: none\nDepends On: [U009]\nEnables: [U011]\nSpec References: [Spec §6.1 (steps 09–10), §6.6, §4.2 (D4, D12)]\nInvariants Enforced: []\nFailure Rows Closed: []\nRequired Reading: [`impl/app/embedder.py` (read first — D4 interleaved embedding); `impl/app/sparse.py` (read first, D2 — reused from U004's port); `impl/app/segstore.py` (read first); `pipeline-guide/08-embedding.md`, `09-indexing.md` (⚠ `entity_keys` index deleted — do not port it); `IMPROVEMENTS.md` B5 (cache embeddings — do not silently reuse stale embeddings across a fingerprint change) and D3 (captions never written — the captions vector must actually be populated and indexed here, completing what U008 started) and E7 (orphan points — index.py must never leave points without a valid run/publish linkage)]\n\nDescription:\n- Port dense/lexical/captions embedding and Qdrant upsert with the `is_current` flag and embedding-fingerprint protection.\n\nCore Requirements:\n- Read `impl/app/embedder.py`, `impl/app/sparse.py`, `impl/app/segstore.py` first.\n- `ingest/embed.py` ← `embedder.py` (D4 interleaved dense embedding: page image + text + captions in one call shape); reuses U004's ported `sparse.py` for the lexical branch.\n- `ingest/index.py` ≈ `segstore.py` (+ text indexes, `is_current`): Qdrant upsert using `point_id=uuid5(page_id)` from U003, `INDEXED` schema from U003, `is_current=False` at this stage (publish flips it — U011).\n- §6.6 embedding fingerprint `{embed_model, dim, distance, composition_version}`: refuse to upsert on mismatch; on mismatch, new collection + re-embed + alias swap (no in-place mutation).\n- dim ∈ {768, 1536, 3072}, concurrency=8, batch_size=8, max_edge_px=1568 per §4.2.\n\nWorking Deliverable:\n- `vsir ingest <pdf> --vlm stub --until index`.\n\nDemo Command:\n- `vsir ingest data/source/synthetic_3window.pdf --vlm stub --until index` — ingests into the ephemeral Qdrant with `is_current=False`; a follow-up raw scroll/count shows N points with correct `point_id`s and the fingerprint stamped in the collection's payload schema; re-running with a mutated `embed_model` shows the refusal.\n\nDeliverables (files):\n- `backend/vsir/ingest/embed.py` (ported from `impl/app/embedder.py`)\n- `backend/vsir/ingest/index.py` (ported from `impl/app/segstore.py`, + text indexes/`is_current` written net new)\n- `backend/tests/unit/test_embed.py`, `test_index.py` (written)\n\nTwelve-Factor Notes:\n- Adds `.env.example` vars: `VSIR_EMBED_MODEL`, `VSIR_EMBED_DIM`, `VSIR_EMBED_CONCURRENCY`, `VSIR_EMBED_BATCH_SIZE`.\n- No local embedding cache on disk; the fingerprint check is enforced against the Qdrant collection itself, never a local file (C11).\n\n---\n\nUnit ID: U011\nName: Gates, export, and run orchestration\nMilestone: M2a\nType: ingest\nPriority: P0-Critical\nSize Estimate: Large\nSpend: none\nDepends On: [U010]\nEnables: [U012, U014]\nSpec References: [Spec §6.1 (steps 11–12), §6.4, §6.7, §6.8, §6.9, §11.1, §4.4]\nInvariants Enforced: [I1, I4, I7]\nFailure Rows Closed: [F7, F12 (M2a half), F17]\nRequired Reading: [`impl/app/pipeline.py`, `impl/app/segjobs.py` (read first — run orchestration being restructured); `pipeline-guide/10-gates-and-publish.md` (⚠ allowlist/`class_totality` replaced by `grounded_rate`), `11-export.md` (⚠ `withheld.jsonl` dropped from this step — it lives only as a frozen M2b parity artefact); `12-reproducibility.md` (§6.3/§6.6); `IMPROVEMENTS.md` E2 (job state on daemon threads — run state must live in the `vsir_runs` Qdrant collection, never a Python thread/global) and E7 (orphan points — the three-clause retirement rule this unit implements exists specifically to prevent this)]\n\nDescription:\n- Close the pipeline: publish gating, the `vsir_runs` control collection, the three-clause retirement rule, exports, and the run record — the unit that makes `vsir ingest` a complete, gated, resumable-by-contract pipeline.\n\nCore Requirements:\n- Read `impl/app/pipeline.py` and `impl/app/segjobs.py` first.\n- `ingest/gates.py` ≈ `pipeline.py` (grounded_rate replaces the allowlist, §11.1): `window_coverage` (block, must be 1.0), `offset_check` (block, both §6.4 checks pass — I4), `grounded_rate ≥ 0.8` provisional (block, `vsir publish --override grounded_rate --reason \"…\"` records `published_with_override`), `text_coverage` (flag `mostly_scanned`, never block; **at 0.0 the grounded_rate gate is skipped entirely**), `label_monotonic` (flag `label_conflict`).\n- `ingest/export.py` (net new): `labels.jsonl` + `observed_tokens.jsonl` streamed over HTTP (§6.8); `safety_flag` derived from manifest `doc_type` + model topics — never a keyword list.\n- `ingest/run.py` ≈ `pipeline.py`/`segjobs.py`: `vsir_runs` control collection (run + window points, state enum `{queued,running,stopped,gated,published,failed}`), advisory lease + `--steal`, §6.7 three-clause retirement (delete same doc+revision earlier `run_id` → F12; set prior *other* revision `is_current=False` and KEEP → F9, owned by M8 since it needs a second revision; never touch other documents).\n- I1: `point_id` uniqueness + `count(doc,rev) == pdf.page_count` asserted after publish. I7: `is_current=False` until gates pass; every tool injects `is_current=True` by default (mechanism proven here, tool-level default enforced from M3 onward).\n- `vsir runs show <run_id>`, `vsir gates rerun <run_id>`, `vsir publish --override <gate> --reason` (§4.4).\n- F17 proof: kill an ingest mid-run (SIGKILL the process) → 0 pages queryable (because `is_current` never flipped).\n\nWorking Deliverable:\n- `vsir ingest <pdf> --vlm stub` (full pipeline, no `--until`) + `vsir runs show` + `vsir gates rerun` + `vsir publish --override`.\n\nDemo Command:\n- `vsir ingest data/source/synthetic_3window.pdf --vlm stub && vsir runs show <run_id>` — the milestone demo: run reaches `published`, gate results shown, F7's off-by-one trap fixture proven caught by `offset_check`, and a second identical ingest shown retiring the first run's points without touching anything else (F12).\n\nDeliverables (files):\n- `backend/vsir/ingest/gates.py` (ported from `impl/app/pipeline.py`, gate logic replaced per §11.1)\n- `backend/vsir/ingest/export.py` (written, net new)\n- `backend/vsir/ingest/run.py` (ported from `impl/app/pipeline.py` / `impl/app/segjobs.py`)\n- `backend/vsir/core/status.py` (written, net new — run state enum)\n- `backend/tests/unit/test_gates.py`, `test_export.py`, `test_run.py` (written)\n- `backend/tests/api/test_publish_gating.py` (written — F17 kill-mid-run proof)\n\nTwelve-Factor Notes:\n- Adds `.env.example` vars: `VSIR_GROUNDED_RATE_THRESHOLD` (provisional, 0.8 — reset by M2b's R4), `VSIR_LEASE_TTL_SECONDS`.\n- Run/window state lives entirely in the `vsir_runs` Qdrant collection — no daemon threads, no local job-state files (E2); SIGTERM during ingest leaves the run in `stopped` state, resumable, not `published` (full checkpoint granularity is M8's).\n\n---\n\nUnit ID: U012\nName: Port legacy fixtures and parity/negative sets\nMilestone: M2b\nType: eval\nPriority: P1-High\nSize Estimate: Medium\nSpend: none\nDepends On: [U011]\nEnables: [U013]\nSpec References: [Spec §6.8, §12.1, §17 (OQ-1)]\nInvariants Enforced: []\nFailure Rows Closed: []\nRequired Reading: [`impl/data/raw/*` (read first — old-schema baseline being ported as-is); `impl/data/exports/r-poc-*/labels.jsonl`, `withheld.jsonl` (read first — the parity and negative sets)]\n\nDescription:\n- Port already-paid-for legacy pipeline outputs into this repo as fixtures, before spending anything new, so the real M2b ingest (U013) has a parity baseline to check against.\n\nCore Requirements:\n- Copy `impl/data/raw/*` → `data/fixtures/legacy/` verbatim as the old-schema baseline (no reshaping — this is intentionally the *old* schema, kept for comparison).\n- Copy `impl/data/exports/r-poc-*/labels.jsonl` and `withheld.jsonl` → `data/fixtures/legacy/` as the parity set and the negative set respectively.\n- `vsir eval parity` (net new CLI subcommand): loads the legacy fixtures, reports counts and basic shape validation (labels present, withheld codes present) — pure read, no model call, so it can run before U013's real spend and before any new-schema data exists.\n- Note OQ-1 (pilot PDF location) blocks only U013's re-bill, not this unit — the S2 responses this unit ports are already paid for and sitting in `impl/data/raw/*`.\n\nWorking Deliverable:\n- `vsir eval parity` CLI subcommand.\n\nDemo Command:\n- `vsir eval parity --legacy data/fixtures/legacy` — prints row counts for the ported `labels.jsonl`/`withheld.jsonl` and confirms the legacy raw dump loads without error.\n\nDeliverables (files):\n- `data/fixtures/legacy/*` (ported verbatim from `impl/data/raw/*` and `impl/data/exports/r-poc-*/`)\n- `backend/vsir/cli.py` (extended — `eval parity` subcommand)\n- `backend/vsir/core/parity.py` (written, net new)\n- `backend/tests/unit/test_parity.py` (written)\n\nTwelve-Factor Notes:\n- N/A — adds no process, endpoint, tool or worker; pure fixture loading.\n\n---\n\nUnit ID: U013\nName: Real TC1E-SF ingest and grounded_rate threshold\nMilestone: M2b\nType: ingest\nPriority: P0-Critical\nSize Estimate: Large\nSpend: paid\nDepends On: [U012, U011]\nEnables: [U016, U019]\nSpec References: [Spec §6.7, §11.1 (R4), §17 (OQ-1, OQ-2)]\nInvariants Enforced: []\nFailure Rows Closed: []\nRequired Reading: [`impl/INGESTION_WALKTHROUGH.md` (M2a/M2b debugging); `IMPROVEMENTS.md` — reconfirm B6 (pinned model) applies to this, the first real Gemini call in the whole plan]\n\nDescription:\n- Run the one real, paid ingest of TC1E-SF (55 pages) under the new S2 schema, freeze the resulting fixtures, and set the `grounded_rate` publish threshold from the observed distribution.\n\nCore Requirements:\n- `VSIR_ALLOW_PAID=1 vsir ingest data/source/TC1E-SF.pdf` (real VLM path via U008's `vlm/client.py`, real embedding via U010's `ingest/embed.py`) — this is the FIRST real spend anywhere in the plan; refuses to run without `VSIR_ALLOW_PAID=1`.\n- Freeze `data/fixtures/TC1E-SF/{raw_window_1.json, raw_window_2.json, text.json, expected.json}` from this one run, for use as `VSIR_FIXTURE` replay data by every later paid unit (U019, U020, U022).\n- Report the `grounded_rate` distribution across the 55 pages and set `VSIR_GROUNDED_RATE_THRESHOLD` from it (R4), replacing U011's provisional 0.8.\n- Runs through the same `vsir ingest`/`vsir gates rerun`/`vsir publish` surface built in U011 — no new pipeline code, only real credentials and real data.\n\nWorking Deliverable:\n- The same `vsir ingest`/`vsir runs show` CLI from U011, now exercised against real data and a real Gemini key.\n\nDemo Command:\n- `VSIR_ALLOW_PAID=1 vsir ingest data/source/TC1E-SF.pdf && vsir runs show <run_id>` — shows a published run over 55 real pages, with the grounded_rate distribution report printed and the frozen fixture files written to `data/fixtures/TC1E-SF/`.\n\nDeliverables (files):\n- `data/fixtures/TC1E-SF/raw_window_1.json`, `raw_window_2.json`, `text.json`, `expected.json` (written, frozen from the real run)\n- `backend/vsir/core/grounded_rate_report.py` (written, net new — distribution report used to set R4)\n- `.env.example` updated with the resolved `VSIR_GROUNDED_RATE_THRESHOLD` documented as \"set by M2b, see report\"\n\nTwelve-Factor Notes:\n- Uses `GEMINI_API_KEY` (declared in U008's `.env.example`) and `VSIR_ALLOW_PAID` (declared here) — no literal credentials committed anywhere (per U002's conformance grep).\n- Blocked on OQ-1 (pilot PDF location) and OQ-2 (Gemini key) per §17 — this unit cannot run until both are resolved; everything upstream of it (U001–U012) is provable without either.\n\n---\n\nUnit ID: U014\nName: serve/app, auth, audit, and budget scaffolding\nMilestone: M3\nType: tool\nPriority: P0-Critical\nSize Estimate: Medium\nSpend: none\nDepends On: [U011, U002]\nEnables: [U015]\nSpec References: [Spec §7.4, §11.3, §15.1]\nInvariants Enforced: []\nFailure Rows Closed: []\nRequired Reading: [`impl/app/main.py` (read first — HTTP app shape being restructured); `IMPROVEMENTS.md` E5 (no auth — the defect this unit directly closes) and E4 (no cost observability — audit line must carry cost, never expose it in the response body)]\n\nDescription:\n- Build the real FastAPI serving app with bearer auth, the ten-field audit log, and request budget scaffolding, replacing U001's minimal health-only stub.\n\nCore Requirements:\n- Read `impl/app/main.py` first.\n- `serve/app.py` ≈ `main.py`: full app boot, reusing U001's `/health`/`/ready` and its boot self-check (INDEXED schema assertion — refuse to serve at boot if schema mismatches, per §11.3).\n- `serve/auth.py` (net new): bearer token auth on every route except `/health`.\n- `serve/audit.py` (net new): the ten-field audit line per request (§7.4) — cost recorded in the audit log, never in the response body.\n- `serve/budget.py` (net new): per-caller request budget scaffolding; `reads_remaining` computed and available for every envelope (actual `read` quota consumption is wired in M5).\n- §11.3 degradation rows relevant here: Qdrant unreachable → `503 qdrant_unavailable` (never an empty result); embedding-model/collection fingerprint mismatch → refuse to upsert (already built in U010, wired to a 503 here at the serving layer too).\n\nWorking Deliverable:\n- `vsir serve` CLI subcommand starting the full authenticated app.\n\nDemo Command:\n- `vsir serve &` then `curl localhost:8000/health` (200, no auth needed) vs. `curl localhost:8000/pages/x/image` (401 without a bearer token) — and the resulting audit log line printed to stdout showing the ten fields including cost=0.\n\nDeliverables (files):\n- `backend/vsir/serve/app.py` (ported from `impl/app/main.py`)\n- `backend/vsir/serve/auth.py`, `serve/audit.py`, `serve/budget.py` (written, net new)\n- `backend/tests/api/test_auth.py`, `test_audit.py` (written)\n\nTwelve-Factor Notes:\n- Adds `.env.example` vars: `VSIR_API_TOKEN` (bearer secret, never a literal in code), `VSIR_READ_QUOTA_PER_CALLER`.\n- Structured JSON audit lines to stdout (no file handler); stateless — auth/budget state derived per-request from the token, no session store.\n\n---\n\nUnit ID: U015\nName: lookup/verify HTTP+MCP tools\nMilestone: M3\nType: tool\nPriority: P0-Critical\nSize Estimate: Large\nSpend: none\nDepends On: [U014, U004, U006]\nEnables: [U016, U017]\nSpec References: [Spec §7.2.2, §7.2.4, §7.5, §7.6]\nInvariants Enforced: []\nFailure Rows Closed: [F2 (tool half), F4 (M3 half)]\nRequired Reading: [`impl/app/retrieve.py::lookup` (read first — being rewritten as a phrase filter per §5.6); `impl/app/api_models.py` (read first — envelope wiring precedent); `IMPROVEMENTS.md` E9 (scroll-4096-and-filter-in-Python — the HTTP layer must call U004's `exact_filter`, never re-implement filtering client-side)]\n\nDescription:\n- Wrap M1's core `lookup`/`verify` logic as the first two real tools, exposed identically over HTTP and MCP, closing the tool-layer halves of F2 and F4.\n\nCore Requirements:\n- Read `impl/app/retrieve.py::lookup` and `impl/app/api_models.py` first.\n- `serve/envelope.py` ≈ `api_models.py`: wires U004's Family A / U006's Family B pydantic models into actual HTTP response models, with the full six-value status enum surfaced (`not_found`, `not_searchable`, `out_of_scope`, `found_only_in_superseded`, `error`, `ok`) — `not_searchable` now reachable end-to-end against a real scanned candidate from M2a data (F4, M3 half).\n- `serve/tools/lookup.py` ≈ `retrieve.py::lookup` (rewritten as phrase filter): thin HTTP wrapper over `core/lookup.py`.\n- `serve/tools/verify.py` (net new): thin HTTP wrapper over `core/verify.py::verify_claims` — this is the tool-layer half of F2 (`verify` confirming a code not on the page must 400/absent, never silently pass).\n- `mcp/server.py` (net new): stdio + SSE transport, exposing `lookup` and `verify` through the exact SAME implementations as the HTTP routes (stateless, §7.5) — no second copy of the logic.\n- §7.6 refusals enforced at this boundary: no `score` field, no routing, no composing outside the runner, no fuzzy matching (all also caught mechanically by U002's conformance grep).\n- CLI one-shots: `vsir lookup`, `vsir verify` (§4.4).\n\nWorking Deliverable:\n- `vsir serve` with working `/lookup` and `/verify` routes, plus `vsir mcp --stdio`/`--sse` exposing the same two tools.\n\nDemo Command:\n- `vsir serve &` then `vsir lookup \"SF 1.1A\" && vsir verify --claims K73 --pages TC1E-SF@1.3#p008` — plus the same two calls issued over `vsir mcp --stdio` piped JSON-RPC, showing byte-identical envelope bodies (proving \"same implementations\").\n\nDeliverables (files):\n- `backend/vsir/serve/envelope.py` (ported from `impl/app/api_models.py`)\n- `backend/vsir/serve/tools/lookup.py` (ported from `impl/app/retrieve.py::lookup`)\n- `backend/vsir/serve/tools/verify.py` (written, net new)\n- `backend/vsir/mcp/server.py` (written, net new)\n- `backend/vsir/cli.py` (extended — `lookup`, `verify`, `serve`, `mcp` subcommands)\n- `backend/tests/api/test_lookup_route.py`, `test_verify_route.py`, `backend/tests/unit/test_mcp_server.py` (written)\n\nTwelve-Factor Notes:\n- MCP server is stateless like the HTTP app — no per-session state; SSE/stdio transport selectable via `.env.example` var `VSIR_MCP_TRANSPORT` (default `stdio`).\n\n---\n\nUnit ID: U016\nName: Acceptance and abstention eval harness\nMilestone: M3\nType: eval\nPriority: P1-High\nSize Estimate: Medium\nSpend: none\nDepends On: [U015]\nEnables: []\nSpec References: [Spec §12.3, §12.4]\nInvariants Enforced: []\nFailure Rows Closed: []\nRequired Reading: [`impl/pipeline-guide/12-reproducibility.md` (§6.3/§6.6 — determinism the eval relies on)]\n\nDescription:\n- Turn §12.3's absolute acceptance table and §12.4's adversarial abstention set into runnable CLI eval commands.\n\nCore Requirements:\n- `vsir eval acceptance` (net new): runs the §12.3 L2 acceptance table (absolute, not comparative — C10) against whatever corpus is currently indexed and published (M2a's synthetic doc now; M2b's TC1E-SF once U013 lands — this unit does not itself require U013, per the ledger note that real-corpus acceptance is a later concern).\n- `vsir eval abstention` (net new): runs the §12.4 L3 adversarial abstention eval (the 8 compact-label set from U005 plus the near-miss set from U006) — designed to run in CI on every commit.\n- Both commands print a pass/fail table, exit non-zero on any failure.\n\nWorking Deliverable:\n- `vsir eval acceptance` and `vsir eval abstention` CLI subcommands.\n\nDemo Command:\n- `vsir eval abstention` — runs the adversarial set against the currently published corpus and prints a pass/fail row per case (must all pass on the M2a synthetic doc with zero spend).\n\nDeliverables (files):\n- `backend/vsir/cli.py` (extended — `eval acceptance`, `eval abstention` subcommands)\n- `backend/vsir/core/eval_acceptance.py`, `core/eval_abstention.py` (written, net new)\n- `backend/tests/api/test_eval_abstention.py` (written — wired into CI)\n\nTwelve-Factor Notes:\n- N/A — adds no process, endpoint, tool or worker; a CLI eval harness only.\n\n---\n\nUnit ID: U017\nName: skim/resolve tools and image queries\nMilestone: M4\nType: tool\nPriority: P0-Critical\nSize Estimate: Large\nSpend: none\nDepends On: [U015]\nEnables: [U018]\nSpec References: [Spec §7.2.1, §7.2.3, D12]\nInvariants Enforced: []\nFailure Rows Closed: [F8 (M4 stateless-scope half), F5 (M4 half)]\nRequired Reading: [`impl/app/retrieve.py::search+rrf+decompose` (read first); `impl/app/retrieve.py::resolve` (read first); `IMPROVEMENTS.md` E9 (scroll-4096-and-filter-in-Python — skim's three branches must use proper Qdrant queries, not scroll+Python filtering, especially for the `scope`/`exclude` mechanics)]\n\nDescription:\n- Build the NARROW ladder (`skim_documents`/`skim_sections`/`skim_pages`) as one implementation exposed three times, plus FOLLOW (`resolve`) and image-query support.\n\nCore Requirements:\n- Read `impl/app/retrieve.py::search+rrf+decompose` and `impl/app/retrieve.py::resolve` first.\n- `serve/tools/skim.py` ≈ `retrieve.py::search+rrf+decompose`: one page query aggregated three ways (doc/section/page), using U004's ported `rrf()`/`sparse.py`; `decompose(query)` splits exact identifiers to `lookup` rather than blurring into the embedding; `why` names every contributing branch; `next: {expand, neighbours, references}`; no full text in a triage row (P2); `effective_scope` always echoed back — the service is stateless (F8, this half).\n- `serve/tools/resolve.py` ← `retrieve.py::resolve`: `printed_label` → `page_id` + `interpolated` + `label_verified`; ambiguity returns every candidate (F5, M4 half — flagged, never silent).\n- Image queries (D12): `embed_query_image(image, text=query)` in one `types.Content`; no instruction prefix on multimodal queries; image-only query runs the dense branch alone (`why: [\"dense\"]`), `lexical`/`captions` skipped since there is no query text.\n- An image can never reach the exact surface — `lookup`/`verify` remain text-only (I2/I3, already enforced upstream).\n- CLI one-shots: `vsir skim`, `vsir resolve` (§4.4).\n\nWorking Deliverable:\n- `vsir skim documents|sections|pages <query>` and `vsir resolve <label>` CLI subcommands + HTTP routes.\n\nDemo Command:\n- `vsir skim pages \"emergency stop reset\" --scope '{\"doc_id\":\"TC1E-SF\"}'` — prints ≤10 ranked triage rows with `why`/`rank`/`ImageRef`, deterministic across repeated calls; then `vsir resolve \"SF 1.1A\"` showing `interpolated: false`.\n\nDeliverables (files):\n- `backend/vsir/serve/tools/skim.py` (ported from `impl/app/retrieve.py::search+rrf+decompose`)\n- `backend/vsir/serve/tools/resolve.py` (ported from `impl/app/retrieve.py::resolve`)\n- `backend/vsir/core/embed_query.py` (written, net new — D12 image-query embedding)\n- `backend/tests/api/test_skim.py`, `test_resolve.py` (written)\n\nTwelve-Factor Notes:\n- N/A beyond U014's existing auth/audit — no new process; `effective_scope` echoed per-request, no server-side session state (C11).\n\n---\n\nUnit ID: U018\nName: Page image endpoint, raster cache, and fetch\nMilestone: M4\nType: tool\nPriority: P0-Critical\nSize Estimate: Large\nSpend: none\nDepends On: [U017]\nEnables: [U019]\nSpec References: [Spec §7.2.5, §7.3, §4.2]\nInvariants Enforced: []\nFailure Rows Closed: [F18 (M4 fetch half)]\nRequired Reading: [`impl/app/render.py` (read first — reused from U007's port for on-demand region rendering); `IMPROVEMENTS.md` E3 (rendering never collected — the in-process LRU cache added here must actually evict, closing the defect U007 flagged but didn't fully solve)]\n\nDescription:\n- Serve page rasters directly, with dpi/region budgets and an in-process LRU cache, and build `fetch` — the tool that returns material instead of an answer.\n\nCore Requirements:\n- `GET /pages/{page_id}/image` (net new route): bearer-authenticated, dpi ∈ {36, 72, 150, 220, 300, 400} (`dpi_not_allowed`), `dpi > 220` requires `region` (`dpi_requires_region`); 36/72 are the triage thumbnail tiers behind `thumb_url`.\n- In-process raster LRU cache (bounded by `VSIR_RASTER_CACHE_SIZE`): PyMuPDF renders the region clip on demand, no new storage — cache is a pure performance optimization, evictable, never correctness-bearing (C11, closes E3).\n- `serve/tools/fetch.py` (net new): `fetch(page_ids, include=[\"image\",\"text\",\"summary\"], dpi=150, region=None, inline=True)`; caps: ≤5 pages and ≤12MP total (`fetch_budget_exceeded {limit, requested}` — F18, fetch half); `url` always present, `bytes_b64` only when `inline=true` (default).\n- CLI one-shot: `vsir fetch` (§4.4); `vsir demo narrow` ties skim → fetch together as the milestone's official walkthrough.\n\nWorking Deliverable:\n- `GET /pages/{page_id}/image` route + `vsir fetch` CLI + `vsir demo narrow`.\n\nDemo Command:\n- `vsir demo narrow` — runs `skim_pages` → `fetch` over the synthetic doc, printing triage rows with `ImageRef` only, then the `fetch` result with `bytes_b64` present, then an over-budget `fetch` (6 pages) failing typed `fetch_budget_exceeded` (F18).\n\nDeliverables (files):\n- `backend/vsir/serve/app.py` (extended — `/pages/{page_id}/image` route)\n- `backend/vsir/serve/tools/fetch.py` (written, net new)\n- `backend/vsir/core/raster_cache.py` (written, net new — in-process LRU)\n- `backend/vsir/cli.py` (extended — `fetch`, `demo narrow` subcommands)\n- `backend/tests/api/test_fetch.py`, `test_page_image.py` (written)\n\nTwelve-Factor Notes:\n- Adds `.env.example` var: `VSIR_RASTER_CACHE_SIZE` (LRU entry count, process-local perf cache only — lost on restart with no correctness impact, satisfying C11).\n\n---\n\nUnit ID: U019\nName: read tool core logic (stub replay)\nMilestone: M5\nType: tool\nPriority: P0-Critical\nSize Estimate: Large\nSpend: none\nDepends On: [U018, U013]\nEnables: [U020]\nSpec References: [Spec §7.2.6, §6.3 (read_key), §7.3]\nInvariants Enforced: []\nFailure Rows Closed: [F19, F18 (M5 read half)]\nRequired Reading: [`impl/app/retrieve.py::read` (read first); `pipeline-guide/METADATA-CONTRACT.md` (§5.3, page_provenance shape); `IMPROVEMENTS.md` D3 (captions never written — `read` must not silently drop the captions channel it inherits from the page record) and B5 (cache embeddings — the read_key cache here must key on the actual question text, not a stale/generic key, which is exactly what closes F19)]\n\nDescription:\n- Build `read`'s core logic — transcription correction, `sufficient`, `page_provenance`, the ≤3-page cap, and the question-keyed cache — proved entirely through `VSIR_VLM=stub` replay against U013's frozen TC1E-SF fixtures, at zero spend.\n\nCore Requirements:\n- Read `impl/app/retrieve.py::read` first.\n- `serve/tools/read.py` ≈ `retrieve.py::read`: renders at pinned `dpi_answer=220` (caller cannot change it — part of `read_key`); every VLM-emitted code phrase-checked against that page's text and stamped `present | absent | unverifiable` — same vocabulary as `verify` (§7.2.4); on a page with no text layer, every code is `unverifiable`.\n- `sufficient` is mandatory in the result; retrieval judgment never happens inside `read` (§7.6).\n- §6.3 `read_key` cache: includes `page_ids` + the pinned dpi + the question text — a second question about the same pages is a cache miss (F19).\n- ≤3-page cap: `read_page_cap_exceeded` typed 400 (F18, read half).\n- `vlm/prompts/read.md` (net new prompt).\n- Proven via `VSIR_VLM=stub VSIR_FIXTURE=data/fixtures/TC1E-SF` replay — no real Gemini call in this unit.\n\nWorking Deliverable:\n- `vsir read --pages <ids> --question <q>` CLI + HTTP route, runnable in stub mode.\n\nDemo Command:\n- `VSIR_VLM=stub VSIR_FIXTURE=data/fixtures/TC1E-SF vsir read --pages TC1E-SF@1.3#p001,TC1E-SF@1.3#p002 --question \"is K158 energised?\"` — prints `ReadResult` with per-code stamps and `sufficient`; repeating the identical call shows a cache hit (instant); asking a *different* question about the same pages shows a cache miss (F19); requesting a 4th page → `read_page_cap_exceeded`.\n\nDeliverables (files):\n- `backend/vsir/serve/tools/read.py` (ported from `impl/app/retrieve.py::read`)\n- `backend/vsir/vlm/prompts/read.md` (written, net new)\n- `backend/vsir/core/read_cache.py` (written, net new — `read_key`)\n- `backend/vsir/cli.py` (extended — `read` subcommand)\n- `backend/tests/unit/test_read_core.py` (written)\n\nTwelve-Factor Notes:\n- Adds `.env.example` var: `VSIR_DPI_ANSWER=220` (pinned, documented as non-overridable at the API layer despite being config).\n- `read_key` cache is stored in Qdrant/keyed storage, not a local file (C11); stub replay via `VSIR_FIXTURE` is the same config-only mechanism from U008, not a code branch.\n\n---\n\nUnit ID: U020\nName: Real Gemini read path and searchable_ratio\nMilestone: M5\nType: tool\nPriority: P0-Critical\nSize Estimate: Medium\nSpend: paid\nDepends On: [U019]\nEnables: [U021]\nSpec References: [Spec §7.2.6, §7.2.1 (searchable_ratio), §17 (OQ-2)]\nInvariants Enforced: []\nFailure Rows Closed: []\nRequired Reading: [`IMPROVEMENTS.md` B6 (pin the model — this is the second real Gemini integration point after U013, re-verify the pinned id here)]\n\nDescription:\n- Wire U019's `read` to the real Gemini client for the first time, and finish `searchable_ratio` population on every `skim_documents` row against the real TC1E-SF corpus.\n\nCore Requirements:\n- Wire `vlm/client.py` (real path, from U008) into `serve/tools/read.py`; `VSIR_ALLOW_PAID=1` required or the call refuses.\n- Verify/complete `searchable_ratio` on every `DocHit` row (already scaffolded in U004's hit models) against the real, published TC1E-SF corpus from U013.\n- This is the FIRST real `read` call — confirms the pinned dpi 220, real transcription correction, and real cache behavior end to end.\n\nWorking Deliverable:\n- `vsir read` against the real Gemini backend.\n\nDemo Command:\n- `VSIR_ALLOW_PAID=1 vsir read --pages TC1E-SF@1.3#p001,TC1E-SF@1.3#p002 --question \"the carton discharge won't restart after an E-stop reset\"` — the milestone's official demo, plus `vsir skim documents \"carton discharge\"` showing a non-null `searchable_ratio` on the TC1E-SF row.\n\nDeliverables (files):\n- `backend/vsir/serve/tools/read.py` (extended — real client wiring, no new file)\n- `backend/vsir/serve/tools/skim.py` (extended — `searchable_ratio` finishing touch)\n- `backend/tests/paid/test_read_real.py` (written, gated by `scripts/test-paid.sh`)\n\nTwelve-Factor Notes:\n- Uses `GEMINI_API_KEY` and `VSIR_ALLOW_PAID` (both already declared); no new vars.\n\n---\n\nUnit ID: U021\nName: Runner triage and routing (stub)\nMilestone: M6\nType: runner\nPriority: P0-Critical\nSize Estimate: Medium\nSpend: none\nDepends On: [U018, U019]\nEnables: [U022]\nSpec References: [Spec §8.1, §8.2, §8.1a]\nInvariants Enforced: []\nFailure Rows Closed: []\nRequired Reading: [`impl/pipeline-guide/` runner precedent is none (net new per §4.1 layout note); `IMPROVEMENTS.md` — general reminder that the runner must never fabricate an abstention on a backend failure]\n\nDescription:\n- Build the tri-state triage stage and fetch-vs-read routing decision logic, provable against already-built free tools without spending on `read`.\n\nCore Requirements:\n- `runner/triage.py` (net new): tri-state triage (`relevant`/`maybe`/`irrelevant`) with `exclude` and the five §8.2 safeguards — auto-promote exact hits, use `why` as a signal, etc.\n- `runner/prompt.py` (net new): the system prompt (§8.1).\n- §8.1a fetch-vs-read routing: default `fetch`, escalate to `read` only when triage judges the page insufficiently searchable — routing decision itself makes no VLM call.\n- Demoed against U017/U018's free tools (`skim`, `fetch`) only — no `read` call in this unit.\n\nWorking Deliverable:\n- `vsir ask --explain <question>` (dry-run mode): runs triage/routing and prints the plan without calling `read`.\n\nDemo Command:\n- `vsir ask --explain \"the carton discharge won't restart after an E-stop reset\"` — prints the triage table (relevant/maybe/irrelevant per candidate page) and the fetch-vs-read routing decision per page, with zero spend.\n\nDeliverables (files):\n- `backend/vsir/runner/triage.py`, `runner/prompt.py` (written, net new)\n- `backend/vsir/cli.py` (extended — `ask --explain` flag)\n- `backend/tests/unit/test_triage.py` (written)\n\nTwelve-Factor Notes:\n- N/A — adds no process, endpoint, tool or worker; runner logic invoked synchronously from the CLI.\n\n---\n\nUnit ID: U022\nName: Runner loop, answer gate, and POST /ask\nMilestone: M6\nType: runner\nPriority: P0-Critical\nSize Estimate: Large\nSpend: paid\nDepends On: [U021, U020]\nEnables: [U023, U025]\nSpec References: [Spec §8.3, §8.4, §8.5, §7.4]\nInvariants Enforced: [I8]\nFailure Rows Closed: []\nRequired Reading: [`IMPROVEMENTS.md` — reconfirm no allowlist/keyword-taxonomy pattern leaks into the answer gate or abstention wording]\n\nDescription:\n- Complete the agentic loop with the six correction loops and the server-side answer gate, and expose it as `POST /ask` / `vsir ask` — the first unit where a full question-to-answer cycle runs for real.\n\nCore Requirements:\n- `runner/loop.py` (net new): the full loop (§8.1) driving U021's triage/routing through real `fetch`/`read`/`verify` calls; the six correction loops (§8.3), including Loop 1's automatic transcription correction (already inside `read` per U019) and the other five orchestrated here.\n- `runner/answer.py` (net new): server-side answer gate (I8) — every asserted code verified against the page it is cited on, per `(claim, page)` via `core/verify.py`; three branches (verified answer / read-from-image answer / abstain); constrained abstention wording (§8.5) — forbidden while `pages_no_text_read < scope_stats.pages_no_text`.\n- `VSIR_READS_PER_QUESTION` default 3 enforced.\n- `POST /ask` route + `vsir ask` CLI (§4.4).\n\nWorking Deliverable:\n- `POST /ask` + `vsir ask`.\n\nDemo Command:\n- `VSIR_ALLOW_PAID=1 vsir ask \"the carton discharge won't restart after an E-stop reset\"` — the milestone's official demo: prints the agent's move-by-move trace, then a gated answer with verified/read-from-image/unverifiable badges per cited code (I8).\n\nDeliverables (files):\n- `backend/vsir/runner/loop.py`, `runner/answer.py` (written, net new)\n- `backend/vsir/serve/app.py` (extended — `POST /ask` route)\n- `backend/vsir/cli.py` (extended — `ask` subcommand)\n- `backend/tests/paid/test_ask_real.py` (written, gated by `scripts/test-paid.sh`)\n\nTwelve-Factor Notes:\n- Adds `.env.example` var: `VSIR_READS_PER_QUESTION` (default 3).\n- Loop state lives entirely in the request/response cycle (agent-side per §7.6, \"state lives in the agent, not the service\") — no server-side session store (C11).\n\n---\n\nUnit ID: U023\nName: Operator console — viewer and agent panel\nMilestone: M7\nType: frontend\nPriority: P1-High\nSize Estimate: Large\nSpend: none\nDepends On: [U022]\nEnables: [U024]\nSpec References: [Spec §13 M7, §7.1 (image.url/preview.thumb_url)]\nInvariants Enforced: []\nFailure Rows Closed: []\nRequired Reading: [none in `impl/` — net new per §4.1 layout note (frontend is M7-only, no port)]\n\nDescription:\n- Build the two-zone React/TypeScript/Vite console: the page viewer on the left, the agent-moves/triage/answer panel on the right.\n\nCore Requirements:\n- Vite + React + TypeScript scaffold under `frontend/`.\n- LEFT zone: zoom-ladder breadcrumbs, high-res page viewer, region zoom at escalated dpi — consumes `image.url`/`preview.thumb_url` directly with `inline=false` (never requests `bytes_b64` from the browser).\n- RIGHT zone: collapsible agent moves (skim/read/verify), tri-state triage panel, draft answer with trust badges (verified / read-from-image / unverifiable) and amber verification warnings.\n- Clicking a cited code scrolls the LEFT viewer to its page.\n- Talks to the backend's real HTTP surface (`/ask`, `/pages/{id}/image`, etc.) built in U014–U022.\n\nWorking Deliverable:\n- Running Vite dev server serving the full two-zone console against a live (or replay-mode) backend.\n\nDemo Command:\n- `npm --prefix frontend run dev` then browse `http://localhost:5173` — LEFT shows a fixture page image with zoom breadcrumbs, RIGHT shows a replayed agent trace with a trust-badged draft answer; clicking a citation scrolls the viewer.\n\nDeliverables (files):\n- `frontend/` (written, net new — full Vite/React/TS app)\n- `frontend/src/components/Viewer/*`, `frontend/src/components/AgentPanel/*` (written)\n\nTwelve-Factor Notes:\n- Adds `.env.example` vars: `VSIR_FRONTEND_DEV_PORT=5173`, `VSIR_BACKEND_URL` (frontend config, not a literal).\n- No frontend-local persisted state beyond the current session's in-memory trace — nothing correctness-bearing survives a reload.\n\n---\n\nUnit ID: U024\nName: E2E replay suite\nMilestone: M7\nType: harness\nPriority: P1-High\nSize Estimate: Medium\nSpend: none\nDepends On: [U023]\nEnables: []\nSpec References: [Spec §13 M7, §12.2]\nInvariants Enforced: []\nFailure Rows Closed: []\nRequired Reading: [none — net new]\n\nDescription:\n- Drive the worked trace through Playwright in replay mode, with assertions independent of which fixture corpus is loaded.\n\nCore Requirements:\n- `e2e/` Playwright suite (extends the existing `e2e/` directory noted in the repo layout) driving the full worked trace against the console in replay mode (`VSIR_VLM=stub` backend + fixture-backed `/ask` responses).\n- Assertions must be fixture-independent — pass on `synthetic_3window` as well as TC1E-SF, per the spec's explicit requirement.\n- `scripts/test-e2e.sh` wires up: backend on test port 8001 in replay mode, Qdrant test instance on 6335, frontend built for test port 5174, then runs Playwright against it.\n\nWorking Deliverable:\n- `scripts/test-e2e.sh` running Playwright end to end.\n\nDemo Command:\n- `bash scripts/test-e2e.sh` then browse `http://localhost:5174` — Playwright report shows the worked trace passing; manually browsing the same URL shows the same console state Playwright asserted against.\n\nDeliverables (files):\n- `e2e/*.spec.ts` (written, extends existing `e2e/` directory)\n- `scripts/test-e2e.sh` (extended, ported from U002's earlier stub)\n\nTwelve-Factor Notes:\n- Confirms test ports from U001 (backend 8001, Qdrant 6335, frontend 5174) are actually used, never dev ports.\n\n---\n\nUnit ID: U025\nName: Revision lifecycle and resumable ingest\nMilestone: M8\nType: ingest\nPriority: P0-Critical\nSize Estimate: Large\nSpend: none\nDepends On: [U022, U011]\nEnables: [U026]\nSpec References: [Spec §6.2 (Level-2 refusal), §6.7 (F9 half), §15 Factor IX, §4.4]\nInvariants Enforced: []\nFailure Rows Closed: [F9, F8 (M8 series_id half), F12 (M8 revision half)]\nRequired Reading: [`impl/app/pipeline.py`, `impl/app/segjobs.py` (read first — resumability being added on top of U011's run orchestration); `IMPROVEMENTS.md` E2 (job state on daemon threads — resumability must checkpoint through `vsir_runs`, never an in-memory thread) and E7 (orphan points — a killed-and-resumed run must not leave duplicate or orphaned points)]\n\nDescription:\n- Extend U011's run orchestration with `is_current` multi-revision lifecycle, `series_id` propagation, resumable `--resume` ingest with per-window checkpoints, graceful-shutdown checkpointing, and the typed Level-2 refusal — proved on a generated large PDF, never the excluded 1,440-page manual.\n\nCore Requirements:\n- Read `impl/app/pipeline.py`/`impl/app/segjobs.py` first (resumability extension).\n- `is_current` lifecycle across revisions: ingesting a new revision of the same `(doc_id)` sets prior *other* revision `is_current=False` and KEEPS it (never deletes — F9, F12 revision half); `found_only_in_superseded` status surfaced through `lookup`/`skim` when a code exists only in a non-current revision.\n- `series_id` propagated across revisions (F8, M8 half) so a straddling-section scope stays correct across a revision boundary.\n- Generate `data/source/synthetic_large.pdf` (a GENERATED large multi-window PDF, per §6.2's explicit note — never the excluded 1,440-page manual) for resume testing.\n- `--resume <run_id>` with per-window checkpoints in `vsir_runs`; SIGTERM handler checkpoints so at most one window's work is lost (Factor IX); `--steal` interplay with U011's advisory lease.\n- Typed `ladder_level_2_required`: attempting to ingest a Level-2-marked document (per U007's ladder check) fails with this typed error, never silently degrades.\n- `vsir retire <doc_id> [--revision]` CLI (§4.4).\n\nWorking Deliverable:\n- `vsir ingest --resume <run_id>` + `vsir retire`.\n\nDemo Command:\n- Start `vsir ingest data/source/synthetic_large.pdf --vlm stub`, kill it mid-run (SIGTERM), then `vsir ingest --resume <run_id>` — completes, `vsir runs show <run_id>` shows `published` with no duplicated pages; separately, `vsir ingest data/source/level2_stub.pdf --vlm stub` fails typed `ladder_level_2_required`.\n\nDeliverables (files):\n- `backend/vsir/ingest/run.py` (extended — resume/checkpoint logic, no new file)\n- `backend/vsir/ingest/stitch.py` (extended — `series_id` revision propagation)\n- `data/source/synthetic_large.pdf` (written, generated fixture)\n- `backend/vsir/cli.py` (extended — `ingest --resume`, `retire` subcommands)\n- `backend/tests/api/test_resume.py`, `test_revision_lifecycle.py` (written)\n\nTwelve-Factor Notes:\n- SIGTERM handler checkpoints the in-flight window's state into `vsir_runs` before exiting — no local job-state file, resumability is entirely Qdrant-backed (C11, Factor IX).\n\n---\n\nUnit ID: U026\nName: Corpus evaluation report\nMilestone: M8\nType: eval\nPriority: P1-High\nSize Estimate: Small\nSpend: none\nDepends On: [U025]\nEnables: []\nSpec References: [Spec §12.6]\nInvariants Enforced: []\nFailure Rows Closed: []\nRequired Reading: [none new — reuses U013/U016's eval patterns]\n\nDescription:\n- Produce the §12.6 corpus-wide evaluation report over whatever is currently published, reading only from the already-indexed corpus (no new model spend).\n\nCore Requirements:\n- `vsir eval corpus` (net new): aggregates grounded_rate/coverage/`is_current` stats across the full published corpus, reusing U013's grounded_rate reporting utility and U011's Prometheus gauge sources.\n- Read-only against the existing index — no fresh ingest or VLM call triggered by this command itself.\n\nWorking Deliverable:\n- `vsir eval corpus` CLI subcommand.\n\nDemo Command:\n- `vsir eval corpus` — prints the corpus evaluation report table (per-document grounded_rate, coverage, current-vs-superseded counts) for everything currently published, run immediately after U025's resume demo.\n\nDeliverables (files):\n- `backend/vsir/cli.py` (extended — `eval corpus` subcommand)\n- `backend/vsir/core/eval_corpus.py` (written, net new)\n- `backend/tests/unit/test_eval_corpus.py` (written)\n\nTwelve-Factor Notes:\n- N/A — adds no process, endpoint, tool or worker; read-only reporting CLI.\n\n---\n\n## Coverage Self-Check\n\n- Units per milestone: M0=2, M1=4, M2a=5, M2b=2, M3=3, M4=2, M5=2, M6=2, M7=2, M8=2, TOTAL=26\n- Every I1–I8 owned: I1→U011, I2→U005, I3→U004, I4→U011, I5→U004, I6→U003, I7→U011, I8→U022\n- Every F1–F19 owned (split rows named per part):\n  - F1→U005\n  - F2→U006 (core) + U015 (tool)\n  - F3→U005\n  - F4→U007 (M2a) + U015 (M3)\n  - F5→U009 (M2a) + U017 (M4)\n  - F6→U009\n  - F7→U011\n  - F8→U009 (M2a stitching) + U017 (M4 stateless scope) + U025 (M8 series_id)\n  - F9→U025\n  - F10→U004\n  - F11→U001 (M0 boot) + U008 (M2a key)\n  - F12→U011 (M2a) + U025 (M8 revision half)\n  - F13→U007\n  - F14→U005\n  - F15→U007\n  - F16→U006\n  - F17→U011\n  - F18→U018 (M4 fetch) + U019 (M5 read)\n  - F19→U019\n- Any unit without a runnable Demo Command: none"}],"resolvedModel":"claude-sonnet-5","totalDurationMs":679938,"totalTokens":108907,"totalToolUseCount":4,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":17255,"cache_read_input_tokens":37494,"output_tokens":54156,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":24418},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":17255},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":54156,"cache_read_input_tokens":37494,"cache_creation_input_tokens":17255,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":17255,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"toolStats":{"readCount":0,"searchCount":0,"bashCount":4,"editFileCount":0,"linesAdded":0,"linesRemoved":0,"otherToolCount":0}}}
