{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01N8Z9927YhFTuT64FupSaAZ","type":"tool_result","content":"### Synthesis Agent 2: Unit Decomposition\n\nUnit ID: U001\nName: Repo skeleton, CLI doctor, and twelve-factor runtime shell\nMilestone: M0\nType: harness\nPriority: P0-Critical\nSize Estimate: Large\nSpend: none\nDepends On: []\nEnables: [U002, U003]\nSpec References: [Spec §4.1, §4.2, §4.3, §4.4, §15, §15.1, §15.2]\nInvariants Enforced: []\nFailure Rows Closed: [F11 (boot half — alias/`-latest` model id refused at boot)]\nRequired Reading: [`impl/README.md §3` (§7.2 twelve-factor precedent); `pipeline-guide/IMPROVEMENTS.md` items E5 (no auth — do not reproduce, stub it out now so M3 has a hook), E4 (no cost observability — plan gauge hooks now)]\n\nDescription:\n- Stand up the installable `backend/vsir/` package, the `vsir` CLI entrypoint, and a self-checking, twelve-factor-compliant runtime shell with nothing paid or ingest-specific in it yet.\n\nCore Requirements:\n- §4.1 repo layout skeleton: `backend/vsir/{core,ingest,vlm,serve,mcp,runner}/__init__.py` placeholders only where a later milestone owns the first real module (never populate a module ahead of its owning milestone).\n- `cli.py` ≈ `impl/scripts/interfaces_demo.py` (read first) — port the argument-parsing skeleton only; wire the `vsir` entrypoint and register `doctor` as the first real subcommand.\n- §4.3 boot self-check: Qdrant reachable, pinned model id does not end in `-latest` (refuse to start — F11 boot half), release_id resolvable.\n- §4.2 pin python 3.11, fastapi==0.141.1, uvicorn[standard]==0.52.4, python-multipart==0.0.32, google-genai==2.22.0, qdrant-client==1.19.0, PyMuPDF==1.28.2, pillow==12.3.0 in `requirements.txt` + generate a lock file.\n- REWRITE `docker-compose.test.yml` from any Postgres service to `qdrant/qdrant:v1.19.0` on test ports (backend 8001, Qdrant REST 6335 gRPC — never reuse dev 6334).\n- §15 Dockerfile: non-root user, digest-pinned base image, read-only rootfs, tmpfs mount for the raster cache; `.env.example` with every Factor III var used so far (`VSIR_ENV`, `VSIR_QDRANT_URL`, `VSIR_RELEASE_ID`, `VSIR_LOG_LEVEL`, `VSIR_PORT`).\n- `GET /health` (always green if process is up) and `GET /ready` (red if Qdrant unreachable) per §15.1, minimal FastAPI app.\n- Structured JSON logs to stdout (no `logging.FileHandler` — §12.5 cloud-native grep); SIGTERM handler that exits cleanly (no in-flight work yet, so this is just the hook).\n- §0/§13 D1–D7 restated in README.\n\nWorking Deliverable:\n- `vsir` CLI binary with a working `doctor` subcommand and a minimal FastAPI process exposing `/health` and `/ready`.\n\nDemo Command:\n- `vsir doctor` — prints PASS/FAIL per boot check (Qdrant reachable, model id not `-latest`, release_id set) and exits non-zero on any FAIL.\n\nDeliverables (files):\n- `backend/vsir/cli.py` (written; skeleton only, ≈ `impl/scripts/interfaces_demo.py` for arg-parsing shape)\n- `backend/vsir/core/health.py` (written — boot checks only; `grounded_rate` logic is M2a's)\n- `backend/vsir/serve/app.py` (written — health/ready only; full app is M3's)\n- `Dockerfile`, `docker-compose.test.yml` (rewritten), `.env.example`, `requirements.txt`, `requirements.lock`\n- `README.md` (D1–D7 section)\n\nTwelve-Factor Notes:\n- Adds `.env.example` vars: `VSIR_ENV`, `VSIR_QDRANT_URL`, `VSIR_RELEASE_ID`, `VSIR_LOG_LEVEL`, `VSIR_PORT`.\n- JSON logs to stdout from process start; SIGTERM handler stub; no process-local correctness-bearing state introduced.\n\n---\n\nUnit ID: U002\nName: Test harness, conformance greps, and AGENTS.md\nMilestone: M0\nType: harness\nPriority: P0-Critical\nSize Estimate: Medium\nSpend: none\nDepends On: [U001]\nEnables: [U003]\nSpec References: [Spec §12.5, §4.4]\nInvariants Enforced: []\nFailure Rows Closed: []\nRequired Reading: [`pipeline-guide/IMPROVEMENTS.md` E6 (no tests — the register item this unit exists to not reproduce)]\n\nDescription:\n- Give every later unit a runnable, growing test/CI surface and turn the §12.5 conformance rules into an executable gate instead of a checklist.\n\nCore Requirements:\n- §12.5 conformance greps as a pytest module scoped to `backend/vsir/**` + `requirements*.txt` (never markdown, never the test's own file): no `MatchText`/`MatchTextAny` under `serve/`; no fuzzy/similarity/edit-distance library in requirements; no field named `score` in a response model; no model id ending `-latest`; no `alembic`/`sqlalchemy`; no `get_text(` outside `ingest/probe.py`; no `SCHEMA_CARD`/`IdClass`/`entity_keys`/`classify(`.\n- Cloud-native grep set, same scope + `Dockerfile*` + `docker-compose*.yml`: no `logging.FileHandler`; no image tagged `latest`; no credential literals (`api_key=`, `token=`, `Bearer ` + literal); no `if TESTING` / `if os.environ.get(\"TESTING\")` branches in `backend/vsir/**`; no `RetrievalState`-style module-level mutable session store.\n- `scripts/test-unit.sh`, `scripts/test-api.sh`, `scripts/test-e2e.sh` extended to run against this repo's actual layout (not placeholders); `scripts/test-paid.sh` added, gated on `VSIR_ALLOW_PAID=1`, refuses to run otherwise.\n- `AGENTS.md` filled with the real, working commands (not aspirational ones) for doctor/test-unit/test-api/test-paid.\n\nWorking Deliverable:\n- Runnable conformance-grep pytest module wired into `scripts/test-unit.sh`.\n\nDemo Command:\n- `bash scripts/test-unit.sh` — runs `vsir doctor`'s underlying checks plus the conformance-grep suite and prints PASS; introducing a `score` field or a `logging.FileHandler` anywhere in scope should be shown failing it once (reviewer can `git stash`/inject to see the red).\n\nDeliverables (files):\n- `backend/tests/unit/test_conformance.py` (written, net new)\n- `scripts/test-unit.sh`, `scripts/test-api.sh`, `scripts/test-e2e.sh`, `scripts/test-paid.sh` (written)\n- `AGENTS.md` (written)\n\nTwelve-Factor Notes:\n- N/A — adds no process, endpoint, tool or worker; it is test tooling only.\n\n---\n\nUnit ID: U003\nName: core/record, ids, and the INDEXED bootstrap\nMilestone: M1\nType: core\nPriority: P0-Critical\nSize Estimate: Medium\nSpend: none\nDepends On: [U001, U002]\nEnables: [U004]\nSpec References: [Spec §5.1, §5.3, §5.4, §5.5]\nInvariants Enforced: [I6]\nFailure Rows Closed: []\nRequired Reading: [`impl/app/pagemodel.py` (record shape and `make_page_id` — read first); `pipeline-guide/METADATA-CONTRACT.md` (§5.3); `IMPROVEMENTS.md` A5 (`image_path` — must NOT be reproduced in the record) and B1/B4 (provenance gaps — provenance must be a first-class field here)]\n\nDescription:\n- Port the page record shape and identifier scheme from `impl/app/pagemodel.py`, and stand up the single `INDEXED` dict that creates and will later gate the Qdrant schema.\n\nCore Requirements:\n- Read `impl/app/pagemodel.py` first.\n- `core/record.py` ≈ `pagemodel.py` (record shape only, no new business logic): facets / text+vlm_codes / three vectors dense+lexical+captions / nested `content` never filtered / provenance — explicitly NO `image_path` field (A5).\n- `core/ids.py` ≈ `pagemodel.py::make_page_id`: `page_id`/`section_id`/`series_id`/`point_id=uuid5(page_id)`/`run_id=ULID` per §5.1.\n- `core/indexed.py` (net new): the one `INDEXED` dict that will create, gate (M2a/M8) and be asserted at boot (I6); scope keys = INDEXED minus `text` and `vlm_codes`.\n- §5.5 `TextIndexParams`: WORD tokenizer, lowercase, `phrase_matching=True`, `min_token_len=1`; collection name carries dim (`pages_1536`).\n- Qdrant collection + text-index creation using an ephemeral/in-memory client for self-test.\n\nWorking Deliverable:\n- `vsir index selftest` CLI subcommand: creates an ephemeral Qdrant collection from `INDEXED`, builds one `core/record.py` record via `core/ids.py`, upserts and reads it back.\n\nDemo Command:\n- `vsir index selftest` — prints the created collection's schema (vector configs, text-index params) next to the round-tripped record, proving `INDEXED` and the record shape agree and that no `image_path` field exists anywhere in the payload.\n\nDeliverables (files):\n- `backend/vsir/core/record.py` (ported from `impl/app/pagemodel.py`, record-shape subset only)\n- `backend/vsir/core/ids.py` (ported from `impl/app/pagemodel.py::make_page_id`)\n- `backend/vsir/core/indexed.py` (written, net new)\n- `backend/tests/unit/test_record.py`, `backend/tests/unit/test_indexed.py` (written)\n\nTwelve-Factor Notes:\n- N/A for new env vars. The ephemeral Qdrant client used by `selftest` is in-process and disposable — not correctness-bearing state (no C11 violation).\n\n---\n\nUnit ID: U004\nName: tok/variants/exact_filter, Family A envelope, and rrf/sparse ports\nMilestone: M1\nType: core\nPriority: P0-Critical\nSize Estimate: Large\nSpend: none\nDepends On: [U003]\nEnables: [U005, U006]\nSpec References: [Spec §5.6, §7.1, §7.2.1 (ordering), §7.3]\nInvariants Enforced: [I3, I5]\nFailure Rows Closed: [F10]\nRequired Reading: [`impl/app/sparse.py` (read first — D2, ported verbatim where possible); `impl/app/retrieve.py` (read first — `rrf()` is ranks-only, decompose()); `IMPROVEMENTS.md` E9 (scroll-4096-and-filter-in-Python — the exact_filter and scope-key check must use a real Qdrant filter, never scroll+Python filtering)]\n\nDescription:\n- Build the single exact-match path, the Family A search/absence envelope, and port the deterministic ranks-only fusion machinery that every retrieval tool will reuse from M3 onward.\n\nCore Requirements:\n- Read `impl/app/sparse.py` and `impl/app/retrieve.py` first.\n- `core/tok.py`: mirrors Qdrant's WORD tokenizer exactly — NOT `impl`'s `TOKEN_RE` (named porting hazard, §5.6).\n- `core/variants.py`: exactly 3 spellings of the same characters (whitespace variants only).\n- `core/exact.py::exact_filter`: the ONLY exact-match path in the system; no `MatchText`/`MatchTextAny` anywhere else (I3).\n- §7.1 Family A envelope (`SearchResponse[HitT]`): six-value status enum scaffold (`ok`/four absences/`error` — full absence semantics land in M2a–M4 as data becomes available), `empty_is_never_ok` validator, `WEAK_ABS=20` server constant, `weak`/`needs_scope` formula, hit models `DocHit`/`SectionHit`/`PageHit`/`LookupHit`/`ResolveHit`, `ImageRef`/`Preview` types (references only, no bytes).\n- §7.3 cap validators as typed 400s: `dpi_not_allowed`, `dpi_requires_region`, `filter_unknown_key {keys}` — the last one is what closes F10 using `core/indexed.py`'s scope-key set from U003.\n- Port `sparse.py` (D2) and `rrf()` (ranks-only fusion, `rrf_k=60`, weights page 1.0/lexical 1.0/captions 0.4) verbatim as `core` utilities for reuse by M3's/M4's tools.\n\nWorking Deliverable:\n- `vsir index selftest --query <text>` extension: runs `tok`/`variants`/`exact_filter` against the seeded collection and prints a Family A envelope.\n\nDemo Command:\n- `vsir index selftest --query \"SF 1.1A\"` — prints the 3 whitespace variants generated, the exact_filter Qdrant filter used, and a valid `SearchResponse` JSON; then `vsir index selftest --query \"\" --unknown-scope-key foo` to show `filter_unknown_key` as a typed 400 (F10).\n\nDeliverables (files):\n- `backend/vsir/core/tok.py`, `backend/vsir/core/variants.py`, `backend/vsir/core/exact.py` (written, net new)\n- `backend/vsir/core/envelope.py` (written, net new — Family A only; Family B in U006)\n- `backend/vsir/core/sparse.py` (ported from `impl/app/sparse.py`)\n- `backend/vsir/core/rrf.py` (ported from `impl/app/retrieve.py::rrf`)\n- `backend/tests/unit/test_exact.py`, `backend/tests/unit/test_envelope.py`, `backend/tests/unit/test_rrf.py` (written)\n\nTwelve-Factor Notes:\n- N/A — adds no process, endpoint, tool or worker; pure library code exercised through the existing `selftest` CLI.\n\n---\n\nUnit ID: U005\nName: Synthetic fixtures, observed-token inventory, and `vsir demo exact`\nMilestone: M1\nType: core\nPriority: P0-Critical\nSize Estimate: Medium\nSpend: none\nDepends On: [U004]\nEnables: [U006]\nSpec References: [Spec §6.8 (observed-token inventory subset), §12.4, §7.2.2]\nInvariants Enforced: [I2]\nFailure Rows Closed: [F1, F3, F14]\nRequired Reading: [`impl/app/retrieve.py::lookup` (read first — being rewritten as a phrase filter per §5.6); `IMPROVEMENTS.md` A1 (always-extract-text — not relevant to hand-written fixtures, but the pattern this unit must avoid once probe.py exists in M2a)]\n\nDescription:\n- Seed an ephemeral Qdrant with four hand-written pages (no PDF) and wire `lookup` end to end as the flagship, zero-spend M1 proof.\n\nCore Requirements:\n- Hand-write four synthetic pages' `text` fields directly into `core/record.py` records (bypassing any VLM/probe step, since none exists yet): (1) a page containing the literal string `SF 1.1A`; (2) a page with tokens `sf`, `1`, `1a` scattered non-adjacently; (3) a page printing `SF121.1)`; (4) a page whose `vlm_codes` claims `K999` but whose `text` does not contain it.\n- `serve/tools/lookup.py`'s core logic lives here as `core`-level function (the HTTP/MCP wrapper comes in M3): `lookup(label, scope?, include_unverified=False, cap=20)` — exact, phrase-only, a set not a ranking, using `exact_filter` from U004.\n- Build the observed-token inventory (§6.8 subset only — display data, not the full export pipeline) from the four seeded pages so `present_instead` (U006) works before any PDF exists.\n- `lookup(\"K999\")` on the hallucinated-claim page → `not_found` (I2); `include_unverified=True` returns it separately in `unverified_hits`, `verified: false`, never merged into `hits`.\n- §12.4's 8 compact-label variants exercised against page (2)/(3) to prove I3's variant matching in practice (F3).\n\nWorking Deliverable:\n- `vsir demo exact --synthetic` CLI subcommand — the milestone's official demo.\n\nDemo Command:\n- `vsir demo exact --synthetic` — seeds the four pages into an ephemeral Qdrant, then runs `lookup(\"SF 1.1A\")` (exactly 1 hit — F1), `lookup(\"sf1.1a\")`/7 other compact spellings (all resolve to the same page — F3), and `lookup(\"K999\")` (→ `not_found`, `unverified_hits` only with `include_unverified=True` — F14/I2).\n\nDeliverables (files):\n- `backend/vsir/core/lookup.py` (written — core lookup logic; tool wrapper is M3's `serve/tools/lookup.py`)\n- `backend/vsir/core/observed_tokens.py` (written, net new — §6.8 subset)\n- `data/fixtures/synthetic_pages/*.json` (written — 4 hand-written page records)\n- `backend/tests/unit/test_lookup.py`, `backend/tests/unit/test_observed_tokens.py` (written)\n\nTwelve-Factor Notes:\n- N/A — adds no process, endpoint, tool or worker.\n\n---\n\nUnit ID: U006\nName: core/verify.py, present_instead, and Family B envelope\nMilestone: M1\nType: core\nPriority: P0-Critical\nSize Estimate: Medium\nSpend: none\nDepends On: [U004, U005]\nEnables: [U007]\nSpec References: [Spec §7.1 (Family B), §7.2.4, §12.4]\nInvariants Enforced: []\nFailure Rows Closed: [F2 (core), F16]\nRequired Reading: [`impl/app/retrieve.py` (verify-adjacent logic, read first — no direct `verify` predecessor, this is mostly net new per layout note); `IMPROVEMENTS.md` — confirms `present_instead` must never become a distance/similarity function (guards against reintroducing a fuzzy-match library, which U002's conformance grep also catches)]\n\nDescription:\n- Implement per-`(claim, page)` verification and the deterministic near-miss generator, and define the Family B envelope used by `verify`/`fetch`/`read`.\n\nCore Requirements:\n- `core/verify.py::verify_claims`: per `(claim, page)` — not per claim — so a draft citing `p001–p002` cannot let a code from the neighbouring page through (this is the mechanism I8 will later gate on; the tool wrapper comes at M3).\n- Three states only: `present | absent | unverifiable` — same vocabulary `read` will reuse later (§7.2.6).\n- `present_instead`: a prefix lookup over U005's observed-token inventory, capped at 5, labelled \"different part\" — never a distance (F16).\n- §12.4 near-miss generator: produces the adversarial near-miss set (e.g. `K73` on a page only containing `K78`) used both here and later by M3's `vsir eval abstention`.\n- Family B envelope (`ToolEnvelope[ResultT]`, `VerifyResult`): `status: ok|error` describes whether the call ran, not what it found; a page with every claim `absent` is still `status: ok`.\n\nWorking Deliverable:\n- `vsir demo exact --synthetic --verify <claims>` extension to U005's CLI.\n\nDemo Command:\n- `vsir demo exact --synthetic --verify K73,K158,K999` — prints a `VerifyResult` map showing `K158: present`, `K73: absent` with `present_instead` from the near-miss fixture, and `K999: absent` with `present_instead: []` (F2 core, F16).\n\nDeliverables (files):\n- `backend/vsir/core/verify.py` (written, net new)\n- `backend/vsir/core/nearmiss.py` (written, net new — §12.4 generator)\n- `backend/vsir/core/envelope.py` (extended — Family B added alongside U004's Family A)\n- `backend/tests/unit/test_verify.py`, `backend/tests/unit/test_nearmiss.py` (written)\n\nTwelve-Factor Notes:\n- N/A — adds no process, endpoint, tool or worker.\n\n---\n\nUnit ID: U007\nName: manifest, probe, render, doc-facts, and windowing\nMilestone: M2a\nType: ingest","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4eefb16f-3989-4441-9cd3-d294cfccb11f","uuid":"6c38dcc1-c214-4494-b0e7-2061a48fe73b","timestamp":"2026-09-09T17:02:31.900Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"### Synthesis Agent 2: Unit Decomposition\n\nUnit ID: U001\nName: Repo skeleton, CLI doctor, and twelve-factor runtime shell\nMilestone: M0\nType: harness\nPriority: P0-Critical\nSize Estimate: Large\nSpend: none\nDepends On: []\nEnables: [U002, U003]\nSpec References: [Spec §4.1, §4.2, §4.3, §4.4, §15, §15.1, §15.2]\nInvariants Enforced: []\nFailure Rows Closed: [F11 (boot half — alias/`-latest` model id refused at boot)]\nRequired Reading: [`impl/README.md §3` (§7.2 twelve-factor precedent); `pipeline-guide/IMPROVEMENTS.md` items E5 (no auth — do not reproduce, stub it out now so M3 has a hook), E4 (no cost observability — plan gauge hooks now)]\n\nDescription:\n- Stand up the installable `backend/vsir/` package, the `vsir` CLI entrypoint, and a self-checking, twelve-factor-compliant runtime shell with nothing paid or ingest-specific in it yet.\n\nCore Requirements:\n- §4.1 repo layout skeleton: `backend/vsir/{core,ingest,vlm,serve,mcp,runner}/__init__.py` placeholders only where a later milestone owns the first real module (never populate a module ahead of its owning milestone).\n- `cli.py` ≈ `impl/scripts/interfaces_demo.py` (read first) — port the argument-parsing skeleton only; wire the `vsir` entrypoint and register `doctor` as the first real subcommand.\n- §4.3 boot self-check: Qdrant reachable, pinned model id does not end in `-latest` (refuse to start — F11 boot half), release_id resolvable.\n- §4.2 pin python 3.11, fastapi==0.141.1, uvicorn[standard]==0.52.4, python-multipart==0.0.32, google-genai==2.22.0, qdrant-client==1.19.0, PyMuPDF==1.28.2, pillow==12.3.0 in `requirements.txt` + generate a lock file.\n- REWRITE `docker-compose.test.yml` from any Postgres service to `qdrant/qdrant:v1.19.0` on test ports (backend 8001, Qdrant REST 6335 gRPC — never reuse dev 6334).\n- §15 Dockerfile: non-root user, digest-pinned base image, read-only rootfs, tmpfs mount for the raster cache; `.env.example` with every Factor III var used so far (`VSIR_ENV`, `VSIR_QDRANT_URL`, `VSIR_RELEASE_ID`, `VSIR_LOG_LEVEL`, `VSIR_PORT`).\n- `GET /health` (always green if process is up) and `GET /ready` (red if Qdrant unreachable) per §15.1, minimal FastAPI app.\n- Structured JSON logs to stdout (no `logging.FileHandler` — §12.5 cloud-native grep); SIGTERM handler that exits cleanly (no in-flight work yet, so this is just the hook).\n- §0/§13 D1–D7 restated in README.\n\nWorking Deliverable:\n- `vsir` CLI binary with a working `doctor` subcommand and a minimal FastAPI process exposing `/health` and `/ready`.\n\nDemo Command:\n- `vsir doctor` — prints PASS/FAIL per boot check (Qdrant reachable, model id not `-latest`, release_id set) and exits non-zero on any FAIL.\n\nDeliverables (files):\n- `backend/vsir/cli.py` (written; skeleton only, ≈ `impl/scripts/interfaces_demo.py` for arg-parsing shape)\n- `backend/vsir/core/health.py` (written — boot checks only; `grounded_rate` logic is M2a's)\n- `backend/vsir/serve/app.py` (written — health/ready only; full app is M3's)\n- `Dockerfile`, `docker-compose.test.yml` (rewritten), `.env.example`, `requirements.txt`, `requirements.lock`\n- `README.md` (D1–D7 section)\n\nTwelve-Factor Notes:\n- Adds `.env.example` vars: `VSIR_ENV`, `VSIR_QDRANT_URL`, `VSIR_RELEASE_ID`, `VSIR_LOG_LEVEL`, `VSIR_PORT`.\n- JSON logs to stdout from process start; SIGTERM handler stub; no process-local correctness-bearing state introduced.\n\n---\n\nUnit ID: U002\nName: Test harness, conformance greps, and AGENTS.md\nMilestone: M0\nType: harness\nPriority: P0-Critical\nSize Estimate: Medium\nSpend: none\nDepends On: [U001]\nEnables: [U003]\nSpec References: [Spec §12.5, §4.4]\nInvariants Enforced: []\nFailure Rows Closed: []\nRequired Reading: [`pipeline-guide/IMPROVEMENTS.md` E6 (no tests — the register item this unit exists to not reproduce)]\n\nDescription:\n- Give every later unit a runnable, growing test/CI surface and turn the §12.5 conformance rules into an executable gate instead of a checklist.\n\nCore Requirements:\n- §12.5 conformance greps as a pytest module scoped to `backend/vsir/**` + `requirements*.txt` (never markdown, never the test's own file): no `MatchText`/`MatchTextAny` under `serve/`; no fuzzy/similarity/edit-distance library in requirements; no field named `score` in a response model; no model id ending `-latest`; no `alembic`/`sqlalchemy`; no `get_text(` outside `ingest/probe.py`; no `SCHEMA_CARD`/`IdClass`/`entity_keys`/`classify(`.\n- Cloud-native grep set, same scope + `Dockerfile*` + `docker-compose*.yml`: no `logging.FileHandler`; no image tagged `latest`; no credential literals (`api_key=`, `token=`, `Bearer ` + literal); no `if TESTING` / `if os.environ.get(\"TESTING\")` branches in `backend/vsir/**`; no `RetrievalState`-style module-level mutable session store.\n- `scripts/test-unit.sh`, `scripts/test-api.sh`, `scripts/test-e2e.sh` extended to run against this repo's actual layout (not placeholders); `scripts/test-paid.sh` added, gated on `VSIR_ALLOW_PAID=1`, refuses to run otherwise.\n- `AGENTS.md` filled with the real, working commands (not aspirational ones) for doctor/test-unit/test-api/test-paid.\n\nWorking Deliverable:\n- Runnable conformance-grep pytest module wired into `scripts/test-unit.sh`.\n\nDemo Command:\n- `bash scripts/test-unit.sh` — runs `vsir doctor`'s underlying checks plus the conformance-grep suite and prints PASS; introducing a `score` field or a `logging.FileHandler` anywhere in scope should be shown failing it once (reviewer can `git stash`/inject to see the red).\n\nDeliverables (files):\n- `backend/tests/unit/test_conformance.py` (written, net new)\n- `scripts/test-unit.sh`, `scripts/test-api.sh`, `scripts/test-e2e.sh`, `scripts/test-paid.sh` (written)\n- `AGENTS.md` (written)\n\nTwelve-Factor Notes:\n- N/A — adds no process, endpoint, tool or worker; it is test tooling only.\n\n---\n\nUnit ID: U003\nName: core/record, ids, and the INDEXED bootstrap\nMilestone: M1\nType: core\nPriority: P0-Critical\nSize Estimate: Medium\nSpend: none\nDepends On: [U001, U002]\nEnables: [U004]\nSpec References: [Spec §5.1, §5.3, §5.4, §5.5]\nInvariants Enforced: [I6]\nFailure Rows Closed: []\nRequired Reading: [`impl/app/pagemodel.py` (record shape and `make_page_id` — read first); `pipeline-guide/METADATA-CONTRACT.md` (§5.3); `IMPROVEMENTS.md` A5 (`image_path` — must NOT be reproduced in the record) and B1/B4 (provenance gaps — provenance must be a first-class field here)]\n\nDescription:\n- Port the page record shape and identifier scheme from `impl/app/pagemodel.py`, and stand up the single `INDEXED` dict that creates and will later gate the Qdrant schema.\n\nCore Requirements:\n- Read `impl/app/pagemodel.py` first.\n- `core/record.py` ≈ `pagemodel.py` (record shape only, no new business logic): facets / text+vlm_codes / three vectors dense+lexical+captions / nested `content` never filtered / provenance — explicitly NO `image_path` field (A5).\n- `core/ids.py` ≈ `pagemodel.py::make_page_id`: `page_id`/`section_id`/`series_id`/`point_id=uuid5(page_id)`/`run_id=ULID` per §5.1.\n- `core/indexed.py` (net new): the one `INDEXED` dict that will create, gate (M2a/M8) and be asserted at boot (I6); scope keys = INDEXED minus `text` and `vlm_codes`.\n- §5.5 `TextIndexParams`: WORD tokenizer, lowercase, `phrase_matching=True`, `min_token_len=1`; collection name carries dim (`pages_1536`).\n- Qdrant collection + text-index creation using an ephemeral/in-memory client for self-test.\n\nWorking Deliverable:\n- `vsir index selftest` CLI subcommand: creates an ephemeral Qdrant collection from `INDEXED`, builds one `core/record.py` record via `core/ids.py`, upserts and reads it back.\n\nDemo Command:\n- `vsir index selftest` — prints the created collection's schema (vector configs, text-index params) next to the round-tripped record, proving `INDEXED` and the record shape agree and that no `image_path` field exists anywhere in the payload.\n\nDeliverables (files):\n- `backend/vsir/core/record.py` (ported from `impl/app/pagemodel.py`, record-shape subset only)\n- `backend/vsir/core/ids.py` (ported from `impl/app/pagemodel.py::make_page_id`)\n- `backend/vsir/core/indexed.py` (written, net new)\n- `backend/tests/unit/test_record.py`, `backend/tests/unit/test_indexed.py` (written)\n\nTwelve-Factor Notes:\n- N/A for new env vars. The ephemeral Qdrant client used by `selftest` is in-process and disposable — not correctness-bearing state (no C11 violation).\n\n---\n\nUnit ID: U004\nName: tok/variants/exact_filter, Family A envelope, and rrf/sparse ports\nMilestone: M1\nType: core\nPriority: P0-Critical\nSize Estimate: Large\nSpend: none\nDepends On: [U003]\nEnables: [U005, U006]\nSpec Ref