{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GtV8PXctXS2az4GevLALkv","type":"tool_result","content":"Unit ID: U007\nName: manifest, probe, render, doc-facts, and windowing\nMilestone: M2a\nType: ingest\nPriority: P0-Critical\nSize Estimate: Large\nSpend: none\nDepends On: [U001, U006]\nEnables: [U008]\nSpec References: [Spec §6.1 (steps 01–05), §6.2, §6.4]\nInvariants Enforced: []\nFailure Rows Closed: [F4 (M2a half), F13, F15]\nRequired Reading: [`impl/app/textlayer.py` (read first — `probe`/`page_texts`/`content_hash`); `impl/app/render.py` (read first); `impl/app/windows.py` (read first); `impl/pipeline-guide/01-entry.md`, `02-probe-and-render.md`, `03-document-facts.md`, `04-windowing-and-keys.md`; `IMPROVEMENTS.md` A1 (always-extract-text — probe.py must gate on actual text presence, not extract unconditionally) and E3 (rendering never collected — render outputs must be eligible for cache eviction, not accumulate unbounded)]\n\nDescription:\n- Port the entry manifest, text-layer probing, page rendering, document facts, and the bisecting windowing ladder, and generate the checked-in 3-window synthetic PDF fixture with its off-by-one and crop traps.\n\nCore Requirements:\n- Read `impl/app/textlayer.py`, `impl/app/render.py`, `impl/app/windows.py` first.\n- `ingest/manifest.py` ≈ `impl/app/pipeline.py` (entry/manifest only — step 01).\n- `ingest/probe.py` ← `textlayer.py::probe/page_texts/content_hash` (steps 02–04: `has_text` facet, full-page text extraction, `content_hash`, doc facts/`doc_type`).\n- `ingest/render.py` ← `render.py`, rendering at `dpi_index=150` (§4.2).\n- `ingest/window.py` ← `windows.py` (+ bisection ladder, F13): target 30 pages/window; bisect-and-re-bill on `MAX_TOKENS`/truncation/offset-failure; typed `window_unsplittable`; v1 is Level 0/1 + bisection only — a Level-2 document fails typed `ladder_level_2_required` (this unit defines the check; M8 exercises it against a real Level-2-marked fixture).\n- §6.4 the two independent offset checks (mechanism only here; the gate that gates on them is M2a's `gates.py`, U011).\n- Generate `data/source/synthetic_3window.pdf`: known printed labels, a deliberate off-by-one trap (printed page numbers vs. physical index diverge), and a crop trap (a code visually cropped at render time but present in the underlying full-page text) — proves `text` always comes from the full page (F15), independent of any render crop.\n\nWorking Deliverable:\n- `vsir ingest <pdf> --vlm stub --until window` (the `--until` debug flag is added here and reused by U008–U010).\n\nDemo Command:\n- `vsir ingest data/source/synthetic_3window.pdf --vlm stub --until window` — prints per-page `has_text`/`content_hash`/doc facts and the resulting window plan (3 windows), and confirms the crop-trap page's indexed `text` contains the full label despite the render crop.\n\nDeliverables (files):\n- `backend/vsir/ingest/manifest.py` (ported from `impl/app/pipeline.py`, entry subset)\n- `backend/vsir/ingest/probe.py` (ported from `impl/app/textlayer.py`)\n- `backend/vsir/ingest/render.py` (ported from `impl/app/render.py`)\n- `backend/vsir/ingest/window.py` (ported from `impl/app/windows.py`, + bisection ladder written net new)\n- `data/source/synthetic_3window.pdf` (written, generated fixture, checked in)\n- `backend/tests/unit/test_probe.py`, `test_render.py`, `test_window.py` (written)\n\nTwelve-Factor Notes:\n- Adds `.env.example` vars: `VSIR_RASTER_CACHE_DIR` (tmpfs path from U001's Dockerfile, not correctness-bearing — rasters are always re-derivable from the PDF, C11-safe).\n- No process-local correctness state: window plans and facts are recomputed from the PDF + content_hash, never cached to disk outside the ephemeral raster cache.\n\n---\n\nUnit ID: U008\nName: VLM stub/client/cache and S2 extraction\nMilestone: M2a\nType: ingest\nPriority: P0-Critical\nSize Estimate: Large\nSpend: none\nDepends On: [U007]\nEnables: [U009]\nSpec References: [Spec §5.2, §6.1 (step 06), §6.3]\nInvariants Enforced: []\nFailure Rows Closed: [F11 (M2a key half)]\nRequired Reading: [`impl/app/segment.py` (read first — Gemini call shape and the old S1 schema being replaced); `impl/pipeline-guide/05-extraction.md`, `../SEGMENTATION.md`; `IMPROVEMENTS.md` B6 (pin the model — `vlm/client.py` must hard-fail on an alias id, reusing U001's boot check pattern) and D3 (captions never written — this unit must actually populate the captions field this VLM call produces, since M1's `rrf` already expects a captions branch)]\n\nDescription:\n- Build the VLM abstraction (stub and real client scaffolding, cache, prompts) and the S2 window extraction step, with `VSIR_VLM=stub` selected purely by config.\n\nCore Requirements:\n- Read `impl/app/segment.py` first.\n- `vlm/client.py` (net new): thin Gemini wrapper; pinned model id only (never `-latest`, reuses U001's boot check).\n- `vlm/stub.py` (net new): deterministic, fixture-driven fake VLM responses selected by `VSIR_VLM=stub` — config, never a code branch or `if TESTING` (rule 5).\n- `vlm/cache.py` (net new): §6.3 cache keys — `facts_key`, `extract_key` (model id + prompt version; `VSIR_VLM_TIER` is explicitly NOT part of `extract_key`).\n- `vlm/prompts/s1.md`, `s2.md` (net new prompt text, versioned).\n- `ingest/extract.py` ≈ `impl/app/segment.py` (new S2 schema per §5.2: `PageOut`/`SectionRef`/`Summary`/`WindowOut`; **Prohibited**: any identifier grammar, classification enum, regex taxonomy, or per-corpus keyword list).\n- Replay mode: `VSIR_VLM=stub` + `VSIR_FIXTURE=<dir>` with a typed `fixture_miss` when the fixture directory lacks the requested key.\n\nWorking Deliverable:\n- `vsir ingest <pdf> --vlm stub --until extract`.\n\nDemo Command:\n- `vsir ingest data/source/synthetic_3window.pdf --vlm stub --until extract` — prints the raw S2 `WindowOut` JSON per window from the stub VLM, and re-running with a changed prompt version shows a different `extract_key` (F11 key half).\n\nDeliverables (files):\n- `backend/vsir/vlm/client.py`, `vlm/stub.py`, `vlm/cache.py` (written, net new)\n- `backend/vsir/vlm/prompts/s1.md`, `vlm/prompts/s2.md` (written, net new)\n- `backend/vsir/ingest/extract.py` (ported from `impl/app/segment.py`, schema rewritten to S2)\n- `backend/tests/unit/test_extract.py`, `test_vlm_cache.py` (written)\n\nTwelve-Factor Notes:\n- Adds `.env.example` vars: `VSIR_VLM` (`stub|real`), `VSIR_VLM_MODEL`, `VSIR_VLM_TIER`, `VSIR_FIXTURE`, `GEMINI_API_KEY` (unused until real path, but declared here since the client scaffold reads it).\n- Stub-vs-real is purely `VSIR_VLM` config, no code branch; no VLM output cached to local disk outside the declared `VSIR_FIXTURE` path (which is itself read-only, checked-in fixture data, not runtime state).\n\n---\n\nUnit ID: U009\nName: Derivation, gating removal, and stitching\nMilestone: M2a\nType: ingest\nPriority: P0-Critical\nSize Estimate: Large\nSpend: none\nDepends On: [U008]\nEnables: [U010]\nSpec References: [Spec §6.1 (steps 07–08), §6.5, §5.7]\nInvariants Enforced: []\nFailure Rows Closed: [F5 (M2a half), F6, F8 (M2a stitching half)]\nRequired Reading: [`impl/app/segment.py` (read first — derivation logic being carried without the allowlist gate); `impl/app/stitch.py` (read first); `impl/pipeline-guide/06-derivation-and-gate.md` (⚠ documents the DELETED allowlist gate — do not port it), `07-stitch-and-numbering.md`; `IMPROVEMENTS.md` — confirms the allowlist/`classify()` pattern must not reappear (also enforced mechanically by U002's conformance grep)]\n\nDescription:\n- Port per-page derivation (grounded_rate, no allowlist gate) and section stitching with cross-window carry-in and code reattribution.\n\nCore Requirements:\n- Read `impl/app/segment.py` and `impl/app/stitch.py` first.\n- `ingest/derive.py` ≈ `segment.py` (derivation logic only, the allowlist/`classify()` gate is deleted — grounded_rate replaces it per §5.7: `None` where `has_text` is false).\n- Label precedence + ambiguity → list; code reattribution with `moved_from` when a code derived on one page actually belongs on its neighbour (F6, per-page `grounded_rate`).\n- `ingest/stitch.py` ← `stitch.py` (sections, + `series_id`): canonical section key + carry-in across window boundaries so a straddling section is not mistaken for a fully-searched chapter (F8, stitching half).\n\nWorking Deliverable:\n- `vsir ingest <pdf> --vlm stub --until stitch`.\n\nDemo Command:\n- `vsir ingest data/source/synthetic_3window.pdf --vlm stub --until stitch` — prints stitched `PageOut` records with `section_id`, per-page `grounded_rate`, and (on a fixture with a deliberately misattributed code) the `moved_from` field populated.\n\nDeliverables (files):\n- `backend/vsir/ingest/derive.py` (ported from `impl/app/segment.py`, gate removed)\n- `backend/vsir/ingest/stitch.py` (ported from `impl/app/stitch.py`, + `series_id` written net new)\n- `backend/tests/unit/test_derive.py`, `test_stitch.py` (written)\n\nTwelve-Factor Notes:\n- N/A — adds no process, endpoint, tool or worker.\n\n---\n\nUnit ID: U010\nName: Embedding and indexing\nMilestone: M2a\nType: ingest\nPriority: P0-Critical\nSize Estimate: Large\nSpend: none\nDepends On: [U009]\nEnables: [U011]\nSpec References: [Spec §6.1 (steps 09–10), §6.6, §4.2 (D4, D12)]\nInvariants Enforced: []\nFailure Rows Closed: []\nRequired Reading: [`impl/app/embedder.py` (read first — D4 interleaved embedding); `impl/app/sparse.py` (read first, D2 — reused from U004's port); `impl/app/segstore.py` (read first); `pipeline-guide/08-embedding.md`, `09-indexing.md` (⚠ `entity_keys` index deleted — do not port it); `IMPROVEMENTS.md` B5 (cache embeddings — do not silently reuse stale embeddings across a fingerprint change) and D3 (captions never written — the captions vector must actually be populated and indexed here, completing what U008 started) and E7 (orphan points — index.py must never leave points without a valid run/publish linkage)]\n\nDescription:\n- Port dense/lexical/captions embedding and Qdrant upsert with the `is_current` flag and embedding-fingerprint protection.\n\nCore Requirements:\n- Read `impl/app/embedder.py`, `impl/app/sparse.py`, `impl/app/segstore.py` first.\n- `ingest/embed.py` ← `embedder.py` (D4 interleaved dense embedding: page image + text + captions in one call shape); reuses U004's ported `sparse.py` for the lexical branch.\n- `ingest/index.py` ≈ `segstore.py` (+ text indexes, `is_current`): Qdrant upsert using `point_id=uuid5(page_id)` from U003, `INDEXED` schema from U003, `is_current=False` at this stage (publish flips it — U011).\n- §6.6 embedding fingerprint `{embed_model, dim, distance, composition_version}`: refuse to upsert on mismatch; on mismatch, new collection + re-embed + alias swap (no in-place mutation).\n- dim ∈ {768, 1536, 3072}, concurrency=8, batch_size=8, max_edge_px=1568 per §4.2.\n\nWorking Deliverable:\n- `vsir ingest <pdf> --vlm stub --until index`.\n\nDemo Command:\n- `vsir ingest data/source/synthetic_3window.pdf --vlm stub --until index` — ingests into the ephemeral Qdrant with `is_current=False`; a follow-up raw scroll/count shows N points with correct `point_id`s and the fingerprint stamped in the collection's payload schema; re-running with a mutated `embed_model` shows the refusal.\n\nDeliverables (files):\n- `backend/vsir/ingest/embed.py` (ported from `impl/app/embedder.py`)\n- `backend/vsir/ingest/index.py` (ported from `impl/app/segstore.py`, + text indexes/`is_current` written net new)\n- `backend/tests/unit/test_embed.py`, `test_index.py` (written)\n\nTwelve-Factor Notes:\n- Adds `.env.example` vars: `VSIR_EMBED_MODEL`, `VSIR_EMBED_DIM`, `VSIR_EMBED_CONCURRENCY`, `VSIR_EMBED_BATCH_SIZE`.\n- No local embedding cache on disk; the fingerprint check is enforced against the Qdrant collection itself, never a local file (C11).\n\n---\n\nUnit ID: U011\nName: Gates, export, and run orchestration\nMilestone: M2a\nType: ingest\nPriority: P0-Critical\nSize Estimate: Large\nSpend: none\nDepends On: [U010]\nEnables: [U012, U014]\nSpec References: [Spec §6.1 (steps 11–12), §6.4, §6.7, §6.8, §6.9, §11.1, §4.4]\nInvariants Enforced: [I1, I4, I7]\nFailure Rows Closed: [F7, F12 (M2a half), F17]\nRequired Reading: [`impl/app/pipeline.py`, `impl/app/segjobs.py` (read first — run orchestration being restructured); `pipeline-guide/10-gates-and-publish.md` (⚠ allowlist/`class_totality` replaced by `grounded_rate`), `11-export.md` (⚠ `withheld.jsonl` dropped from this step — it lives only as a frozen M2b parity artefact); `12-reproducibility.md` (§6.3/§6.6); `IMPROVEMENTS.md` E2 (job state on daemon threads — run state must live in the `vsir_runs` Qdrant collection, never a Python thread/global) and E7 (orphan points — the three-clause retirement rule this unit implements exists specifically to prevent this)]\n\nDescription:\n- Close the pipeline: publish gating, the `vsir_runs` control collection, the three-clause retirement rule, exports, and the run record — the unit that makes `vsir ingest` a complete, gated, resumable-by-contract pipeline.\n\nCore Requirements:\n- Read `impl/app/pipeline.py` and `impl/app/segjobs.py` first.\n- `ingest/gates.py` ≈ `pipeline.py` (grounded_rate replaces the allowlist, §11.1): `window_coverage` (block, must be 1.0), `offset_check` (block, both §6.4 checks pass — I4), `grounded_rate ≥ 0.8` provisional (block, `vsir publish --override grounded_rate --reason \"…\"` records `published_with_override`), `text_coverage` (flag `mostly_scanned`, never block; **at 0.0 the grounded_rate gate is skipped entirely**), `label_monotonic` (flag `label_conflict`).\n- `ingest/export.py` (net new): `labels.jsonl` + `observed_tokens.jsonl` streamed over HTTP (§6.8); `safety_flag` derived from manifest `doc_type` + model topics — never a keyword list.\n- `ingest/run.py` ≈ `pipeline.py`/`segjobs.py`: `vsir_runs` control collection (run + window points, state enum `{queued,running,stopped,gated,published,failed}`), advisory lease + `--steal`, §6.7 three-clause retirement (delete same doc+revision earlier `run_id` → F12; set prior *other* revision `is_current=False` and KEEP → F9, owned by M8 since it needs a second revision; never touch other documents).\n- I1: `point_id` uniqueness + `count(doc,rev) == pdf.page_count` asserted after publish. I7: `is_current=False` until gates pass; every tool injects `is_current=True` by default (mechanism proven here, tool-level default enforced from M3 onward).\n- `vsir runs show <run_id>`, `vsir gates rerun <run_id>`, `vsir publish --override <gate> --reason` (§4.4).\n- F17 proof: kill an ingest mid-run (SIGKILL the process) → 0 pages queryable (because `is_current` never flipped).\n\nWorking Deliverable:\n- `vsir ingest <pdf> --vlm stub` (full pipeline, no `--until`) + `vsir runs show` + `vsir gates rerun` + `vsir publish --override`.\n\nDemo Command:\n- `vsir ingest data/source/synthetic_3window.pdf --vlm stub && vsir runs show <run_id>` — the milestone demo: run reaches `published`, gate results shown, F7's off-by-one trap fixture proven caught by `offset_check`, and a second identical ingest shown retiring the first run's points without touching anything else (F12).\n\nDeliverables (files):\n- `backend/vsir/ingest/gates.py` (ported from `impl/app/pipeline.py`, gate logic replaced per §11.1)\n- `backend/vsir/ingest/export.py` (written, net new)\n- `backend/vsir/ingest/run.py` (ported from `impl/app/pipeline.py` / `impl/app/segjobs.py`)\n- `backend/vsir/core/status.py` (written, net new — run state enum)\n- `backend/tests/unit/test_gates.py`, `test_export.py`, `test_run.py` (written)\n- `backend/tests/api/test_publish_gating.py` (written — F17 kill-mid-run proof)\n\nTwelve-Factor Notes:\n- Adds `.env.example` vars: `VSIR_GROUNDED_RATE_THRESHOLD` (provisional, 0.8 — reset by M2b's R4), `VSIR_LEASE_TTL_SECONDS`.\n- Run/window state lives entirely in the `vsir_runs` Qdrant collection — no daemon threads, no local job-state files (E2); SIGTERM during ingest leaves the run in `stopped` state, resumable,