{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CWr4YRR1o4skdds8LBU1KA","type":"tool_result","content":"Unit ID: U014\nName: serve/app, auth, audit, and budget scaffolding\nMilestone: M3\nType: tool\nPriority: P0-Critical\nSize Estimate: Medium\nSpend: none\nDepends On: [U011, U002]\nEnables: [U015]\nSpec References: [Spec §7.4, §11.3, §15.1]\nInvariants Enforced: []\nFailure Rows Closed: []\nRequired Reading: [`impl/app/main.py` (read first — HTTP app shape being restructured); `IMPROVEMENTS.md` E5 (no auth — the defect this unit directly closes) and E4 (no cost observability — audit line must carry cost, never expose it in the response body)]\n\nDescription:\n- Build the real FastAPI serving app with bearer auth, the ten-field audit log, and request budget scaffolding, replacing U001's minimal health-only stub.\n\nCore Requirements:\n- Read `impl/app/main.py` first.\n- `serve/app.py` ≈ `main.py`: full app boot, reusing U001's `/health`/`/ready` and its boot self-check (INDEXED schema assertion — refuse to serve at boot if schema mismatches, per §11.3).\n- `serve/auth.py` (net new): bearer token auth on every route except `/health`.\n- `serve/audit.py` (net new): the ten-field audit line per request (§7.4) — cost recorded in the audit log, never in the response body.\n- `serve/budget.py` (net new): per-caller request budget scaffolding; `reads_remaining` computed and available for every envelope (actual `read` quota consumption is wired in M5).\n- §11.3 degradation rows relevant here: Qdrant unreachable → `503 qdrant_unavailable` (never an empty result); embedding-model/collection fingerprint mismatch → refuse to upsert (already built in U010, wired to a 503 here at the serving layer too).\n\nWorking Deliverable:\n- `vsir serve` CLI subcommand starting the full authenticated app.\n\nDemo Command:\n- `vsir serve &` then `curl localhost:8000/health` (200, no auth needed) vs. `curl localhost:8000/pages/x/image` (401 without a bearer token) — and the resulting audit log line printed to stdout showing the ten fields including cost=0.\n\nDeliverables (files):\n- `backend/vsir/serve/app.py` (ported from `impl/app/main.py`)\n- `backend/vsir/serve/auth.py`, `serve/audit.py`, `serve/budget.py` (written, net new)\n- `backend/tests/api/test_auth.py`, `test_audit.py` (written)\n\nTwelve-Factor Notes:\n- Adds `.env.example` vars: `VSIR_API_TOKEN` (bearer secret, never a literal in code), `VSIR_READ_QUOTA_PER_CALLER`.\n- Structured JSON audit lines to stdout (no file handler); stateless — auth/budget state derived per-request from the token, no session store.\n\n---\n\nUnit ID: U015\nName: lookup/verify HTTP+MCP tools\nMilestone: M3\nType: tool\nPriority: P0-Critical\nSize Estimate: Large\nSpend: none\nDepends On: [U014, U004, U006]\nEnables: [U016, U017]\nSpec References: [Spec §7.2.2, §7.2.4, §7.5, §7.6]\nInvariants Enforced: []\nFailure Rows Closed: [F2 (tool half), F4 (M3 half)]\nRequired Reading: [`impl/app/retrieve.py::lookup` (read first — being rewritten as a phrase filter per §5.6); `impl/app/api_models.py` (read first — envelope wiring precedent); `IMPROVEMENTS.md` E9 (scroll-4096-and-filter-in-Python — the HTTP layer must call U004's `exact_filter`, never re-implement filtering client-side)]\n\nDescription:\n- Wrap M1's core `lookup`/`verify` logic as the first two real tools, exposed identically over HTTP and MCP, closing the tool-layer halves of F2 and F4.\n\nCore Requirements:\n- Read `impl/app/retrieve.py::lookup` and `impl/app/api_models.py` first.\n- `serve/envelope.py` ≈ `api_models.py`: wires U004's Family A / U006's Family B pydantic models into actual HTTP response models, with the full six-value status enum surfaced (`not_found`, `not_searchable`, `out_of_scope`, `found_only_in_superseded`, `error`, `ok`) — `not_searchable` now reachable end-to-end against a real scanned candidate from M2a data (F4, M3 half).\n- `serve/tools/lookup.py` ≈ `retrieve.py::lookup` (rewritten as phrase filter): thin HTTP wrapper over `core/lookup.py`.\n- `serve/tools/verify.py` (net new): thin HTTP wrapper over `core/verify.py::verify_claims` — this is the tool-layer half of F2 (`verify` confirming a code not on the page must 400/absent, never silently pass).\n- `mcp/server.py` (net new): stdio + SSE transport, exposing `lookup` and `verify` through the exact SAME implementations as the HTTP routes (stateless, §7.5) — no second copy of the logic.\n- §7.6 refusals enforced at this boundary: no `score` field, no routing, no composing outside the runner, no fuzzy matching (all also caught mechanically by U002's conformance grep).\n- CLI one-shots: `vsir lookup`, `vsir verify` (§4.4).\n\nWorking Deliverable:\n- `vsir serve` with working `/lookup` and `/verify` routes, plus `vsir mcp --stdio`/`--sse` exposing the same two tools.\n\nDemo Command:\n- `vsir serve &` then `vsir lookup \"SF 1.1A\" && vsir verify --claims K73 --pages TC1E-SF@1.3#p008` — plus the same two calls issued over `vsir mcp --stdio` piped JSON-RPC, showing byte-identical envelope bodies (proving \"same implementations\").\n\nDeliverables (files):\n- `backend/vsir/serve/envelope.py` (ported from `impl/app/api_models.py`)\n- `backend/vsir/serve/tools/lookup.py` (ported from `impl/app/retrieve.py::lookup`)\n- `backend/vsir/serve/tools/verify.py` (written, net new)\n- `backend/vsir/mcp/server.py` (written, net new)\n- `backend/vsir/cli.py` (extended — `lookup`, `verify`, `serve`, `mcp` subcommands)\n- `backend/tests/api/test_lookup_route.py`, `test_verify_route.py`, `backend/tests/unit/test_mcp_server.py` (written)\n\nTwelve-Factor Notes:\n- MCP server is stateless like the HTTP app — no per-session state; SSE/stdio transport selectable via `.env.example` var `VSIR_MCP_TRANSPORT` (default `stdio`).\n\n---\n\nUnit ID: U016\nName: Acceptance and abstention eval harness\nMilestone: M3\nType: eval\nPriority: P1-High\nSize Estimate: Medium\nSpend: none\nDepends On: [U015]\nEnables: []\nSpec References: [Spec §12.3, §12.4]\nInvariants Enforced: []\nFailure Rows Closed: []\nRequired Reading: [`impl/pipeline-guide/12-reproducibility.md` (§6.3/§6.6 — determinism the eval relies on)]\n\nDescription:\n- Turn §12.3's absolute acceptance table and §12.4's adversarial abstention set into runnable CLI eval commands.\n\nCore Requirements:\n- `vsir eval acceptance` (net new): runs the §12.3 L2 acceptance table (absolute, not comparative — C10) against whatever corpus is currently indexed and published (M2a's synthetic doc now; M2b's TC1E-SF once U013 lands — this unit does not itself require U013, per the ledger note that real-corpus acceptance is a later concern).\n- `vsir eval abstention` (net new): runs the §12.4 L3 adversarial abstention eval (the 8 compact-label set from U005 plus the near-miss set from U006) — designed to run in CI on every commit.\n- Both commands print a pass/fail table, exit non-zero on any failure.\n\nWorking Deliverable:\n- `vsir eval acceptance` and `vsir eval abstention` CLI subcommands.\n\nDemo Command:\n- `vsir eval abstention` — runs the adversarial set against the currently published corpus and prints a pass/fail row per case (must all pass on the M2a synthetic doc with zero spend).\n\nDeliverables (files):\n- `backend/vsir/cli.py` (extended — `eval acceptance`, `eval abstention` subcommands)\n- `backend/vsir/core/eval_acceptance.py`, `core/eval_abstention.py` (written, net new)\n- `backend/tests/api/test_eval_abstention.py` (written — wired into CI)\n\nTwelve-Factor Notes:\n- N/A — adds no process, endpoint, tool or worker; a CLI eval harness only.\n\n---\n\nUnit ID: U017\nName: skim/resolve tools and image queries\nMilestone: M4\nType: tool\nPriority: P0-Critical\nSize Estimate: Large\nSpend: none\nDepends On: [U015]\nEnables: [U018]\nSpec References: [Spec §7.2.1, §7.2.3, D12]\nInvariants Enforced: []\nFailure Rows Closed: [F8 (M4 stateless-scope half), F5 (M4 half)]\nRequired Reading: [`impl/app/retrieve.py::search+rrf+decompose` (read first); `impl/app/retrieve.py::resolve` (read first); `IMPROVEMENTS.md` E9 (scroll-4096-and-filter-in-Python — skim's three branches must use proper Qdrant queries, not scroll+Python filtering, especially for the `scope`/`exclude` mechanics)]\n\nDescription:\n- Build the NARROW ladder (`skim_documents`/`skim_sections`/`skim_pages`) as one implementation exposed three times, plus FOLLOW (`resolve`) and image-query support.\n\nCore Requirements:\n- Read `impl/app/retrieve.py::search+rrf+decompose` and `impl/app/retrieve.py::resolve` first.\n- `serve/tools/skim.py` ≈ `retrieve.py::search+rrf+decompose`: one page query aggregated three ways (doc/section/page), using U004's ported `rrf()`/`sparse.py`; `decompose(query)` splits exact identifiers to `lookup` rather than blurring into the embedding; `why` names every contributing branch; `next: {expand, neighbours, references}`; no full text in a triage row (P2); `effective_scope` always echoed back — the service is stateless (F8, this half).\n- `serve/tools/resolve.py` ← `retrieve.py::resolve`: `printed_label` → `page_id` + `interpolated` + `label_verified`; ambiguity returns every candidate (F5, M4 half — flagged, never silent).\n- Image queries (D12): `embed_query_image(image, text=query)` in one `types.Content`; no instruction prefix on multimodal queries; image-only query runs the dense branch alone (`why: [\"dense\"]`), `lexical`/`captions` skipped since there is no query text.\n- An image can never reach the exact surface — `lookup`/`verify` remain text-only (I2/I3, already enforced upstream).\n- CLI one-shots: `vsir skim`, `vsir resolve` (§4.4).\n\nWorking Deliverable:\n- `vsir skim documents|sections|pages <query>` and `vsir resolve <label>` CLI subcommands + HTTP routes.\n\nDemo Command:\n- `vsir skim pages \"emergency stop reset\" --scope '{\"doc_id\":\"TC1E-SF\"}'` — prints ≤10 ranked triage rows with `why`/`rank`/`ImageRef`, deterministic across repeated calls; then `vsir resolve \"SF 1.1A\"` showing `interpolated: false`.\n\nDeliverables (files):\n- `backend/vsir/serve/tools/skim.py` (ported from `impl/app/retrieve.py::search+rrf+decompose`)\n- `backend/vsir/serve/tools/resolve.py` (ported from `impl/app/retrieve.py::resolve`)\n- `backend/vsir/core/embed_query.py` (written, net new — D12 image-query embedding)\n- `backend/tests/api/test_skim.py`, `test_resolve.py` (written)\n\nTwelve-Factor Notes:\n- N/A beyond U014's existing auth/audit — no new process; `effective_scope` echoed per-request, no server-side session state (C11).\n\n---\n\nUnit ID: U018\nName: Page image endpoint, raster cache, and fetch\nMilestone: M4\nType: tool\nPriority: P0-Critical\nSize Estimate: Large\nSpend: none\nDepends On: [U017]\nEnables: [U019]\nSpec References: [Spec §7.2.5, §7.3, §4.2]\nInvariants Enforced: []\nFailure Rows Closed: [F18 (M4 fetch half)]\nRequired Reading: [`impl/app/render.py` (read first — reused from U007's port for on-demand region rendering); `IMPROVEMENTS.md` E3 (rendering never collected — the in-process LRU cache added here must actually evict, closing the defect U007 flagged but didn't fully solve)]\n\nDescription:\n- Serve page rasters directly, with dpi/region budgets and an in-process LRU cache, and build `fetch` — the tool that returns material instead of an answer.\n\nCore Requirements:\n- `GET /pages/{page_id}/image` (net new route): bearer-authenticated, dpi ∈ {36, 72, 150, 220, 300, 400} (`dpi_not_allowed`), `dpi > 220` requires `region` (`dpi_requires_region`); 36/72 are the triage thumbnail tiers behind `thumb_url`.\n- In-process raster LRU cache (bounded by `VSIR_RASTER_CACHE_SIZE`): PyMuPDF renders the region clip on demand, no new storage — cache is a pure performance optimization, evictable, never correctness-bearing (C11, closes E3).\n- `serve/tools/fetch.py` (net new): `fetch(page_ids, include=[\"image\",\"text\",\"summary\"], dpi=150, region=None, inline=True)`; caps: ≤5 pages and ≤12MP total (`fetch_budget_exceeded {limit, requested}` — F18, fetch half); `url` always present, `bytes_b64` only when `inline=true` (default).\n- CLI one-shot: `vsir fetch` (§4.4); `vsir demo narrow` ties skim → fetch together as the milestone's official walkthrough.\n\nWorking Deliverable:\n- `GET /pages/{page_id}/image` route + `vsir fetch` CLI + `vsir demo narrow`.\n\nDemo Command:\n- `vsir demo narrow` — runs `skim_pages` → `fetch` over the synthetic doc, printing triage rows with `ImageRef` only, then the `fetch` result with `bytes_b64` present, then an over-budget `fetch` (6 pages) failing typed `fetch_budget_exceeded` (F18).\n\nDeliverables (files):\n- `backend/vsir/serve/app.py` (extended — `/pages/{page_id}/image` route)\n- `backend/vsir/serve/tools/fetch.py` (written, net new)\n- `backend/vsir/core/raster_cache.py` (written, net new — in-process LRU)\n- `backend/vsir/cli.py` (extended — `fetch`, `demo narrow` subcommands)\n- `backend/tests/api/test_fetch.py`, `test_page_image.py` (written)\n\nTwelve-Factor Notes:\n- Adds `.env.example` var: `VSIR_RASTER_CACHE_SIZE` (LRU entry count, process-local perf cache only — lost on restart with no correctness impact, satisfying C11).\n\n---\n\nUnit ID: U019\nName: read tool core logic (stub replay)\nMilestone: M5\nType: tool\nPriority: P0-Critical\nSize Estimate: Large\nSpend: none\nDepends On: [U018, U013]\nEnables: [U020]\nSpec References: [Spec §7.2.6, §6.3 (read_key), §7.3]\nInvariants Enforced: []\nFailure Rows Closed: [F19, F18 (M5 read half)]\nRequired Reading: [`impl/app/retrieve.py::read` (read first); `pipeline-guide/METADATA-CONTRACT.md` (§5.3, page_provenance shape); `IMPROVEMENTS.md` D3 (captions never written — `read` must not silently drop the captions channel it inherits from the page record) and B5 (cache embeddings — the read_key cache here must key on the actual question text, not a stale/generic key, which is exactly what closes F19)]\n\nDescription:\n- Build `read`'s core logic — transcription correction, `sufficient`, `page_provenance`, the ≤3-page cap, and the question-keyed cache — proved entirely through `VSIR_VLM=stub` replay against U013's frozen TC1E-SF fixtures, at zero spend.\n\nCore Requirements:\n- Read `impl/app/retrieve.py::read` first.\n- `serve/tools/read.py` ≈ `retrieve.py::read`: renders at pinned `dpi_answer=220` (caller cannot change it — part of `read_key`); every VLM-emitted code phrase-checked against that page's text and stamped `present | absent | unverifiable` — same vocabulary as `verify` (§7.2.4); on a page with no text layer, every code is `unverifiable`.\n- `sufficient` is mandatory in the result; retrieval judgment never happens inside `read` (§7.6).\n- §6.3 `read_key` cache: includes `page_ids` + the pinned dpi + the question text — a second question about the same pages is a cache miss (F19).\n- ≤3-page cap: `read_page_cap_exceeded` typed 400 (F18, read half).\n- `vlm/prompts/read.md` (net new prompt).\n- Proven via `VSIR_VLM=stub VSIR_FIXTURE=data/fixtures/TC1E-SF` replay — no real Gemini call in this unit.\n\nWorking Deliverable:\n- `vsir read --pages <ids> --question <q>` CLI + HTTP route, runnable in stub mode.\n\nDemo Command:\n- `VSIR_VLM=stub VSIR_FIXTURE=data/fixtures/TC1E-SF vsir read --pages TC1E-SF@1.3#p001,TC1E-SF@1.3#p002 --question \"is K158 energised?\"` — prints `ReadResult` with per-code stamps and `sufficient`; repeating the identical call shows a cache hit (instant); asking a *different* question about the same pages shows a cache miss (F19); requesting a 4th page → `read_page_cap_exceeded`.\n\nDeliverables (files):\n- `backend/vsir/serve/tools/read.py` (ported from `impl/app/retrieve.py::read`)\n- `backend/vsir/vlm/prompts/read.md` (written, net new)\n- `backend/vsir/core/read_cache.py` (written, net new — `read_key`)\n- `backend/vsir/cli.py` (extended — `read` subcommand)\n- `backend/tests/unit/test_read_core.py` (written)\n\nTwelve-Factor Notes:\n- Adds `.env.example` var: `VSIR_DPI_ANSWER=220` (pinned, documented as non-overridable at the API layer despite being config).\n- `read_key` cache is stored in Qdrant/keyed storage, not a local file (C11); stub replay via `VSIR_FIXTURE` is the same config-only mechanism from U008, not a code branch.\n\n---\n\nUnit ID: U020\nName: Real Gemini read path and searchable_ratio\nMilestone: M5\nType: tool\nPriority: P0-Critical\nSize Estimate: Medium\nSpend: paid\nDepends On: [U019]\nEnables: [U021]\nSpec References: [Spec §7.2.6, §7.2.1 (searchable_ratio), §17 (OQ-2)]\nInvariants Enforced: []\nFailure Rows Closed: []\nRequired Reading: [`IMPROVEMENTS.md` B6 (pin the model — this is the second real Gemini integration point after U013, re-verify the pinned id here)]\n\nDescription:\n- Wire U019's `read` to the real Gemini client for the first time, and finish `searchable_ratio` population on every `skim_documents` row against the real TC1E-SF corpus.\n\nCore Requirements:\n- Wire `vlm/client.py` (real path, from U008) into `serve/tools/read.py`; `VSIR_ALLOW_PAID=1` required or the call refuses.\n- Verify/complete `searchable_ratio` on every `DocHit` row (already scaffolded in U004's hit models) against the real, published TC1E-SF corpus from U013.\n- This is the FIRST real `read` call — confirms the pinned dpi 220, real transcription correction, and real cache behavior end to end.\n\nWorking Deliverable:\n- `vsir read` against the real Gemini backend.\n\nDemo Command:\n- `VSIR_ALLOW_PAID=1 vsir read --pages TC1E-SF@1.3#p001,TC1E-SF@1.3#p002 --question \"the carton discharge won't restart after an E-stop reset\"` — the milestone's official demo, plus `vsir skim documents \"carton discharge\"` showing a non-null `searchable_ratio` on the TC1E-SF row.\n\nDeliverables (files):\n- `backend/vsir/serve/tools/read.py` (extended — real client wiring, no new file)\n- `backend/vsir/serve/tools/skim.py` (extended — `searchable_ratio` finishing touch)\n- `backend/tests/paid/test_read_real.py` (written, gated by `scripts/test-paid.sh`)\n\nTwelve-Factor Notes:\n- Uses `GEMINI_API_KEY` and `VSIR_ALLOW_PAID` (both already declared)