{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MACjVLozP1ffRP1RdyJzW7","type":"tool_result","content":"Unit ID: U025\nName: Revision lifecycle and resumable ingest\nMilestone: M8\nType: ingest\nPriority: P0-Critical\nSize Estimate: Large\nSpend: none\nDepends On: [U022, U011]\nEnables: [U026]\nSpec References: [Spec §6.2 (Level-2 refusal), §6.7 (F9 half), §15 Factor IX, §4.4]\nInvariants Enforced: []\nFailure Rows Closed: [F9, F8 (M8 series_id half), F12 (M8 revision half)]\nRequired Reading: [`impl/app/pipeline.py`, `impl/app/segjobs.py` (read first — resumability being added on top of U011's run orchestration); `IMPROVEMENTS.md` E2 (job state on daemon threads — resumability must checkpoint through `vsir_runs`, never an in-memory thread) and E7 (orphan points — a killed-and-resumed run must not leave duplicate or orphaned points)]\n\nDescription:\n- Extend U011's run orchestration with `is_current` multi-revision lifecycle, `series_id` propagation, resumable `--resume` ingest with per-window checkpoints, graceful-shutdown checkpointing, and the typed Level-2 refusal — proved on a generated large PDF, never the excluded 1,440-page manual.\n\nCore Requirements:\n- Read `impl/app/pipeline.py`/`impl/app/segjobs.py` first (resumability extension).\n- `is_current` lifecycle across revisions: ingesting a new revision of the same `(doc_id)` sets prior *other* revision `is_current=False` and KEEPS it (never deletes — F9, F12 revision half); `found_only_in_superseded` status surfaced through `lookup`/`skim` when a code exists only in a non-current revision.\n- `series_id` propagated across revisions (F8, M8 half) so a straddling-section scope stays correct across a revision boundary.\n- Generate `data/source/synthetic_large.pdf` (a GENERATED large multi-window PDF, per §6.2's explicit note — never the excluded 1,440-page manual) for resume testing.\n- `--resume <run_id>` with per-window checkpoints in `vsir_runs`; SIGTERM handler checkpoints so a