"verified\" | Mitigation: core/status.py's six-value enum must carry an explicit \"unverifiable\" state distinct from \"absent\"; U020 stamps present/absent/unverifiable per page | Owning unit: U020.\n- R3 PyMuPDF is the single point of truth for exact search | Units: U004 | Impact: a PyMuPDF bug/version quirk silently corrupts every \"exact\" result system-wide | Mitigation: pin the version in U001's lockfile; run U005's four synthetic pages + observed-token inventory as a regression fixture on every PyMuPDF bump | Owning unit: U001 (pin) + U005 (fixture).\n- R4 grounded_rate ≥0.8 is set, not derived | Units: U013 (measures it), U026 (gates on it) | Impact: a 55-page sample may be unrepresentative of the full 5,505-page corpus, mis-calibrating the abstention threshold | Mitigation: treat U013's threshold as provisional; re-validate it against U025/U026's full-corpus run before it is treated as a hard gate | Owning unit: U013.\n- R5 multi-tenancy out of scope | Units: U003, U014 (bearer auth) | Impact: no isolation between callers sharing one token/collection; not a near-term blocker but constrains reuse | Mitigation: document explicitly as single-tenant in U001's .env.example / U002's AGENTS.md so it's never assumed safe for multi-customer deployment | Owning unit: U002.\n- R6 prompt-level rules advisory on raw MCP | Units: U015 | Impact: a non-compliant MCP client can exceed §7.3 caps or skip verification since MCP is a rawer surface than HTTP | Mitigation: enforce caps/verification server-side in the shared tool implementation (see integration point 5), not via prompt text | Owning unit: U015.\n- R7 the port is a rewrite of a 3,268-line, zero-test system; parity can't cover ~70% of §7/§8 | Units: U012 | Impact: silent regressions in code paths legacy `impl` never exercised, surfacing late in M5/M6/M8 against real data | Mitigation: don't treat U012's parity suite as sufficient sign-off alone — U006's abstention eval, U016's acceptance eval, and U026's D11 corpus gates are the real safety net; U012 must explicitly flag which §7/§8 paths have zero legacy coverage | Owning unit: U012 (immediate) / U026 (final safety net).\n- New: paid-spend sequencing risk — a paid unit (U013/U020/U022/U026) could get run before its free prerequisite milestone is fully green, burning budget re-running work a free test would have caught | Units: U012, U016 | Impact: wasted Gemini spend, violates the \"free before paid\" constraint | Mitigation: process/CI gate — no SPEND PAID unit runs until every unit in its own and all prior milestones is green | Owning unit: U002 (owns the test-*.sh gating scripts).\n- New: OQ-5 single-collection scale risk — one Qdrant collection at 5,505 pages is unproven until M8 | Units: U003 (schema), U025 (lifecycle at scale) | Impact: late-discovered latency/index-build problems could force an architecture change after most of the system is built | Mitigation: default to doc_id-scoped single collection now, but load-test early using U025's own generated data/source/synthetic_large.pdf rather than waiting for the real corpus | Owning unit: U025.\n\nRecommended Implementation Order:\n1. U001 — root of the graph; nothing else can start without the runtime skeleton and `vsir doctor`.\n2. U002 — the test harness/conformance suite must exist before any downstream unit's behavior can be proven.\n3. U003 — record/id/Qdrant-schema layer every later component reads or writes.\n4. U004 — tokenization/variants/exact/status/envelope; the fan-out point that unlocks both the M1 tail and the M2a ingest pipeline.\n5. U007 — start the ingest pipeline (needs only U001/U003) in parallel with the M1 tail below.\n6. U005 — synthetic pages + pure lookup; parallel with U007/U008, needs only U004.\n7. U008 — VLM client/cache/stub + extract; continues the ingest track opened by U007.\n8. U006 — verify/abstention eval; parallel with U008/U009, closes the M1 correctness proof.\n9. U009 — derive/health/stitch, next serial link in the ingest chain.\n10. U010 — embed/index; needs both U009 (ingest) and U004 (core), the two streams' first join point.\n11. U011 — gates/publish/retire/export/run record; closes M2a and unlocks both M2b and M3.\n12. U012 — legacy parity port (SPEND NONE); must go before U013 so paid spend is gated by a green parity suite.\n13. U014 — serve/app/auth/audit/budget (M3); only needs U011, so run it in parallel with U012/U013 rather than waiting on M2b.\n14. U013 — the one paid TC1E-SF ingest (SPEND PAID); gated by U012 and by OQ-1/OQ-2 resolution (else replay fallback).\n15. U015 — HTTP+MCP wrappers around lookup/verify; needs U014, U005, U006, the core→tool integration seam.\n16. U016 — eval acceptance/abstention; needs U015 and U012's parity fixtures.\n17. U017 — skim_pages/resolve (M4); needs U015 and U010, the retrieval-tool layer proper.\n18. U018 — fetch.py/image endpoint; needs U017 and U007 (raster access back to the render stage).\n19. U019 — skim_documents/sections aggregation; needs only U017, run in parallel with U020.\n20. U020 — read.py (SPEND PAID); needs U018, U008, U006, run in parallel with U019.\n21. U021 — triage/prompt routing (M6); needs U019 and U018.\n22. U022 — the loop/answer gate (SPEND PAID); needs U021 and U020, closes the ask pipeline.\n23. U023 — frontend console (M7); needs only U022, run in parallel with U025.\n24. U025 — retirement lifecycle at scale (M8, SPEND NONE); needs U022 and U011, run in parallel with U023.\n25. U024 — Playwright e2e replay suite; needs U023.\n26. U026 — corpus eval / final D11 gates (SPEND PAID); needs U025, U016, U013 — the last unit, closing the project."},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: aed51ec74c1cae7de (use SendMessage with to: 'aed51ec74c1cae7de', summary: '<5-10 word recap>' to continue this agent)\n<usage>subagent_tokens: 49439\ntool_uses: 0\nduration_ms: 275204</usage>"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4eefb16f-3989-4441-9cd3-d294cfccb11f","uuid":"ab59c3a8-180f-4e00-9e03-ec2a15d5332c","timestamp":"2026-09-09T17:10:50.313Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"You are Synthesis Agent S4 (dependency and risk analysis) for a PLAN-ONLY planning task. DO NOT WRITE FILES. DO NOT IMPLEMENT CODE. Output your analysis as your final message only. You do not need to read the spec — the unit list and constraints below are authoritative. If you must check one thing, use a single targeted `sed -n` on `development/cr1/spec/spec.md` in /Users/sabesonk/Documents/DILMAH/dilmah-engineering-solutioning/poc/vision_segmentation_index_and_retrieval.\n\n## The 26 units, with milestone, spend and the dependencies proposed so far\nM0 (spend none)\n- U001 Runtime skeleton, pins/lock, Dockerfile, .env.example (all twelve §15 Factor III vars), JSON logs to stdout, SIGTERM handler, release_id stamping, `vsir` CLI, `vsir doctor` (§4.3's five refusals). Depends: []. Closes F11 (boot half).\n- U002 docker-compose.test.yml rewritten Postgres→Qdrant (test ports backend 8001 / Qdrant 6335), GET /health + GET /ready (§15.1), scripts/test-{unit,api,e2e,paid}.sh, the §12.5 conformance greps as a pytest module, AGENTS.md filled. Depends: [U001].\nM1 (none) — the whole correctness proof, zero spend\n- U003 core/record.py (≈pagemodel.py), core/ids.py, core/indexed.py (the one INDEXED dict), Qdrant collection + text-index creation (§5.5). Depends: [U001, U002]. I6.\n- U004 core/tok.py, core/variants.py, core/exact.py, core/status.py (six-value enum), serve/envelope.py (both families, ≈api_models.py), §7.3 cap validators, ports ingest/sparse.py and rrf(). Depends: [U003]. I3, I5, F10.\n- U005 four hand-written synthetic pages, serve/tools/lookup.py as a pure function, the observed-token inventory, `vsir demo exact --synthetic`. Depends: [U004]. I2, F1, F3, F14.\n- U006 core/verify.py::verify_claims, present_instead, the near-miss generator, the L3 abstention eval. Depends: [U004, U005]. F2 (core), F16.\nM2a (none)\n- U007 ingest/manifest.py, probe.py, render.py, window.py (+ bisection), the generated data/source/synthetic_3window.pdf with an off-by-one trap and a crop trap. Depends: [U001, U003]. F13, F15.\n- U008 vlm/{client,cache,stub}.py, prompts/{s1,s2}.md, ingest/extract.py (new S2 schema), replay mode + typed fixture_miss. Depends: [U007]. F11 (key half).\n- U009 ingest/derive.py, core/health.py (grounded_rate), label precedence, code reattribution, ingest/stitch.py. Depends: [U008]. F5 (M2a), F6, F8 (stitching).\n- U010 ingest/embed.py (D4 interleaved), lexical+captions sparse surfaces, §6.6 fingerprint, ingest/index.py. Depends: [U009, U004]. \n- U011 ingest/gates.py, publish, the three-clause retirement, the vsir_runs control collection + advisory lease, ingest/export.py, the run record, `vsir runs show`/`gates rerun`/`publish --override`. Depends: [U010]. I1, I4, I7, F4 (M2a), F7, F12 (M2a), F17.\nM2b (milestone spend: paid)\n- U012 port impl/data/raw/* and impl/data/exports/r-poc-*/{labels,withheld}.jsonl into data/fixtures/legacy/, plus the L2 parity and negative-set suite. Depends: [U011]. SPEND NONE.\n- U013 the one real paid TC1E-SF ingest (55 pages, new S2 schema), freeze data/fixtures/TC1E-SF/*, set the grounded_rate threshold from the measured distribution (R4). Depends: [U012]. SPEND PAID.\nM3 (none)\n- U014 serve/app.py, serve/auth.py (bearer), serve/audit.py (the ten-field line), serve/budget.py, `vsir serve`, §11.3 degradation. Depends: [U011].\n- U015 serve/tools/lookup.py + verify.py HTTP wrappers, the six-value status surfaced end to end, next.suggest, mcp/server.py (stdio+SSE, same implementations), `vsir lookup`/`verify`/`mcp`. Depends: [U014, U005, U006]. F2 (tool), F4 (M3).\n- U016 `vsir eval acceptance` + `vsir eval abstention`. Depends: [U015, U012].\nM4 (none)\n- U017 serve/tools/skim.py `skim_pages` + RRF ordering + decompose + exclude + next affordances + image queries (D12, embed_query_image), serve/tools/resolve.py. Depends: [U015, U010]. F5 (M4), F8 (stateless scope).\n- U018 GET /pages/{page_id}/image, the in-process raster LRU cache, serve/tools/fetch.py, the §7.3 caps, `vsir demo narrow`. Depends: [U017, U007]. F18 (fetch half).\nM5 (milestone spend: paid)\n- U019 skim_documents + skim_sections aggregation, searchable_ratio on every DocHit. Depends: [U017]. SPEND NONE.\n- U020 serve/tools/read.py: per-code present/absent/unverifiable stamps, sufficient, page_provenance, the ≤3-page cap, the question-keyed read_key cache, vlm/prompts/read.md. Depends: [U018, U008, U006]. F18 (read half), F19. SPEND PAID.\nM6 (milestone spend: paid)\n- U021 runner/triage.py (tri-state), runner/prompt.py, §8.1a fetch-vs-read routing, `vsir ask --explain`. Depends: [U019, U018]. SPEND NONE.\n- U022 runner/loop.py, the six correction loops, runner/answer.py (the server-side answer gate), §8.5 abstention wording, POST /ask, `vsir ask`. Depends: [U021, U020]. I8. SPEND PAID.\nM7 (none, fixture-backed replay)\n- U023 frontend/ React+TS+Vite two-zone console with trust badges, consuming image.url/preview.thumb_url with inline=false. Depends: [U022].\n- U024 Playwright E2E replay suite + scripts/test-e2e.sh (backend 8001, Qdrant 6335, frontend 5174). Depends: [U023].\nM8 (milestone spend: paid)\n- U025 is_current lifecycle, found_only_in_superseded, series_id across revisions, `--resume` with per-window checkpoints, SIGTERM checkpointing, `vsir retire`, the generated data/source/synthetic_large.pdf, typed `ladder_level_2_required`. Depends: [U022, U011]. F8 (series_id), F9, F12 (revision half). SPEND NONE.\n- U026 `vsir eval corpus` — the §12.6 report against the five ground-truth sets with the D11 gate numbers (code_precision = 1.00, code_recall ≥ 0.95 block below 0.90, abstention_correctness = 1.00, alarm_label_hit ≥ 0.99, xref_resolve ≥ 0.99). Depends: [U025, U016, U013]. SPEND PAID.\n\n## Constraints\n- Milestone order M0 → M1 → M2a → M2b → M3 → M4 → M5 → M6 → M7/M8 is fixed and no unit may cross a boundary.\n- Everything provable without a model call is planned before anything that spends.\n- Open questions (Spec §17): **OQ-1** = where the pilot PDF `TC1E-SF.pdf` lives and whether it may be checked in — blocks ONLY the M2b re-bill, because the S2 responses are already in `impl/data/raw/`; default: the operator places it at `data/source/TC1E-SF.pdf` and `data/source/` stays gitignored. **OQ-2** = which Gemini project/key and quota — blocks M2b, M5 and M6 paid paths only; default: run in replay mode (D10) off the ported responses, paid paths stay behind `VSIR_ALLOW_PAID=1`. **OQ-3/OQ-7** = Part A export sign-off (HTTP vs files on disk) — blocks the M8 export hand-off; default: serve over HTTP and additionally write to an attached object store if Part A needs files, never to local disk. **OQ-5** = one collection at 5,505-page scale — M8; default: one collection with doc_id scoping.\n- Residual risks (Spec §18): R1 recall is not guaranteed; R2 a scanned page's codes are never text-verified; R3 PyMuPDF is the single point of truth for exact search; R4 grounded_rate ≥ 0.8 is chosen, not derived — set it from the M2b distribution; R5 multi-tenancy is out of scope; R6 prompt-level rules are advisory on the raw MCP surface; R7 **the port is a rewrite of a system with 3,268 lines and zero tests**, so `impl`'s behaviour is only observable through its outputs — the parity set (U012) is the mitigation, and it cannot cover the ~70% of §7/§8 that `impl` never exercised.\n\n## Your task\nValidate the dependency graph (find any cycle or any dependency that crosses a milestone boundary backwards), identify the critical path, find genuinely parallelisable streams, name integration points with a risk and a mitigation each, flag every externally-blocked unit with the fallback that keeps it deliverable, and give a recommended implementation order.\n\nOutput EXACTLY this format:\n\n### Synthesis Agent 4: Dependency & Risk Analysis\n\nDependency Graph:\n- <Unit ID> → depends on → [<Unit IDs>]\n(all 26, and flag with ⚠ any edge you are changing from the list above, with a one-line reason)\n\nGraph Validation:\n- Cycles: <none, or name them>\n- Backwards milestone edges: <none, or name them>\n- Unreachable / orphan units: <none, or name them>\n\nCritical Path:\n- <ordered unit chain> — <total unit count> — <the one-line reason this is the longest chain>\n\nParallel Work Streams:\n- Stream <n> (<milestone>): <units> — <what makes them independent> — <who could own it>\n\nIntegration Points:\n- <point> | Units: <…> | Risk: <…> | Mitigation: <…>\n(cover at minimum: Qdrant schema vs INDEXED; the core→tool wrapper seam at M1/M3; the stub-VLM replay seam; the fixture handoff M2a→M2b→M5; the HTTP↔MCP same-implementation seam; the backend↔frontend contract at M7; the ingest lease seam at M8)\n\nExternal-Blocker Units:\n- <Unit ID> — blocked on <OQ-n> — fallback: <exactly what ships anyway, and which acceptance bullets are deferred>\n\nRisk Register (unit-attached):\n- <R-n or a new risk> | Units: <…> | Impact: <…> | Mitigation: <…> | Owning unit: <…>\n\nRecommended Implementation Order:\n1. <Unit ID> — <reason, one line>\n(all 26, respecting milestone order)\n","agentId":"aed51ec74c1cae7de","agentType":"general-purpose","harnessNoteCount":0,"harnessTailCount":0,"harnessSectionHash":"0cac7370d574f62b","content":[{"type":"text","text":"### Synthesis Agent 4: Dependency & Risk Analysis\n\nDependency Graph:\n- U001 → depends on → []\n- U002 → depends on → [U001]\n- U003 → depends on → [U001, U002]\n- U004 → depends on → [U003]\n- U005 → depends on → [U004]\n- U006 → depends on → [U004, U005]\n- U007 → depends on → [U001, U003]\n- U008 → depends on → [U007]\n- U009 → depends on → [U008]\n- U010 → depends on → [U009, U004]\n- U011 → depends on → [U010]\n- U012 → depends on → [U011]\n- U013 → depends on → [U012]\n- U014 → depends on → [U011]\n- U015 → depends on → [U014, U005, U006]\n- U016 → depends on → [U015, U012]\n- U017 → depends on → [U015, U010]\n- U018 → depends on → [U017, U007]\n- U019 → depends on → [U017]\n- U020 → depends on → [U018, U008, U006]\n- U021 → depends on → [U019, U018]\n- U022 → depends on → [U021, U020]\n- U023 → depends on → [U022]\n- U024 → depends on → [U023]\n- U025 → depends on → [U022, U011]\n- U026 → depends on → [U025, U016, U013]\n\nNo edges were changed from the proposed list — every edge already points to a same- or earlier-milestone unit, and the graph is a DAG as given.\n\nGraph Validation:\n- Cycles: none (topological order exists: U001,U002,U003,U004,U007,U005,U008,U006,U009,U010,U011,U012,U014,U013,U015,U016,U017,U018,U019,U020,U021,U022,U023,U025,U024,U026 — every dependency precedes its unit).\n- Backwards milestone edges: none. Checked all 26 edges against milestone order M0→M1→M2a→M2b→M3→M4→M5→M6→M7/M8; every dependency sits in the same or a strictly earlier milestone (e.g. U014 (M3) depends only on U011 (M2a), skipping M2b, but that is a same-direction skip, not a backwards edge).\n- Unreachable / orphan units: none. All 26 units are reachable from U001, and every non-terminal unit is depended on by at least one other unit. Two legitimate terminal (no-dependent) nodes: U024 (M7 e2e suite) and U026 (M8 corpus eval) — both are intended final deliverables, not orphans.\n\nCritical Path:\n- U001 → U002 → U003 → U007 → U008 → U009 → U010 → U011 → U014 → U015 → U017 → U018 → U020 → U022 → U025 → U026 — 16 units — the ingest pipeline (U007→U011) is a strictly serial, single-writer data pipeline (manifest→probe→render→window→extract→derive→embed/index→gates/publish) that gates everything above it, and the retrieval/ask stack that stacks on top (U014→U022) is itself serial through the U017→U018→U020→U022 spine; U021/U019 tie U018/U020 in depth (both required by U022, run in parallel, same length) and U023→U024 (M7) ties U025→U026 (M8) in depth off U022, so this is one of two equal-length (16-unit) longest chains — the other ends at U024.\n\nParallel Work Streams:\n- Stream 1 (M1 tail ∥ M2a head): U005→U006 vs U007→U008→U009 — independent because U005/U006 need only U004 and U007/U008/U009 need only U001/U003 (U010 is the first M2a unit that needs U004) — owners: a core-semantics/eval engineer on U005/U006, a separate ingest-pipeline engineer on U007–U009.\n- Stream 2 (M2a tail ∥ M2b ∥ M3 head): once U011 lands, U012→U013 (paid legacy port + paid TC1E-SF ingest) and U014 (serve/app/auth/audit/budget) are mutually independent — U013 only needs U012, U014 only needs U011, neither touches the other — owners: a data/fixtures engineer on U012/U013 (paid-gated, can stall on OQ-1/OQ-2 without blocking anyone else), a backend-platform engineer on U014.\n- Stream 3 (M5): U019 (skim_documents/sections) ∥ U020 (read.py, paid) — U019 needs only U017, U020 needs U018+U008+U006, neither depends on the other — owners: a retrieval-aggregation engineer on U019, a VLM/read engineer on U020.\n- Stream 4 (M7 ∥ M8): U023→U024 (frontend + Playwright e2e) ∥ U025→U026 (retirement lifecycle + corpus eval) — both branches are gated only on U022 (plus U011/U016/U013, all long since satisfied) and never reference each other — owners: a frontend engineer on U023/U024, a data/eval engineer on U025/U026.\n\nIntegration Points:\n- Qdrant schema vs INDEXED | Units: U003, U010, U011 | Risk: the Qdrant collection (payload schema, text index) and the in-process INDEXED dict can desync — e.g. a point exists in Qdrant but not in INDEXED, or vice versa — producing phantom or missing hits | Mitigation: single-writer discipline — only U010's ingest/index.py may write both, gated by the §6.6 fingerprint; add a conformance check (in U002's pytest module) asserting INDEXED keys == Qdrant point IDs after every ingest run.\n- core→tool wrapper seam at M1/M3 | Units: U004–U006 (pure-python core), U015 (HTTP/MCP wrappers) | Risk: U015 re-implements status/cap logic in the wrapper instead of calling into core, so the M1-proven correctness silently stops applying at the tool boundary | Mitigation: U015 must import and call core/verify.py and serve/tools/lookup.py directly; replay the M1 fixture suite through the HTTP layer as a contract test asserting byte-identical output.\n- Stub-VLM replay seam | Units: U008 (client/cache/stub, D10 replay), U009, U020, U022 (all consume VLM output) | Risk: cached/replayed fixtures go stale relative to prompt edits (s1/s2/read.md), so replay-mode tests pass against an outdated contract while real paid calls would fail | Mitigation: key the cache on a hash of (input, prompt template, schema version), not input alone, so any prompt change forces an explicit typed fixture_miss instead of a silent stale hit; CI checks fixture hashes against current prompt hashes.\n- Fixture handoff M2a→M2b→M5 | Units: U011 (publish/run record), U012 (legacy parity fixtures), U013 (frozen TC1E-SF fixtures), U020 (paid read.py consumer) | Risk: legacy fixtures (old schema) and the new S2 TC1E-SF fixtures could diverge in schema version, letting derive/stitch logic pass parity on legacy shape but break on real data, or letting R4's grounded_rate threshold get baked in before parity is proven | Mitigation: stamp every fixture directory with release_id/schema_version (from U001) and have U016/U026 assert compatibility; run U012's parity suite as a hard gate before U013 spends paid budget.\n- HTTP↔MCP same-implementation seam | Units: U015 | Risk: HTTP route handlers and MCP handlers each hand-roll request validation/cap enforcement, diverging over time; R6 flags that prompt-level rules are only advisory on the raw MCP surface, so a non-compliant MCP client could bypass §7.3 caps that HTTP enforces | Mitigation: factor validation/cap-checking into one shared function called by both transports; never let MCP rely on prompt instructions for enforcement — hard-enforce server-side identically to HTTP.\n- Backend↔frontend contract at M7 | Units: U014/U004 (envelope.py), U018 (fetch.py, image.url/thumb_url), U023 (React console) | Risk: U023 is the first real consumer of inline=false/thumb_url and trust-badge status fields, built milestones after those envelopes were frozen, so contract mismatches surface only at final integration | Mitigation: version serve/envelope.py explicitly and generate frontend fixtures from U024's Playwright replay data as soon as U020/U022 exist, so U023 can be developed against a frozen contract before M7 formally starts.\n- Ingest lease seam at M8 | Units: U011 (vsir_runs control collection + advisory lease), U025 (--resume, per-window checkpoints, SIGTERM checkpointing at 5,505-page scale) | Risk: the lease logic proven at small (synthetic/55-page) scale in U011 may not handle a crashed-and-resumed run at full scale, leaving a stale lease (deadlock) or a race between two resumed runs (double write) | Mitigation: build the lease with heartbeat+expiry semantics from U011 onward, and require U025's --resume to reuse the exact same lease-renewal path as a fresh run (no parallel \"resume\" code path), validated by a kill-and-resume test.\n\nExternal-Blocker Units:\n- U013 — blocked on OQ-1 and OQ-2 — fallback: run in replay mode (D10) off the already-ported impl/data/raw responses (SPEND NONE fallback path, gated behind VSIR_ALLOW_PAID=1 for the real path); deferred: the \"fresh paid re-ingest freezes fixtures from a live run\" acceptance bullet and the live-measured R4 grounded_rate threshold — both ship once the operator supplies data/source/TC1E-SF.pdf and Gemini credentials.\n- U020 — blocked on OQ-2 — fallback: ships fully code-complete and test-covered against replayed/stubbed VLM responses; deferred: the acceptance bullet requiring a live paid read.md call against real Gemini for grounded present/absent/unverifiable stamping.\n- U022 — blocked on OQ-2 — fallback: the loop/answer-gate logic, correction loops, and §8.5 abstention wording ship and are tested end-to-end in replay mode; deferred: the acceptance bullet requiring live paid triage+answer calls.\n- U026 — blocked on OQ-2 (transitively via U013) — fallback: `vsir eval corpus` and the D11 gate report run against the replay-derived/ported distribution and the default single-collection/doc_id-scoped architecture (OQ-5 default); deferred: the acceptance bullet requiring the report to reflect a live paid full-corpus run and a live-derived R4 threshold.\n- U011 (ingest/export.py only) — blocked on OQ-3/OQ-7 — fallback: serve exports over HTTP and additionally dual-write to an attached object store, never local disk, per the stated default; deferred: the \"confirmed to exactly match Part A's chosen hand-off mechanism\" sign-off bullet, without blocking U011's own delivery or anything downstream.\n\nRisk Register (unit-attached):\n- R1 recall not guaranteed | Units: U004, U010, U017 | Impact: false negatives (relevant pages missed) with no system-visible signal | Mitigation: U006's abstention eval plus U026's code_recall ≥0.95 gate catch it at eval time; U019's searchable_ratio exposes coverage gaps to callers | Owning unit: U026.\n- R2 scanned pages never text-verified | Units: U004 (exact.py), U006 (verify_claims), U020 (per-code stamps) | Impact: a claimed code on an image-only page can't be confirmed, risking a false \"verified\" | Mitigation: core/status.py's six-value enum must carry an explicit \"unverifiable\" state distinct from \"absent\"; U020 stamps present/absent/unverifiable per page | Owning unit: U020.\n- R3 PyMuPDF is the single point of truth for exact search | Units: U004 | Impact: a PyMuPDF bug/version quirk silently corrupts every \"exact\" result system-wide | Mitigation: pin the version in U001's lockfile; run U005's four synthetic pages + observed-token inventory as a regression fixture on every PyMuPDF bump | Owning unit: U001 (pin) + U005 (fixture).\n- R4 grounded_rate ≥0.8 is set, not derived | Units: U013 (measures it), U026 (gates on it) | Impact: a 55-page sample may be unrepresentative of the full 5,505-page corpus, mis-calibrating the abstention threshold | Mitigation: treat U013's threshold as provisional; re-validate it against U025/U026's full-corpus run before