ill present in the result set (never omitted)\n- [ ] `skim_sections(query=\"valve\")` section boundaries match the fixture's known section structure\n- [ ] for a document with N pages and M `has_text` pages, `searchable_ratio == M/N` exactly\n\n---\n\nUnit ID: U020\nTest Levels: [L0, L2, L4]\nSuites / Commands: `bash scripts/test-unit.sh -k \"read_stamps\"` ; `bash scripts/test-api.sh -k \"read_page_cap or read_key_cache or read_sufficient\"` ; `VSIR_ALLOW_PAID=1 bash scripts/test-paid.sh -k \"read_worked_trace or read_failure_branch\"`\nTest Coverage:\n- Happy Path: `test_read_present_absent_unverifiable_stamps`, `test_sufficient_true_only_with_present_and_provenance`\n- Edge Cases: `test_read_key_cache_hit_single_vlm_call`, `test_read_page_cap_boundary_exactly_3_passes`\n- Error Cases (typed 4xx per §7.3): `test_read_page_cap_exceeded_at_4_pages`\n- Degradation (§11.3): `test_503_vlm_unavailable_on_read`\nTest Data: Fixtures `data/fixtures/synthetic_3window/` (replay, zero-cost), `data/fixtures/TC1E-SF/` (replay for L0-L2; live paid call only in the gated L4 test) | Stubs stub VLM for L0-L2; real Gemini only in the gated L4 test\nNotes: one of exactly four units permitted an L4 test (rule 2), gated behind `VSIR_ALLOW_PAID=1`.\nAcceptance Criteria (Testable):\n- [ ] `read(question=\"...\", pages=[p1,p2,p3])` succeeds; the same call with a 4th page raises `read_page_cap_exceeded`\n- [ ] a code confirmed present in the page image is stamped `present`; a code the phrase index has but the image read cannot confirm is stamped `unverifiable`; a code neither present nor confirmable is stamped `absent`\n- [ ] `sufficient == True` only when at least one queried code resolves `present` with matching `page_provenance`\n- [ ] calling `read` twice with an identical `(question, pages)` key results in exactly 1 stub VLM call across both calls (`read_key` cache hit, zero extra spend)\n- [ ] (L4, paid, gated) a real read against a frozen TC1E-SF page produces stamps matching a human-verified `expected.json` entry, run only under `VSIR_ALLOW_PAID=1`\n- [ ] (L4, paid, gated) the failure-branch case: a genuinely ambiguous code is stamped `unverifiable`, never falsely `present`\n- [ ] Qdrant available, Gemini stubbed to raise unreachable → `read` returns `503 vlm_unavailable`\n\n---\n\nUnit ID: U021\nTest Levels: [L0, L2]\nSuites / Commands: `bash scripts/test-unit.sh -k \"triage or prompt_builder\"` ; `bash scripts/test-api.sh -k \"fetch_vs_read_routing or ask_explain\"`\nTest Coverage:\n- Happy Path: `test_triage_returns_one_of_three_states`, `test_prompt_builder_deterministic`\n- Edge Cases: `test_relevant_routes_fetch_no_vlm_call`, `test_uncertain_routes_read_vlm_call`\n- Error Cases (typed 4xx per §7.3): N/A — this unit exposes no caller-facing bound\n- Degradation (§11.3): N/A\nTest Data: Fixtures `data/fixtures/synthetic_3window/`, `data/fixtures/TC1E-SF/` | Stubs stub VLM (replay), ephemeral Qdrant\nAcceptance Criteria (Testable):\n- [ ] `triage.classify(hit)` returns exactly one of `\"relevant\"`, `\"uncertain\"`, `\"irrelevant\"` for every fixture hit tested\n- [ ] a `\"relevant\"` triage result routes to `fetch` with zero VLM calls (spy); an `\"uncertain\"` result routes to `read` with exactly one stubbed VLM call\n- [ ] `vsir ask --explain \"...\"` prints the triage state and routing decision for each candidate page, with a spy confirming zero live Gemini calls (SPEND NONE)\n- [ ] `runner/prompt.py` produces a byte-identical prompt string given identical triage inputs\n\n---\n\nUnit ID: U022\nTest Levels: [L0, L2, L3, L4]\nSuites / Commands: `bash scripts/test-unit.sh -k \"answer_gate\"` ; `bash scripts/test-api.sh -k \"ask_post or correction_loop or near_miss_ask\"` ; `VSIR_ALLOW_PAID=1 bash scripts/test-paid.sh -k \"ask_worked_trace or ask_abstention_wording\"`\nTest Coverage:\n- Happy Path: `test_ask_answer_every_cited_code_verified`, `test_cli_vsir_ask`\n- Edge Cases: `test_six_correction_loops_fire_and_terminate` (six named sub-tests, one per loop, each bounded-iteration)\n- Error Cases (typed 4xx per §7.3): inherits caps/budgets from U004/U014/U020 — no new error type introduced by this unit\n- Degradation (§11.3): `test_answer_gate_rejects_unverified_cited_code`, `test_abstention_wording_on_insufficient_evidence`\nTest Data: Fixtures `data/fixtures/synthetic_3window/`, `data/fixtures/TC1E-SF/` | Stubs stub VLM for L0-L3; real Gemini only in the gated L4 test\nNotes: I8 — the highest-severity assertion in this unit is that `answer.py`'s server-side gate never surfaces a code `verify` did not clear. This is the unit that extends the L3 abstention eval (owned by U006) to the full end-to-end `/ask` loop.\nAcceptance Criteria (Testable):\n- [ ] `POST /ask {\"question\": \"...\"}` (replay mode) returns an answer where every cited code passed `verify` (no cited code has an uncleared verify status)\n- [ ] each of the six correction loops fires under a crafted fixture scenario and terminates within a bounded iteration count (six named tests)\n- [ ] `answer.py`'s gate rejects/strips a candidate answer citing an unverified code rather than passing it through\n- [ ] feeding `near_misses(n=100)` (from U006) as `/ask` question payloads never yields an answer citing the fake code, and uses the exact §8.5 abstention wording\n- [ ] `vsir ask \"...\"` CLI exits 0 and prints either an answer or the exact abstention wording\n- [ ] (L4, paid, gated) one real end-to-end `/ask` call against TC1E-SF under `VSIR_ALLOW_PAID=1` produces a worked trace matching a human-verified expected answer\n- [ ] (L4, paid, gated) an intentionally unanswerable question against TC1E-SF returns the §8.5 abstention wording verbatim, not a fabricated answer\n\n---\n\nUnit ID: U023\nTest Levels: [L0]\nSuites / Commands: `bash scripts/test-unit.sh -k \"trust_badge_mapping\"` (frontend TS unit tests, e.g. via `npm test -- -t trustBadge`)\nTest Coverage:\n- Happy Path: `test_trust_badge_for_each_status_distinct`\n- Edge Cases: `test_not_searchable_badge_differs_from_not_found_badge`\n- Error Cases (typed 4xx per §7.3): N/A — the frontend displays typed errors, it does not originate them\n- Degradation (§11.3): N/A — degradation-state rendering is exercised at E2E level (U024)\nTest Data: Fixtures none (pure literal status strings) | Stubs none\nNotes: full interactive/browser rendering of the two-zone console is owned by U024's Playwright suite; this unit's own tests are limited to pure TS badge-mapping logic.\nAcceptance Criteria (Testable):\n- [ ] `trustBadgeFor(status)` returns a distinct badge identifier for each of the six status values (no two statuses collapse to the same badge)\n- [ ] `trustBadgeFor(\"not_searchable\") !== trustBadgeFor(\"not_found\")`\n\n---\n\nUnit ID: U024\nTest Levels: [E2E]\nSuites / Commands: `bash scripts/test-e2e.sh -k \"search_result_badge or abstention_ui or qdrant_down_banner or no_gemini_calls\"`\nTest Coverage:\n- Happy Path: `test_search_sf_1_1a_shows_single_result_card_with_correct_badge`\n- Edge Cases: `test_near_miss_query_shows_abstention_never_fabricated_card`\n- Error Cases (typed 4xx per §7.3): `test_read_over_3_pages_shows_read_page_cap_message_not_crash`\n- Degradation (§11.3): `test_qdrant_stopped_shows_retry_banner_never_blank_page`\nTest Data: Fixtures `data/fixtures/synthetic_3window/`, `data/fixtures/TC1E-SF/` | Stubs stub VLM (replay), docker-compose.test.yml (U002) with Qdrant; E2E must never call Gemini (rule 2)\nAcceptance Criteria (Testable):\n- [ ] typing `\"SF 1.1A\"` surfaces exactly one result card with a trust badge matching the backend's status\n- [ ] querying a near-miss/fake code shows the abstention/not-found UI state, never a fabricated result card\n- [ ] stopping the Qdrant container mid-session and issuing a query shows a retry/unavailable banner, never a blank page or unhandled exception\n- [ ] a network-call assertion confirms zero requests to any Gemini/`*.googleapis.com` endpoint across the entire suite run\n- [ ] `bash scripts/test-e2e.sh` runs the full suite headless in CI and exits nonzero on any failed assertion\n\n---\n\nUnit ID: U025\nTest Levels: [L0, L1, L2]\nSuites / Commands: `bash scripts/test-unit.sh -k \"is_current_lifecycle or ladder_level\"` ; `bash scripts/test-api.sh -k \"found_only_in_superseded or resume_checkpoint or sigterm_ingest or retire\"`\nTest Coverage:\n- Happy Path: `test_publish_new_revision_flips_is_current_shares_series_id`, `test_retire_idempotent`\n- Edge Cases: `test_code_only_on_superseded_page_returns_found_only_in_superseded`, `test_resume_skips_completed_windows`\n- Error Cases (typed 4xx per §7.3): `test_ladder_level_2_required_on_insufficient_trust`\n- Degradation (§11.3): `test_sigterm_mid_ingest_synthetic_large_leaves_resumable_checkpoint`\nTest Data: Fixtures `data/source/synthetic_large.pdf` / `data/fixtures/synthetic_large/` (produced by U025 itself) | Stubs stub VLM (replay), ephemeral Qdrant\nNotes: explicitly named for a SIGTERM test by rule 5. If `--resume`/checkpoint export reuses U011's `ingest/export.py`, the same superseded-shape caution from `impl/pipeline-guide/11-export.md` (step 12, `withheld.jsonl`) applies transitively — do not port that shape verbatim.\nAcceptance Criteria (Testable):\n- [ ] publishing a new revision flips the prior revision's pages to `is_current == False` and the new revision's to `is_current == True`, both sharing `series_id`\n- [ ] a code present only on a superseded revision's page returns `found_only_in_superseded == True` rather than a silent miss\n- [ ] `SIGTERM` sent mid-ingest of `synthetic_large.pdf` produces a per-window checkpoint; `vsir ingest ... --resume` afterward reprocesses zero already-completed windows (stub VLM call count for those windows unchanged) and completes the remainder\n- [ ] `vsir retire <series_id>` sets `is_current == False` for every page in the series and is idempotent (a second call is a no-op, no error)\n- [ ] an operation requiring ladder level 2 on a document only established at ladder level 1 raises typed `ladder_level_2_required`\n- [ ] `data/source/synthetic_large.pdf` is generated large enough to force at least 3 checkpoints in a single ingest run\n\n---\n\nUnit ID: U026\nTest Levels: [L5]\nSuites / Commands: `VSIR_ALLOW_PAID=1 vsir eval corpus` (manual canary, not part of automated `scripts/test-*.sh` tiers per §12.2)\nTest Coverage:\n- Happy Path: `test_code_precision_1_00_over_component_register`, `test_alarm_label_hit_and_xref_resolve_thresholds`\n- Edge Cases: `test_single_precision_miss_triggers_p0_stop`, `test_recall_between_0_90_and_0_95_blocks_without_p0`\n- Error Cases (typed 4xx per §7.3): N/A — this is an offline eval report, not a caller-facing API\n- Degradation (§11.3): N/A\nTest Data: Fixtures none checked-in — the real corpus (component register E pp.59-125, alarm catalogue, cross-references), consumed only at this manual/full-stack level | Stubs none — the one legitimate live level\nNotes: manual canary per §12.2; explicitly permitted to touch the real corpus (rule 3 constrains L0-L3/E2E, not L5) and gated behind `VSIR_ALLOW_PAID=1` for any step that triggers a live Gemini call. Re-baselines §12.6/D11 thresholds from the M2b measurement with a recorded rationale (C10). One of exactly four units permitted an L4-class spend (rule 2); this report is classified L5 per §12.2's own table.\nAcceptance Criteria (Testable):\n- [ ] `code_precision == 1.00` over the component register (2,053 rows / 748 tags / 484 codes); any single miss halts the report with a P0 marker\n- [ ] `code_recall >= 0.95` passes; a value `< 0.90` marks the run `blocked`\n- [ ] `abstention_correctness == 1.00` over the 100-sample near-miss set (reusing U006's `near_misses`)\n- [ ] `alarm_label_hit >= 0.99` over the alarm catalogue (numbers 0-539, ~494 records)\n- [ ] `xref_resolve >= 0.99` over the 6,880 cross-reference tokens\n- [ ] the report records a rationale note for any re-baselined threshold (C10)\n- [ ] `vsir eval corpus` requires `VSIR_ALLOW_PAID=1` before executing any step that would trigger a live Gemini call\n\n---\n\nCross-Cutting Test Obligations:\n- Conformance greps (§12.5): owned by U002, re-run by every unit's Definition of Done\n- L3 abstention eval in CI from M1: owned by U006, extended by U013 (real TC1E-SF corpus swaps in for the synthetic seed), U016 (`vsir eval abstention` CLI wrapper), U022 (extended to the full `/ask` loop), U026 (extended to the full-corpus canary)\n- Probe behaviour (§15.1): owned by U002\n- SIGTERM: owned by U011, U025 (long-running ingest/publish/export work); light boot-time SIGTERM smoke-tested by U001\n- Fixture producers: `data/fixtures/synthetic_pages/` → U005 · `data/source/synthetic_3window.pdf` + `data/fixtures/synthetic_3window/` → U007 · `data/fixtures/legacy/` (labels.jsonl, withheld.jsonl, raw/*) → U012 · `data/fixtures/TC1E-SF/` (raw_window_1.json, raw_window_2.json, text.json, expected.json) → U013 · `data/source/synthetic_large.pdf` / `data/fixtures/synthetic_large/` → U025\n- Units planning an L4 test: U013, U020, U022 (U026 is classified L5 per §12.2 and is not planned as an L4 test, though it is one of the four SPEND PAID units permitted to)","usage":{"total_tokens":69368,"tool_uses":3,"duration_ms":458683},"uuid":"3d01d6cb-23b3-4991-a385-18b6a4516d94","session_id":"4eefb16f-3989-4441-9cd3-d294cfccb11f"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HS3KxCzkDNYobUM2ef9FX1","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"### Synthesis Agent 3: Test Strategy\n\nUnit ID: U001\nTest Levels: [L0, conformance]\nSuites / Commands: `bash scripts/test-unit.sh -k \"doctor or boot_refusal or json_logs or sigterm_boot\"`\nTest Coverage:\n- Happy Path: `test_doctor_exits_zero_on_valid_env`, `test_json_logs_parse_and_contain_release_id`\n- Edge Cases: `test_sigterm_during_boot_clean_exit`\n- Error Cases (typed 4xx per §7.3): N/A — this unit exposes no caller-facing bound\n- Degradation (§11.3): `test_boot_refuses_model_id_ending_latest`\nTest Data: Fixtures none (pure skeleton) | Stubs none\nNotes: conformance greps themselves are owned by U002; this unit's Definition of Done re-runs them.\nAcceptance Criteria (Testable):\n- [ ] `vsir doctor` exits 0 with a valid `.env` and exits nonzero with `GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-1.5-pro-latest`, printing a message naming `model id ends in -latest`\n- [ ] every log line emitted at startup parses via `json.loads` and contains `release_id` and `level` keys\n- [ ] a `SIGTERM` sent to the process during startup produces exit code 0 within 5s and leaves no orphan process\n\n---\n\nUnit ID: U002\nTest Levels: [L2, conformance]\nSuites / Commands: `bash scripts/test-api.sh -k \"health or ready or conformance_grep\"`\nTest Coverage:\n- Happy Path: `test_health_200_qdrant_up`, `test_ready_200_qdrant_up`\n- Edge Cases: `test_health_200_while_qdrant_stopped` (§15.1 probe split)\n- Error Cases (typed 4xx per §7.3): N/A — no caller-bound endpoints beyond health/ready at this unit\n- Degradation (§11.3): `test_ready_503_qdrant_unavailable_while_health_green`\nTest Data: Fixtures none (infra) | Stubs ephemeral Qdrant (docker-compose.test.yml)\nNotes: This unit owns the §12.5 conformance greps and the §15.1 probe-split behaviour; every later unit's Definition of Done re-runs the grep suite.\nAcceptance Criteria (Testable):\n- [ ] with the Qdrant container running, `GET /health` → 200 and `GET /ready` → 200\n- [ ] with the Qdrant container stopped (`docker stop`), `GET /health` still returns 200 and `GET /ready` returns 503 with body containing `qdrant_unavailable`\n- [ ] `scripts/test-unit.sh`, `scripts/test-api.sh`, `scripts/test-e2e.sh`, `scripts/test-paid.sh` all exist and are executable; `scripts/test-paid.sh` skips/exits nonzero when `VSIR_ALLOW_PAID` is unset\n- [ ] injecting `entity_keys` into a scratch file under `backend/vsir/serve/` makes the conformance grep fail; removing it makes the grep pass\n- [ ] the conformance grep test excludes its own source file from the scan (does not fail on its own banned-string list)\n\n---\n\nUnit ID: U003\nTest Levels: [L0, L2]\nSuites / Commands: `bash scripts/test-unit.sh -k \"ids or record\"` ; `bash scripts/test-api.sh -k \"indexed_collection\"`\nTest Coverage:\n- Happy Path: `test_ids_deterministic`, `test_record_roundtrip`, `test_collection_has_text_index`\n- Edge Cases: `test_ids_differ_by_page_no`, `test_record_normalizes_empty_text`\n- Error Cases (typed 4xx per §7.3): N/A — this unit exposes no caller-facing bound\n- Degradation (§11.3): N/A — the `index schema ≠ INDEXED → refuse to serve` refusal is enforced and tested at U014's boot path; U003 only defines the schema value it checks against\nTest Data: Fixtures none (ad hoc records built in-test) | Stubs ephemeral Qdrant (collection-creation portion only)\nAcceptance Criteria (Testable):\n- [ ] `ids.page_id(doc_id, page_no)` returns the same string across two calls with identical inputs, and a different string when `page_no` differs\n- [ ] `core.indexed.create_collection()` creates a Qdrant collection whose payload schema includes a full-text index on the `text` field (I6)\n- [ ] `record.PageRecord(**minimal_kwargs).to_payload()` then `.from_payload()` round-trips with no field loss\n\n---\n\nUnit ID: U004\nTest Levels: [L0]\nSuites / Commands: `bash scripts/test-unit.sh -k \"tok or variants or exact or status or envelope or caps or rrf\"`\nTest Coverage:\n- Happy Path: `test_tok_splits_alphanumeric_codes`, `test_variants_compact_label`, `test_status_enum_has_six_values`, `test_envelope_family_a_and_b_shapes`, `test_rrf_matches_hand_computed_fusion`\n- Edge Cases: `test_tok_handles_br_x20si4100_punctuation`, `test_cap_validator_boundary_at_exactly_cap`\n- Error Cases (typed 4xx per §7.3): `test_read_page_cap_exceeded_at_4_pages`, `test_fetch_budget_exceeded_payload_shape`, `test_dpi_not_allowed_for_100`, `test_dpi_requires_region_above_220`, `test_filter_unknown_key_lists_offending_keys`\n- Degradation (§11.3): N/A — the 429 quota logic itself lives in `serve/budget.py` (U014); this unit only supplies the pure validators\nTest Data: Fixtures none (pure) | Stubs none\nAcceptance Criteria (Testable):\n- [ ] `len(list(core.status.Status)) == 6`\n- [ ] `envelope.family_a(hits=[...])` and `envelope.family_b(hit=...)` produce distinct top-level shapes, both containing `reads_remaining`\n- [ ] cap validator raises `read_page_cap_exceeded` at `pages=4` and passes at `pages=3`\n- [ ] cap validator raises `fetch_budget_exceeded {limit, requested}` with `requested==6, limit==5` when 6 pages requested (limit 5)\n- [ ] cap validator raises `dpi_not_allowed` for `dpi=100` and passes for `dpi=150`\n- [ ] cap validator raises `dpi_requires_region` for `dpi=300, region=None` and passes for `dpi=300, region={...}`\n- [ ] cap validator raises `filter_unknown_key {keys}` for `scope={\"bogus_key\": 1}` with `keys==[\"bogus_key\"]`\n- [ ] `rrf([rank_list_a, rank_list_b], k=60)` matches a hand-computed `1/(k+rank)` sum for a fixed pair of rank lists\n\n---\n\nUnit ID: U005\nTest Levels: [L0, L1]\nSuites / Commands: `bash scripts/test-unit.sh -k \"lookup_exact or observed_token_inventory or demo_exact\"`\nTest Coverage:\n- Happy Path: `test_lookup_sf_1_1a_single_hit`, `test_demo_exact_synthetic_cli`\n- Edge Cases: `test_lookup_mutated_code_not_found`\n- Error Cases (typed 4xx per §7.3): N/A — pure function, no HTTP bound yet (wrapped in U015)\n- Degradation (§11.3): N/A — `not_searchable` handling requires scanned-page semantics introduced later; deferred\nTest Data: Fixtures `data/fixtures/synthetic_pages/` (four hand-written pages, produced by U005 itself) | Stubs none\nNotes: This unit produces the observed-token inventory that U006's `near_misses()` and the CI L3 eval consume from M1 onward (rule 8).\nAcceptance Criteria (Testable):\n- [ ] `lookup(\"SF 1.1A\")` against the four hand-written pages returns `total == 1` and `len(hits) == 1`\n- [ ] `lookup(<one-char mutation of a real fixture code>)` returns `hits == []` and `status == \"not_found\"`\n- [ ] the observed-token inventory extracted from the four pages contains every code embedded in the fixture text\n- [ ] `vsir demo exact --synthetic` exits 0 and prints at least one exact match referencing a known fixture code\n\n---\n\nUnit ID: U006\nTest Levels: [L0, L3]\nSuites / Commands: `bash scripts/test-unit.sh -k \"verify_claims or near_misses\"` ; `bash scripts/test-api.sh -k \"test_near_miss_codes_never_answer\"`\nTest Coverage:\n- Happy Path: `test_verify_claims_absent_when_tokens_present_phrase_not`\n- Edge Cases: `test_near_misses_returns_exactly_100_one_char_off`\n- Error Cases (typed 4xx per §7.3): N/A — this unit exposes no caller-facing bound\n- Degradation (§11.3): N/A — replay-safe by construction (near_misses derives purely from the local inventory, never calls Gemini)\nTest Data: Fixtures `data/fixtures/synthetic_pages/` (from U005) | Stubs none\nNotes: This is the unit that stands up the §12.4 L3 abstention eval in CI from M1 onward, per rule 8.\nAcceptance Criteria (Testable):\n- [ ] `verify_claims(\"SF 1.1A\", pages=[p008])` returns `status == \"absent\"` when the tokens exist on p008 but not as the contiguous phrase\n- [ ] `len(near_misses(n=100)) == 100` and every element differs from its source code by exactly one character\n- [ ] `test_near_miss_codes_never_answer` (verbatim from §12.4): for each of 100 near-misses, `lookup(fake).hits == []`, `status in (\"not_found\",\"not_searchable\")`, and no `present_instead` value `== fake`\n- [ ] this L3 test runs in `scripts/test-api.sh`, against the M1 synthetic-pages fixture, and is wired into CI to run on every commit from M1 onward\n\n---\n\nUnit ID: U007\nTest Levels: [L0, L1]\nSuites / Commands: `bash scripts/test-unit.sh -k \"manifest or probe or render or window_bisect or off_by_one or crop_trap\"`\nTest Coverage:\n- Happy Path: `test_manifest_page_count`, `test_window_bisect_returns_3_windows`\n- Edge Cases: `test_off_by_one_trap_page_text_matches_correct_page`, `test_crop_trap_page_not_split_across_windows`\n- Error Cases (typed 4xx per §7.3): N/A — this unit exposes no caller-facing bound\n- Degradation (§11.3): N/A\nTest Data: Fixtures `data/source/synthetic_3window.pdf` → `data/fixtures/synthetic_3window/` (produced by U007 itself) | Stubs none (pure PDF processing)\nAcceptance Criteria (Testable):\n- [ ] `manifest.build(synthetic_3window.pdf).page_count` matches the fixture's known page count\n- [ ] on the off-by-one trap page, `probe.get_text(pdf, page_no=K)` returns the marker string unique to page K, not K±1\n- [ ] on the crop trap page, `window.bisect(manifest)` keeps the trap page's content whole inside a single window (never splits its region)\n- [ ] `window.bisect(...)` returns exactly 3 windows for `synthetic_3window.pdf`\n- [ ] conformance grep confirms `get_text(` appears only inside `ingest/probe.py` within `backend/vsir/**`\n\n---\n\nUnit ID: U008\nTest Levels: [L0, L1]\nSuites / Commands: `bash scripts/test-unit.sh -k \"vlm_stub or vlm_cache or fixture_miss or extract\"`\nTest Coverage:\n- Happy Path: `test_extract_s1_from_fixture_zero_network_calls`, `test_cache_memoizes_by_key`\n- Edge Cases: `test_prompts_s1_s2_non_empty_and_selected_deterministically`\n- Error Cases (typed 4xx per §7.3): N/A — `fixture_miss` is an internal typed replay-mod