 serve` + §11.3 degradation · U015 serve/tools/lookup.py and verify.py HTTP wrappers + the six-value status surfaced + next.suggest + mcp/server.py stdio+SSE + `vsir lookup`/`vsir verify`/`vsir mcp` [F2 tool, F4 M3] · U016 `vsir eval acceptance` + `vsir eval abstention`\nM4 (none): U017 serve/tools/skim.py `skim_pages` + RRF ordering + decompose + exclude + next affordances + image queries (D12) + serve/tools/resolve.py [F5 M4, F8 stateless] · U018 GET /pages/{page_id}/image + the in-process raster LRU cache + serve/tools/fetch.py + §7.3 caps + `vsir demo narrow` [F18 fetch]\nM5 (milestone spend paid): U019 `skim_documents` + `skim_sections` aggregation + `searchable_ratio` on every DocHit — SPEND NONE · U020 serve/tools/read.py: per-code present/absent/unverifiable stamps, `sufficient`, `page_provenance`, ≤3-page cap, question-keyed `read_key` cache, vlm/prompts/read.md [F18 read, F19] — SPEND PAID\nM6 (milestone spend paid): U021 runner/triage.py (tri-state relevant|uncertain|irrelevant) + runner/prompt.py + §8.1a fetch-vs-read routing + `vsir ask --explain` — SPEND NONE · U022 runner/loop.py + the six correction loops + runner/answer.py (server-side answer gate) + §8.5 abstention wording + POST /ask + `vsir ask` [I8] — SPEND PAID\nM7 (none): U023 frontend/ React+TS+Vite two-zone console with trust badges · U024 Playwright E2E replay suite + scripts/test-e2e.sh\nM8 (milestone spend paid): U025 is_current lifecycle + found_only_in_superseded + series_id + `--resume` with per-window checkpoints + SIGTERM checkpointing + `vsir retire` + generated data/source/synthetic_large.pdf + typed `ladder_level_2_required` [F8 series_id, F9, F12 revision] — SPEND NONE · U026 `vsir eval corpus` — the §12.6 report with the D11 gate numbers — SPEND PAID\n\n## Rules you MUST obey\n1. Levels come from {L0, L1, L2, L3, L4, L5, E2E, conformance}. §12.2: L0 pure functions <1s `scripts/test-unit.sh`; L1 derivation over frozen `raw_window_*.json` <5s `scripts/test-unit.sh`; L2 index contract vs ephemeral Qdrant <30s `scripts/test-api.sh`; L3 adversarial abstention <60s `scripts/test-api.sh`; L4 worked trace + failure branch, docker + Gemini, `scripts/test-paid.sh` requiring `VSIR_ALLOW_PAID=1`; L5 manual canary `vsir eval corpus`; E2E Playwright `scripts/test-e2e.sh`.\n2. **L0–L3 and E2E must NEVER call Gemini.** They run in replay mode (D10): `VSIR_VLM=stub` + `VSIR_FIXTURE=<dir>`; a fixture miss is a typed `fixture_miss`, never a live call. **Only units marked SPEND PAID (U013, U020, U022, U026) may plan an L4 test, and it must be gated behind `VSIR_ALLOW_PAID=1`.**\n3. Before M2b the only fixture is `data/fixtures/synthetic_3window/` (produced by U007) plus M1's four hand-written synthetic pages (produced by U005) plus the ported legacy set (produced by U012). **No unit may plan a test that REQUIRES the real corpus (OQ-1) or an API key (OQ-2).** Name the fixture each test consumes and the unit that produces it.\n4. Acceptance criteria must be **executable assertions**, not prose. Write them as checkable statements with concrete values (e.g. \"`lookup(\\\"SF 1.1A\\\")` returns `total == 1` and `len(hits) == 1`\"), not \"lookup works correctly\".\n5. Plan the §12.5 conformance greps and the §15.1 probe behaviour as REAL tests: `/health` returns 200 while Qdrant is stopped, `/ready` returns 503, and a `SIGTERM` test for any unit that adds long-running work (U011, U025).\n6. Cover Error Cases as **typed 4xx per §7.3**: `read_page_cap_exceeded`, `fetch_budget_exceeded {limit, requested}`, `dpi_not_allowed`, `dpi_requires_region`, `filter_unknown_key {keys}`, `429 budget_exhausted`. Cover Degradation from §11.3: `503 qdrant_unavailable`, `503 vlm_unavailable`, boot refusals, never-an-empty-result, never-a-clamp.\n7. The §12.3 acceptance table assertions (exact strings): `lookup(\"SF 1.1A\")` → exactly 1 page; `lookup(\"SF 5.5b\")` → exactly 1; `lookup(\"SF 121.1\")` → 1; `lookup(\"EAO 84-5140.0020\")` → total 10, capped:true; `lookup(\"B&R X20SI4100\")` → total 54, capped:true at cap=20; `lookup(\"3\")` unscoped → weak:true, needs_scope:true at ANY cap; `lookup(\"alarm 152\")` → not_found + next.suggest:[\"skim_pages\"]; `verify(\"SF 1.1A\", [p008])` → absent; scanned document → not_searchable never not_found; PARITY: every identifier the old `entity_keys` gate accepted is still findable by phrase, and every raw in `withheld.jsonl` is NOT findable in `text` (only via `include_unverified`).\n8. §12.4 L3: `near_misses(n=100)` mutates one character of codes taken from the observed-token inventory of whatever corpus is indexed; asserts `r.hits == []`, `r.status in (\"not_found\",\"not_searchable\")`, and no `present_instead` value equals the fake. It runs in CI on every commit **from M1 onward**.\n9. Note in the unit's Notes when the `impl/pipeline-guide/NN-*.md` for the ported step documents **superseded** behaviour: step 07 (`06-derivation-and-gate.md` — the deleted allowlist gate), step 10 (`09-indexing.md` — `entity_keys`), step 11 (`10-gates-and-publish.md` — `allowlist`/`class_totality`), step 12 (`11-export.md` — `withheld.jsonl`). Units U009, U010, U011 must carry this note.\n\n## Output format — one block per unit, all 26, in order\n### Synthesis Agent 3: Test Strategy\n\nUnit ID: U001\nTest Levels: [L0, conformance]\nSuites / Commands: `bash scripts/test-unit.sh -k <selector>` (give a real, specific -k selector per unit)\nTest Coverage:\n- Happy Path: <named tests>\n- Edge Cases: <named tests>\n- Error Cases (typed 4xx per §7.3): <named tests, or \"N/A — this unit exposes no caller-facing bound\">\n- Degradation (§11.3): <named tests, or N/A>\nTest Data: Fixtures <path, produced by U0xx> | Stubs <stub VLM / ephemeral Qdrant / none>\nNotes: <superseded-guide warnings, replay-mode notes, OQ fallbacks — omit the line if there are none>\nAcceptance Criteria (Testable):\n- [ ] <executable assertion with concrete values>\n- [ ] <…>\n\n---\n\nEnd with:\n\nCross-Cutting Test Obligations:\n- Conformance greps (§12.5): owned by <unit>, re-run by every unit's Definition of Done\n- L3 abstention eval in CI from M1: owned by <unit>, extended by <units>\n- Probe behaviour (§15.1): owned by <unit>\n- SIGTERM: owned by <units>\n- Fixture producers: <fixture path → producing unit>, for all fixtures\n- Units planning an L4 test: <must be exactly U013, U020, U022, U026 or a subset>\n","agentId":"a7c48b981be064d66","agentType":"general-purpose","harnessNoteCount":0,"harnessTailCount":0,"harnessSectionHash":"a67765cf886cfa0a","content":[{"type":"text","text":"### Synthesis Agent 3: Test Strategy\n\nUnit ID: U001\nTest Levels: [L0, conformance]\nSuites / Commands: `bash scripts/test-unit.sh -k \"doctor or boot_refusal or json_logs or sigterm_boot\"`\nTest Coverage:\n- Happy Path: `test_doctor_exits_zero_on_valid_env`, `test_json_logs_parse_and_contain_release_id`\n- Edge Cases: `test_sigterm_during_boot_clean_exit`\n- Error Cases (typed 4xx per §7.3): N/A — this unit exposes no caller-facing bound\n- Degradation (§11.3): `test_boot_refuses_model_id_ending_latest`\nTest Data: Fixtures none (pure skeleton) | Stubs none\nNotes: conformance greps themselves are owned by U002; this unit's Definition of Done re-runs them.\nAcceptance Criteria (Testable):\n- [ ] `vsir doctor` exits 0 with a valid `.env` and exits nonzero with `GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-1.5-pro-latest`, printing a message naming `model id ends in -latest`\n- [ ] every log line emitted at startup parses via `json.loads` and contains `release_id` and `level` keys\n- [ ] a `SIGTERM` sent to the process during startup produces exit code 0 within 5s and leaves no orphan process\n\n---\n\nUnit ID: U002\nTest Levels: [L2, conformance]\nSuites / Commands: `bash scripts/test-api.sh -k \"health or ready or conformance_grep\"`\nTest Coverage:\n- Happy Path: `test_health_200_qdrant_up`, `test_ready_200_qdrant_up`\n- Edge Cases: `test_health_200_while_qdrant_stopped` (§15.1 probe split)\n- Error Cases (typed 4xx per §7.3): N/A — no caller-bound endpoints beyond health/ready at this unit\n- Degradation (§11.3): `test_ready_503_qdrant_unavailable_while_health_green`\nTest Data: Fixtures none (infra) | Stubs ephemeral Qdrant (docker-compose.test.yml)\nNotes: This unit owns the §12.5 conformance greps and the §15.1 probe-split behaviour; every later unit's Definition of Done re-runs the grep suite.\nAcceptance Criteria (Testable):\n- [ ] with the Qdrant container running, `GET /health` → 200 and `GET /ready` → 200\n- [ ] with the Qdrant container stopped (`docker stop`), `GET /health` still returns 200 and `GET /ready` returns 503 with body containing `qdrant_unavailable`\n- [ ] `scripts/test-unit.sh`, `scripts/test-api.sh`, `scripts/test-e2e.sh`, `scripts/test-paid.sh` all exist and are executable; `scripts/test-paid.sh` skips/exits nonzero when `VSIR_ALLOW_PAID` is unset\n- [ ] injecting `entity_keys` into a scratch file under `backend/vsir/serve/` makes the conformance grep fail; removing it makes the grep pass\n- [ ] the conformance grep test excludes its own source file from the scan (does not fail on its own banned-string list)\n\n---\n\nUnit ID: U003\nTest Levels: [L0, L2]\nSuites / Commands: `bash scripts/test-unit.sh -k \"ids or record\"` ; `bash scripts/test-api.sh -k \"indexed_collection\"`\nTest Coverage:\n- Happy Path: `test_ids_deterministic`, `test_record_roundtrip`, `test_collection_has_text_index`\n- Edge Cases: `test_ids_differ_by_page_no`, `test_record_normalizes_empty_text`\n- Error Cases (typed 4xx per §7.3): N/A — this unit exposes no caller-facing bound\n- Degradation (§11.3): N/A — the `index schema ≠ INDEXED → refuse to serve` refusal is enforced and tested at U014's boot path; U003 only defines the schema value it checks against\nTest Data: Fixtures none (ad hoc records built in-test) | Stubs ephemeral Qdrant (collection-creation portion only)\nAcceptance Criteria (Testable):\n- [ ] `ids.page_id(doc_id, page_no)` returns the same string across two calls with identical inputs, and a different string when `page_no` differs\n- [ ] `core.indexed.create_collection()` creates a Qdrant collection whose payload schema includes a full-text index on the `text` field (I6)\n- [ ] `record.PageRecord(**minimal_kwargs).to_payload()` then `.from_payload()` round-trips with no field loss\n\n---\n\nUnit ID: U004\nTest Levels: [L0]\nSuites / Commands: `bash scripts/test-unit.sh -k \"tok or variants or exact or status or envelope or caps or rrf\"`\nTest Coverage:\n- Happy Path: `test_tok_splits_alphanumeric_codes`, `test_variants_compact_label`, `test_status_enum_has_six_values`, `test_envelope_family_a_and_b_shapes`, `test_rrf_matches_hand_computed_fusion`\n- Edge Cases: `test_tok_handles_br_x20si4100_punctuation`, `test_cap_validator_boundary_at_exactly_cap`\n- Error Cases (typed 4xx per §7.3): `test_read_page_cap_exceeded_at_4_pages`, `test_fetch_budget_exceeded_payload_shape`, `test_dpi_not_allowed_for_100`, `test_dpi_requires_region_above_220`, `test_filter_unknown_key_lists_offending_keys`\n- Degradation (§11.3): N/A — the 429 quota logic itself lives in `serve/budget.py` (U014); this unit only supplies the pure validators\nTest Data: Fixtures none (pure) | Stubs none\nAcceptance Criteria (Testable):\n- [ ] `len(list(core.status.Status)) == 6`\n- [ ] `envelope.family_a(hits=[...])` and `envelope.family_b(hit=...)` produce distinct top-level shapes, both containing `reads_remaining`\n- [ ] cap validator raises `read_page_cap_exceeded` at `pages=4` and passes at `pages=3`\n- [ ] cap validator raises `fetch_budget_exceeded {limit, requested}` with `requested==6, limit==5` when 6 pages requested (limit 5)\n- [ ] cap validator raises `dpi_not_allowed` for `dpi=100` and passes for `dpi=150`\n- [ ] cap validator raises `dpi_requires_region` for `dpi=300, region=None` and passes for `dpi=300, region={...}`\n- [ ] cap validator raises `filter_unknown_key {keys}` for `scope={\"bogus_key\": 1}` with `keys==[\"bogus_key\"]`\n- [ ] `rrf([rank_list_a, rank_list_b], k=60)` matches a hand-computed `1/(k+rank)` sum for a fixed pair of rank lists\n\n---\n\nUnit ID: U005\nTest Levels: [L0, L1]\nSuites / Commands: `bash scripts/test-unit.sh -k \"lookup_exact or observed_token_inventory or demo_exact\"`\nTest Coverage:\n- Happy Path: `test_lookup_sf_1_1a_single_hit`, `test_demo_exact_synthetic_cli`\n- Edge Cases: `test_lookup_mutated_code_not_found`\n- Error Cases (typed 4xx per §7.3): N/A — pure function, no HTTP bound yet (wrapped in U015)\n- Degradation (§11.3): N/A — `not_searchable` handling requires scanned-page semantics introduced later; deferred\nTest Data: Fixtures `data/fixtures/synthetic_pages/` (four hand-written pages, produced by U005 itself) | Stubs none\nNotes: This unit produces the observed-token inventory that U006's `near_misses()` and the CI L3 eval consume from M1 onward (rule 8).\nAcceptance Criteria (Testable):\n- [ ] `lookup(\"SF 1.1A\")` against the four hand-written pages returns `total == 1` and `len(hits) == 1`\n- [ ] `lookup(<one-char mutation of a real fixture code>)` returns `hits == []` and `status == \"not_found\"`\n- [ ] the observed-token inventory extracted from the four pages contains every code embedded in the fixture text\n- [ ] `vsir demo exact --synthetic` exits 0 and prints at least one exact match referencing a known fixture code\n\n---\n\nUnit ID: U006\nTest Levels: [L0, L3]\nSuites / Commands: `bash scripts/test-unit.sh -k \"verify_claims or near_misses\"` ; `bash scripts/test-api.sh -k \"test_near_miss_codes_never_answer\"`\nTest Coverage:\n- Happy Path: `test_verify_claims_absent_when_tokens_present_phrase_not`\n- Edge Cases: `test_near_misses_returns_exactly_100_one_char_off`\n- Error Cases (typed 4xx per §7.3): N/A — this unit exposes no caller-facing bound\n- Degradation (§11.3): N/A — replay-safe by construction (near_misses derives purely from the local inventory, never calls Gemini)\nTest Data: Fixtures `data/fixtures/synthetic_pages/` (from U005) | Stubs none\nNotes: This is the unit that stands up the §12.4 L3 abstention eval in CI from M1 onward, per rule 8.\nAcceptance Criteria (Testable):\n- [ ] `verify_claims(\"SF 1.1A\", pages=[p008])` returns `status == \"absent\"` when the tokens exist on p008 but not as the contiguous phrase\n- [ ] `len(near_misses(n=100)) == 100` and every element differs from its source code by exactly one character\n- [ ] `test_near_miss_codes_never_answer` (verbatim from §12.4): for each of 100 near-misses, `lookup(fake).hits == []`, `status in (\"not_found\",\"not_searchable\")`, and no `present_instead` value `== fake`\n- [ ] this L3 test runs in `scripts/test-api.sh`, against the M1 synthetic-pages fixture, and is wired into CI to run on every commit from M1 onward\n\n---\n\nUnit ID: U007\nTest Levels: [L0, L1]\nSuites / Commands: `bash scripts/test-unit.sh -k \"manifest or probe or render or window_bisect or off_by_one or crop_trap\"`\nTest Coverage:\n- Happy Path: `test_manifest_page_count`, `test_window_bisect_returns_3_windows`\n- Edge Cases: `test_off_by_one_trap_page_text_matches_correct_page`, `test_crop_trap_page_not_split_across_windows`\n- Error Cases (typed 4xx per §7.3): N/A — this unit exposes no caller-facing bound\n- Degradation (§11.3): N/A\nTest Data: Fixtures `data/source/synthetic_3window.pdf` → `data/fixtures/synthetic_3window/` (produced by U007 itself) | Stubs none (pure PDF processing)\nAcceptance Criteria (Testable):\n- [ ] `manifest.build(synthetic_3window.pdf).page_count` matches the fixture's known page count\n- [ ] on the off-by-one trap page, `probe.get_text(pdf, page_no=K)` returns the marker string unique to page K, not K±1\n- [ ] on the crop trap page, `window.bisect(manifest)` keeps the trap page's content whole inside a single window (never splits its region)\n- [ ] `window.bisect(...)` returns exactly 3 windows for `synthetic_3window.pdf`\n- [ ] conformance grep confirms `get_text(` appears only inside `ingest/probe.py` within `backend/vsir/**`\n\n---\n\nUnit ID: U008\nTest Levels: [L0, L1]\nSuites / Commands: `bash scripts/test-unit.sh -k \"vlm_stub or vlm_cache or fixture_miss or extract\"`\nTest Coverage:\n- Happy Path: `test_extract_s1_from_fixture_zero_network_calls`, `test_cache_memoizes_by_key`\n- Edge Cases: `test_prompts_s1_s2_non_empty_and_selected_deterministically`\n- Error Cases (typed 4xx per §7.3): N/A — `fixture_miss` is an internal typed replay-mode signal, not a caller-facing HTTP 4xx\n- Degradation (§11.3): N/A here — the caller-facing `503 vlm_unavailable` behaviour is tested at U014/U015; this unit defines the exception type those higher units catch\nTest Data: Fixtures `data/fixtures/synthetic_3window/` (from U007) | Stubs stub VLM (`VSIR_VLM=stub`)\nNotes: replay-mode enforcement point for D10 — a fixture miss must raise typed `fixture_miss`, never fall back to a live call.\nAcceptance Criteria (Testable):\n- [ ] with `VSIR_VLM=stub, VSIR_FIXTURE=data/fixtures/synthetic_3window`, `extract.run_s1(window_1)` is built purely from fixture JSON and a spy on the stub client shows zero HTTP calls made\n- [ ] requesting a cache key absent from the fixture dir raises typed `fixture_miss` (assert exception type), and no network call is attempted\n- [ ] `vlm/cache.py` returns the identical object for two calls with the same cache key\n- [ ] `prompts/s1.md` and `prompts/s2.md` load non-empty, and `extract.py` selects between them deterministically by window/page role\n\n---\n\nUnit ID: U009\nTest Levels: [L0, L1]\nSuites / Commands: `bash scripts/test-unit.sh -k \"derive_grounded_rate or health or label_precedence or reattribution or stitch\"`\nTest Coverage:\n- Happy Path: `test_grounded_rate_median_over_has_text_pages`, `test_label_precedence_deterministic`\n- Edge Cases: `test_stitch_reattributes_code_split_across_crop_trap_boundary`, `test_label_conflict_flag_on_non_monotonic_sequence`\n- Error Cases (typed 4xx per §7.3): N/A — this unit exposes no caller-facing bound\n- Degradation (§11.3): N/A — `derive.py` computes metrics only; gating is entirely U011's responsibility\nTest Data: Fixtures `data/fixtures/synthetic_3window/` (U007), `raw_window_*.json` | Stubs none (pure L1 derivation)\nNotes: **Superseded guide warning** — `impl/pipeline-guide/06-derivation-and-gate.md` (step 07) documents the deleted allowlist gate. This codebase's `derive.py` computes `grounded_rate` with **no gate**; gating moved entirely to U011's `ingest/gates.py`. Do not resurrect allowlist logic from that guide.\nAcceptance Criteria (Testable):\n- [ ] `derive.grounded_rate(pages)` returns the median grounded-token ratio over exactly the pages where `has_text==True`, excluding scanned pages from the denominator\n- [ ] calling `derive.py` never raises or blocks regardless of the computed rate (assert no exception even when rate == 0.0) — confirming it carries no gate\n- [ ] a code whose evidence spans the U007 crop-trap boundary is reattributed by `stitch.py` to exactly one page\n- [ ] `label_precedence` resolves two conflicting printed labels for the same page identically across repeated runs\n- [ ] a non-monotonic label sequence sets `core.health`'s `label_conflict == True`\n\n---\n\nUnit ID: U010\nTest Levels: [L0, L1, L2]\nSuites / Commands: `bash scripts/test-unit.sh -k \"embed or fingerprint or sparse_surface\"` ; `bash scripts/test-api.sh -k \"index_is_current_false or fingerprint_refusal\"`\nTest Coverage:\n- Happy Path: `test_embed_interleaved_order_matches_pages`, `test_fingerprint_deterministic`, `test_index_upsert_is_current_false`\n- Edge Cases: `test_sparse_caption_surface_contains_known_tokens`\n- Error Cases (typed 4xx per §7.3): N/A — this unit exposes no caller-facing bound\n- Degradation (§11.3): `test_fingerprint_mismatch_refuses_upsert_and_realiases`\nTest Data: Fixtures `data/fixtures/synthetic_3window/` (U007) | Stubs ephemeral Qdrant (L2 portion), stub VLM for derived text inputs\nNotes: **Superseded guide warning** — `impl/pipeline-guide/09-indexing.md` (step 10) documents the old `entity_keys` field. That field is gone; `ingest/index.py` indexes via the phrase/text index (I2) and code payload fields only.\nAcceptance Criteria (Testable):\n- [ ] every point upserted by `ingest/index.py` for a newly-ingested document has payload `is_current == False`\n- [ ] `fingerprint(embedding_model, schema_version)` is identical across two calls with identical inputs and differs when `embedding_model` changes\n- [ ] upserting into a collection whose stored fingerprint differs from the current fingerprint raises a refusal, never silently upserts, and selects a new collection name distinct from the stale one\n- [ ] `embed.py`'s interleaved (D4) output list index `i` corresponds to `pages[i]` for the 3-window synthetic fixture\n- [ ] a page's sparse lexical/caption surface contains that page's known caption tokens (fixture-known substring match)\n\n---\n\nUnit ID: U011\nTest Levels: [L0, L1, L2, conformance]\nSuites / Commands: `bash scripts/test-unit.sh -k \"gates or export_pure\"` ; `bash scripts/test-api.sh -k \"publish_atomic or grounded_rate_gate or scanned_skip or lease or sigterm_publish or runs_show or gates_rerun\"`\nTest Coverage:\n- Happy Path: `test_window_coverage_blocks_below_1_0`, `test_offset_check_blocks_failing_window`, `test_publish_override_flags_pages`, `test_runs_show_prints_run_record`, `test_gates_rerun_no_new_vlm_calls`\n- Edge Cases: `test_scanned_doc_skips_grounded_rate_gate_publishes_not_searchable`, `test_label_monotonic_flags_without_blocking`, `test_three_clause_retirement_isolated_evaluation`\n- Error Cases (typed 4xx per §7.3): N/A — gates/publish are ingest-side operations, not the query API's caller-facing bound\n- Degradation (§11.3): `test_sigterm_mid_publish_checkpoints_resumable`, `test_lease_prevents_double_run_same_doc_id`\nTest Data: Fixtures `data/fixtures/synthetic_3window/` (U007) plus derived outputs from U009/U010 | Stubs ephemeral Qdrant (`vsir_runs` control collection)\nNotes: **Superseded guide warnings** — `impl/pipeline-guide/10-gates-and-publish.md` (step 11) documents deleted `allowlist`/`class_totality` gates; only `window_coverage`, `offset_check`, `grounded_rate`, `text_coverage`, `label_monotonic` (§11.1) exist here. `impl/pipeline-guide/11-export.md` (step 12) documents the old `withheld.jsonl` shape; this unit's `ingest/export.py` semantics differ (see U012/U013 parity notes) — do not port that shape verbatim.\nAcceptance Criteria (Testable):\n- [ ] a document with `window_coverage < 1.0` after retries is blocked; run record shows `status=\"blocked\", gate=\"window_coverage\"`\n- [ ] a document with any window failing `offset_check` (I4) is blocked, naming the failing window\n- [ ] `grounded_rate == 0.75` (below the provisional 0.8 threshold) blocks publish and lists worst pages; `vsir publish --override grounded_rate --reason \"test\"` then publishes with every page flagged `published_with_override == True`\n- [ ] a fully-scanned document (`text_coverage == 0.0`) publishes without ever evaluating `grounded_rate`, and its pages resolve `not_searchable` (never quarantined)\n- [ ] a non-monotonic label sequence publishes successfully with `label_conflict == True` set (flag, not block)\n- [ ] publish is atomic: forcing a mid-publish failure leaves zero pages with `is_current=True` for that document\n- [ ] acquiring a `vsir_runs` lease for `doc_id=X` while another lease is held for the same `doc_id` blocks/raises\n- [ ] `vsir runs show <run_id>` prints the run record including gate results and override reason when present\n- [ ] `vsir gates rerun <doc_id>` leaves the stub VLM call count unchanged before/after rerun\n- [ ] `SIGTERM` sent mid-publish/export leaves a per-window checkpoint; a subsequent run skips already-completed windows (assert stub VLM call count for those windows does not increase)\n\n---\n\nUnit ID: U012\nTest Levels: [L1, L2]\nSuites / Commands: `bash scripts/test-unit.sh -k \"legacy_port_byte_identical\"` ; `bash scripts/test-api.sh -k \"parity_labels or 