ion, the generated synthetic_3window.pdf with an off-by-one trap and a crop trap) · U008 (vlm client/cache/stub, prompts, ingest/extract.py, replay mode, the four cache keys) · U009 (derive, core/health.py grounded_rate, label precedence, code reattribution + moved_from, stitch + series_id) · U010 (embed D4 interleaved, lexical + captions sparse, §6.6 fingerprint, index with is_current=False) · U011 (gates §11.1, publish, the three-clause retirement, vsir_runs + advisory lease, export §6.8, run record §6.9, `vsir runs show`/`gates rerun`/`publish --override`)\nM2b: U012 (port the impl fixtures + the parity and negative-set L2 suite) · U013 (the one real paid TC1E-SF ingest, freeze the fixtures, set the grounded_rate threshold)\nM3: U014 (serve/app.py, bearer auth, the audit line, budget, `vsir serve`, §11.3 degradation) · U015 (lookup + verify HTTP wrappers, the six-value status end to end, next.suggest, unverified_hits, mcp/server.py, `vsir lookup`/`verify`/`mcp`) · U016 (`vsir eval acceptance` + `vsir eval abstention`)\nM4: U017 (skim_pages, RRF ordering, decompose, exclude, next affordances, image queries, resolve) · U018 (GET /pages/{page_id}/image, the raster LRU cache, fetch, the §7.3 caps, `vsir demo narrow`)\nM5: U019 (skim_documents + skim_sections + searchable_ratio) · U020 (read: stamps, sufficient, page_provenance, the ≤3-page cap, the question-keyed read_key cache)\nM6: U021 (runner triage tri-state + routing + prompt) · U022 (runner loop, the six correction loops, the server-side answer gate, abstention wording, POST /ask, `vsir ask`)\nM7: U023 (the two-zone console) · U024 (the Playwright E2E replay suite)\nM8: U025 (is_current lifecycle, found_only_in_superseded, series_id, --resume + checkpoints, SIGTERM checkpointing, `vsir retire`) · U026 (`vsir eval corpus`, the §12.6 report with the D11 gates)\n\n## Proposed assignment to verify\nI1→U011 · I2→U005 · I3→U004 · I4→U011 · I5→U004 · I6→U003 · I7→U011 · I8→U022\nF1→U005 · F2→U006(core)+U015(tool) · F3→U005 · F4→U011(M2a)+U015(M3) · F5→U009(M2a)+U017(M4) · F6→U009 · F7→U011 · F8→U009(stitching)+U017(stateless scope)+U025(series_id) · F9→U025 · F10→U004 · F11→U001(boot)+U008(key) · F12→U011(M2a)+U025(revision half) · F13→U007 · F14→U005 · F15→U007 · F16→U006 · F17→U011 · F18→U018(fetch)+U020(read) · F19→U020\n\n## Your task\nFor EVERY invariant I1–I8 and EVERY failure row F1–F19: confirm the owning unit, confirm its milestone matches the spec's \"Asserted from\" / \"Closed at\" column, name the concrete mechanical assertion that enforces it, and name the concrete test (test function name + level) that proves it. Then do the same for every conformance grep. Then report anything uncovered — an uncovered row is a BLOCKER.\n\nOutput EXACTLY this format:\n\n### Synthesis Agent 6: Invariant & Failure Coverage\n\nOwnership Verification Against The Spec:\n- <any mismatch between the proposed assignment's milestone and the spec's column, or \"All 8 invariants and all 19 failure rows are assigned to a unit whose milestone matches the spec column.\">\n\nInvariants:\n- I1 → owned by [U0xx] → milestone <Mx> matches Spec §9 \"Asserted from\" <Mx> ✓/✗ → enforced by <the concrete mechanical assertion> → tested by <test_function_name> (<level>)\n- (repeat for I1–I8; every row must have an owner and a test)\n\nFailure Rows:\n- F1 → owned by [U0xx] → milestone <Mx> matches Spec §10 \"Closed at\" <Mx> ✓/✗ → guard <name of the guard mechanism> → test <test_function_name> (<level>)\n- (repeat for F1–F19; for split rows give one line PER PART, each with its own owning unit, guard and test)\n\nConformance Greps (Spec §12.5):\n- <the exact banned pattern> → owned by [U0xx] → scope <the paths scanned and the exclusions> → test <test_function_name>\n(one line per banned pattern, including the cloud-native set)\n\nPublish Gates (Spec §11.1) — each needs an owner and a test:\n- <gate> → owned by [U0xx] → block-or-flag → test <test_function_name> (<level>)\n\nDegradation Rows (Spec §11.3) — each needs an owner and a test:\n- <condition> → owned by [U0xx] → behaviour → test <test_function_name> (<level>)\n\nUncovered:\n- <any I, F, grep, gate or degradation row with no owner or no test — a BLOCKER that must be resolved before the plan is written. Write \"None.\" if the safety net is complete.>\n\nCoverage Warnings (not blockers, but the plan must state them):\n- <e.g. a row whose only proof is a paid L4 test and therefore cannot be demonstrated until OQ-2 is answered; a row proved only on synthetic data until M2b>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01Kj9Qq7A69jyPbw6wPfVug3","session_id":"4eefb16f-3989-4441-9cd3-d294cfccb11f","uuid":"33a6de69-91f6-4011-92d7-4b884240cd6b","timestamp":"2026-09-09T17:14:33.799Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Invariant and failure coverage"}
