)\n- F18 (M4, fetch) → owned by [U018] → milestone M4 matches Spec §10 \"Closed at\" M4(fetch) ✓ → guard §7.3 caps on `fetch`, typed 400 naming the bound → test `test_fetch_over_budget_returns_typed_400` (L1)\n- F18 (M5, read) → owned by [U020] → milestone M5 matches Spec §10 \"Closed at\" M5(read) ✓ → guard §7.3 caps on `read` (≤3-page), typed 400 → test `test_read_over_page_cap_returns_typed_400` (L1)\n- F19 → owned by [U020] → milestone M5 matches Spec §10 \"Closed at\" M5 ✓ → guard `read_key` includes the question → test `test_read_key_includes_question_cache_miss_on_new_question` (L1)\n\nConformance Greps (Spec §12.5):\n- `MatchText`/`MatchTextAny` under `serve/` → owned by [U002] → scope `backend/vsir/serve/**`, excludes markdown and the conformance test itself → test `test_no_matchtext_in_serve` (L1)\n- any fuzzy/similarity/edit-distance library in `requirements*.txt` → owned by [U002] → scope `requirements*.txt` → test `test_no_fuzzy_lib_in_requirements` (L1)\n- any field named `score` in a response model → owned by [U002] → scope `backend/vsir/**` → test `test_no_score_field_in_response_models` (L1)\n- a model id ending `-latest` → owned by [U002] → scope `backend/vsir/**` → test `test_no_latest_model_id_in_source` (L1)\n- `alembic` or `sqlalchemy` anywhere → owned by [U002] → scope `backend/vsir/**` + `requirements*.txt` → test `test_no_alembic_or_sqlalchemy` (L1)\n- `get_text(` outside `ingest/probe.py` → owned by [U002] → scope `backend/vsir/**`, excluding `ingest/probe.py` → test `test_get_text_only_in_probe` (L1)\n- struck legacy names `SCHEMA_CARD`, `IdClass`, `entity_keys`, `classify(` → owned by [U002] → scope `backend/vsir/**` → test `test_no_struck_legacy_names` (L1)\n- (cloud-native) no `logging.FileHandler` → owned by [U002] → scope `backend/vsir/**`, `Dockerfile*`, `docker-compose*.yml` → test `test_no_filehandler_logging` (L1)\n- (cloud-native) no container image tagged `latest` → owned by [U002] → scope `Dockerfile*`, `docker-compose*.yml` → test `test_no_latest_tagged_image` (L1)\n- (cloud-native) no credential literal (`api_key=`, `token=`, `Bearer ` + literal) → owned by [U002] → scope `backend/vsir/**`, `Dockerfile*`, `docker-compose*.yml` → test `test_no_credential_literals` (L1)\n- (cloud-native) no test-only branch (`if TESTING`, `if os.environ.get(\"TESTING\")`) → owned by [U002] → scope `backend/vsir/**` only → test `test_no_testing_only_branches` (L1)\n- (cloud-native) no `RetrievalState`-style module-level mutable session store (C11) → owned by [U002] → scope `backend/vsir/**`, `Dockerfile*`, `docker-compose*.yml` → test `test_no_retrievalstate_module_store` (L1)\n\nPublish Gates (Spec §11.1) — each needs an owner and a test:\n- `window_coverage` (must be 1.0 after retries) → owned by [U011] → block → test `test_publish_blocks_on_incomplete_window_coverage` (L2)\n- `offset_check` (all windows pass I4) → owned by [U011] → block → test `test_publish_blocks_on_offset_check_failure` (L2)\n- `grounded_rate` (≥0.8, provisional) → owned by [U011] → block, override recorded as `published_with_override` → test `test_publish_blocks_on_low_grounded_rate_and_override_flags_pages` (L2/L3 — threshold itself is only finalized once U013's M2b real-ingest distribution sets R4)\n- `text_coverage` → owned by [U011] (computed via U009's derive) → flag `mostly_scanned`, never block; at 0.0 skips `grounded_rate` entirely → test `test_fully_scanned_doc_skips_grounded_rate_gate` (L2)\n- `label_monotonic` → owned by [U011] (computed via U009's derive) → flag `label_conflict` → test `test_publish_flags_label_conflict_on_non_monotonic_labels` (L2)\n\nDegradation Rows (Spec §11.3) — each needs an owner and a test:\n- Qdrant unreachable → owned by [U014] → `503 qdrant_unavailable` retryable, never empty result; `/ready` red, `/health` green → test `test_qdrant_down_returns_503_ready_red_health_green` (L2)\n- Gemini unreachable → owned by [U020] (read path) using U008's vlm client → `503 vlm_unavailable` on `read`; free tools keep working → test `test_gemini_down_returns_503_on_read_free_tools_ok` (L2)\n- index schema ≠ `INDEXED` → owned by [U001] (boot/doctor refusal) → refuse to serve at boot → test `test_boot_refuses_serve_on_schema_mismatch` (L1) — ownership inferred, not explicit in the proposed assignment (see Coverage Warnings)\n- embedding model ≠ collection fingerprint → owned by [U010] (§6.6 fingerprint) → refuse to upsert; new collection + re-embed + alias swap → test `test_upsert_refused_on_fingerprint_mismatch_triggers_realias` (L2)\n- model id ends `-latest` → owned by [U001] → refuse to start → test `test_doctor_refuses_latest_model_alias` (L1, shared with F11 boot half)\n- a document's `grounded_rate` collapses → owned by [U009] (core/health.py) → `text_trust=\"untrusted\"`; pages unsearchable; `verify` → `unverifiable` → test `test_collapsed_grounded_rate_sets_text_trust_untrusted` (L2)\n- per-caller `read` quota exhausted → owned by [U020] → `429 budget_exhausted`, not silent truncation → test `test_read_quota_exhausted_returns_429` (L1)\n- over-budget `fetch` → owned by [U018] → typed 400 naming the bound, never a dpi clamp/truncation → test `test_fetch_over_budget_returns_typed_400_naming_bound` (L1, shared family with F18-fetch)\n\nUncovered:\n- None. Every invariant (I1–I8), every failure row and sub-part (F1–F19, including the three-way split F8 and two-way splits F2/F4/F5/F11/F18), every conformance grep (§12.5 core set + cloud-native set), every publish gate (§11.1), and every degradation row (§11.3) has a proposed owning unit and a named test above.\n\nCoverage Warnings (not blockers, but the plan must state them):\n- F12's extension to M8/U025 (\"revision half\") is asserted in the proposed-assignment text but is not present in the §10 table as I read it (`sed -n '1146,1229p'`), which shows F12 \"Closed at\" = `M2a` only. If §13 (out of my read scope) genuinely splits F12 across M8, the plan should cite that section explicitly rather than relying on an unverified cross-reference.\n- The `grounded_rate` publish-gate threshold (≥0.8) is explicitly \"provisional — set from the M2b distribution, R4\" (§11.1); `test_publish_blocks_on_low_grounded_rate_and_override_flags_pages` therefore cannot be finalized/demonstrated with a real threshold until U013's paid TC1E-SF ingest (M2b, L4) runs. Until then it is only meaningful against a placeholder threshold on synthetic data.\n- Several M2a-owned proofs (I4, F7, F13, F15) depend on U007's synthetic fixtures (`synthetic_3window.pdf`, crop fixture) and are not exercised against real scanned/production PDFs until U013 (M2b, paid, L4). Same caveat applies to I2/F1/F3/F14/F16, which rely on U005's four hand-written synthetic pages.\n- Test levels L1 (\"assertion\", per §12.5's own wording for I2) and L2/L3 (per the unit descriptions' \"L2 suite\" and \"L3 abstention eval\") are taken from the material given to me; the L4 tier used above for paid/real-data tests is this agent's own inference from U013's \"one real paid TC1E-SF ingest\" description — the spec sections I was scoped to read do not themselves define an \"L4\" label, so the plan should confirm or rename this tier explicitly.\n- Ownership for the three §11.3 degradation rows not covered by the proposed I/F assignment (Qdrant unreachable, Gemini unreachable, index-schema-mismatch-at-boot) was inferred by this agent from unit descriptions rather than verified against an existing assignment document — worth a second pass by whoever owns gate/degradation-row assignment specifically.\n- I8's proof (`test_answer_gate_rejects_unverified_claim`) sits at M6 and is inherently an end-to-end integration point across nearly every earlier milestone's guards (I1–I7); it cannot be meaningfully green until M1–M5 units are all in place, so it should not be treated as an early-milestone deliverable despite being a single named test.","usage":{"total_tokens":44169,"tool_uses":2,"duration_ms":194620},"uuid":"6d501a52-e0a3-49b9-bbfb-8feba2bb4859","session_id":"4eefb16f-3989-4441-9cd3-d294cfccb11f"}
