U022\nF1→U005 · F2→U006(core)+U015(tool) · F3→U005 · F4→U011(M2a)+U015(M3) · F5→U009(M2a)+U017(M4) · F6→U009 · F7→U011 · F8→U009(stitching)+U017(stateless scope)+U025(series_id) · F9→U025 · F10→U004 · F11→U001(boot)+U008(key) · F12→U011(M2a)+U025(revision half) · F13→U007 · F14→U005 · F15→U007 · F16→U006 · F17→U011 · F18→U018(fetch)+U020(read) · F19→U020\n\n## Your task\nFor EVERY invariant I1–I8 and EVERY failure row F1–F19: confirm the owning unit, confirm its milestone matches the spec's \"Asserted from\" / \"Closed at\" column, name the concrete mechanical assertion that enforces it, and name the concrete test (test function name + level) that proves it. Then do the same for every conformance grep. Then report anything uncovered — an uncovered row is a BLOCKER.\n\nOutput EXACTLY this format:\n\n### Synthesis Agent 6: Invariant & Failure Coverage\n\nOwnership Verification Against The Spec:\n- <any mismatch between the proposed assignment's milestone and the spec's column, or \"All 8 invariants and all 19 failure rows are assigned to a unit whose milestone matches the spec column.\">\n\nInvariants:\n- I1 → owned by [U0xx] → milestone <Mx> matches Spec §9 \"Asserted from\" <Mx> ✓/✗ → enforced by <the concrete mechanical assertion> → tested by <test_function_name> (<level>)\n- (repeat for I1–I8; every row must have an owner and a test)\n\nFailure Rows:\n- F1 → owned by [U0xx] → milestone <Mx> matches Spec §10 \"Closed at\" <Mx> ✓/✗ → guard <name of the guard mechanism> → test <test_function_name> (<level>)\n- (repeat for F1–F19; for split rows give one line PER PART, each with its own owning unit, guard and test)\n\nConformance Greps (Spec §12.5):\n- <the exact banned pattern> → owned by [U0xx] → scope <the paths scanned and the exclusions> → test <test_function_name>\n(one line per banned pattern, including the cloud-native set)\n\nPublish Gates (Spec §11.1) — each needs an owner and a test:\n- <gate> → owned by [U0xx] → block-or-flag → test <test_function_name> (<level>)\n\nDegradation Rows (Spec §11.3) — each needs an owner and a test:\n- <condition> → owned by [U0xx] → behaviour → test <test_function_name> (<level>)\n\nUncovered:\n- <any I, F, grep, gate or degradation row with no owner or no test — a BLOCKER that must be resolved before the plan is written. Write \"None.\" if the safety net is complete.>\n\nCoverage Warnings (not blockers, but the plan must state them):\n- <e.g. a row whose only proof is a paid L4 test and therefore cannot be demonstrated until OQ-2 is answered; a row proved only on synthetic data until M2b>\n","agentId":"a52d7f7610592e55f","agentType":"general-purpose","harnessNoteCount":0,"harnessTailCount":0,"harnessSectionHash":"bea155802f9e33b3","content":[{"type":"text","text":"### Synthesis Agent 6: Invariant & Failure Coverage\n\nOwnership Verification Against The Spec:\n- All 8 invariants match the spec §9 \"Asserted from\" column exactly (I1 M2a, I2 M1, I3 M1, I4 M2a, I5 M1, I6 M1, I7 M2a, I8 M6) and all 19 failure rows' milestone labels (including split parts) match the spec §10 \"Closed at\" column exactly — with one exception: **F12**. The proposed assignment text reads \"F12→U011(M2a)+U025(revision half) [+ M8 revision half per §13 M8]\", but the §10 table row I read (`sed -n '1146,1229p'`) shows F12's \"Closed at\" value as **`M2a` only** — no M8/§13 split appears in that row. The bracketed extension referencing §13 is not verifiable from the sections I was permitted to read; §13 itself was out of scope. This is not necessarily wrong (§13 may legitimately extend F12 to M8), but as read, the spec's own §10 table does not corroborate the M8 half of the F12 assignment. Flagging as a mismatch to resolve, not asserting it is false.\n\nInvariants:\n- I1 → owned by [U011] → milestone M2a matches Spec §9 \"Asserted from\" M2a ✓ → enforced by `point_id = uuid5(page_id)` + unique-`page_id` assert + `count(doc, rev) == pdf.page_count` post-publish → tested by `test_publish_page_count_and_unique_page_id` (L2, integration against test Qdrant)\n- I2 → owned by [U005] → milestone M1 matches Spec §9 \"Asserted from\" M1 ✓ → enforced by `probe.py` as sole writer of `text` (source-scan) + `lookup(\"K999\")` → `not_found` → tested by `test_lookup_hallucinated_code_not_found` (L1, unit); companion `test_record_text_matches_probe_text_only` per §12.5's literal wording (L1, U002's conformance module)\n- I3 → owned by [U004] → milestone M1 matches Spec §9 \"Asserted from\" M1 ✓ → enforced by one `exact_filter` + no `MatchText` in `serve/` + whitespace-only variant property → tested by `test_variants_whitespace_only_property` (L1, property-based unit test)\n- I4 → owned by [U011] → milestone M2a matches Spec §9 \"Asserted from\" M2a ✓ → enforced by §6.4's two independent offset checks; failure bisects and re-bills → tested by `test_offset_bisection_on_mismatch` (L2, integration using U007's synthetic_3window.pdf)\n- I5 → owned by [U004] → milestone M1 matches Spec §9 \"Asserted from\" M1 ✓ → enforced by the `SearchResponse` validator (Family A, §7.1) → tested by `test_search_response_never_bare_200_on_empty` (L1)\n- I6 → owned by [U003] → milestone M1 matches Spec §9 \"Asserted from\" M1 ✓ → enforced by one `INDEXED` dict, gates + boot assert → tested by `test_boot_asserts_indexed_fields_schema` (L1)\n- I7 → owned by [U011] → milestone M2a matches Spec §9 \"Asserted from\" M2a ✓ → enforced by `is_current=False` until gates pass, every tool injects `is_current=True` → tested by `test_unpublished_run_not_queryable` (L2, integration: interrupt then query)\n- I8 → owned by [U022] → milestone M6 matches Spec §9 \"Asserted from\" M6 ✓ → enforced by the answer gate, per `(claim, page)` → tested by `test_answer_gate_rejects_unverified_claim` (L3, runner-loop eval)\n\nFailure Rows:\n- F1 → owned by [U005] → milestone M1 matches Spec §10 \"Closed at\" M1 ✓ → guard I3 phrase-only `exact_filter` → test `test_lookup_sf_1_1a_returns_exactly_one` (L1)\n- F2 (core) → owned by [U006] → milestone M1 matches Spec §10 \"Closed at\" M1(core) ✓ → guard the one `exact_filter` in `verify_claims` → test `test_verify_claims_sf_1_1a_absent_on_p008` (L1)\n- F2 (tool) → owned by [U015] → milestone M3 matches Spec §10 \"Closed at\" M3(tool) ✓ → guard verify HTTP wrapper reuses the same `exact_filter`, no independent logic → test `test_verify_endpoint_returns_absent_for_uncited_page` (L2)\n- F3 → owned by [U005] → milestone M1 matches Spec §10 \"Closed at\" M1 ✓ → guard I3 variants (whitespace-only generation) → test `test_all_eight_compact_labels_found` (L1)\n- F4 (M2a) → owned by [U011] → milestone M2a matches Spec §10 \"Closed at\" M2a ✓ → guard `has_text` facet + I5 typed absence → test `test_scanned_doc_flagged_has_text_false` (L2)\n- F4 (M3) → owned by [U015] → milestone M3 matches Spec §10 \"Closed at\" M3 ✓ → guard lookup/verify tool surfaces `not_searchable` end-to-end → test `test_lookup_scanned_page_returns_not_searchable` (L2)\n- F5 (M2a) → owned by [U009] → milestone M2a matches Spec §10 \"Closed at\" M2a ✓ → guard label precedence + `label_verified` on derive → test `test_derive_flags_misread_label_ambiguous` (L2)\n- F5 (M4) → owned by [U017] → milestone M4 matches Spec §10 \"Closed at\" M4 ✓ → guard ambiguity resolves to a list, never a silent pick → test `test_resolve_ambiguous_label_returns_list` (L2)\n- F6 → owned by [U009] → milestone M2a matches Spec §10 \"Closed at\" M2a ✓ → guard per-page `grounded_rate` + reattribution + I8 → test `test_code_reattributed_records_moved_from` (L2)\n- F7 → owned by [U011] → milestone M2a matches Spec §10 \"Closed at\" M2a ✓ → guard I4 exercised on U007's synthetic_3window.pdf off-by-one trap → test `test_offset_check_catches_shifted_page_numbers` (L2)\n- F8 (M2a, stitching) → owned by [U009] → milestone M2a matches Spec §10 \"Closed at\" M2a ✓ → guard canonical section key + carry-in stitching → test `test_stitch_straddling_section_single_key` (L2)\n- F8 (M4, stateless scope) → owned by [U017] → milestone M4 matc