s\n\n| AC | Units | Named test(s) | Level |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| AC-001 | U006, U015 | `test_verify.py::test_claimed_code_absent_from_text_is_unfindable`; `test_lookup_api.py::test_unverified_hits_opt_in_only` | L0 + L2 |\n| AC-002 | U004 | `test_variants.py::test_exact_variant_differs_only_by_whitespace` | L0 |\n| AC-003 | U004 | `test_status.py::test_status_enum_has_six_values`; `test_envelope.py::test_family_a_never_returns_empty_ok` | L0 + conformance |\n| AC-004 | U004, U009, U005 | `test_lookup.py::test_scanned_page_returns_not_searchable_not_not_found` | L0 + L1 |\n| AC-005 | U006, U020 | `test_verify.py::test_present_absent_unverifiable_per_claim_page`; `test_verify.py::test_near_miss_labelled_different_part` | L0 + L3 |\n| AC-006 | U007 | `test_window.py::test_offset_proof_bisects_on_mismatch` (synthetic_3window.pdf off-by-one trap) | L1 |\n| AC-007 | U011 | `test_gates.py::test_unpublished_run_has_zero_queryable_pages`; `test-api.sh::gates_rerun_then_publish_flow` | L0 + L2 |\n| AC-008 | U004, U018 | `test_caps.py::test_every_cap_is_typed_400_naming_bound`; `test_fetch_api.py::test_region_dpi_cap_no_silent_clamp` | L0 + L2 |\n| AC-009 | U022 | `test-api.sh::ask_worked_trace_fixture_costs_one_paid_read_with_citations` (frozen worked-trace fixture, `VSIR_READS_PER_QUESTION` ceiling) | L2 (fixture-backed — see Part D) |\n| AC-010 | U022 | `test_answer.py::test_abstention_states_coverage_never_claims_absence_with_unread_image_pages` | L3 |\n| AC-011 | U006, U016 | `test-unit.sh::l3_abstention_eval_100_near_miss_codes` (gated in CI on every commit) | L3 |\n| AC-012 | U001 | `test_doctor.py::test_refuses_on_schema_drift`; `test_refuses_on_fingerprint_mismatch`; `test_refuses_on_latest_model_id` | L0 |\n| AC-013 | U011 | `test_export.py::test_labels_jsonl_has_codes_range_sections_summaries_safety_flag` | L0 + L1 |\n| AC-014 | U001/U002 (M0), U005 (M1), U007/U011 (M2a), U013 (M2b), U015 (M3), U018 (M4), U020 (M5), U021/U022 (M6), U023/U024 (M7), U025/U026 (M8) | M0: `vsir doctor` + `scripts/test-unit.sh`; M1: `vsir demo exact --synthetic`; M2a: stub-ingest-and-publish demo (`vsir runs show`); M2b: real TC1E-SF ingest demo; M3: `vsir lookup`/`vsir verify`/`vsir mcp`; M4: `vsir demo narrow`; M5: read demo over frozen fixture; M6: `vsir ask --explain`; M7: console + `scripts/test-e2e.sh`; M8: `vsir retire <doc_id>` + `vsir eval corpus` | L0–L2 (M0,M1,M3,M4,M7); L1/L2 (M5,M6,M8); **L4** (M2b — paid) |\n| AC-015 | U001, U014 | `test-unit.sh::conformance_single_image_all_process_types`; `test_config.py::test_all_deployment_values_from_env_no_local_disk_state` | conformance |\n| AC-016 | U025, U002 | `test_ingest_resume.py::test_sigterm_mid_window_then_resume_completes_no_partial_document`; `test_health_ready.py::test_health_ready_during_qdrant_outage` | L1 + L2 |\n\n#### D. Unmapped items\n\n- **Spec sections with no unit:** none — every section maps to ≥1 unit above (several via a rationale-carrier note rather than direct implementation: §0, §1.3, §2.1, §2.2, §2.5, §16, §17, §19, §20, §20.1).\n- **Units with no spec section:** none — all 26 units have an explicit primary section in Table B.\n- **ACs with no unit or no test:** none — all sixteen have at least one unit and one named test in Table C.\n- **ACs whose only coverage is a paid (L4/L5) test:** **AC-014**, specifically its M2b-milestone demo command. M2b's entire purpose is \"the one real paid TC1E-SF ingest\" (U013) — there is no fixture-backed substitute for demonstrating that milestone's demo command green on a clean checkout without paid spend, so this slice of AC-014 is provable only at L4 and is blocked on the same OQ-2 cost/budget question implicit in U013's DoD. **AC-009** is a secondary, softer instance of the same risk: its CI-repeatable test runs at L2 against the frozen worked-trace fixture, but that fixture's fidelity (and therefore AC-009's ultimate truth about real paid-read cost) traces back to the same one-time paid calibration performed in U013/M2b — worth flagging even though a deterministic L2 proxy exists today."},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: a537a0ddada603798 (use SendMessage with to: 'a537a0ddada603798', summary: '<5-10 word recap>' to continue this agent)\n<usage>subagent_tokens: 52447\ntool_uses: 1\nduration_ms: 244351</usage>"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4eefb16f-3989-4441-9cd3-d294cfccb11f","uuid":"d0f0f64f-d5d8-4322-b317-fbc0e1b49dec","timestamp":"2026-09-09T17:18:08.488Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"You are Synthesis Agent S5 (traceability matrix) for a PLAN-ONLY planning task. DO NOT WRITE FILES. DO NOT IMPLEMENT CODE. Output the matrix as your final message only.\n\nSpec: `development/cr1/spec/spec.md` in /Users/sabesonk/Documents/DILMAH/dilmah-engineering-solutioning/poc/vision_segmentation_index_and_retrieval. The section list below is complete — you do not need to read the spec, but you MAY run one `grep -n \"^## \\|^### \" <spec>` to confirm section numbering.\n\n## The 26 units (authoritative)\n- U001 M0 Runtime skeleton, pins/lock, Dockerfile, `.env.example` (all §15 Factor III vars), JSON logs to stdout, SIGTERM handler, release_id stamping, `vsir` CLI, `vsir doctor` (§4.3)\n- U002 M0 docker-compose.test.yml→Qdrant, `GET /health` + `GET /ready`, scripts/test-{unit,api,e2e,paid}.sh, §12.5 conformance greps as a test, AGENTS.md\n- U003 M1 core/record.py, core/ids.py, core/indexed.py, Qdrant collection + text-index creation (§5.5)\n- U004 M1 core/tok.py, core/variants.py, core/exact.py, core/status.py (six-value enum), serve/envelope.py (Family A + Family B, hit models, ImageRef/Preview), §7.3 cap validators, ports ingest/sparse.py + rrf()\n- U005 M1 four hand-written synthetic pages, serve/tools/lookup.py pure function, observed-token inventory, `vsir demo exact --synthetic`\n- U006 M1 core/verify.py::verify_claims, present_instead, near-miss generator, the §12.4 L3 abstention eval\n- U007 M2a ingest/manifest.py + probe.py + render.py + window.py (bisection ladder), the generated data/source/synthetic_3window.pdf (off-by-one trap + crop trap)\n- U008 M2a vlm/{client,cache,stub}.py, prompts/{s1,s2}.md, ingest/extract.py (new S2 schema), replay mode + typed `fixture_miss`, the four §6.3 cache keys\n- U009 M2a ingest/derive.py, core/health.py (grounded_rate/text_trust/searchable_ratio), label precedence + ambiguity→list, code reattribution + moved_from, ingest/stitch.py (+series_id)\n- U010 M2a ingest/embed.py (D4 interleaved, embed_query_image), lexical + captions sparse surfaces, §6.6 fingerprint, ingest/index.py (is_current=False)\n- U011 M2a ingest/gates.py (§11.1), publish, three-clause retirement (§6.7), vsir_runs control collection + advisory lease, ingest/export.py (§6.8 labels.jsonl + observed_tokens.jsonl, safety_flag), run record (§6.9), `vsir runs show` / `gates rerun` / `publish --override`\n- U012 M2b port impl/data/raw/* and impl/data/exports/r-poc-*/{labels,withheld}.jsonl into data/fixtures/legacy/, plus the L2 parity and negative-set suite (§12.1, §12.3 PARITY rows)\n- U013 M2b the one real paid TC1E-SF ingest, freeze data/fixtures/TC1E-SF/*, set the grounded_rate threshold from the measured distribution (R4, C10)\n- U014 M3 serve/app.py, serve/auth.py (bearer), serve/audit.py (ten-field line, cost-in-audit-not-body), serve/budget.py (reads_remaining), `vsir serve`, §11.3 degradation rows\n- U015 M3 serve/tools/lookup.py + verify.py HTTP wrappers, six-value status surfaced end to end, next.suggest, unverified_hits, mcp/server.py stdio+SSE (same implementations, stateless), `vsir lookup`/`verify`/`mcp`\n- U016 M3 `vsir eval acceptance` (§12.3 incl. PARITY) + `vsir eval abstention` (§12.4)\n- U017 M4 serve/tools/skim.py `skim_pages`, §7.2.1 deterministic RRF ordering + decompose + why + rank, exclude, next affordances, image queries (D12), serve/tools/resolve.py (interpolated, label_verified, ambiguity→every candidate)\n- U018 M4 `GET /pages/{page_id}/image`, in-process raster LRU cache, serve/tools/fetch.py (region, dpi, inline, bytes_b64), §7.3 caps, `vsir demo narrow`\n- U019 M5 `skim_documents` + `skim_sections` aggregation (pages_matched, best_rank, preview.thumb_url), searchable_ratio on every DocHit\n- U020 M5 serve/tools/read.py (present/absent/unverifiable stamps, sufficient, page_provenance, ≤3-page cap, question-keyed read_key cache, pinned dpi 220), vlm/prompts/read.md\n- U021 M6 runner/triage.py (tri-state relevant|uncertain|irrelevant + the five §8.2 safeguards), runner/prompt.py, §8.1a fetch-vs-read routing, `vsir ask --explain`\n- U022 M6 runner/loop.py + the six correction loops (§8.3), runner/answer.py (server-side answer gate, §8.4), §8.5 abstention wording, VSIR_READS_PER_QUESTION, POST /ask, `vsir ask`\n- U023 M7 frontend/ React+TS+Vite two-zone console (viewer + agent panel + trust badges + click-to-scroll citations)\n- U024 M7 Playwright E2E replay suite + scripts/test-e2e.sh\n- U025 M8 is_current lifecycle, found_only_in_superseded, series_id across revisions, `--resume` + per-window checkpoints, SIGTERM checkpointing, `vsir retire <doc_id> [--revision]`, generated data/source/synthetic_large.pdf, typed `ladder_level_2_required`\n- U026 M8 `vsir eval corpus` — the §12.6 report against the five ground-truth sets with the D11 gates\n\n## Test levels already assigned (from S3)\nU001 L0+conformance · U002 L2+conformance · U003 L0+L2 · U004 L0 · U005 L0+L1 · U006 L0+L3 · U007 L0+L1 · U008 L0+L1 · U009 L0+L1 · U010 L0+L1+L2 · U011 L0+L1+L2+conformance · U012 L1+L2 · U013 L1+L2+L4 · U014 L2+conformance · U015 L2 · U016 L2+L3 · U017 L2 · U018 L2 · U019 L2 · U020 L0+L2+L4 · U021 L0+L2 · U022 L0+L2+L3+L4 · U023 L0 · U024 E2E · U025 L0+L1+L2 · U026 L5\n\n## The sixteen acceptance criteria (Spec §14)\n- AC-001 A code the model claimed but the page's text does not contain is unfindable through `lookup`, and appears only in `unverified_hits` when explicitly opted into (I2, F14)\n- AC-002 Exact matching is phrase-only; no variant of a label ever differs from it by more than whitespace (I3, F1, F3)\n- AC-003 The status enum has six values — `ok`, four distinct absences and `error` — and no Family A tool can return an empty `ok` (I5, F4, §7.1)\n- AC-004 A scanned document answers `not_searchable`, never `not_found` (F4)\n- AC-005 `verify` distinguishes present/absent/unverifiable, per (claim, page), and offers near-misses only as labelled different parts (F2, F16, I8)\n- AC-006 Every page number is proved by two independent checks; an offset failure bisects and re-bills instead of publishing (I4, F7)\n- AC-007 A run that has not passed its gates has zero queryable pages (I7, F17)\n- AC-008 Every cap in §7.3 is a typed 400 naming its bound; no silent clamp exists (F18)\n- AC-009 On the worked-trace fixture the answer costs exactly one paid `read`, with citations; the runner's ceiling for any question is `VSIR_READS_PER_QUESTION` (§8.4)\n- AC-010 The failure branch abstains with coverage numbers and never claims absence while unread image-only pages remain in scope (§8.5)\n- AC-011 The L3 abstention eval passes on 100 near-miss codes, in CI, on every commit\n- AC-012 The boot self-check refuses to serve on schema drift, fingerprint mismatch or a `-latest` model id (§4.3, F11)\n- AC-013 `labels.jsonl` delivers per-page codes_in_text, page_range, sections[], summaries[] and safety_flag to Part A (D1, C8)\n- AC-014 Every milestone's demo command in §0 runs green on a clean checkout\n- AC-015 One image runs every process type (web, ingest-worker, one-off admin); every deployment-varying value comes from the environment; no correctness-bearing state lives in a process or on local disk (§15 Factors III, V, VI, VIII, XII; C11)\n- AC-016 `SIGTERM` at any instant leaves no queryable half-document and `--resume` completes the run; `/health` and `/ready` behave per §15.1 during a Qdrant outage\n\n## Every spec section that must map to ≥1 unit\n§0 deliverable ledger · §1.1 the guarantee · §1.2 the one rule · §1.3 what this CR builds · §2.1 in scope · §2.2 out of scope · §2.3 corrections C1–C12 · §2.4 the port ledger · §2.5 the feature-removal ledger · §3 decisions D1–D12 · §4.1 layout · §4.2 pins and config · §4.3 boot self-check · §4.4 the CLI · §5.1 identifiers · §5.2 the S2 schema · §5.3 the page record · §5.4 INDEXED · §5.5 text index config · §5.6 tokenisation/variants/exact_filter · §5.7 health signals · §6.1 steps 01–12 · §6.2 windowing and bisection · §6.3 cache keys and replay · §6.4 the offset proof · §6.5 labels and code attribution · §6.6 embedding fingerprint · §6.7 publish gating and retirement · §6.8 exports · §6.9 the run record · §7.1 envelopes · §7.2.1 skim rungs · §7.2.2 lookup · §7.2.3 resolve · §7.2.4 verify · §7.2.5 fetch · §7.2.6 read · §7.3 caps · §7.4 HTTP surface/auth/audit · §7.5 MCP · §7.6 refusals · §8.1 the loop · §8.1a fetch-vs-read · §8.2 triage · §8.3 correction loops · §8.4 the answer gate · §8.5 abstention wording · §9 invariants · §10 failure catalogue · §11.1 publish gates · §11.2 answer gates · §11.3 degradation · §11.4 observability · §12.1 fixtures · §12.2 levels · §12.3 acceptance table · §12.4 abstention eval · §12.5 conformance greps · §12.6 corpus evaluation · §13 milestones · §14 acceptance criteria · §15 twelve factors · §15.1 orchestrator requirements · §15.2 bans · §16 NFRs · §17 open questions · §18 residual risks · §19 traceability to plan2 · §20 document map · §20.1 the known-defect register\n\n## Output format\n### Synthesis Agent 5: Traceability Matrix\n\n#### A. Spec section → units\n| Spec § | Units | Note |\n(one row per section in the list above, in order; if a section is inherently non-implementable — a rationale table, a document map — say so in the Note and still name the unit(s) whose Required Reading or Definition of Done carries it, so nothing is orphaned)\n\n#### B. Unit → spec sections → test levels\n| Unit | Primary spec sections | Test levels |\n(all 26)\n\n#### C. AC → units → tests\n| AC | Units | Named test(s) | Level |\n(all sixteen; the named tests should be concrete test names, and for AC-014 name the demo command per milestone)\n\n#### D. Unmapped items (report explicitly — this is the point of the exercise)\n- Spec sections with no unit: <list, or \"none\">\n- Units with no spec section: <list, or \"none\">\n- ACs with no unit or no test: <list, or \"none\">\n- ACs whose only coverage is a paid (L4/L5) test — a risk, because they cannot be proved without OQ-2: <list>\n","agentId":"a537a0ddada603798","agentType":"general-purpose","harnessNoteCount":0,"harnessTailCount":0,"harnessSectionHash":"8853d0d0a535a1a7","content":[{"type":"text","text":"### Synthesis Agent 5: Traceability Matrix\n\n#### A. Spec section → units\n\n| Spec § | Units | Note |\n|---|---|---|\n| §0 deliverable ledger | U001–U026 (all) | Ledger table aggregating every milestone's deliverables; not itself implemented — each unit's DoD instantiates one ledger line. |\n| §1.1 the guarantee | U006, U022 | Grounding guarantee enforced by `verify_claims` and the server-side answer gate. |\n| §1.2 the one rule | U006, U022 | Same enforcement path as §1.1. |\n| §1.3 what this CR builds | U001 | Scope narrative; carried by the M0 skeleton's DoD framing the whole CR. |\n| §2.1 in scope | U001 | Rationale; realized cumulatively by all 26 units, no single implementing unit. |\n| §2.2 out of scope | U002 | Enforced negatively via §12.5 conformance greps rather than built. |\n| §2.3 corrections C1–C12 | U001, U009, U011, U013, U025 | Distributed table; listed units are those whose description explicitly cites a correction (e.g., C10→U013). |\n| §2.4 the port ledger | U012 | Explicit — ports `impl/data/raw/*` and legacy exports into `data/fixtures/legacy/`. |\n| §2.5 the feature-removal ledger | U001, U002 | Rationale table of removed features; enforced by omission (skeleton DoD) and conformance greps. |\n| §3 decisions D1–D12 | U001, U010 (D4), U011 (D1), U017 (D12), U026 (D11) | Decisions distributed across units; representative citations shown. |\n| §4.1 layout | U001 | Explicit. |\n| §4.2 pins and config | U001 | Explicit (pins/lock, `.env.example`). |\n| §4.3 boot self-check | U001 | Explicit (`vsir doctor`). |\n| §4.4 the CLI | U001 | Explicit (base CLI); subcommands added incrementally by U011, U015, U018, U020, U022, U025, U026. |\n| §5.1 identifiers | U003 | Explicit (`core/ids.py`). |\n| §5.2 the S2 schema | U008 | Explicit (new S2 schema, `ingest/extract.py`). |\n| §5.3 the page record | U003 | Explicit (`core/record.py`). |\n| §5.4 INDEXED | U003 | Explicit (`core/indexed.py`, I6). |\n| §5.5 text index config | U003 | Explicit (Qdrant text-index creation). |\n| §5.6 tokenisation/variants/exact | U004 | Explicit (`core/tok.py`, `variants.py`, `exact.py`). |\n| §5.7 health signals | U009, U019 | Explicit (`core/health.py`); `searchable_ratio` also surfaced on DocHit by U019. |\n| §6.1 steps 01–12 | U007 | Explicit (`manifest.py`, `probe.py`, `render.py`, `window.py`). |\n| §6.2 windowing and bisection | U007, U025 | Explicit ladder in U007; `ladder_level_2_required` extends it in U025. |\n| §6.3 cache keys and replay | U008 | Explicit (four §6.3 cache keys, replay mode). |\n| §6.4 the offset proof | U007 | Bisection ladder implements the two-independent-check proof (I4). |\n| §6.5 labels and code attribution | U009 | Explicit (precedence, ambiguity→list, `moved_from`). |\n| §6.6 embedding fingerprint | U010 | Explicit. |\n| §6.7 publish gating and retirement | U011, U025 | Three-clause retirement (U011); `is_current` lifecycle across revisions (U025). |\n| §6.8 exports | U011 | Explicit (`export.py`, labels/observed_tokens, safety_flag). |\n| §6.9 the run record | U011 | Explicit. |\n| §7.1 envelopes | U004 | Explicit (Family A/B, hit models). |\n| §7.2.1 skim rungs | U017, U019 | `skim_pages` + RRF (U017); `skim_documents`/`skim_sections` aggregation (U019). |\n| §7.2.2 lookup | U005, U015 | Pure function (U005); HTTP/MCP wrapper (U015). |\n| §7.2.3 resolve | U017 | Explicit. |\n| §7.2.4 verify | U006, U015 | Core logic (U006); HTTP wrapper (U015). |\n| §7.2.5 fetch | U018 | Explicit. |\n| §7.2.6 read | U020 | Explicit. |\n| §7.3 caps | U004, U018 | Cap validators (U004); applied at fetch (U018). |\n| §7.4 HTTP surface/auth/audit | U014 | Explicit. |\n| §7.5 MCP | U015 | Explicit (`mcp/server.py`). |\n| §7.6 refusals | U004, U014 | Status-enum-driven refusals (U004); degradation rows (U014). |\n| §8.1 the loop | U022 | Explicit (`runner/loop.py`). |\n| §8.1a fetch-vs-read routing | U021 | Explicit. |\n| §8.2 tri-state triage | U021 | Explicit (`runner/triage.py`, five safeguards). |\n| §8.3 six correction loops | U022 | Explicit. |\n| §8.4 the answer gate | U022 | Explicit (`runner/answer.py`). |\n| §8.5 abstention wording | U022 | Explicit. |\n| §9 invariants | U003 (I6), U004 (I3, I5), U006 (I2, I8), U007 (I4), U011 (I7) | Distributed; each invariant maps to the unit enforcing it (mirrors Table C). |\n| §10 failure catalogue | U001 (F11), U004 (typed status), U006 (F2, F16), U007 (F7), U008 (fixture_miss), U011 (F17), U018 (F18) | Cross-cutting; each F-code lands in the unit whose error path implements it. |\n| §11.1 publish gates | U011 | Explicit. |\n| §11.2 answer gates | U022 | Explicit. |\n| §11.3 runtime degradation | U014 | Explicit (degradation rows). |\n| §11.4 observability | U001, U014 | JSON logs/release_id (U001); ten-field audit line (U014). |\n| §12.1 fixtures | U005, U007, U012, U013, U025 | Synthetic pages, synthetic_3window.pdf, legacy port, TC1E-SF, synthetic_large.pdf respectively. |\n| §12.2 levels | U002, U024 | Test-level scripts (U002); E2E level specifically (U024). |\n| §12.3 L2 acceptance table | U012, U016 | PARITY rows (U012); `vsir eval acceptance` (U016). |\n| §12.4 L3 abstention eval | U006, U016 | Eval logic (U006); `vsir eval abstention` CLI (U016). |\n| §12.5 conformance greps | U002 | Explicit. |\n| §12.6 corpus evaluation | U026 | Explicit. |\n| §13 milestones | U001–U026 (all, grouped by M-tag) | Milestone table is the union of all units grouped by phase. |\n| §14 acceptance criteria | U001–U026 (per Table C) | See Table C for the full AC↔unit mapping. |\n| §15 twelve factors | U001, U014, U025 | Factor III env config (U001); statelessness (U014); resume/checkpointing (U025). |\n| §15.1 orchestrator requirements | U002, U025 | `/health`+`/ready` (U002); SIGTERM/resume checkpointing (U025). |\n| §15.2 bans | U001, U002 | `-latest` model-id ban enforced by doctor (U001) and conformance greps (U002). |\n| §16 NFRs | U002, U026 | Non-implementable target table; enforced via test harness (U002) and measured in corpus eval (U026). |\n| §17 open questions | U013 | Non-implementable rationale; OQ-2/paid-calibration tension surfaces in U013's DoD (see Part D). |\n| §18 residual risks | U013 | Explicit (R4 cited directly in U013's description). |\n| §19 traceability to plan2 | U001, U002 | Non-implementable cross-reference; carried by repo layout (U001) and AGENTS.md (U002). |\n| §20 document map | U002 | Non-implementable; carried by AGENTS.md. |\n| §20.1 known-defect register | U006, U012 | Non-implementable register; informs the abstention eval's near-miss design (U006) and legacy-data porting awareness (U012). |\n\n#### B. Unit → spec sections → test levels\n\n| Unit | Primary spec sections | Test levels |\n|---|---|---|\n| U001 | §4.1, §4.2, §4.3, §4.4, §11.4, §15, §15.2 | L0+conformance |\n| U002 | §2.2, §11.4, §12.2, §12.5, §15.1, §19, §20 | L2+conformance |\n| U003 | §5.1, §5.3, §5.4, §5.5 | L0+L2 |\n| U004 | §5.6, §7.1, §7.3, §7.6, §9 | L0 |\n| U005 | §7.2.2, §12.1 | L0+L1 |\n| U006 | §1.1, §1.2, §7.2.4, §9, §12.4, §20.1 | L0+L3 |\n| U007 | §6.1, §6.2, §6.4, §12.1 | L0+L1 |\n| U008 | §5.2, §6.3, §10 | L0+L1 |\n| U009 | §5.7, §6.5 | L0+L1 |\n| U010 | §3 (D4), §6.6 | L0+L1+L2 |\n| U011 | §6.7, §6.8, §6.9, §9, §10, §11.1 | L0+L1+L2+conformance |\n| U012 | §2.4, §12.1, §12.3, §20.1 | L1+L2 |\n| U013 | §2.3 (C10), §12.1, §17, §18 | L1+L2+L4 |\n| U014 | §7.4, §7.6, §11.3, §11.4, §15 | L2+conformance |\n| U015 | §7.2.2, §7.2.4, §7.5 | L2 |\n| U016 | §12.3, §12.4 | L2+L3 |\n| U017 | §3 (D12), §7.2.1, §7.2.3 | L2 |\n| U018 | §7.2.5, §7.3 | L2 |\n| U019 | §5.7, §7.2.1 | L2 |\n| U020 | §7.2.6 | L0+L2+L4 |\n| U021 | §8.1a, §8.2 | L0+L2 |\n| U022 | §8.1, §8.3, §8.4, §8.5, §11.2 | L0+L2+L3+L4 |\n| U023 | §13 (M7) | L0 |\n| U024 | §12.2 | E2E |\n| U025 | §6.2, §6.7, §15, §15.1 | L0+L1+L2 |\n| U026 | §3 (D11), §12.6 | L5 |\n\n#### C. AC → units → tests\n\n| AC | Units | Named test(s) | Level |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| AC-001 | U006, U015 | `test_verify.py::test_claimed_code_absent_from_text_is_unfindable`; `test_lookup_api.py::test_unverified_hits_opt_in_only` | L0 + L2 |\n| AC-002 | U004 | `test_variants.py::test_exact_variant_differs_only_by_whitespace` | L0 |\n| AC-003 | U004 | `test_status.py::test_status_enum_has_six_values`; `test_envelope.py::test_family_a_never_returns_empty_ok` | L0 + conformance |\n| AC-004 | U004, U009, U005 | `test_lookup.py::test_scanned_page_returns_not_searchable_not_not_found` | L0 + L1 |\n| AC-005 | U006, U020 | `test_verify.py::test_present_absent_unverifiable_per_claim_page`; `test_verify.py::test_near_miss_labelled_different_part` | L0 + L3 |\n| AC-006 | U007 | `test_window.py::test_offset_proof_bisects_on_mismatch` (synthetic_3window.pdf off-by-one trap) | L1 |\n| AC-007 | U011 | `test_gates.py::test_unpublished_run_has_zero_queryable_pages`; `test-api.sh::gates_rerun_then_publish_flow` | L0 + L2 |\n| AC-008 | U004, U018 | `test_caps.py::test_every_cap_is_typed_400_naming_bound`; `test_fetch_api.py::test_region_dpi_cap_no_silent_clamp` | L0 + L2 |\n| AC-009 | U022 | `test-api.sh::ask_worked_trace_fixture_costs_one_paid_read_with_citations` (frozen worked-trace fixture, `VSIR_READS_PER_QUESTION` ceiling) | L2 (fixture-backed — see Part D) |\n| AC-010 | U022 | `test_answer.py::test_abstention_states_coverage_never_claims_absence_with_unread_image_pages` | L3 |\n| AC-011 | U006, U016 | `test-unit.sh::l3_abstention_eval_100_near_miss_codes` (gated in CI on every commit) | L3 |\n| AC-012 | U001 | `test_doctor.py::test_refuses_on_schema_drift`; `test_refuses_on_fingerprint_mismatch`; `test_refuses_on_latest_model_id` | L0 |\n| AC-013 | U011 | `test_export.py::test_labels_jsonl_has_codes_range_sections_summaries_safety_flag` | L0 + L1 |\n| AC-014 | U001/U002 (M0), U005 (M1), U007/U011 (M2a), U013 (M2b), U015 (M3), U018 (M4), U020 (M5), U021/U022 (M6), U023/U024 (M7), U025/U026 (M8) | M0: `vsir doctor` + `scripts/test-unit.sh`; M1: `vsir demo exact --synthetic`; M2a: stub-ingest-and-publish demo (`vsir runs show`); M2b: real TC1E-SF ingest demo; M3: `vsir lookup`/`vsir verify`/`vsir mcp`; M4: `vsir demo narrow`; M5: read demo over frozen fixture; M6: `vsir ask --explain`; M7: console + `scripts/test-e2e.sh`; M8: `vsir retire <doc_id>` + `vsir eval corpus` | L0–L2 (M0,M1,M3,M4,M7); L1/L2 (M5,M6,M8); **L4** (M2b — paid) |\n| AC-015 | U001, U014 | `test-unit.sh::conformance_single_image_all_process_types`; `test_config.py::test_all_deployment_values_from_env_no_local_disk_state` | conformance |\n| AC-016 | U025, U002 | `test_ingest_resume.py::test_sigterm_mid_window_then_resume_completes_no_partial_document`; `test_health_ready.py::test_health_ready_during_qdrant_outage` | L1 + L2 |\n\n#### D. Unmapped items\n\n- **Spec sections with no unit:** none — every section maps to ≥1 unit above (several via a rationale-carrier note rather than direct implementation: §0, §1.3, §2.1, §2.2, §2.5, §16, §17, §19, §20, §20.1).\n- **Units with no spec section:** none — all 26 units have an explicit primary section in Table B.\n- **ACs with no unit or no test:** none — all sixteen have at least one unit and one named test in Table C.\n- **ACs whose only coverage is a paid (L4/L5) test:** **AC-014**, specifically its M2b-milestone demo command. M2b's entire purpose is \"the one real paid TC1E-SF ingest\" (U013) — there is no fixture-backed substitute for demonstrating that milestone's demo command green on a clean checkout without paid spend, so this slice of AC-014 is provable only at L4 and is blocked on the same OQ-2 cost/budget question implicit in U013's DoD. **AC-009** is a secondary, softer instance of the same risk: its CI-repeatable test runs at L2 against the frozen worked-trace fixture, but that fixture's fidelity (and therefore AC-009's ultimate truth about real paid-read cost) traces back to the same one-time paid calibration performed in U013/M2b — worth flagging even though a deterministic L2 proxy exists today."}],"resolvedModel":"claude-sonnet-5","totalDurationMs":244351,"totalTokens":52447,"totalToolUseCount":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3340,"cache_read_input_tokens":22480,"output_tokens":26625,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":20795},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3340},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":26625,"cache_read_input_tokens":22480,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3340,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3340,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"toolStats":{"readCount":0,"searchCount":0,"bashCount":1,"editFileCount":0,"linesAdded":0,"linesRemoved":0,"otherToolCount":0}}}
