{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CetGiPQdFW8YezgQYAABs","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Plan written. `development/cr1/plan/cr1-implementation-plan.md` — 3,442 lines, **26 units across M0–M8**. No code implemented; the spec is unchanged.\n\n## What's in it\n\n**Structure:** Milestone Map → 26 units (full template each) → dependency graph → test strategy → invariant/failure coverage → assumptions/risks → traceability → order → parallel bundles.\n\n**Unit distribution:** M0=2, M1=4, M2a=5, M2b=2, M3=3, M4=2, M5=2, M6=2, M7=2, M8=2. Every unit has a Working Deliverable, a Demo Command, a Rollback Plan and executable acceptance criteria (26/26 verified).\n\n**Safety net is complete.** All eight invariants and all nineteen failure rows — including the seven split parts (F2, F4, F5, F8×3, F11, F12, F18) — have an owning unit whose milestone matches Spec §9's *\"Asserted from\"* and §10's *\"Closed at\"* columns, plus a named test. Every conformance grep, publish gate and degradation row is owned. **No uncovered rows.**\n\n**Spend discipline:** only U013, U020, U022 plan an L4 test and U026 an L5 report, all behind `VSIR_ALLOW_PAID=1`. Everything else runs in replay (`VSIR_VLM=stub` + `VSIR_FIXTURE`). No test requires the real corpus or an API key. U012 (free — ports the already-paid `impl` fixtures and the parity suite) is ordered *before* U013, the first spend anywhere.\n\n## Two things worth your attention\n\n**1. Twelve stale-text adjudications (§8, SA-1…SA-12).** Gap analysis found **no true blockers**, but the spec contradicts itself in places its own corrections tables already resolved. Three are load-bearing:\n\n- **SA-1** — §4.2's *\"Text only — page rasters are not embedded\"* and §19's C12 row are **stale**. C12 (explicitly \"reversed on evidence\") and D4 win: the dense vector **is** a fused image+text embedding with the raster as the last `Part`. A builder reading §4.2 would drop it.\n- **SA-2/SA-3** — §2.2 lists sparse+RRF as out of scope and §7.2.1 says *\"there is no sparse vector\"*; **D2 reversed both**. All three surfaces ship.\n- **SA-4** — §8.2's `relevant → read` is the generic verb; §8.1a's **\"Default: `fetch`\"** governs the route.\n\n**2. One deviation from your prompt, flagged as SA-6.** You said a unit \"inherits its milestone's spend class.\" I marked `Spend` per what the unit *actually* spends instead — because §13 M2b explicitly orders the free fixture port before the paid ingest, and because your S3 rule (\"only `Spend: paid` units may plan an L4 test\") would otherwise let U012/U019/U021/U025 plan paid tests they don't need. Milestone ceilings live in the Milestone Map. Say the word if you want it the literal way.\n\nThe progress file is populated with all 26 unit IDs, the ten milestone demo commands as a checklist, and the open questions with their §17 defaults."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1008,"cache_read_input_tokens":384685,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1008},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4eefb16f-3989-4441-9cd3-d294cfccb11f","uuid":"e0dec258-5ec8-4643-a244-2d8e041ac919","timestamp":"2026-09-09T17:37:37.682Z","request_id":"req_011CetGiLspRiedTNCSqsbC1"}
